ser":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T10:50:51-08:00","id":1000885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1000851#post1000851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.cbsnews.com/news/cbs-news-exit-polls-how-donald-trump-won-the-us-presidency/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.cbsnews.com/news/cbs-news...us-presidency/</a><br /> <br /> More details. More Black men voted for Trump then was expected, he beat Hillary amoung Republican and Independant female voters.<br /> <br /> 25% of Trump voters felt he was unqualified.<br /> <br /> The democracts should have run an outsider this election, but they only listened to their own voices and picked the establishment candiate. And now some are blaming it on her gender, so they've learned nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. Apparently Hillary did much worse than expected with African-Americans (especially in comparison to Obama) and she also did worse with female voters than Obama did in 2008 and 2012 - I think after all the misogynistic comments that Trump made, plus the fact that Hillary was a women, a lot of people were assumed she would run away with the female vote. But women didn't come out in droves to support Hillary and doing worse among female voters than Obama did was a mortal wound to her campaign. Women by and large just plain didn't like her.<br /> <br /> Further, while Hillary did better among Latino voters than Obama did, it was more of a protest vote against Trump than support for her, and it still wasn't a game changer - it wasn't enough to balance out her drop in other segments of the populace.<br /> <br /> I think the Democrats will need to spend the next two years soul searching and contemplating all the places they went wrong. Hopefully they understand that, to a large degree, the sense of outrage against perceived corruption among the status quo was the biggest reason Hillary lost and the Democrats should take the opportunity to clean house a little bit. It's the only way I can see them being able to possibly take back the Senate in two years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T11:13:39-08:00","id":1000898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/amp/www.mirror.co.uk/news/world-news/trump-win-sparks-riots-across-9225317.amp?client=ms-android-bell-ca\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/amp/www.mirror.co.uk/news/world-news/trump-win-sparks-riots-across-9225317.amp?client=ms-android-bell-ca\" target=\"_blank\"> Redirect Notice </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/amp/www.mirror.co.uk/news/world-news/trump-win-sparks-riots-across-9225317.amp?client=ms-android-bell-ca\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.google.ca/amp/www.mirror.co.uk/news/world-news/trump-win-sparks-riots-across-9225317.amp?client=ms-android-bell-ca </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> My main concern is far too many Democracts will blame sexism against women and racism for Trumps win, and so will believe they did nothing wrong and that they have nothing learn from this.<br /> <br /> Yes Trump does have some racist supporters, but he also has black supporters, Latino supporters and tons of female supporters.<br /> <br /> The trust is most people hated Hillary before she ran for president, democracts ignored this, just saying its because she's a woman, ignored the majoritynof Americans, and payed the price.<br /> <br /> The democracts also ignored the fact that the public didn't want an establishment candiate, that they were sick of free trade agreements written by and for corporations. People got fed up with being ignored and they said fuck her burning this shit down and they did.<br /> <br /> The democracts are as responsible for this as the republicans, so stop blaming it on her being a woman, its a cop out so that they don't have to take any kind of responsiblity for picking an obvious dud.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T11:23:34-08:00","id":1000906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1000847#post1000847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly I don't know what Trump is going to do on healthcare. There was a time believe it or not when Trump supported universal public health. I just pray Trump finds his soul whereever he placed it.<br /> <br /> I do wish the Demoacts had won the senate and congress, just to balance out Trump.<br /> <br /> I apologize if my comments came off as insensitive or cold. It all seems surreal to me. And I'm sorry about you losing a beloved family member.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it's not you. It's me. Any notion I had of loyalty or love for America as an institution died yesterday. Also if you don't think that gender had anything to do with this then you've not learned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T11:32:04-08:00","id":1000909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/amp/www.telegraph.co.uk/news/2016/11/09/hillary-clinton-failed-to-win-over-black-hispanic-and-female-vot/amp/?client=ms-android-bell-ca\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/amp/www.telegraph.co.uk/news/2016/11/09/hillary-clinton-failed-to-win-over-black-hispanic-and-female-vot/amp/?client=ms-android-bell-ca\" target=\"_blank\"> Redirect Notice </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.ca/amp/www.telegraph.co.uk/news/2016/11/09/hillary-clinton-failed-to-win-over-black-hispanic-and-female-vot/amp/?client=ms-android-bell-ca\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.google.ca/amp/www.telegraph.co.uk/news/2016/11/09/hillary-clinton-failed-to-win-over-black-hispanic-and-female-vot/amp/?client=ms-android-bell-ca </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Trump actually did better then Romney did amoung black, hispanic, and young voters. Hillary did worse then Obama with all these groups.<br /> <br /> In fact I heard someone say Trump did better among black voters then any republican presidential candiate in along time time, but I can't firm that yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T11:48:23-08:00","id":1000915,"title":"","content":"Honestly this just shows what a great candidate Obama was. He galvanized a coalition that worked for him. You can not go ahead and just hope this will happen all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T12:02:17-08:00","id":1000920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1000898#post1000898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.google.ca/amp/www.mirror.co.uk/news/world-news/trump-win-sparks-riots-across-9225317.amp?client=ms-android-bell-ca\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.google.ca/amp/www.mirror...ndroid-bell-ca</a><br /> <br /> My main concern is far too many Democracts will blame sexism against women and racism for Trumps win, and so will believe they did nothing wrong and that they have nothing learn from this.<br /> <br /> Yes Trump does have some racist supporters, but he also has black supporters, Latino supporters and tons of female supporters.<br /> <br /> The trust is most people hated Hillary before she ran for president, democracts ignored this, just saying its because she's a woman, ignored the majoritynof Americans, and payed the price.<br /> <br /> The democracts also ignored the fact that the public didn't want an establishment candiate, that they were sick of free trade agreements written by and for corporations. People got fed up with being ignored and they said fuck her burning this shit down and they did.<br /> <br /> The democracts are as responsible for this as the republicans, so stop blaming it on her being a woman, its a cop out so that they don't have to take any kind of responsiblity for picking an obvious dud.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's nonsense to say that her being a woman wasn't a contributing factor. It wasn't, however, the only contributing factor, and it would be equally nonsense to say that it was. The fact is, the election was the result of a lot of issues all coming together in a perfect shitstorm. And of course the Democratic Party needs to learn from this, and hopefully they don't just take away the notion that running a woman is untenable, because it's not. But they do need to keep in mind that a female candidate will be held to a different standard than a male candidate, because sexism is still a huge issue. They also need to learn not to count on any demographic's vote as a given. Also, hopefully the young voters will wake up and smell the reality that if they vote third party, they do in fact hurt the democratic candidate's campaign, and if they don't like the republican candidate, they're going to have to compromise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T12:19:07-08:00","id":1000926,"title":"","content":"Puerto Rico's new governor is a statehood supporter whose platform has been joining the US proper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T12:23:15-08:00","id":1000931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/inspired-life/wp/2016/11/02/what-is-this-election-missing-empathy-for-trump-voters/?tid=sm_tw\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/inspired-life/wp/2016/11/02/what-is-this-election-missing-empathy-for-trump-voters/?tid=sm_tw\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/inspired-life/wp/2016/11/02/what-is-this-election-missing-empathy-for-trump-voters/?tid=sm_tw\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/inspired-life/wp/2016/11/02/what-is-this-election-missing-empathy-for-trump-voters/?tid=sm_tw </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Just another reminder that reminder that this is a self inflicted defeat. Democracts demonized just as many people unfairly as republicans have. Democracts should try empathy and understanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T12:26:15-08:00","id":1000932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1000931#post1000931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/inspired-life/wp/2016/11/02/what-is-this-election-missing-empathy-for-trump-voters/?tid=sm_tw\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/...ers/?tid=sm_tw</a><br /> <br /> Just another reminder that reminder that this is a self inflicted defeat. Democracts demonized just as many people unfairly as republicans have. Democracts should try empathy and understanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>If both sides demonized 'just as many people unfairly' and one side won, why do you think changing tactics would work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T12:28:17-08:00","id":1000933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1000920#post1000920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, it's nonsense to say that her being a woman wasn't a contributing factor. It wasn't, however, the only contributing factor, and it would be equally nonsense to say that it was. The fact is, the election was the result of a lot of issues all coming together in a perfect shitstorm. And of course the Democratic Party needs to learn from this, and hopefully they don't just take away the notion that running a woman is untenable, because it's not. But they do need to keep in mind that a female candidate will be held to a different standard than a male candidate, because sexism is still a huge issue. They also need to learn not to count on any demographic's vote as a given. Also, hopefully the young voters will wake up and smell the reality that if they vote third party, they do in fact hurt the democratic candidate's campaign, and if they don't like the republican candidate, they're going to have to compromise.</div> </div> </div> </div> Your absolutely right a female will be treated differently, she will be treated better on average and any pointing out of her flaws will be white washed by pointing to her gender and saying it was sexism.<br /> <br /> Britian, Canada, India, Isreal, Pakistan, various American states have had have all had female leaders, this is weak arguement for which you have no proof.<br /> <br /> Polls asking people if they'd vote for a female President say YES, but that doesn't mean they don't have standard (okay Trump won so they're not high standards, but they still have standards).<br /> <br /> You keep ignoring the fact that democract picked a woman that they knew was unpopular, knew had a history of scandals, know who voted in support of various wars, knew who was bought and payed for by Wall Street, knew it, still picked her anyways, and then say damn it America must not be ready for a female president. <br /> <br /> That a cheap cop out. How did crap like that fit the democracts issues?<br /> <br /> Trump was beatable, at one point Hillary even had a strong lead even with all the baggage, but more piled on and it was too much.<br /> <br /> Democracts could have crushed this election, this was a 100% winnable, instead you scrapped the bottom of every rock you could find and came up with someone with more dirty laundry then a laundry mat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 11-09-2016, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T12:31:07-08:00","id":1000935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1000932#post1000932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If both sides demonized 'just as many people unfairly' and one side won, why do you think changing tactics would work?</div> </div> </div> </div> Because I think the democracts need to start pulling in some of those voters who feel disrespected or Trump and others like him will continue to win.<br /> <br /> Look many of these people used to vote Democract once.<br /> <br /> Democracts need to stop acting like snobs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T12:37:26-08:00","id":1000937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1000933#post1000933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your absolutely right a female will be treated differently, she will be treated better on average and any pointing out of her flaws will be white washed by pointing to her gender and saying it was sexism.<br /> <br /> Britian, Canada, India, Isreal, Pakistan, various American states have had have all had female leaders, this is weak arguement for which you have no proof.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're so insanely wrong here I almost crushed my mouse in anger. How the media treated Clinton this election is proof that the double standards women are held to hurt them more than help. Just because other places have female leaders doesn't mean that sexism unfairly helps her.<br /> <br /> I don't care how you respond to this. I'm ignoring you at this point for your obvious sexism and privilege blindness. Nothing you have to say will have anything resembling value.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T12:37:49-08:00","id":1000938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1000935#post1000935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I think the democracts need to start pulling in some of those voters who feel disrespected or Trump and others like him will continue to win.<br /> <br /> Look many of these people used to vote Democract once.<br /> <br /> Democracts need to stop acting like snobs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Half the campaign was about pulling in people disrespected by the masses.<br /> <br /> Part of the problem is that just because you feel disrespected by Trump doesn't mean you're going to vote for Clinton. Because Clinton came with her own baggage, and leaks kept making that baggage worse and worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T1