userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-09-2016, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T12:46:35-08:00","id":1000941,"title":"","content":"Tons of people have said bad things about Trump, the media hates him, hell even Foxes news doesn't like him, he got made fun of by every comedian in the Western world.<br /> <br /> Almost the entire establishment was against him. Many republican elected official wouldn't endorse him or withdrew endorsements.<br /> <br /> So no Trump didn't get a free ride.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T12:52:23-08:00","id":1000942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1000940#post1000940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, because the voter base totally ignored all of Hillary Clinton's flaws and was comparatively harsh on Donald Trump... Wait, what?<br /> <br /> <br /> I specifically said I hope the Democratic Party doesn't take away from this election the idea that a female candidate is untenable, because it isn't. Stating that there have been female leaders doesn't contradict what I said in any way.</div> </div> </div> </div> I absolutely agree that democracts shouldn't assume a female condiate can't win, one can. Just pick wiser next, male or female, who ever has the best ideas.<br /> <br /> In my own country I voted for Alexa McDough, former NDP leader twice to be Prime Minister (indirectly of course, parliamentary democracy, but that was my intent), I voted twice for Andrea Howrath for Premier, and dispite being a major critic of Premier Kathleen Wynne's over Privatization, I support her experiment in BMI and Sex Education reforms (mostly), and that she gave boys fair access to vaccines, the previously only girls got access to in Ontario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T12:52:41-08:00","id":1000943,"title":"","content":"I... seriously hope you're not holding up Kim Campbell as an example of an elected Canadian Prime Minister. Because she was the acting Prime Minister for six months before she was utterly crushed in an election for voicing such controversial opinions as, <br /> &quot;discussing a complete overhaul of Canada's social policies in all their complexities could not be done in just 47 days&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">and,</span></span></span><br /> <br /> &quot;it was unlikely that the deficit or unemployment would be much reduced before the &quot;end of the century&quot;.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The man who preceded her, Brian Mulroney, is generally considered the most unpopular Prime Minister in Canadian history. This is including William Lyon Mackenzie King, the Prime Minister who held seances with his dead mother to get policy advice, and is described as &quot;cold and tactless&quot;. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">So, yeah, she counts as a Prime Minister, and she was a woman who was Prime Minister, but Canada sure as hell didn't vote her in. In fact, when given the opportunity, the voters of the time obliterated her.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T13:11:59-08:00","id":1000951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1000932#post1000932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If both sides demonized 'just as many people unfairly' and one side won, why do you think changing tactics would work?</div> </div> </div> </div>No clue. But it was part of the problem the other way, so can't hurt.<br /> <br /> Really, a lot of those people are convinced you can't have natural beauty and economic well-being. That's a huge sticking point that I hope to help unstick in my career.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T13:53:07-08:00","id":1000966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1000943#post1000943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I... seriously hope you're not holding up Kim Campbell as an example of an elected Canadian Prime Minister. Because she was the acting Prime Minister for six months before she was utterly crushed in an election for voicing such controversial opinions as, <br /> &amp;quot;discussing a complete overhaul of Canada's social policies in all their complexities could not be done in just 47 days&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">and,</span></span></span><br /> <br /> &amp;quot;it was unlikely that the deficit or unemployment would be much reduced before the &amp;quot;end of the century&amp;quot;.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The man who preceded her, Brian Mulroney, is generally considered the most unpopular Prime Minister in Canadian history. This is including William Lyon Mackenzie King, the Prime Minister who held seances with his dead mother to get policy advice, and is described as &amp;quot;cold and tactless&amp;quot;. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">So, yeah, she counts as a Prime Minister, and she was a woman who was Prime Minister, but Canada sure as hell didn't vote her in. In fact, when given the opportunity, the voters of the time obliterated her.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div> Kim Campbell lost because her team put out an ad making fun of Jean Chetiens facial paralysis and because the lying liberals promised to dump Brian's bad trade agreement (but sadly didn't bye bye large chunk of Canada's munufacturing sector).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T14:12:56-08:00","id":1000976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1000966#post1000966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kim Campbell lost because her team put out an ad making fun of Jean Chetiens facial paralysis and because the lying liberals promised to dump Brian's bad trade agreement (but sadly didn't bye bye large chunk of Canada's munufacturing sector).</div> </div> </div> </div>They teach that in schools.it was the first big Canadian Attack Ad in politics. It had huge backlash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11257-volver","name":"Volver","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T14:30:57-08:00","id":1000985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1000937#post1000937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're so insanely wrong here I almost crushed my mouse in anger. How the media treated Clinton this election is proof that the double standards women are held to hurt them more than help. Just because other places have female leaders doesn't mean that sexism unfairly helps her.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Democrats managed to pick the most disliked, divisive, corrupt-seeming and scandal-laden politician that Washington had to offer and she still <i>barely</i> lost the election. Outside of the far right news groups like Breitbart, the media (even Fox) was pretty damn anti-Trump as a whole. Even many &quot;centrist&quot; organizations like CNN were constantly running anti-Trump articles and news stories. In fact, I haven't seen the mainstream media come down against a candidate that hard in my entire life.<br /> <br /> Hell, many news agencies changed the way they write articles, including fact checking in the article as a way to combat the blatant lies told by Donald Trump.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the media was hard on Clinton at several points, but a lot of that was due to the way she refused to allow the media to have much access to her and would keep information hidden (like when she had pneumonia, didn't tell the media and then after she fainted on the way out of the 9/11 event kept the media stuck speculating for several days before finally telling them what had happened.)<br /> <br /> Overall, I honestly didn't see much evidence to suggest that the media was all <i>that</i> much harsher on her than it's been on many presidential candidates - certainly not enough to cite it as definitive proof that she was hamstrung by a double standard. Really, the worst you can say is that the media wasn't pulling for Hillary the way they did when Obama was running, but it seemed pretty clear they were trying their best to tear into Donald Trump.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T14:35:39-08:00","id":1000987,"title":"","content":"The presidency is, and has been for some time, a complete farce. Look at how Trump was predicted by the Simpsons. Look at how both candidates were so dirty it was a race to see who could be the lesser evil. Both played on tokenism, Trump with Xenophobia and other forms of bigotry, and Hillary using gender politics and the wage gap. Both had so many scandals neither should've been allowed near the race, let alone to win the primaries. Hillary is in fact the deciding vote on casting Trump in this case though, as she sabotaged Bernie in the primary, who was a clear win should he be the candidate, then elevated Trump due to polls showing him as the weakest link among RNC candidates. Both are very corrupt, only Trump is also seemingly inept, much like George Bush Jr was. Both had media coverage that pandered to their viewers and hid flaws from the public. Both parties attempted things with the voting and so forth. Trump has never disclosed his earnings and Hillary has had people assassinated, among many, many other things. As far as I'm concerned this election was just an escalation of the shitshow it has been for some time. One need only look at what happened to JFK when he attempted to speak out against the elite, or at treasonous trash legislation like the Patriot Act and how it was not only allowed but encouraged, to see where this country has been going. The President is merely a high paid actor in most situations, although they do have leeway over several aspects of government. The clear and present dangers of things like the NSA were never addressed, not even by Bernie, what does that tell you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","ra