div>This. This is why I say it's nonsense to believe sexism wasn't a factor and also nonsense to believe sexism was the only factor (or even the primary reason).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T15:33:00-08:00","id":1001030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001021#post1001021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't say it wasn't relevant: I'm saying political assassinations like that are fiction. Paranoid delusions created by a mind looking for greater meaning.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's your source for saying that they're all paranoia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T15:45:21-08:00","id":1001036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1000996#post1000996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, the most baffling thing that people believe relevant to the election is that the Clintons have assassinated people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I always found it amusing. In a lot of people's minds Hillary is the greatest criminal mastermind of the last hundred years. She had carried out assassinations and murders, she had engaged in bribery, blackmail, espionage and treason. She and her henchmen had the election rigged. What's more, she had done all of this and even after Republicans had carried out hundreds of thousands of manhours of investigation and spent millions of dollars looking at every thing she had done, they weren't able to find any proof that she had actually done any of these things. She was so smart, so clever and so sneaky she made Lex Luthor look like a 5 year old kid. Or at least that's the way a lot of people perceived her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T15:49:35-08:00","id":1001039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001003#post1001003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, basically this. We got Brexit from the roughly same stratum of population. We got, here in Hungary the massive success of Fidesz and Orb\u00e1n from the same too. I don't like these worldwide trends and it scares me a lot more than Trump on itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. In Sweden, the anti-immigration Sverigedemokraterna is the third biggest party. It's a very concerning development.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't think it's a movement in the sense that there's a group of people instigating all of this. I think it's more a case of certain values reacting to the rapidly changing conditions in the world. Both the progress of information technology and the questioning of cultural assumptions are moving at a break-neck speed. I can see a reactionary stance as a means of relating to that without feeling like you lose your grasp on your own life and the basis of your identity. That, of course, doesn't legitimate it in my eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 11-09-2016, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T15:50:30-08:00","id":1001040,"title":"","content":"More recently they're claiming she's a cannibal and Satanic pedophile.<br /> <br /> If anything the results of the election should be working to prove wrong a lot of long-running conspiracies like the media and media controlling who wins. I don't like it but people voted and the people who wanted Trump got what they wanted, even if no one else really did.<br /> <br /> Got to educate your kids, got to get people voting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-09-2016, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T15:55:52-08:00","id":1001043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001040#post1001040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More recently they're claiming she's a cannibal and Satanic pedophile.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Sigh* makes me miss the old days, when most pedophiles were God fearing vegans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T15:57:51-08:00","id":1001044,"title":"","content":"You know the default ending of the Exalted universe? Welcome to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T16:13:42-08:00","id":1001051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001039#post1001039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed. In Sweden, the anti-immigration Sverigedemokraterna is the third biggest party. It's a very concerning development.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't think it's a movement in the sense that there's a group of people instigating all of this. I think it's more a case of certain values reacting to the rapidly changing conditions in the world. Both the progress of information technology and the questioning of cultural assumptions are moving at a break-neck speed. I can see a reactionary stance as a means of relating to that without feeling like you lose your grasp on your own life and the basis of your identity. That, of course, doesn't legitimate it in my eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting return to nationalistic parties.<br /> <br /> As of now, the reds have control over the white house, congress, soon to be supreme court, and the large majority of the state governments.<br /> <br /> This is not the party of Mccain, Eisenhower or even Bush. This is the party of Giuliani, Chris Christie, and Trump.<br /> <br /> May God help us all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T16:21:55-08:00","id":1001057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1000985#post1000985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Democrats managed to pick the most disliked, divisive, corrupt-seeming and scandal-laden politician that Washington had to offer and she still <i>barely</i> lost the election. Outside of the far right news groups like Breitbart, the media (even Fox) was pretty damn anti-Trump as a whole. Even many &amp;quot;centrist&amp;quot; organizations like CNN were constantly running anti-Trump articles and news stories. In fact, I haven't seen the mainstream media come down against a candidate that hard in my entire life.<br /> <br /> Hell, many news agencies changed the way they write articles, including fact checking in the article as a way to combat the blatant lies told by Donald Trump.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the media was hard on Clinton at several points, but a lot of that was due to the way she refused to allow the media to have much access to her and would keep information hidden (like when she had pneumonia, didn't tell the media and then after she fainted on the way out of the 9/11 event kept the media stuck speculating for several days before finally telling them what had happened.)<br /> <br /> Overall, I honestly didn't see much evidence to suggest that the media was all <i>that</i> much harsher on her than it's been on many presidential candidates - certainly not enough to cite it as definitive proof that she was hamstrung by a double standard. Really, the worst you can say is that the media wasn't pulling for Hillary the way they did when Obama was running, but it seemed pretty clear they were trying their best to tear into Donald Trump.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I think Trump even managed to piss off Breitbart for a time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T16:26:31-08:00","id":1001060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001057#post1001057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually I think Trump even managed to piss off Breitbart for a time.</div> </div> </div> </div>The executive chairman of Breitbart's parent company is the chief executive of Trump's campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T16:28:48-08:00","id":1001062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001036#post1001036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I always found it amusing. In a lot of people's minds Hillary is the greatest criminal mastermind of the last hundred years. She had carried out assassinations and murders, she had engaged in bribery, blackmail, espionage and treason. She and her henchmen had the election rigged. What's more, she had done all of this and even after Republicans had carried out hundreds of thousands of manhours of investigation and spent millions of dollars looking at every thing she had done, they weren't able to find any proof that she had actually done any of these things. She was so smart, so clever and so sneaky she made Lex Luthor look like a 5 year old kid. Or at least that's the way a lot of people perceived her.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah alot of that kind of stuff is silly, but I doubt most of Trump voters actually believed the more extreme things.<br /> <br /> There was far more realistic reality based compaints, like major ties to Wall Street, investiagtions by the FBI that got crushed thanks to Hillary's connections, voting favour multiple wars that killed countless civilians, ect...<br /> <br /> If Hillary had hit squads Trump and Pence would be dead now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T16:34:24-08:00","id":1001067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1000851#post1000851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The democracts should have run an outsider this election, but they only listened to their own voices and picked the establishment candiate. And now some are blaming it on her gender, so they've learned nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be brutally honest, Hillary's gender is one reason why she catches so much shit. You can't separate the sexism from everything else aimed at her and claim that it plays no role. Well, you can, but it's not accurate to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T16:39:15-08:00","id":1001070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001040#post1001040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More recently they're claiming she's a cannibal and Satanic pedophile.<br /> <br /> If anything the results of the election should be working to prove wrong a lot of long-running conspiracies like the media and media controlling who wins. I don't like it but people voted and the people who wanted Trump got what they wanted, even if no one else really did.<br /> <br /> Got to educate your kids, got to get people voting.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the result of circular thinking: if anyone claims something wild or outside of the scope of your experience, it must be false as appealed by the authority of the media in question. Never mind that those media stations are owned by only six corporations or who owns those, it is assumed to be a given since the majority believes it to be so. Therefore, you don't feel the need to present any evidence at all, just to point to this bias as proof. Meanwhile, any proof I might present will be dismissed on the grounds of the presenters being &quot;quackpots&quot; or the theory itself being ludicrous. There is literally no way to disprove this argument since it's never been proven in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T16:48:01-08:00","id":1001074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zeroninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001070#post1001070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the result of circular thinking: if anyone claims something wild or outside of the scope of your experience, it must be false as appealed by the authority of the media in question.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the result of the media not influencing the election to go against Trump despite most media personalities being vocally against him, even those traditionally pro-Republican in stance. Such as Glenn Beck.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Therefore, you don't feel the need to present any evidence at all, just point to this bias as truth. </div> </div> </div>This is what you're doing. The election didn't go one way, so some mysterious force is the cause. This mysterious force that apparently elected Bush twice, then Obama twice, then Trump. Because of mysterious plans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-09-2016, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T16:50:27-08:00","id":1001075,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=nofather;n1001074]<br /> <br /> It's the result of the media not influencing the election to go against Trump despite most media personalities being vocally against him, even those traditionally pro-Republican in stance.<br /> <br /> [quote]Therefore, you don't feel the need to present any evidence at all, just point to this bias as truth.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> This is what you're doing. The election didn't go one way, so some mysterious force is the cause. </div> </div> </div>It did influence the popular vote against Trump, just not the electoral college vote. That's conflating two different things. And no, that's not what I'm doing, I am as stated willing to provide evidence if it would be considered. However, since you've already made up your mind on the basis of popular opinion on the matter, there's no point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T16:55:37-08:00","id":1001077,"title":"","content":"On that note, please sign if you agree the electoral college is a complete farce:<br /> <a href=\"https://www.dailykos.com/campaigns/petitions/sign-the-petition-abolish-the-electoral-college\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dailykos.com/campaigns/p...ctoral-college</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T17:08:03-08:00","id":1001082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zeroninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001075#post1001075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It did influence the popular vote against Trump, just not the electoral college vote. That's conflating two different things.</div> </div> </div> </div>The electoral college is there for a reason, and while it might be worth reconsidering, it's there so a popular block can't make decisions for the rest of the country. So urban centers can't push through a president who wants to ban livestock, which might affect those wide swaths of America in between. Said vote is still based on the popular vote in its corresponding area.<br /> <br /> It's literally working the way it's supposed to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And no, that's not what I'm doing, I am as stated willing to provide evidence if it would be considered. However, since you've already made up your mind on the basis of popular opinion on the matter, there's no point. </div> </div> </div>Not at all. I'm very open minded. Incredibly doubtful, because just the other day all the conspiracy theorists, including Trump, thought Clinton was going to win, even if she cheated. But still, open-minded and curious. You said that the presidency is a complete farce and to 'Look at how Trump was predicted by the Simpsons.' So is the Simpsons the determinator of our futures? Or is it just tv? Or movies?<br /> <br /> You also stated that Sanders 'was a clear win should he be the candidate.' Do you have proof of this? Do you think the older Democrats who abhor socialism would have embraced him? Or that all those who don't like free healthcare would decide for vote for him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T17:29:06-08:00","id":1001090,"title":"","content":"While I'm surprised Trump was elected(and sad because he is a giant sack of orange-colored shit), I'm even more surprised that my moronic state re-elected the human waste of oxygen that is Marco Rubio. <br /> <br /> Okay. It's Florida. So maybe I'm not surprised.<br /> <br /> I need to get the fuck out of this state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T17:45:11-08:00","id":1001096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001090#post1001090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I'm surprised Trump was elected(and sad because he is a giant sack of orange-colored shit), I'm even more surprised that my moronic state re-elected the human waste of oxygen that is Marco Rubio.<br /> <br /> Okay. It's Florida. So maybe I'm not surprised.<br /> <br /> I need to get the fuck out of this state.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be wise, considering the parts that will be underwater soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T18:07:04-08:00","id":1001111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001039#post1001039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed. In Sweden, the anti-immigration Sverigedemokraterna is the third biggest party. It's a very concerning development.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't think it's a movement in the sense that there's a group of people instigating all of this. I think it's more a case of certain values reacting to the rapidly changing conditions in the world. Both the progress of information technology and the questioning of cultural assumptions are moving at a break-neck speed. I can see a reactionary stance as a means of relating to that without feeling like you lose your grasp on your own life and the basis of your identity. That, of course, doesn't legitimate it in my eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's clearly a large scale backlash against immigration and globalization going on throughout the world right now. A lot of people are seeing their homes and countries and communities changing, and not necessarily in good, positive ways.<br /> <br /> In general, I feel that most people in Europe and America have (at least for the last half century or so) been fine with reasonable immigration and immigrants who are willing to assimilate and adapt into the larger national identity. But there are issues in Europe and America with immigrants who refuse to assimilate into the national character, going beyond rejecting the national cultural traditions and beliefs, but even extending to the point of refusing to learn the local language. And there's no doubt that these immigrants are placing major stress on the social fabric of various nations in different ways.<br /> <br /> I mean, that's why you're seeing this kind of backlash throughout Europe especially. Of course, while these sorts of immigrants who refuse to assimilate <i>at all</i>. are obviously not the majority, they do pose various problems to the nations in which they reside.<br /> <br /> And, unfortunately there's no easy way to tackle those sorts of problems, so you get these hardcore anti-immigration parties that are usually colored heavily by racist and xenophobic beliefs as being the only ones who are willing to discuss the issue and they tend to offer the most extreme &quot;solutions&quot; you can imagine.<br /> <br /> Still, I think at heart most people aren't nearly as radical and anti-immigrant as those groups tend to represent themselves, there just isn't anyone else who talks about the problem or has any solution on how to &quot;solve&quot; it so people get on board the wagon because at least these guys are willing to talk about the problem, even if they are fairly deplorable in most on other ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 11-09-2016, 09:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T18:26:26-08:00","id":1001118,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised how rarely, in the post-election discussions, free trade comes up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T18:33:09-08:00","id":1001122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001118#post1001118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm surprised how rarely, in the post-election discussions, free trade comes up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I don't think most people have a firm grasp on what &quot;free trade&quot; actually means other than the idea that it's a &quot;job killer,&quot; or maybe that it &quot;helps create jobs&quot; depending on their political ideology. I think for a lot of people free trade and globalization are just things they don't like because people on their side of the political aisle say it's bad, and maybe they can point at the old factory that used to churn out products but shut down 20 years ago to go overseas as a victim of free trade, but they probably don't have a good understanding of how free trade works and how it actually affects nations on the bigger scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T18:43:51-08:00","id":1001127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001082#post1001082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The electoral college is there for a reason, and while it might be worth reconsidering, it's there so a popular block can't make decisions for the rest of the country. So urban centers can't push through a president who wants to ban livestock, which might affect those wide swaths of America in between. Said vote is still based on the popular vote in its corresponding area.<br /> <br /> It's literally working the way it's supposed to.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Not at all. I'm very open minded. Incredibly doubtful, because just the other day all the conspiracy theorists, including Trump, thought Clinton was going to win, even if she cheated. But still, open-minded and curious. You said that the presidency is a complete farce and to 'Look at how Trump was predicted by the Simpsons.' So is the Simpsons the determinator of our futures? Or is it just tv? Or movies?<br /> <br /> You also stated that Sanders 'was a clear win should he be the candidate.' Do you have proof of this? Do you think the older Democrats who abhor socialism would have embraced him? Or that all those who don't like free healthcare would decide for vote for him?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. No, it's based on the popular vote in theory.<br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Republicans choose 29 Republican electors, from among people who are long-time, committed and loyal party activists in New York. The Democrats choose 29 Democratic electors, from among loyal Democratic party activists. A similar process unfolds in every other state, based on that state\u2019s electoral vote. Which, right off the bat shuts out all and any independents from having any real shot.</span></span></span> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">If you like to see the math, lets take a look at California vs Pennsylvania as an example (since PA played a big role in this election).</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">California population 38.8 million, electors: 55</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Pennsylvania population 12.8 million, electors: 20</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">California: 38.8 million / 55 = 705454 voters per elector</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Pennsylvania: 12.8 million / 20 = 640000 voters per elector</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">difference between CA and PA: 640000 / 705454 = 0.907</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">so an individual Californians vote is only worth 90% of an individual Pennsylvanian vote.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">or to look at it another way, one out of every ten Californians votes dont count / are not represented in the elector college.<br /> <br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:cabinregular\"><span style=\"font-size:19px\">The fact that on some occasions, electors do not vote as pledged, is enough to make any voting citizen\u2019s blood boil. You can thank the Electoral College.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:cabinregular\"><span style=\"font-size:19px\">Only 29 states plus the District of Columbia have laws regulating how their electors vote, while the rest are free to vote in whatever manner they want with NO legal repercussions.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:cabinregular\"><span style=\"font-size:19px\">As if that isn\u2019t angering enough, most states with legal control over electors only punish those who break their oath and go against the popular vote with a misdemeanor or a small fine, usually of $1,000.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:cabinregular\"><span style=\"font-size:19px\">There have been more than 700 proposals introduced in Congress to reform or eliminate the Electoral College. Where are the results?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VS40ox_2dqc\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VS40ox_2dqc</a></span></span></span><br /> As to Simpsons, well, it has predicted the Ebola Outbreak, Farmville, and so forth on top of Trump, so yeah I think it's a fair point in some aspects at least. It's not particular to only Simpsons, but that is a marked example. For instance, the show the Purge had a clown scare weeks before it happened in real life. Could the clown scare be a case of life imitating art? Perhaps, we don't really know for sure. But it's a huge stretch to say the same of predicting Trump's presidency or the Ebola scare.<br /> <br /> As for Bernie, it was proven Hillary had an inside track from his own campaign:<br /> <a href=\"http://www.huffingtonpost.com/russ-belville/hillarys-superdelegate-co_b_9206252.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://yournewswire.com/wikileaks-dnc-committed-election-fraud-against-bernie-sanders/</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.huffingtonpost.com/russ-belville/hillarys-superdelegate-co_b_9206252.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://img.huffingtonpost.com/asset/default-entry.jpg?ops=1200_630\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.huffingtonpost.com/russ-belville/hillarys-superdelegate-co_b_9206252.html\" target=\"_blank\"> Hillary's Superdelegate Coup Just Confirms to Millennials: The System Is Rigged </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.huffingtonpost.com/russ-belville/hillarys-superdelegate-co_b_9206252.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.huffingtonpost.com/russ-belville/hillarys-superdelegate-co_b_9206252.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> One vote from these one-percenters for the Wall Street candidate is worth 10,105 votes from the 99-percenters for the Democratic Socialist candidate. Unfortunately, one-man-one-vote only applies to actual federal elections, not party primary processes. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> As to older democrats, that's kind of a what if scenario, but I'd wager strongly they would over Trump and Hillary given Bernie as a third option. Same goes for Republicans and Libertarians if Gary Johnson was given a real shot.<br /> <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, after you've still provided literally 0 proof of your claims, and I'm being asked for proof of mine, as predicted, I await your &quot;debunking&quot; of mine. As stated, what has never been proved cannot be disproved.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T19:05:00-08:00","id":1001134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zeroninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001127#post1001127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, take it easy on the formatting. It's really jarring when a post changes size and font out of nowhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zeroninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001127#post1001127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile, after you've still provided literally 0 proof of your claims, and I'm being asked for proof of mine, as predicted, I await your &amp;quot;debunking&amp;quot; of mine. As stated, what has never been proved cannot be disproved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you understand how burden of proof works? Because it doesn't look like it from this quote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T19:09:52-08:00","id":1001136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001122#post1001122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I don't think most people have a firm grasp on what &quot;free trade&quot; actually means other than the idea that it's a &quot;job killer,&quot; or maybe that it &quot;helps create jobs&quot; depending on their political ideology. I think for a lot of people free trade and globalization are just things they don't like because people on their side of the political aisle say it's bad, and maybe they can point at the old factory that used to churn out products but shut down 20 years ago to go overseas as a victim of free trade, but they probably don't have a good understanding of how free trade works and how it actually affects nations on the bigger scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>The perception is what it is, and it's strong enough to overcome decades of apparent social agreement with the Democratic Party in reasonably secure Northern states. The rust belt turning for Trump shows the animus.<br /> <br /> Rather than listen to it, the Dems put forth one of the most pro-free-trade candidates since... Well, since Bill Clinton. The results speak for themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T19:11:54-08:00","id":1001139,"title":"","content":"and furthermore:<br /> <a href=\"http://www.sparknotes.com/us-government-and-politics/american-government/political-parties/section2.rhtml\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.bbc.com/news/blogs-echochambers-27074746</a><br /> <a href=\"http://usavsus.info/usA--Original13thAmend.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.sparknotes.com/us-government-and-politics/american-government/political-parties/section2.rhtml<br /> 13th amendment<br /> T</a><a href=\"http://www.apfn.org/apfn/fed_reserve.htm\" target=\"_blank\">he Fed is Illegal</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T19:21:46-08:00","id":1001142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001134#post1001134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude, take it easy on the formatting. It's really jarring when a post changes size and font out of nowhere.<br /> <br /> <br /> Do you understand how burden of proof works? Because it doesn't look like it from this quote.</div> </div> </div> </div>To state the burden of proof is simply all on me is a fallacy. I understand how it works. I was pointing out that he hasn't provided any proof of his argument to rebut my arguments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T20:07:52-08:00","id":1001166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zeroninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001127#post1001127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which, right off the bat shuts out all and any independents from having any real shot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's vastly more difficult for independents to run for the highest office in the nation. This is not a conspiracy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The fact that on some occasions, electors do not vote as pledged, is enough to make any voting citizen\u2019s blood boil. You can thank the Electoral College. </div> </div> </div>That's not necessarily a bad thing. For instance in an occasion where the difference is narrow, a sworn member of a party voting for the other side can be a good thing. In other situations, a faithless elector or group of them could be doing so because of some reason important to them. It's also not a conspiracy.<br /> <br /> You've stated that the popular vote doesn't matter, when it does. While electors can go against it, they usually do not. It's noteworthy when it happens, you can see every instance of it happening <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Faithless_elector#List_of_faithless_electors\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> Again, the world is complex. I don't want Donald Trump to be president, but there's a lot of people who do, for their own reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As to Simpsons, well, it has predicted the Ebola Outbreak, Farmville, and so forth on top of Trump, so yeah I think it's a fair point in some aspects at least. It's not particular to only Simpsons, but that is a marked example. For instance, the show the Purge had a clown scare weeks before it happened in real life. Could the clown scare be a case of life imitating art? Perhaps, we don't really know for sure. But it's a huge stretch to say the same of predicting Trump's presidency or the Ebola scare. </div> </div> </div>It's a show for entertainment purposes. What you call predicting, I call a joke. Everyone was worried about Ebola during the first breakout because it was big, scary news. There were movies made about it. The Simpsons had a three second joke about a book entitled 'Curious George and the Ebola Virus,' after the original outbreak, which doesn't insinuate a new one, it comments on the idea of Ebola being spread by monkeys. How does this book predict that in 2014 there would be another outbreak?<br /> <br /> If they writers said Simpsons was their vision of the future, or really made any attempt to suggest the show was serious, you would have more of an argument here. But as evidenced <a href=\"http://www.mirror.co.uk/news/world-news/simpsons-writer-why-predicted-donald-9230649\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, it was just for laughs. 'Beyond satire.' 'An absurd placeholder.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for Bernie, it was proven Hillary had an inside track from his own campaign </div> </div> </div>Yes, it was. And the collusion was reprehensible. But there's no Simpsons clips of Bernie winning the election if Hillary lost the primaries. And the Republicans did their best to try and make sure a more traditional candidate won the primaries, but it just wasn't happening. This, too, wasn't so much a grand conspiracy as much as the parties wanting candidates more representative of their platform. Even so, you said he 'was a clear win should he win the candidate,' but have no evidence for this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Meanwhile, after you've still provided literally 0 proof of your claims, and I'm being asked for proof of mine, as predicted, I await your &quot;debunking&quot; of mine. As stated, what has never been proved cannot be disproved. </div> </div> </div>My claim that the media and money didn't control the outcome of the election? I apologize, I edited that one last and realize I put 'media and media.'<br /> <br /> Well, there's <a href=\"http://www.washingtontimes.com/news/2016/oct/20/voters-agree-media-biased-against-donald-trump/\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> that suggests that 88% of Republicans cite a media bias against him. There's also a variety of posters in this thread and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist\">the</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus\">se</a> other ones who believe the media was against Trump. If they influenced people not to vote for Trump, wouldn't he have lost?<br /> <br /> Among the leaks we've seen from wikileaks, there's a number of examples of the media working with Hillary Clinton <a href=\"http://thefreethoughtproject.com/wikileaks-10-most-damning-clinton-emails-media/\" target=\"_blank\">to favor her</a>. And even work against <a href=\"http://www.aim.org/don-irvine-blog/latest-wikileaks-emails-show-cnn-asked-dnc-for-potential-interview-questions-for-trump-and-cruz/\" target=\"_blank\">Trump</a> and other Republicans.<br /> <br /> You also stated 'he who has the gold, makes the rules.' But Clinton <a href=\"http://www.bloomberg.com/politics/graphics/2016-presidential-campaign-fundraising/\" target=\"_blank\">had more than twice as much money</a> to spend for their campaign as Donald Trump.<br /> <br /> Your argument is that someone or something leaked the result of a future election to a writer on the Simpsons 16 years ago, sabotaged Bernie Sanders, though we have actual proof that it was high ranking members of the DNC who worked against him, then forced the country to ignore the popular vote, which it isn't doing, in order to make Donald Trump president. And you argue that the media influenced it. I'm open-minded but you have to have some connectivity and flow to it. If they can time travel or see the future, why are they bothering with this other stuff? How is it not just a horrible comedy of errors, with mistakes compounding upon others and leading to the end result, like everything else?<br /> <br /> I get it. It's a chaotic world out there. But there's no pattern to it beyond people wanting what they think is best for themselves. And not enough people thought Hillary Clinton would offer them that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T20:41:18-08:00","id":1001173,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">1. the act of <a href=\"http://www.dictionary.com/browse/conspire\" target=\"_blank\">conspiring</a>.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">2. an evil, unlawful, treacherous, or surreptitious plan formulated in secretby two or more persons; plot.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">3. a combination of persons for a secret, unlawful, or evil purpose: <span style=\"color:#979797\"><i>He joined the conspiracy to overthrow the government.</i></span><br /> <br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">4. <i>Law. </i>an agreement by two or more persons to commit a crime, fraud,or other wrongful act.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">5. any concurrence in action; <span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">any</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">concurrence</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">in</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">action;</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">combination</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">in</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">bringing</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">about</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">a</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">given</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#3D7BBF\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">result.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Yes, it's vastly more difficult for independents to run for the highest office in the nation. This is not a conspiracy.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#3D7BBF\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">If we're going by definitions, then yes, it is conspiring to usurp the election from all independent parties. It is literally not possible for an independent to win the electoral college really, unless you think somehow they have some longshot if all undecideds switched?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> That's not necessarily a bad thing. For instance in an occasion where the difference is narrow, a sworn member of a party voting for the other side can be a good thing. In other situations, a faithless elector or group of them could be doing so because of some reason important to them. It's also not a conspiracy.<br /> <br /> You've stated that the popular vote doesn't matter, when it does. While electors can go against it, they usually do not. It's noteworthy when it happens, you can see every instance of it happening <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Faithless_elector#List_of_faithless_electors\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. <br /> <br /> Again, the world is complex. I don't want Donald Trump to be president, but there's a lot of people who do, for their own reasons.<br /> <br /> This also banks on there being some kind of oversight on the electoral reps as to keeping their promises.<br /> <br /> It's a show for entertainment purposes. What you call predicting, I call a joke. Everyone was worried about Ebola during the first breakout because it was big, scary news. There were movies made about it. The Simpsons had a three second joke about a book entitled 'Curious George and the Ebola Virus,' after the original outbreak, which doesn't insinuate a new one, it comments on the idea of Ebola being spread by monkeys. How does this book predict that in 2014 there would be another outbreak?<br /> <br /> If they writers said Simpsons was their vision of the future, or really made any attempt to suggest the show was serious, you would have more of an argument here. But as evidenced <a href=\"http://www.mirror.co.uk/news/world-news/simpsons-writer-why-predicted-donald-9230649\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, it was just for laughs. 'Beyond satire.' 'An absurd placeholder.'<br /> <br /> It is arguably satire and beyond. I'm not arguing for it being some kind of specific crystal ball or nostradamus device, as you seem to imply here. What I am saying is that it's more than likely it wasn't just satire from a non-sequitur, but may be partially informed by planned future events.<br /> <br /> Yes, it was. And the collusion was reprehensible. But there's no Simpsons clips of Bernie winning the election if Hillary lost the primaries. And the Republicans did their best to try and make sure a more traditional candidate won the primaries, but it just wasn't happening. This, too, wasn't so much a grand conspiracy as much as the parties wanting candidates more representative of their platform. Even so, you said he 'was a clear win should he win the candidate,' but have no evidence for this.<br /> <br /> There was overwhelming popular support for Bernie all over as evidenced by the link I supplied: <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:NotoNashkArabic\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">First, in Iowa, they battle for a statistical tie, with just a quarter-percent of the vote between Hillary and Bernie. So, naturally, the delegates from Iowa are divided fairly. Bernie gets 21 delegates and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_presidential_election_in_Iowa,_2016#Results\" target=\"_blank\">Hillary gets... 29?</a></span></span><br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:NotoNashkArabic\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Next, in New Hampshire, Bernie demolishes Hillary in a 22-point landslide victory. So, naturally, the delegates from New Hampshire are divided fairly. Bernie gets 15 delegates and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Hampshire_Democratic_primary,_2016#Results\" target=\"_blank\">Hillary gets... 15?</a></span></span><br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:NotoNashkArabic\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What is this strange world where a Bernie tie is an 8-delegate loss and a Bernie landslide is a tie? That\u2019s when our intrepid Millennials start Googling and learn all about Marvel\u2019s <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Democratic_Party_superdelegates,_2016\" target=\"_blank\">Democratic Superdelegates</a>! (Just kidding; Marvel\u2019s heroes are better-looking.)</span></span><br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:NotoNashkArabic\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><a href=\"http://www.pastemagazine.com/articles/2016/02/after-sanders-big-win-in-new-hampshire-establishme.html\" target=\"_blank\">What they learn</a> is that there are 4,763 delegates who pick the Democratic nominee for president. But roughly 15 percent of them are Superdelegates (712 to be exact) who are the Democratic elected officials and party bigwigs. Regular delegates are split according to popular vote, but Superdelegates can vote for anybody they wish (that\u2019s their super power).</span></span><br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:NotoNashkArabic\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Hillary, being the Queen Democratic Bigwig, has amassed quite a collection of these other bigwigs pledging to vote for her (355 to be exact). With some quick Excel work, Millennials figure out that Hillary already had 14.9 percent of the votes she needed to get the nomination before the first caucus was ever tallied in Iowa.</span></span><br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:NotoNashkArabic\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Then they plug in a few more formulas and learn that in New Hampshire, it took convincing 60,631 voters to choose Bernie to match the choice of Gov. Maggie Hassan, Rep. Ann Kuster, Sen. Jeanne Shaheen, and three Democratic National Committee cronies for Hillary.</span></span><br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:NotoNashkArabic\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">In other words, one vote from these one-percenters for the Wall Street candidate is worth 10,105 votes from the 99-percenters for the Democratic Socialist candidate. Unfortunately, one-man-one-vote only applies to actual federal elections, not party primary processes.</span></span><br /> <br /> My claim that the media and money didn't control the outcome of the election? I apologize, I edited that one last and realize I put 'media and media.'<br /> <br /> Well, there's <a href=\"http://www.washingtontimes.com/news/2016/oct/20/voters-agree-media-biased-against-donald-trump/\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> that suggests that 88% of Republicans cite a media bias against him. There's also a variety of posters in this thread and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/979988-any-conservative-gamers-around-yes-we-do-exist\">the</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus\">se</a> other one who believe the media was against Trump. If they influenced people not to vote for Trump, wouldn't he have lost?<br /> <br /> Among the leaks we've seen from wikileaks, there's a number of examples of the media working with Hillary Clinton <a href=\"http://thefreethoughtproject.com/wikileaks-10-most-damning-clinton-emails-media/\" target=\"_blank\">to favor her</a>. And even work against <a href=\"http://www.aim.org/don-irvine-blog/latest-wikileaks-emails-show-cnn-asked-dnc-for-potential-interview-questions-for-trump-and-cruz/\" target=\"_blank\">Trump</a> and other Republicans.<br /> <br /> Did you bother watching the video I linked? Of course Hillary funded the media to support her, and of course that meant it was against Trump. I never stated it was rigged FOR Trump, only that it was rigged in general, in the sense that &quot;here are two candidates we've hand picked and you get no other options, at all.&quot;<br /> <br /> You also stated 'he who has the gold, makes the rules.' But Clinton <a href=\"http://www.bloomberg.com/politics/graphics/2016-presidential-campaign-fundraising/\" target=\"_blank\">had more than twice as much money</a> to spend for their campaign as Donald Trump. <br /> <br /> You're comparing a wealthy businessman to an even wealthier senator. What about the rest of us?<br /> <br /> Your argument is that someone or something leaked the result of a future election to a writer on the Simpsons 16 years ago, sabotaged Bernie Sanders, though we have actual proof that it was high ranking members of the DNC who worked against him, then forced the country to ignore the popular vote, which it isn't doing, in order to make Donald Trump president. And you argue that the media influenced it. I'm open-minded but you have to have some connectivity and flow to it. If they can time travel or see the future, why are they bothering with this other stuff?<br /> <br /> I'm not 100% on it, but it's as likely as what's put on television and newspapers these days. And no, I didn't argue that writer sabotaged Bernie at all. When something is being planned or considered, it would make sense that no definite people involved would be implicated yet if henchman were doing the dirty work and the power players could keep their hands clean, wouldn't it? I'm not saying there's some specific, finite connection between the Simpsons and world events so much as many world events are scripted to the point of absurdity in advance and thus may be predictable by shows like the Simpsons.<br /> <br /> As an example: <a href=\"http://www.wanttoknow.info/falseflag\" target=\"_blank\">False Flag Terrorism</a>, of which the US is one of the biggest enactors. Also, the term <a href=\"http://www.zerohedge.com/news/2015-02-23/1967-he-cia-created-phrase-conspiracy-theorists-and-ways-attack-anyone-who-challenge\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Conspiracy Theory&quot;</a>.<br /> <br /> I get it. It's a chaotic world out there. But there's no pattern to it beyond people wanting what they think is best for themselves. And not enough people thought Hillary Clinton would offer them that.<br /> <br /> That's where you're wrong. There is a definite pattern to it, and it relates directly to the agendas of those who've been in power much longer than we've been alive to ponder it. JFK said it best: &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The very word \u201csecrecy\u201d is repugnant in a free and open society; and we are as a people inherently and historically opposed to secret societies, to secret oaths and to secret proceedings. We decided long ago that the dangers of excessive and unwarranted concealment of pertinent facts far outweighed the dangers which are cited to justify it. Even today, there is little value in opposing the threat of a closed society by imitating its arbitrary restrictions. Even today, there is little value in insuring the survival of our nation if our traditions do not survive with it. And there is very grave danger that an announced need for increased security will be seized upon by those anxious to expand its meaning to the very limits of official censorship and concealment. That I do not intend to permit to the extent that it is in my control. And no official of my Administration, whether his rank is high or low, civilian or military, should interpret my words here tonight as an excuse to censor the news, to stifle dissent, to cover up our mistakes or to withhold from the press and the public the facts they deserve to know.&quot;<br /> <br /> And I still haven't seen anything substantial as far as a rebuttal. Yes, it is chaotic, and hard to get a &quot;big picture&quot; view of the events in the world. But to point to that as evidence that there's no greater rhyme or reason is foolhardy at best and dangerous at worst.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T20:53:40-08:00","id":1001176,"title":"","content":"Well I had written out a long and well thought out response but for some reason, it was &quot;unapproved.&quot; So I guess I'm unable to respond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T21:14:22-08:00","id":1001179,"title":"","content":"You can't link to reddit. It's been blocked due to the spam. You can edit out the reddit link.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-10-2016, 12:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T21:49:12-08:00","id":1001183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\