nk\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T23:35:35-08:00","id":1001220,"title":"","content":"No, WoD-Trump should be head of the Technocracy and wear powered armour. We're talking like Second Edition, over the top, balls to the wall crazy up in here. Behold, the Trump-Emperor of America!<br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.redditmedia.com/4As6bs6UNbXhQQLq2AyZXnSET0grf3AfUkbUQyTTqt4.jpg?w=320&amp;s=c36d72897c6a41703faa22a3bd64c6b6\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> By the grace of His Majesty, and the strength of His Will, we shall come together to build a mighty Wall that will forever sunder us from reality deviants!<br /> And we're going to make the Wyrm pay for it!<br /> <br /> ALL HAIL THE TRUMP-EMPEROR!<br /> ALL HAIL THE TRUMP-EMPEROR!<br /> ALL HAIL THE TRUMP-EMPEROR!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1450,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1450-lys","user":"Lys","date":". 11-10-2016, 02:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1450-lys","name":"Lys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1450_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"480"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T23:57:17-08:00","id":1001227,"title":"","content":"For the Trumperor! For the Trumpire!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T01:11:11-08:00","id":1001242,"title":"","content":"In the British media, if you're interested, I think Thomas Frank has been pretty good on the Presidential race, and worth reading for his article yesterday - <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2016/nov/09/donald-trump-white-house-hillary-clinton-liberals\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.theguardian.com/commenti...inton-liberals</a><br /> <br /> Though I think it's easy to overstate the change in support. The whole flipping of some of Democrat voting workers whose regions used to have good, skilled unionised manufacturing work and now don't that has helped Trump, but I think it's less exaggerated than in Frank's article.<br /> <br /> The biggest thing that to me seems to have worked in his favour I think that wasn't is that many Republican voters in the US seem likely to basically not care either way much about his gaffes and likely lack of competence, if it meant keeping a Clinton and a Democrat out of control of the Presidency and out of control of the judicial appointments. I think a lot of people thought much of the traditional Republican mainstream would #NeverTrump, but maybe #NeverAgainClinton seems like a bigger factor. Or at least, the #NeverTrumpers among Republicans weren't as significant as the voters on the other side that dropped Clinton.<br /> <br /> Apparently turnout for both candidates were down from expectations and previous elections, Clinton and Trump were both unpopular candidates, and neither have rebuilt trust with a general segment of the population (which continues to decline). Trump might've built a little with blue collar workers, but he lost some of most others. It seems like the turnout drop was worse for Clinton, and that's a big factor in why she ended up being beaten.<br /> <br /> Seems like a yuge (sorry) social desirability bias in the polling when we look at actual results yesterday vs predictions. If anyone actually cares to try and make get accurate polls, then they have to be able to account for this, or ideally, get rid of whatever is stopping people openly stating their opinion so people would actually state their true preference.<br /> <br /> Re: demographics raised by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2241\" data-vbnamecard=\"2241\">Omegaphallic</a>, exit polling does seems to suggest that Trump has done relatively better among all non-White ethnic groups than Romney did in 2012. So it seems like the &quot;Trump Effect&quot; of his racist &quot;gaffes&quot; and foolish statements depleting minority Republicans and independents seems of slightly less effect than the &quot;Obama Effect&quot; was of shoring up his support and turnout among non-White ethnic groups. Possibly this is because Trump only targeted &quot;illegals&quot; and Muslims and that just didn't effect his support base among Republican supporting minority ethnic groups too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T01:16:24-08:00","id":1001243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001111#post1001111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, I feel that most people in Europe and America have (at least for the last half century or so) been fine with reasonable immigration and immigrants who are willing to assimilate and adapt into the larger national identity. But there are issues in Europe and America with immigrants who refuse to assimilate into the national character, going beyond rejecting the national cultural traditions and beliefs, but even extending to the point of refusing to learn the local language. And there's no doubt that these immigrants are placing major stress on the social fabric of various nations in different ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's part of an issue, but most migrants do try to integrate quite heavily.<br /> <br /> I think it's to me to a great degree that, however much effort people make towards integration quite a lot of cultural change and new culture is inevitable. Also, to some degree the integrating new groups, however much they try to really sincerely get along with the majority, are still going to always think of themselves as special and different (and usually better). They'll be very sensitive to underrepresentation and overrepresentation in different areas of life and to their perception by the majority. There's also often cultural resistance among Western born second generation folk, who didn't choose to take up a life where they'd be in a minority, to reconnect with the parent culture and assert its greatness and equality with the dominant culture.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't expect anything more or less from any group of people really. People aren't going to give up their culture and they are going to have pride in their background.<br /> <br /> This all introduces stresses into daily life and the public life that weren't there before and creates the backlash. Concern over representation and perception of different subgroups in society seems to have taken over politics and media to an omnipresent, 24 hour degree that people in many Western countries seem to be beginning to find quite an oppressive experience. Large swathes of people eventually just simply will not see why they should bother with having a welcoming attitude to new people when there will inevitably be constant frictions that degrade their experience of life, and create potential flashpoints for of political destablisation and political violence, no matter how well people try to integrate and now matter how welcoming the majority is. The standard mainstream media line that whatever happens, it is a duty to welcome new people who want to make a better life for themselves eventually wears thin, especially on top of economic decline.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's something that we can or should can blame on scapegoated recalcitrant people who don't try to integrate; just something that happens with large migration waves even when people have the best will in the world to integrate (which many migrants do). It's not really about effort, it's just an inevitable thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T02:23:51-08:00","id":1001267,"title":"","content":"Among Trumps first 100 day policies are included among other things these two points:<br /> <br /> - Freezing hiring for the government to decrease the size of it.<br /> - The mass deportation of illegal immigrants in huge numbers never before seen.<br /> <br /> Won't his plans to deport people en masses require him to significantly increase the size of border and immigration agencies in the government? How does he do that if he freezes hiring? Will taxes go up to pay for a big organization to oversee the mass deportation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T02:36:54-08:00","id":1001269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001242#post1001242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the British media, if you're interested, I think Thomas Frank has been pretty good on the Presidential race, and worth reading for his article yesterday - <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2016/nov/09/donald-trump-white-house-hillary-clinton-liberals\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.theguardian.com/commenti...inton-liberals</a></div> </div> </div> </div>My problem with this line of thinking, is that it neglects the issue of the popular vote. The scant majority of the voting population did not want to take a sledgehammer to the machine. While the wave of people that do want this result were what carried Trump over the line in the electoral system, it isn't actually something you can solidly claim as what defines the current American political climate's totality.<br /> <br /> The article also seems to not really understand the Democratic primary electorate either. Clinton didn't win because it &quot;was her time,&quot; though that was certainly part of it. She won because she represents more of the Democratic coalition than Sanders, and none of the other candidates had any traction. Nate Silver did a whole article trying to point out that (though this was before the email leaks) that even if you removed all the levers the DNC uses to get the candidates it wants via the super-delegates and so on, Sanders wouldn't have won the nomination. Outside of the DNC overtly rigging things in Sanders favor an order of magnitude more than what they did for Clinton, he was never going to win (and this goes back to the fact that a significant portion of the American voters did not want the sledgehammer thing, because as is obvious, most of those are Democrats). Biden wasn't forced out of anything. He never ran. If Biden had run in the Democratic Primary, there were good odds he would have managed to take it, and he would have probably not suffered the fate Clinton did because of his own &quot;tell it like it is&quot; style, a significant amount of emotional sympathy to counteract his own past scandals and gaffes, and greater overall popularity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T02:39:05-08:00","id":1001270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001267#post1001267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Won't his plans to deport people en masses require him to significantly increase the size of border and immigration agencies in the government? How does he do that if he freezes hiring? Will taxes go up to pay for a big organization to oversee the mass deportation?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the silver lining for many of us right here. Since Trumps campaign promises are contradictory, there's a chance he uses that to weasel out of them completely and has the chance to let someone better at governing feed him decent policies to push in their place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T03:29:41-08:00","id":1001286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001242#post1001242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the British media, if you're interested, I think Thomas Frank has been pretty good on the Presidential race, and worth reading for his article yesterday - <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2016/nov/09/donald-trump-white-house-hillary-clinton-liberals\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.theguardian.com/commenti...inton-liberals</a><br /> <br /> Though I think it's easy to overstate the change in support. The whole flipping of some of Democrat voting workers whose regions used to have good, skilled unionised manufacturing work and now don't that has helped Trump, but I think it's less exaggerated than in Frank's article.<br /> <br /> The biggest thing that to me seems to have worked in his favour I think that wasn't is that many Republican voters in the US seem likely to basically not care either way much about his gaffes and likely lack of competence, if it meant keeping a Clinton and a Democrat out of control of the Presidency and out of control of the judicial appointments. I think a lot of people thought much of the traditional Republican mainstream would #NeverTrump, but maybe #NeverAgainClinton seems like a bigger factor. Or at least, the #NeverTrumpers among Republicans weren't as significant as the voters on the other side that dropped Clinton.<br /> <br /> Apparently turnout for both candidates were down from expectations and previous elections, Clinton and Trump were both unpopular candidates, and neither have rebuilt trust with a general segment of the population (which continues to decline). Trump might've built a little with blue collar workers, but he lost some of most others. It seems like the turnout drop was worse for Clinton, and that's a big factor in why she ended up being beaten.<br /> <br /> Seems like a yuge (sorry) social desirability bias in the polling when we look at actual results yesterday vs predictions. If anyone actually cares to try and make get accurate polls, then they have to be able to account for this, or ideally, get rid of whatever is stopping people openly stating their opinion so people would actually state their true preference.<br /> <br /> Re: demographics raised by <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, exit polling does seems to suggest that Trump has done relatively better among all non-White ethnic groups than Romney did in 2012. So it seems like the &amp;quot;Trump Effect&amp;quot; of his racist &amp;quot;gaffes&amp;quot; and foolish statements depleting minority Republicans and independents seems of slightly less effect than the &amp;quot;Obama Effect&amp;quot; was of shoring up his support and turnout among non-White ethnic groups. Possibly this is because Trump only targeted &amp;quot;illegals&amp;quot; and Muslims and that just didn't effect his support base among Republican supporting minority ethnic groups too much.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think part of it maybe his promise to fix inner cities, hopefully he keeps his promise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T03:32:36-08:00","id":1001288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001090#post1001090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I'm surprised Trump was elected(and sad because he is a giant sack of orange-colored shit), I'm even more surprised that my moronic state re-elected the human waste of oxygen that is Marco Rubio. <br /> <br /> Okay. It's Florida. So maybe I'm not surprised.<br /> <br /> I need to get the fuck out of this state.</div> </div> </div> </div> Anyone else think democracts are hypocritics for complaining about racist comments and then showering the guy with ginger hate. Okay, he's a red head, we get it. If democracts want to win next time, enough with the hypocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T03:52:00-08:00","id":1001292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zeroninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001030#post1001030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's your source for saying that they're all paranoia?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, stop right there.<br /> <br /> It works like this:<br /> <br /> 1. You make a postive claim (meaning a claim which posits the existence of an entity or object).<br /> 2. Charlaquin and other people then make negative claims (meaning claims which dispute the existence of said entity or object).<br /> 3. Now it falls to you to prove that this entity or object exists, because if it didn't work like that, neither courts nor science could work.<br /> <br /> You don't get to ask for proof for a negative claim, because a negative claim is basically a differently worded question (which means that going &quot;that doesn't exist&quot; actually means &quot;where is the proof for it?&quot;). This means that you either find some proof and reliable sources to back up your claims or you <i>must forfeit the argument</i>.<br /> <br /> This is how courts work, it's how universities work, it's how debates work and it <i>damn fucking should be how this forum works</i>.<br /> <br /> Otherwise debates never end.<br /> <br /> Ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T04:37:00-08:00","id":1001305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001111#post1001111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there's clearly a large scale backlash against immigration and globalization going on throughout the world right now. A lot of people are seeing their homes and countries and communities changing, and not necessarily in good, positive ways.<br /> <br /> In general, I feel that most people in Europe and America have (at least for the last half century or so) been fine with reasonable immigration and immigrants who are willing to assimilate and adapt into the larger national identity. But there are issues in Europe and America with immigrants who refuse to assimilate into the national character, going beyond rejecting the national cultural traditions and beliefs, but even extending to the point of refusing to learn the local language. And there's no doubt that these immigrants are placing major stress on the social fabric of various nations in different ways.<br /> <br /> I mean, that's why you're seeing this kind of backlash throughout Europe especially. Of course, while these sorts of immigrants who refuse to assimilate <i>at all</i>. are obviously not the majority, they do pose various problems to the nations in which they reside.<br /> <br /> And, unfortunately there's no easy way to tackle those sorts of problems, so you get these hardcore anti-immigration parties that are usually colored heavily by racist and xenophobic beliefs as being the only ones who are willing to discuss the issue and they tend to offer the most extreme &quot;solutions&quot; you can imagine.<br /> <br /> Still, I think at heart most people aren't nearly as radical and anti-immigrant as those groups tend to represent themselves, there just isn't anyone else who talks about the problem or has any solution on how to &quot;solve&quot; it so people get on board the wagon because at least these guys are willing to talk about the problem, even if they are fairly deplorable in most on other ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think it's really a manyfold problem. Xenophobism and tribalism is unfortunately pretty hard-coded into the human psyche, that's one part of it (in Hungary there was a survey about which ethnic groups are the least accepted and it turned out that the majority effectively hates Pirezes, which was a completely made-up group, it's somewhat funny and sad). Also, certain parties and groups using this heavily to gain popularity, thus playing into and strengthening these negative instincts. Another part is there really IS some problem with immigrants and the liberal-left side just acts as there isn't. Yet another part is that there aren't easy solutions and a lot of people just don't want to deal with the problem, they want to shut down the borders and that's it. Also also, it's a difficult subject and requires a lot of empathy and a lot of people just doesn't want to deal with long-term and difficult things, they are just being afraid and want a strong leader who deals with the whole mess for them, preferably via eliminating the source of their fears (by shutting down borders as above, for example). Also also also, putting this problem and generating more fear in the citizenship is a VERY effective way to diverting attention from the local problems and corruption scandals and uniting the voting base. At least I got these impressions there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T05:42:41-08:00","id":1001324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001288#post1001288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Anyone else think democracts are hypocritics for complaining about racist comments and then showering the guy with ginger hate.</b> Okay, he's a red head, we get it. If democracts want to win next time, enough with the hypocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. I don't. He has orange colored hair. He LOOKS like an orange. I call them like I see them. <br /> <br /> And even better?<br /> <br /> <u><b>I'm not a democrat. </b></u>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T05:50:00-08:00","id":1001325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.currentaffairs.org/2016/11/what-this-means-how-this-happened-what-to-do-now\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.currentaffairs.org/hubfs/5440392565_4634fb9d24_b-1024x646.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.currentaffairs.org/2016/11/what-this-means-how-this-happened-what-to-do-now\" target=\"_blank\"> What This Means, How This Happened, What To Do Now </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.currentaffairs.org/2016/11/what-this-means-how-this-happened-what-to-do-now\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.currentaffairs.org/2016/11/what-this-means-how-this-happened-what-to-do-now </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Dealing with the election of Donald Trump </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm not entirely sure what's going to happen now, but I'm confident of 3 things:<br /> 1. We'll never move forward if we spend all our time wallowing in self-pity or blaming each other. <br /> 2. Writing off all supporters of the opposing candidate as stupid or morally bankrupt means we'll never connect to them, and we need to connect. <br /> 3. There is nothing to fear but fear itself... mostly because fear makes people crazy. <br /> <br /> So let's all take a breath. The world hasn't ended, and we're not done yet. Now is a good time to reflect on ourselves and what we can do better next time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T05:54:53-08:00","id":1001327,"title":"","content":"State and local politics generally mean more to the average Joe than presidential politics, anyway. I'm not going to panic, just like I haven't panicked the last 8 years. Or during Bush's horrific terms.<br /> <br /> I disagree with most(like 99%) of what Trump stands for, but I'm willing to have an open mind and see exactly what he can actually accomplish. Just like I did with every other president.<br /> <br /> Only difference is, I'm not sure I've ever been less optimistic than I am now. That's okay. Skyrim Enhanced Edition is calling my name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T06:51:12-08:00","id":1001338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001305#post1001305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I think it's really a manyfold problem. Xenophobism and tribalism is unfortunately pretty hard-coded into the human psyche, that's one part of it (in Hungary there was a survey about which ethnic groups are the least accepted and it turned out that the majority effectively hates Pirezes, which was a completely made-up group, it's somewhat funny and sad). Also, certain parties and groups using this heavily to gain popularity, thus playing into and strengthening these negative instincts. Another part is there really IS some problem with immigrants and the liberal-left side just acts as there isn't. Yet another part is that there aren't easy solutions and a lot of people just don't want to deal with the problem, they want to shut down the borders and that's it. Also also, it's a difficult subject and requires a lot of empathy and a lot of people just doesn't want to deal with long-term and difficult things, they are just being afraid and want a strong leader who deals with the whole mess for them, preferably via eliminating the source of their fears (by shutting down borders as above, for example). Also also also, putting this problem and generating more fear in the citizenship is a VERY effective way to diverting attention from the local problems and corruption scandals and uniting the voting base. At least I got these impressions there.</div> </div> </div> </div> I actually agree, there are alot real issues that the left just kind of hand waves. To be fair same with the right and centre, but its doing more damage to the left right now as shown by the &quot;left&quot;.<br /> <br /> I also wish the left would stop with acting hysterics. They accused Trump followers of planning on continueing stirring up shit when he lost, then when he wins they do the exact thing they accused Trump supporters of doing.<br /> <br /> They complain about about Republican obstructionism and were right to do so, but now call for democracts to do the same thing.<br /> <br /> And the protests are just embarrassing. He hasn't done anything yet, what are you protesting, democracy? I could see protesting the electoral college, but you do that before the election, not after.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T06:53:04-08:00","id":1001339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001325#post1001325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.currentaffairs.org/2016/11/what-this-means-how-this-happened-what-to-do-now\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.currentaffairs.org/2016/...what-to-do-now</a><br /> <br /> I'm not entirely sure what's going to happen now, but I'm confident of 3 things:<br /> 1. We'll never move forward if we spend all our time wallowing in self-pity or blaming each other. <br /> 2. Writing off all supporters of the opposing candidate as stupid or morally bankrupt means we'll never connect to them, and we need to connect. <br /> 3. There is nothing to fear but fear itself... mostly because fear makes people crazy. <br /> <br /> So let's all take a breath. The world hasn't ended, and we're not done yet. Now is a good time to reflect on ourselves and what we can do better next time.</div> </div> </div> </div> Now this is talking sense!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T10:48:59-08:00","id":1001403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001292#post1001292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, stop right there.<br /> <br /> It works like this:<br /> <br /> 1. You make a postive claim (meaning a claim which posits the existence of an entity or object).<br /> 2. Charlaquin and other people then make negative claims (meaning claims which dispute the existence of said entity or object).<br /> 3. Now it falls to you to prove that this entity or object exists, because if it didn't work like that, neither courts nor science could work.<br /> <br /> You don't get to ask for proof for a negative claim, because a negative claim is basically a differently worded question (which means that going &quot;that doesn't exist&quot; actually means &quot;where is the proof for it?&quot;). This means that you either find some proof and reliable sources to back up your claims or you <i>must forfeit the argument</i>.<br /> <br /> This is how courts work, it's how universities work, it's how debates work and it <i>damn fucking should be how this forum works</i>.<br /> <br /> Otherwise debates never end.<br /> <br /> Ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I add like 1,000 likes to this one?<br /> <br /> Maybe sticky it at the top of every forum?<br /> <br /> Something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T11:50:29-08:00","id":1001413,"title":"","content":"Wisdom from Shoeonhead<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/LpnAlGG6Bk8\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/LpnAlGG6Bk8\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/LpnAlGG6Bk8\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/LpnAlGG6Bk8 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1