ou agree that there is a system in place that favors traditional belief systems over progressive ones? That favors the majority of a region? And that, in America, that majority is white? And that the people in power have a strong tendency to be white and male, and that these white males traditionally favor other white males over non-white non-males?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you've spoken for me more eloquently than I seem to have been doing. Thank you. This.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002039#post1002039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">I see no need for infraction, but I will ask the thread to move back on topic.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>And thank you. Sorry for instigating that tangent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T19:03:23-08:00","id":1002043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002006#post1002006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're confusing who said what. Charlaquin didn't say she'd villify anyone.<br /> <br /> You can claim that the election was won because one side didn't want to use proper pronouns, but that wasn't part of Clinton's platform and it didn't decide the election. Wherever this conversation belongs, it's not in this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div> Agreed by itself it didn't decide the election, its just an example of the PC culture gone mad, that was a contributing factor in his Trumps win, it create an oppressive enviroment at war with free speech so that, while people might not have agree with what Trump was saying, it felt like a release valve that he said it at all.<br /> <br /> And even that wasn't the only fact, just that factor that helped shield Trump from consquences for the shit he said.<br /> <br /> Other factors include ignoring the damage the free trade agreements did in the west to the manufacturing sector, another factor was the bullshit the DNC did in Hillary's race against Bernie Sanders, also Hillary utter corruption, one of Trumps biggest says is I drain the Swamp in Washington.<br /> <br /> All together it helped get Trump the win.<br /> <br /> I don't like having that dip shit President of America, we share the worlds largest unprotected border.<br /> <br /> So I hope Americans, both Democracts and republicans can do better in 2020.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T19:13:42-08:00","id":1002045,"title":"","content":"It takes a lot of nerve to try and say queer people asking to be respected is a major factor in Trump's ascension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T19:15:24-08:00","id":1002047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002043#post1002043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like having that dip shit President of America, we share the worlds largest unprotected border.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I admit, I never really saw an issue with the wall. But I grew up in El Paso, Texas on the Mexican/American border and we have big fences and walls in place on the border there, so I never really saw what was so terrible about expanding it. Well, I guess maybe it's just growing up around the border fences and walls made it seem fairly normal and not overly horrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T19:17:24-08:00","id":1002048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002025#post1002025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like speaking for people, if you have a problem flag them.<br /> <br /> That said.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Where? As far as I see she's said that blaming individuals or groups isn't the problem. The structure that causes all this is.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You're the only one who said you couldn't call it out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 'Not all anyone' doesn't need to be stated. It's understood from the start. But when it's used it's used to just derail things, like how the last dozen posts which have careened from talking about the fucking election results and how peoples health care can be taken away to this. You can't have a discussion about the problems with injustice if you have to answer every, 'Well I'm a 'something' and I never did this or that.'<br /> <br /> Basically, can you agree that there is a system in place that favors traditional belief systems over progressive ones? That favors the majority of a region? And that, in America, that majority is white? And that the people in power have a strong tendency to be white and male, and that these white males traditionally favor other white males over non-white non-males?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What if it wasn't irrelevant? What if there was a bathroom only sexual dominates were allowed to go in, or risk getting arrested? What if it mattered when you went to the doctor, or a psychiatrist? What if, legally, sexually dominates were only allowed to marry a sexually submissive and you had to prove what you were first? What if the police pull you over and ask why you look like a dominate if your driver's license says you're a submissive? Gender and sexuality isn't something that only matters behind closed doors.</div> </div> </div> </div> I have always supported unisex bathrooms, I would proudly piss beside a trans person any day of the weak.<br /> <br /> Yes of course there situations where being trans matters, hell there situations where being a Dom or Sub matter, but it doesn't have always about that.<br /> <br /> Why does your gender identity matter when ordering a burger? <br /> <br /> Look I'm on your side, but I do that by being real, not just agreeing with everything and saying what you want to hear. <br /> <br /> Anyways it just one small piece of a much bigger picture, by itself its minor, its PC culture out of control.<br /> <br /> If you don't want Trump to get a second term and others like him, you have choices to make, and that means chilling out on msn hate, white male hate, cis hate, and PC culture in general.<br /> <br /> And it means taking back the DNC and the Democractic Party to salvage your broken system and focusing not too much on identity politics, you have some carefully picked stuff as long as its balanced, but rather focus on economics and a more universal equality, a generally fairer system, like BCI, fixing the manufacturing sector.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T19:21:00-08:00","id":1002049,"title":"","content":"I'm happy to move the discussion back on topic.<br /> <br /> How do you guys plan on making sure the DNC doesn't pooch things again, leading Trump to a second term?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T19:37:00-08:00","id":1002055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JBRocky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002034#post1002034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets see if we can get back on topic and have a civil discussion. Since it's in the new a lot now what do people think of the Electoral College, should we keep it or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think we should scrap it, but I do think it needs to be re-evaluated and possibly revised. Like, I get why it's a thing. The idea of electing the president based on what the most <i>states</i> want, rather than what the most <i>individuals</i> want isn't bad, nor is the idea of states with larger populations having greater influence. The problem as I see it is that such a system necessarily makes some votes worth more than others, as pointed out earlier in the thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T19:48:39-08:00","id":1002058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002049#post1002049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you guys plan on making sure the DNC doesn't pooch things again, leading Trump to a second term?</div> </div> </div> </div>Really all it would take is getting more people out to vote and apparently not having Hillary Clinton as a candidate. A lot of people have hated the Clintons since Bill avoided impeachment, and they have kept those irons hot in the fire.<br /> <br /> Since it is evidently clear that most people voted for Trump primarily to show their dislike of Clinton, and the fact that the vote difference was fairly narrow, we've definitely made some progress. It just needs to be taken advantage of when the time comes to vote.<br /> <br /> Ideally the people won over by Trump's claims have noticed that he has already gone back on two of them, and so far his staff looks to be full of the insiders he said he wanted to get rid of. But you can't trust other people to be their best, which is why we need to get people registered and voting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T19:49:59-08:00","id":1002059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002049#post1002049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm happy to move the discussion back on topic.<br /> <br /> How do you guys plan on making sure the DNC doesn't pooch things again, leading Trump to a second term?</div> </div> </div> </div>I read this op-ed on CNN the other day, and I think it sums up more or less what I am thinking - though the author is an ardent Bernie supporter, some of his specific takes on the Democratic Party and how it managed to lose its way resonate pretty well.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <a href=\"http://www.cnn.com/2016/11/09/opinions/democratic-party-burn-tasini/\" target=\"_blank\">(CNN)</a> - There is only one silver lining in yesterday's election results, which will allow a con man, a pathological liar, a bold racist and a sexual predator to succeed the first African-American president.<br /> <br /> We can now launch a difficult but urgent mission \u2014 shaking the Democratic Party down to its foundation, ejecting the failed Bill/Hillary Clinton economic and global worldview and standing up for a set of populist, sound economic and foreign policy principles that could earn majority support.<br /> <br /> On the surface, it's astounding that a man who ripped off thousands of people who worked for him became the champion of the regular Joe. But, as Bernie Sanders reiterated in a recent podcast with me, the problem is that people have ceased to see a difference between the parties, particularly on economic issues. I'll briefly cite a few examples.<br /> <br /> Starting out with NAFTA, Bill Clinton forced &quot;free trade&quot; upon the party. I warned multiple times during the election that Trump would make inroads with voters in the Rust Belt unless Democrats made a clean break from corporate trade deals. Around the globe, these deals are a key tool to drive down wages, exploit workers and prosecute global class warfare. But, the current president still serves up the malarkey about the benefits of these deals.<br /> <br /> Bill Clinton's broader economic agenda was even more corrosive. During Clinton's so-called &quot;good economy,&quot; the decline of organized labor continued. The president, and his secretary of labor, Robert Reich, did very little to arrest the decline.<br /> <br /> No Democratic president was more focused on letting business interests off the leash. He gave more power to media companies, triggering consolidation and a powerful wave of concentration of the media into a few hands. The average person, not steeped in policy, understood this every time he or she opened their skyrocketing cable bills.<br /> <br /> Hand-in-glove with Wall Street, Clinton got rid of the Glass Steagall Act, which removed the separation between commercial banks, insurers and investment banks, allowing the self-dealing manipulation of mortgages and interest rates and accelerating the shifting of huge wealth into the hands of a few.<br /> <br /> Again, the average person, just trying to make ends meet, eventually got the sharpest end of that spear when millions of people lost their homes, jobs and retirement in the thundering collapse known as the Great Recession, which, for many, has been a depression.<br /> <br /> There is so much more: A planet dying because for years fossil fuel interests were coddled. Welfare reform. Mass incarceration of people of color, which had both racial and economic consequences. The praise of the Clinton years, and red-faced defense by its leader, was always couched in contrast to the Reagan and two Bush Administrations. Great.<br /> <br /> Feeding off the Clinton machine, the Democratic Party has become riddled with lobbyists, billionaires, and hustlers who pocket huge sums of money by running either nonprofit &quot;think tanks&quot; or election-cycle networks, and politicians who, indeed, are focused mostly on reelection. Surrounding the party are extremely well-paid non-profit leaders, who end up defending the status quo.<br /> <br /> Chief component of the Clinton machine in recent years, the Clinton Foundation operated somewhat out of sight.<br /> <br /> The big donations streaming from anti-union powerhouses like Wal-Mart or big financial entities like Bank of America not only whitewashed the policies of interests directly opposed to what the Democratic Party should stand for, but they also clouded the deeper systemic crisis within the party. We can only address climate change, poverty and global inequality by axing the very system benefiting many of the donors to the Clinton Foundation.<br /> <br /> Fast forward to the 2016 election. There is no doubt in my mind that Bernie Sanders would have defeated Trump. His authenticity would have pierced through Trump's fraudulent appeal. His concise, point-by-point evisceration of a failed economic model and aggressive, blundering foreign policy was entirely understandable to voters.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* At this point the author goes into a tangent about how awesome Bernie Sander is and how he was cheated out of a win, before he finally gets around his solution. *EDIT*<br /> <br /> First, the Clinton machine must be rooted out of the party. A quarter of a century is enough time to understand that its ideology has failed the American people.<br /> <br /> Second, the Democratic National Committee has to be turned inside out. The disgraced and deposed chair, Debbie Wasserman Schultz, is only the worst symptom of this wider truth. The party has lost hundreds of state legislative seats, Republicans now control two-thirds of state chambers and have a comfortable majority of governorships (who will determine redistricting in 2020). They have a historic margin in the House of Representatives, will continue to run the Senate and, thus, likely put a Trump-stamp on the Supreme Court.<br /> <br /> Third, we need to run targeted primary contests broadly and across the board to replace elected officials who don't want to see a more open, vibrant and inclusive party. The Sanders movement has shown we can raise the money to fund challengers \u2014 and they are ready, by the thousands, to compete.<br /> <br /> With these changes, and drawing from the energy of many great activists, a new Democratic Party can be revitalized. The progressive movement, in all its elements \u2014 advocates for labor, environmentalists, and civil rights of all stripes \u2014 can shape that future. </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I don't necessarily agree with everything this author says - I think some of his ideas are non-starters. But, I think he gets a few major points correct. The Democrats lost because they completely failed to connect with voters. Many saw them as no different from the Republicans. The &quot;free trade&quot; and close ties with Wallstreet elites manage to drive away the blue collar union workers who have been a reliable and core constituency of the Democrats for decades - it's not extreme to say that those were the voters who cost Hillary states like Pennsylvania and Ohio and with those states, the election.<br /> <br /> But more important than just the presidency, look at how badly the Democrats lost in the state elections. They got absolutely clobbered, and that wasn't all just because people didn't like Hillary. It's because people didn't like the Democrats in general.<br /> <br /> The Democrats need to go &quot;all in&quot; on some ideas to set themselves apart from the Republicans. They also need to regain the trust of the union workers, which is what cost them this election. They need to cut ties with lobbying and corporate interest groups as the Democratic Party is viewed as incredibly corrupt by many Americans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T19:56:40-08:00","id":1002062,"title":"","content":"Hillary's main flaw was representing the establishment and the status quo in a time when folks across the political spectrum feel like the system has failed them. It's distressing to see a lot of the left fail to recognize that, instead blaiming her failure solely on sexism or ardent Trump supporters. I'm not sure devout socialist Bernie would've made many more converts out of Republicans than Clinton did, but I bet you many Trump voters might not have gone down that path had he been the other option on the ballot.<br /> <br /> I'll admit to personal bias in saying that Pence scares me much more than Trump does, because while I'm appalled at the things the latter has said about Muslims and Latinx folks, it's a more distant horror I'm shielded from by my own privilege as a white person. Not so on runaway anti-queer bigot Pence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T20:12:22-08:00","id":1002065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002055#post1002055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think we should scrap it, but I do think it needs to be re-evaluated and possibly revised. Like, I get why it's a thing. The idea of electing the president based on what the most <i>states</i> want, rather than what the most <i>individuals</i> want isn't bad, nor is the idea of states with larger populations having greater influence. The problem as I see it is that such a system necessarily makes some votes worth more than others, as pointed out earlier in the thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYou are right that some votes mean more than others but that's kind of the point. If states like Wyoming, Montana, North and South Dakota didn't get a boost who would really care what they though or what was effecting them. Why go with something that small when you can hit Chicago, NY or LA?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T20:12:30-08:00","id":1002066,"title":"","content":"I'm really curious what's going to happen to Puerto Rico and DC. Both seem like they're going to apply for statehood, possibly becoming our 51st and 52nd state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T22:36:47-08:00","id":1002124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GLG9g7BcjKs\" data-code=\"GLG9g7BcjKs\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/GLG9g7BcjKs/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T22:47:02-08:00","id":1002127,"title":"","content":"I'm very much in favor of doing away with the EC as I see it as a primary reason voter participation in the US being so low. It absolutely supports peoples' notion that their votes don't matter, because they aren't directly voting for a candidate but for someone who is supposed to cast a vote for a candidate they may or may not have chosen. They feel as if their vote is nullified so why bother voting at all. At the very least the system should be amended to have weighted representational results like most states have during the party primaries. &quot;Winner takes all&quot; is a shitty way to institute a representational system.<br /> In years when the GOP candidate lost my conservative friends supported the idea, now that it has failed to match the popular vote and favored the GOP candidate for the second time in our lifetimes those friends are telling me the system is working as intended. I wonder how they'd feel if the shoe was on the other foot?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T22:52:18-08:00","id":1002130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002124#post1002124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GLG9g7BcjKs\" data-code=\"GLG9g7BcjKs\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/GLG9g7BcjKs/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I only regret that I have but one like to give for your post, stylanski. I don't know who that dude is, but he hit the nail on the head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T00:58:59-08:00","id":1002149,"title":"","content":"On the Electoral Collage:<br /> <br /> It's needed reform for over 200 years. Hamilton - one of the key authors of the concept - wanted to amend it almost immediately after seeing it in practice as the electors immediately starting gaming the system rather than acting as a check on the every-day citizen. The electors were meant to counter the ability to sway what we now call low information voters by having a group of high information individuals be who actually makes the final decision. Madison and Hamilton actually tried to amend the Constitution to mandate that the vote was clearly for electors, not Presidential candidates, and that you would vote for your own district's elector directly instead of as a whole state. Obviously they failed.<br /> <br /> I don't think we could scrap it, since that would take an amendment; and the people doing the amending would be going against their own self-interests; as well as many philosophic beliefs about how to approach the Constitution. But I don't think how it works now is any good since it isn't the explicit intent of the Framers (since they said so and tried to change it), nor is it representative of a more modern ideology of direct democratic selection of the executive.<br /> <br /> If we're stuck with the current state of the electors being robots who's job is to be symbol and fulfill the letter of the Constitution despite the spirit of it, there's a simple solution that some states have already actually implemented: bind electors to vote to the national popular candidate instead of the state popular candidate (either in total, or in part). Just write them completely out of the picture and get rid of the ability for what happened this election. If every state agreed to bind 50% - 1 of their electors to the national popular candidate, we don't get this problem any more. Winning the national vote nets you so many electors that there's mathematically no way you could have won the most votes nationally and not end up with the most electors as well.<br /> <br /> I also think the &quot;let the small states matter more&quot; argument holds much weight. They matter to a ridiculous degree since the number of Representatives is locked and the minimum is set at 3. This already has a huge impact on the make up of the House. As well, swing states matter more. Delaware and Wyoming don't get Presidential attention despite their proportionally more valuable electors, because both are so solidly locked in by one of the parties it's not worth it. California and Florida have similar electoral strength in relation to their population, but California is Democrat country, and Florida is a swing state... so Florida gets way more attention. The point of the Electoral College was never to give smaller states more power in the presidential election anyway.<br /> <br /> On the DNC:<br /> <br /> The DNC's only real issue is an image problem. Rep. Ellison will most likely be the new head. He's younger, a Sanders guy, a Rust Belt guy (from Detroit, represents a 2/3s white part of Minneapolis, etc.), and a double up on minority status. Howard Dean might have more experience bringing the Dems back from this same situation, but that's effectively also a negative in this political climate. The Dems are pretty agreed already on what the path forward looks like, so the biggest thing to do with the DNC is make sure the new head of the DNC is a good messenger for what they want to accomplish.<br /> <br /> Of course, the Dems have always been good at talking about the right way to move forward, but their history in midterms and smaller local elections shows they've got an execution problem that's much more complicated. Even Obama's highly energized electorate wasn't there in the midterms. But the DNC also has a great leverage now: the Trump administration is what happens when Dems slack off for four years between presidential elections.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002130#post1002130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know who that dude is, but he hit the nail on the head.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. He misses plenty.<br /> <br /> For example... the Republicans do just fine getting elected by doing little more than insulting the other side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T06:10:58-08:00","id":1002193,"title":"","content":"It is interesting to see this discussion from the outside. From my pov it is a normal &quot;Divide et impera&quot; situation. People who voted for Obama and were part of his coalition did a.) not vote or b.) voted for Trump. The latter people were once called Reagan democrats, but they exist in every country: blue collar workers that just want that things get better and who are structurally disadvantaged by default as they are not part of the economy that is recovering in the cities.<br /> The others were Latinos and Afro Americans who did not vote for Clinton in the general, who felt misunderstood and disadvantaged as well. They did not want more incremental change. <br /> <br /> Trump was able to get the first group and Clinton was not able to convince the second. <br /> <br /> It is important not to tone police people for many reasons.<br /> &quot;Marginalized people often do not have the luxury of emotionally distancing themselves from discussions on their rights and experiences.&quot;<br /> is something that i read and always have in the back of my head. If it is helping is secondary - as this is about venting - but venting also stops and becomes toxic if it consumes you, which is the real danger for the individual doing it. <br /> <br /> On the other side everything has consequences. Many rural white people are not able to just pack their bags and leave. They are not able to afford it, they do not have a support system in the city and would have to live in the same ghettos that African American, Latinos and other minorities live. They will think about that carefully for the same reasons why white flight happened in the first place. <br /> <br /> This add up with the the other reasons for segregation that we see in the US society at the moment and this IS a fault of the democratic elite, as we can see in NY even more. Parts of the LGBTQ community have who center themselves around the cities will have better opportunities for a job or other essential items. Their support system is intact there. <br /> <br /> So from a class perspective both the minorities in the ghetto an the rural should be in the same class, but because of conflicts no people do not see this, aside of the far (European normal) left around Bernie and he was still attacked by feminists as well as minority groups, who are at least partially responsible for making Hillary the nominee of the democratic party.<br /> <br /> What the rural vote wants is decentralization. They want more middle class companies, not more Apple or Tesla. <br /> <br /> Now my pov is clearly biased towards that because Germany basically lives on these middle class companies, but we still have a similar region which is the eastern part, the ex-GDR. Structural deficits there make it difficult as well, but we would never think that we should just forget about them. Not only that but our election system is just superior. The electoral college is only partially useful and should be counterbalanced. A mixed-member proportional representation system is just superior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T07:18:36-08:00","id":1002208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001822#post1001822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, if you wealthy it doesn't matter if your gay, black, white, trans, ect..., you'll be fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll be <i>less</i> inclined to face prejudice, but that doesn't mean you'll face prejudice. There's plenty of incidences of prominent black leaders being profiled or having the police called on them for unwarranted reasons, and institutional policy effects everyone. All women stand to have their rights stripped away by the defunding of PP and the criminalization of abortion. All people of color can be victimized by increased search and frisk laws and police militarization.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001822#post1001822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its the poor and the lower middle class that has to be concerned. Or Prime Minister Justin Trudeau, who now has to deal with this guy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most leftists are <i>very</i> concerned about classism and income inequality, But identifying a single problem doesn't make the other problems go away.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001822#post1001822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the up side Canada will get to brain drain the shit out of a America, and hopefully Nafta and the TPP dies. What both countries need is a new autopact, you know the trade agreement that ACTUALLLY CREATED MANUFACTURING JOBS, instead of destroying them or sending over seas.</div> </div> </div> </div>What we really need to do is bring back the blacksmithing jobs that modernization took away from our country!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001822#post1001822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still I worry for Americans poor of all races, if your rich you'll make out like a bandit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Me too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001831#post1001831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll also point out that excessive PC stuff helped Trump to win, don't kill the messanger, experts have pointed this out, just my advice, toned down the PC stuff, don't worry about microaggressions and correct gender pronouns, when the fucking wolf is at the door.</div> </div> </div> </div>If someone tells you the pronoun they prefer to be used by, alerts you to psychological triggers, or points out an act of micro-aggression that draws from entitlement or privilege, it's flat out disrespectful to them to ignore that. I'm not here to play respectability politics, and I'm not here to teach people lessons in common decency.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001822#post1001822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And stop villifying cis white males, no likes being demonized, it just drives people to Trump.</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll stop questioning the motives of cis white males (and females, to a lesser extent) when they stop disregarding the voices of everyone else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001822#post1001822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And no more of this free speech zones, America, no, North America IS a Free Speech zone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree here 100%.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001822#post1001822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The left calls unemployed white blue-collar workers privileged sending them into the arms of the Trumps of the world then blames the right.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I won't argue that we need more outreach to all poor people. We need more outreach in general. We lost because we didn't mobilize. Trump had less voter turnout than the last two Republican nominees. Clinton lost because too many people stayed in and didn't vote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 11-12-2016, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T09:27:58-08:00","id":1002247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002208#post1002208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You'll be <i>less</i> inclined to face prejudice, but that doesn't mean you'll face prejudice. There's plenty of incidences of prominent black leaders being profiled or having the police called on them for unwarranted reasons, and institutional policy effects everyone. All women stand to have their rights stripped away by the defunding of PP and the criminalization of abortion. All people of color can be victimized by increased search and frisk laws and police militarization.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Most leftists are <i>very</i> concerned about classism and income inequality, But identifying a single problem doesn't make the other problems go away.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What we really need to do is bring back the blacksmithing jobs that modernization took away from our country!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sure. Me too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If someone tells you the pronoun they prefer to be used by, alerts you to psychological triggers, or points out an act of micro-aggression that draws from entitlement or privilege, it's flat out disrespectful to them to ignore that. I'm not here to play respectability politics, and I'm not here to teach people lessons in common decency.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> We'll stop questioning the motives of cis white males (and females, to a lesser extent) when they stop disregarding the voices of everyone else.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I agree here 100%.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I won't argue that we need more outreach to all poor people. We need more outreach in general. We lost because we didn't mobilize. Trump had less voter turnout than the last two Republican nominees. Clinton lost because too many people stayed in and didn't vote.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hillary out spent and out mobilized Trump by a massive margin.<br /> <br /> It didn't work because people can't stand Hillary and her scandals.<br /> <br /> And the truth is is calling Trump supporters bigots, while smearing a gender and a race is hypocritical, if you don't learn Trump will win again and I won't have any sympathy for you, because you simply refuse to learn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.nationalpost.com/m/wp/news/blog.html?b=news.nationalpost.com/news/world/wed-cried-wolf-too-many-times-eight-ways-liberals-can-blame-themselves-for-president-donald-trump&amp;pubdate=2016-11-12\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.nationalpost.com/m/wp/news/blog.html?b=news.nationalpost.com/news/world/wed-cried-wolf-too-many-times-eight-ways-liberals-can-blame-themselves-for-president-donald-trump&amp;pubdate=2016-11-12\" target=\"_blank\"> 404 Not Found - National Post </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.nationalpost.com/m/wp/news/blog.html?b=news.nationalpost.com/news/world/wed-cried-wolf-too-many-times-eight-ways-liberals-can-blame-themselves-for-president-donald-trump&amp;pubdate=2016-11-12\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.nationalpost.com/m/wp/news/blog.html?b=news.nationalpost.com/news/world/wed-cried-wolf-too-many-times-eight-ways-liberals-can-blame-themselves-for-president-donald-trump&amp;pubdate=2016-11-12 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 8 ways Liberals can blame themselves for Trumps victory.<br /> <br /> My country now has a President Doland Trump on its border and I blame you for that. <br /> <br /> I didn't get a vote, you did, it was your responsiblity, and you and your fellow democracts fucked up, but Canada and Mexico will pay the price for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T09:58:42-08:00","id":1002257,"title":"","content":"Trump calling national protests &quot;unfair&quot;...based on what he said last election...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.theverge.com/2016/11/11/13596932/trump-protestors-electoral-college-tweets\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/chorus/uploads/chorus_asset/file/15923537/GettyImages-622165118.0.1478863917.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C14.041194407687%2C100%2C71.917611184627&amp;w=1200\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.theverge.com/2016/11/11/13596932/trump-protestors-electoral-college-tweets\" target=\"_blank\"> Trump complains about &lsquo;unfair&rsquo; protestors, deletes his tweets calling for revolution in 2012 </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.theverge.com/2016/11/11/13596932/trump-protestors-electoral-college-tweets\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.theverge.com/2016/11/11/13596932/trump-protestors-electoral-college-tweets </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The Verge is about technology and how it makes us feel. Founded in 2011, we offer our audience everything from breaking news to reviews to award-winning features and investigations, on our site, in video, and in podcasts. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ...is fucking hiLARious.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T10:40:25-08:00","id":1002265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002247#post1002247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hillary out spent and out mobilized Trump by a massive margin.<br /> <br /> It didn't work because people can't stand Hillary and her scandals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Accurate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002247#post1002247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the truth is is calling Trump supporters bigots, while smearing a gender and a race is hypocritical,</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's not get into this again, Pendragon has already said to drop the subject.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002247#post1002247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if you don't learn Trump will win again and I won't have any sympathy for you, because you simply refuse to learn.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, though it's clear we disagree on what needs to be learned. The party needs to learn what its voters actually want, and the voters need to learn that not voting or voting third party favors the Republican candidate. Trump got fewer votes than both McCain and Romney, but won anyway because Clinto. got <i>much</i> fewer votes than Obama either election. And even then she won the popular vote. The biggest lesson to be learned here is that democrats are in the majority, but that majority doesn't matter if people in swing states don't contribute to weighting the pendulum to the left.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002247#post1002247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My country now has a President Doland Trump on its border and I blame you for that. <br /> <br /> I didn't get a vote, you did, it was your responsiblity, and you and your fellow democracts fucked up, but Canada and Mexico will pay the price for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't blame me. I voted Hillary and my State was blue. The real thing to blame here is the electoral college system. This is twice now in as many decades that the candidate the majority of the country voted for lost anyway, because it's not enough that you have the majority of the votes, you need them to come from the right places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T11:48:39-08:00","id":1002289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://m.huffpost.com/ca/entry/12929810\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://img.huffingtonpost.com/asset/5cd65b082500002f00a5c452.jpeg?ops=1200_630\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://m.huffpost.com/ca/entry/12929810\" target=\"_blank\"> TPP Trade Deal Likely Dead After Trump Win </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://m.huffpost.com/ca/entry/12929810\" target=\"_blank\"> http://m.huffpost.com/ca/entry/12929810 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> It was one of the world's most ambitious trade deals. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It looks like Trump may have saved 58,000 Canadian Jobs by causing the death of the TPP.<br /> <br /> Oh and over 400,000 American jobs.<br /> <br /> Also Trudeau said he's willing to reopen NAFTA in discussions with Trump.<br /> <br /> So I know Trump is surrounded by alot of social conservatives and bad people, but at least this is a silver lining and as a Canadian something to celebrate, if your Canadian and don't have to deal with all the bad stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T12:22:18-08:00","id":1002303,"title":"","content":"Additional though on the Electoral College:<br /> <br /> I wonder how people in general will feel if the EC does work as intended by Hamilton and Madison, and elect Hillary. People tend to assume that the EC will just puppet the vote in their state, but they can easily tank Trump if they want to. In 21 states electors are unbound and can legally vote however they want. In the 29 + DC that do restrict, the worst thing that can happen with an elector's faithless vote is that their vote is treated as an abstention (and theoretically they could be criminally prosecuted for $1,000 but the general consensus of legal scholars is that it would be unconstitutional to do so). Pennsylvania and Florida alone could reverse the election. Assuming Trump gets Michigan and Clinton gets New Hampshire (as not everyone considers these called), if PA's unbound electoral delegation all go Clinton, and if FL's bound delegation all just don't go Trump, Clinton would take the EC by 1 elector.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crytash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002193#post1002193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trump was able to get the first group and Clinton was not able to convince the second.</div> </div> </div> </div>By a tiny margin in a small number of states to turn the Electoral College against the popular vote. It's worth remembering there was no landslide here. The election was ultimately decided by less than 200,000 people in a nation of 300 million (obviously not all voters) across four out of 50 States. If Hillary had gotten 0.5% better in all the swing states, she'd be president elect right now.<br /> <br /> Sure, one vote or a million votes doesn't matter if you don't get more votes than the other candidates to the results. But losing by a tiny fraction of the vote is far less of a condemnation that people make it out to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is important not to tone police people for many reasons. </div> </div> </div>You realize you're saying this from a country that has extremely strong hate speech laws... right? Trump's campaign could be considered outright criminal by German law. Not even getting into the vast majority of Trump supporters, but the clear and vocal bigots among them have been incited to violence against minority groups by his campaign.<br /> <br /> The Left's tendency towards &quot;tone-policing&quot; in the US is a result of the fact that our Free Speech laws are so strong. It's on the public to push against hate speech, so it's what the public does; on both sides. There is little to no legal recourse, so the fight goes to the people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This add up with the the other reasons for segregation that we see in the US society at the moment and this IS a fault of the democratic elite, as we can see in NY even more. </div> </div> </div>Pointing at the segregation in NY isn't really an example of the &quot;fault&quot; of the modern Democrat elite (it's something that hasn't been fixed, but its causes go back well before most of us were born, and many attempts by said elite failed for reasons far to varied to pin just on one group).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Parts of the LGBTQ community have who center themselves around the cities will have better opportunities for a job or other essential items. Their support system is intact there. </div> </div> </div>This is... just wrong. The LGBTQ community center themselves around cities for survival. Their support system isn't &quot;intact&quot; there, it's the only place it actively exists.<br /> <br /> To give you an idea, as a lefty living in a rural right-wing part of the US, I was told directly that my Facebook page was costing me job opportunities because I have too many LGBTQ activist friends; and I'm a straight cis while male. That's what it's like out here. Being openly pro-LGBTQ here means I'm less competitive in an already rough economy.<br /> <br /> Where I live, you either leave, pass, or fall into the narrow acceptable range of token minority that doesn't make people uncomfortable (one of my wife's high school friends naturally falls into the slightly campy artistic white gay man persona and never faced much overt problems as an example, because he's the &quot;safe&quot; kind of gay to most people around here).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So from a class perspective both the minorities in the ghetto an the rural should be in the same class, but because of conflicts no people do not see this, aside of the far (European normal) left around Bernie and he was still attacked by feminists as well as minority groups, who are at least partially responsible for making Hillary the nominee of the democratic party. </div> </div> </div>The bigger problem is that the Democrats take the working class white vote for granted rather than not seeing them. The Democrats knew this election was going to mean that part of their coalition was not going to be out in the strength it has been in the past, they just underestimated by how much and thus failed to solidify it properly. And again, they only failed to do this by a tiny fraction for the presidential election.<br /> <br /> And Sanders screwed up the primaries doing the same thing in the other direction. He took for granted the racial and orientation minorities would fall in line with him as a progressive liberal to focus on the working class white vote, and it cost him dearly. He didn't lose the black vote because some BLM people interrupted him. He lost them because Hillary has a wonderful reputation among the older southern black voter base because they remember what she did earlier in her career that either directly benefited them, or at least was her listening to them even if it didn't turn out well. The younger black vote didn't have that reaction to her, but they don't vote as much in the primary. Sanders needed to prove himself to the black community writ large - not just the motivated younger activists - and utterly failed to. He also made other key mistakes by not doing enough to connect with his own political supporters in various states. A lot of people on the fence between Sanders and Clinton in Pennsylvania <b>hated</b> his &quot;snubbing&quot; of John Fetterman (a Sanders supporting mayor that was running for Senate and exactly the kind of guy the Dems need to be pushing right now)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What the rural vote wants is decentralization. They want more middle class companies, not more Apple or Tesla. </div> </div> </div>Not really. They want stability (mostly economic, but some social as well), and have very strongly proven by their fickle support (aka dominating swing states) because they don't actually care how it happens as long as it happens. That's how Trump was so effective. He recognized they didn't actually care about a well thought out policy paper that explains how that economic stability would be achieved through a large number of incremental improvements. They don't care if a middle class company is the driving force of the economy in their town, or a giant multinational, as long as they have reliable good paying jobs.<br /> <br /> Coal miners aren't lamenting the death of coal miner jobs because coal companies used to be middle class companies, but because the jobs dried up as automation replaced them. Again there's no political party to blame for the death of coal jobs. It's a simple situation. Coal companies mine as much coal as they want to avoid saturating the market and driving down prices, so there's no issue with not getting enough coal out of the ground. Coal companies via technology can also mine the same amount of coal with 1/100th of the employees as they used to. 5,000 coal miners could be the core economic bloc of a small town that then supports schools, heath services, etc. 50 people can't do that. So the town &quot;dies.&quot;<br /> <br /> Decentralized companies are an exceptionally effective way to accomplish revitalizing the Rust Belt, but again, that's policy that the electorate doesn't seem to care about over the promise that something will be done.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002247#post1002247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It didn't work because people can't stand Hillary and her scandals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because a small fraction of people in just the right places bought into this as one of many factors.<br /> <br /> Of course, it would be nice if people commenting from the outside would stop acting like they know Hillary's factual domestic history, or the public's general impression of her. She won the popular vote. That's not all people holding their nose.<br /> <br /> It also very much bolsters the lies about Hillary when people from other countries that don't know the full record advocate the, &quot;well even if most of it isn't true, something must be, right?&quot; mentality about her. I don't care if you don't like her politics, but her scandals are 90% manufactured crap, and 5% stupid mistakes that should barely matter to anything. Yes, there's some actual valid scandals in there (just like every politician ever, and plenty of the general public). But almost nobody pays any attention to them because the manufactured stuff is way juicier.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My country now has a President Doland Trump on its border and I blame you for that. </div> </div> </div>When you spend 5x the energy yelling at the people that elected him instead of the people that voted against him, we might care.<br /> <br /> Or how about this: You Canadians did jack shit to stop the tide of unrest in the Middle East by failing to make Afghanistan and Iraq operations successful. ISIS, Boko Haram, the Syria civil war, the Saudi-Yemen conflict, the Paris attacks? All of that is Canada's fault for not doing enough to make sure it didn't happen. You guys fucked up, and the rest of us are paying the price for it. Harper enabled the US lead coalition both actively in Afghanistan, and under the table in Iraq, so it can't be the US's fault that things didn't go well.<br /> <br /> Sound fair? We don't blame the people leading the charge to elect Trump, so we don't blame the people leading the charge elsewhere. We find people that we can validly blame for being part of the problem and put all the blame on them instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002257#post1002257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...is fucking hiLARious.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, turning into scary as his transition team, list of cabinet appointees, and health care plans get detailed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T12:29:01-08:00","id":1002311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002289#post1002289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It looks like Trump may have saved 58,000 Canadian Jobs by causing the death of the TPP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't count on it.<br /> <br /> He said he was going to replace Obamacare without removing the vital protections for people with pre-existing conditions... and his new plan is just Paul Ryan's plan which doesn't nothing for those people; leaving the only option a new high risk individual plan which will cost at least three times what Obamacare costs the Federal government to run, and will likely have even higher premiums (we know, because states tried it before). Trump's already caving his campaign promises to the free trade wing of the Republicans, so don't count on TPP being dead. It simply means it will be a Republican only TPP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T12:32:08-08:00","id":1002313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002303#post1002303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additional though on the Electoral College:<br /> <br /> I wonder how people in general will feel if the EC does work as intended by Hamilton and Madison, and elect Hillary. People tend to assume that the EC will just puppet the vote in their state, but they can easily tank Trump if they want to. In 21 states electors are unbound and can legally vote however they want. In the 29 + DC that do restrict, the worst thing that can happen with an elector's faithless vote is that their vote is treated as an abstention (and theoretically they could be criminally prosecuted for $1,000 but the general consensus of legal scholars is that it would be unconstitutional to do so). Pennsylvania and Florida alone could reverse the election. Assuming Trump gets Michigan and Clinton gets New Hampshire (as not everyone considers these called), if PA's unbound electoral delegation all go Clinton, and if FL's bound delegation all just don't go Trump, Clinton would take the EC by 1 elector.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see the theoretical and incredibly unlikely possibility that a dozen, maybe even two dozen delegates could swap their votes. But with only 228 delegates, Hillary needs 42(!) delegates to swap votes for her to win. I think there is a better chance of Donald Trump being hit by a meteorite when he next steps out of Trump Tower than for 42 delegates to all swap their votes for Hillary - and even if 42 delegates swapped votes for her, it's possible that other delegates from states she won could end up swapping their votes and going for Trump.<br /> <br /> If Hillary was only short 5 or 6 votes it might be within the realm of possibility for delegates to break for her, but Hillary ended up being so far behind in the Electoral College that the chance of anything like this happening is too low to really bother spending much time speculating on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T12:49:25-08:00","id":1002316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <a href=\"http://www.cnn.com/2016/11/12/politics/hillary-clinton-james-comey-fbi/index.html\" target=\"_blank\">(CNN)</a> - Hillary Clinton told donors in a conference call Saturday that FBI Director James Comey delivered a double whammy to her candidacy in the final days of the campaign by taking another look at emails related to Clinton's private server before abruptly saying he found no wrongdoing.<br /> <br /> A member of her national finance committee who was on the call told CNN that Clinton placed at least some of the blame on Comey for her stunning defeat to Donald Trump.<br /> <br /> She said the first letter from Comey, sent to Congress on October 28, stopped the momentum she had built after three debates and the release of Trump's &quot;Access Hollywood&quot; tape.<br /> <br /> She said the second letter, which came nine days later and exonerated Clinton, simply fired up Trump supporters and didn't put any on-the-fence voters who had been leaning her way at ease.<br /> <br /> She said the FBI development was too much to &quot;overcome,&quot; the donor on the call told CNN, but she acknowledged there were other headwinds facing her campaign that they didn't adequately combat.<br /> She urged supporters to move forward and keep fighting for their beliefs.<br /> <br /> The conversation, which lasted about 30 minutes, was not open to the press. Another Democrat on the call said Clinton described the loss as &quot;heartbreaking.&quot;<br /> <br /> As she said in her concession speech Wednesday, Clinton told supporters that she was sorry for not being able to defeat Trump.<br /> <br /> The call was far from a full accounting of the stunning upset, but rather a chance for Clinton to thank her supporters directly after the hard-fought campaign.<br /> <br /> She was not overtly critical of Trump, two participants on the call told CNN, but she did urge those to rise up and continue fighting against divisive rhetoric targeting immigrants and others.<br /> <br /> She did not engage in a back-and-forth over other factors that contributed to her loss, including what many Democrats said was a failure to articulate an economic message that appealed to working-class voters across the Rust Belt. </div> </div> </div>So basically, Clinton feels that Comey's letters were the final &quot;nails in the coffin&quot; of her campaign. Did Comey overreach by informing Congress of his investigation? Or should he have kept quiet and not told them what he was doing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T13:05:39-08:00","id":1002323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1001935#post1001935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although not for lack of young me trying. Let me tell you, it didn't work out so well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The line I used that made my aunt really mad, but she couldn't argue was... &quot;You can make me do this, but you can't make me LIKE DOING IT.&quot; I always felt like being angry over something like that was more about getting verbally outmanuevered by a kid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T13:09:20-08:00","id":1002325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/xXH5agV7skw\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/xXH5agV7skw\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/xXH5agV7skw\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/xXH5agV7skw </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think if Obama had been able to run again he'd have crushed Trump, he's an excellent speaker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T13:18:03-08:00","id":1002327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002265#post1002265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, though it's clear we disagree on what needs to be learned. The party needs to learn what its voters actually want, and the voters need to learn that not voting or voting third party favors the Republican candidate. Trump got fewer votes than both McCain and Romney, but won anyway because Clinto. got <i>much</i> fewer votes than Obama either election. And even then she won the popular vote. The biggest lesson to be learned here is that democrats are in the majority, but that majority doesn't matter if people in swing states don't contribute to weighting the pendulum to the left.<br /> <br /> <br /> Don't blame me. I voted Hillary and my State was blue. The real thing to blame here is the electoral college system. This is twice now in as many decades that the candidate the majority of the country voted for lost anyway, because it's not enough that you have the majority of the votes, you need them to come from the right places.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the fact that a VERY SIGNIFICANT (9%, if what I've heard is right) number of Democrats voted Trump. That's... way more damaging to Clinton than people voting 3rd party. The fact is, in a lot of the elections where a 3rd party candidate gets blamed for the loss, a far more significant number of Democrats went to the Republican candidate. It's just pointing at 3rd parties as the problem is a nice narrative if you want to keep the 2 party system running things. I'm not saying you're WRONG... just that blame on 3rd party voters feels a bit unjustified (even if it does tend to help Republicans... then again, Gary Johnson took a fair number of people who WOULD have voted for Trump otherwise).<br /> <br /> My state was red, but I voted against Trump. Just due to the Electoral college, my vote didn't matter. Remember, a lot of states are winner take all, also.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T13:22:57-08:00","id":1002329,"title":"","content":"Well, at least we're not going to die in nuclear fire now. That's something at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T13:27:20-08:00","id":1002331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002327#post1002327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also the fact that a VERY SIGNIFICANT (9%, if what I've heard is right) number of Democrats voted Trump. That's... way more damaging to Clinton than people voting 3rd party. The fact is, in a lot of the elections where a 3rd party candidate gets blamed for the loss, a far more significant number of Democrats went to the Republican candidate. It's just pointing at 3rd parties as the problem is a nice narrative if you want to keep the 2 party system running things. I'm not saying you're WRONG... just that blame on 3rd party voters feels a bit unjustified (even if it does tend to help Republicans... then again, Gary Johnson took a fair number of people who WOULD have voted for Trump otherwise).</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, and I didn't mean to suggest that 3rd party voters are solely to blame. It's only one factor among many. The main point I wanted to express was that the Democrats have the majority opinion, but that only matters if we are all on the same page.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002327#post1002327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My state was red, but I voted against Trump. Just due to the Electoral college, my vote didn't matter. Remember, a lot of states are winner take all, also.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's another problem with the EC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T13:41:13-08:00","id":1002338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002059#post1002059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read this op-ed on CNN the other day, and I think it sums up more or less what I am thinking - though the author is an ardent Bernie supporter, some of his specific takes on the Democratic Party and how it managed to lose its way resonate pretty well...<br /> ...But, I think he gets a few major points correct. The Democrats lost because they completely failed to connect with voters. Many saw them as no different from the Republicans. The &quot;free trade&quot; and close ties with Wallstreet elites manage to drive away the blue collar union workers who have been a reliable and core constituency of the Democrats for decades...</div> </div> </div> </div>I would caution everybody to think quite a bit harder about the issue before slamming NAFTA or TPP too harshly. If you think it's hard for blue collar folks to get a job now, I assure you you do <i>not</i> want to see what a no-shit trade-war actually looks like. Also, if TPP fails (which it probably will under a Trump Administration) it will very likely mean that <b><i>our</i></b> trade policies will end up being dictated to us by China. And the Tea Party and Bernie-bros can blow that off all they want (and what a peculiar meeting or the minds <i>that</i> represents), but <i>that's</i> the reality. The Soviets found out the hard way that when you allow ideology to blind you to reality, reality will inevitably bite you in the ass -- and hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 11-12-2016, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T13:41:39-08:00","id":1002339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002313#post1002313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could see the theoretical and incredibly unlikely possibility that a dozen, maybe even two dozen delegates could swap their votes. But with only 228 delegates, Hillary needs 42(!) delegates to swap votes for her to win. I think there is a better chance of Donald Trump being hit by a meteorite when he next steps out of Trump Tower than for 42 delegates to all swap their votes for Hillary - and even if 42 delegates swapped votes for her, it's possible that other delegates from states she won could end up swapping their votes and going for Trump.<br /> <br /> If Hillary was only short 5 or 6 votes it might be within the realm of possibility for delegates to break for her, but Hillary ended up being so far behind in the Electoral College that the chance of anything like this happening is too low to really bother spending much time speculating on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I have high expectations for this actually happening, but Hillary doesn't actually need 42 delegates to change their votes. She only needs 21, which would leave Trump with less than the 270 electoral college votes required to win. If neither candidate receives enough electoral college votes, the presidency goes to the winner of the popular vote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T13:57:46-08:00","id":1002345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002339#post1002339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that I have high expectations for this actually happening, but Hillary doesn't actually need 42 delegates to change their votes. She only needs 21, which would leave Trump with less than the 270 electoral college votes required to win. If neither candidate receives enough electoral college votes, the presidency goes to the winner of the popular vote.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought the result went to the House? Which, is Republican... and the VP is chosen by the Senate... which is Republican.<br /> <br /> Edit: The Founding Fathers were elitist assholes who didn't want the general population to screw things up, and therefore made the electoral college and such so they could keep the power where they felt it belonged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","user":"haren","date":". 11-12-2016, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T14:02:05-08:00","id":1002346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002345#post1002345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I thought the result went to the House? Which, is Republican... and the VP is chosen by the Senate... which is Republican.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're correct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T14:03:12-08:00","id":1002348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/whk68Q6rAfk\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/whk68Q6rAfk\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/whk68Q6rAfk\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/whk68Q6rAfk </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Aggressive Progressives on the election.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/pRkYg_jHQJw\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/pRkYg_jHQJw\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/pRkYg_jHQJw\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/pRkYg_jHQJw </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Canada Immigration website crashed after Trump victory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.mainstreetresearch.ca/trump-wins-canadians-wont-make-easier-move-canada/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.mainstreetresearch.ca/trump-wins-canadians-wont-make-easier-move-canada/\" target=\"_blank\"> Not Found </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.mainstreetresearch.ca/trump-wins-canadians-wont-make-easier-move-canada/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.mainstreetresearch.ca/trump-wins-canadians-wont-make-easier-move-canada/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 72% of Canadians don't want to make it easier for Americans to immigrate to Canada.<br /> <br /> So far no serious talk of actually making a wall and having Americans pay for it is occurring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T14:09:35-08:00","id":1002349,"title":"","content":"Also, the electors don't &quot;change&quot; their votes. They refuse to vote for who the people voted for (which is actually their constitutional right if they feel the need); they're not actually supposed to decide ahead of time (though nothing legally stops them from it and some states mandate that the decision is made for them anyway).<br /> <br /> Though Hillary doesn't need to get to 270, she still needs the majority of the counted votes (which is why Florida essentially abstaining by doing anything but voting for Trump works, it reduces the number of elector votes from 538 to 509 and thus the needed number to win to 255). It's not at all likely, but it remains a legal possibility as well as an action that actually reflects the desires of the authors of the EC; that it act a a check against exactly this sort of popular wave upsetting the system they designed.<br /> <br /> Though <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> is off a bit in that if none of the candidates have a majority of the cast ballots it doesn't go to the people, it goes to the House for President and Senate for Vice President (and they could opt to split the ticket as well, which is a whole different set of strangeness).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T14:10:59-08:00","id":1002350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002338#post1002338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would caution everybody to think quite a bit harder about the issue before slamming NAFTA or TPP too harshly. If you think it's hard for blue collar folks to get a job now, I assure you you do <i>not</i> want to see what a no-shit trade-war actually looks like. Also, if TPP fails (which it probably will under a Trump Administration) it will very likely mean that <b><i>our</i></b> trade policies will end up being dictated to us by China. And the Tea Party and Bernie-bros can blow that off all they want (and what a peculiar meeting or the minds <i>that</i> represents), but <i>that's</i> the reality. The Soviets found out the hard way that when you allow ideology to blind you to reality, reality will inevitably bite you in the ass -- and hard.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not suggesting a full on trade war.<br /> <br /> But the truth is along side automation, manufacturing has already been devestated by free trade, national soveriegnty has been devestated, tax revenues have hurt as corporations and the rich play nation against nation.<br /> <br /> The rich and corporations were at the table for these treaties, but regular people effected by them were not. <br /> <br /> It sends the message that the 1% can't just do whatever they want with these treaties, and fuck everybody else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T14:15:16-08:00","id":1002351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002316#post1002316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So basically, Clinton feels that Comey's letters were the final &quot;nails in the coffin&quot; of her campaign. Did Comey overreach by informing Congress of his investigation? Or should he have kept quiet and not told them what he was doing?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> He shouldn't have said anything until he had concrete evidence one way or the other as to what was contained on Weiner's laptop. My stepfather is a retired federal agent and he still has friends within that community who are angry with Comey for politicizing the FBI, who think he botched the handling of the investigation and believe he's damaged both the FBI's credibility and non partisan image. The appearance of impartiality and professionalism is very important to these people and Comey shit all over it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 11-12-2016, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T14:16:45-08:00","id":1002352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002345#post1002345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: The Founding Fathers were elitist assholes who didn't want the general population to screw things up, and therefore made the electoral college and such so they could keep the power where they felt it belonged.</div> </div> </div> </div>Madison and Hamilton's reasoning for the EC is a bit more nuanced than that; though it certainly is true that it was an extremely elitist minded decision. One of their reasons which is a bit more compelling is that the US is a compromise of direct democracy and representative democracy in the form of multiple bodies. Just like the House is supposed to be the people's chamber of Congress and the Senate is supposed be the states' chamber of Congress, the EC was intended to also embody that same mindset. A mixture of power between the general electorate and the power of individual states that's more fair between them despite differences in size.<br /> <br /> Not that it worked, and at least Madison and Hamilton recognized that and tried to fix it, but once they failed to stop their fellow Founding Fathers political savvy, only the elitist aspect of the EC remained as functional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T14:20:32-08:00","id":1002354,"title":"","content":"9% of democracts voted for Trump.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T14:25:07-08:00","id":1002356,"title":"","content":"Bill Burr on celebraties during this election <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/_lLxlvLx__A\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/_lLxlvLx__A\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/_lLxlvLx__A\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/_lLxlvLx__A </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T14:30:19-08:00","id":1002358,"title":"","content":"Doink, my mistake there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T14:44:49-08:00","id":1002367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002345#post1002345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: The Founding Fathers were elitist assholes who didn't want the general population to screw things up, and therefore made the electoral college and such so they could keep the power where they felt it belonged.</div> </div> </div> </div>The creation of the Electoral College was more complicated than that.<br /> <br /> First, keep in mind that most of them were incredibly weary of a strong federal government, which they were afraid would quickly take control of the country at the expense of the individual states and colonies. That's why their first attempt at a government, via the Articles of Confederation, created a federal government so weak that it was actually incapable of doing much of anything. The Constitution was written in reaction to the weakness of the original federal government, but the authors still took great pains to keep the federal government from being so strong it would be able to usurp states rights.<br /> <br /> Part of the idea with the Electoral College was that less populated states would still have a stronger say in the election of the president - that the president wouldn't only need to have to win the votes in 3 or 4 most populated states states and then get to ignore all the rest. It was a way to ensure that individual states retained a voice in the presidential election and, in fact, when one looks at elections such as this where one candidate wins the popular vote but loses the election because they weren't able to convince enough people in enough states to vote for them, that is the Electoral College performing <i>exactly</i> as it was intended to.<br /> <br /> Of course, there were also other ideas wrapped up in the Electoral College, like the worry that Americans might elect a demagogue - many of the framers of the Constitution were all very aware of the kind of mortal damage that demagogues such as Alcibiades or Cleon inflicted on ancient Athens and the Electoral College was one method by which they hoped would that sort of event would be prevented from happening in America.<br /> <br /> But the idea that the Electoral College was just created to fuck over the common man isn't really very accurate. There were a lot of reasons that it helped bring about its inception and dicking over the common man only had a tiny part to do with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T15:10:38-08:00","id":1002377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002338#post1002338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would caution everybody to think quite a bit harder about the issue before slamming NAFTA or TPP too harshly. If you think it's hard for blue collar folks to get a job now, I assure you you do <i>not</i> want to see what a no-shit trade-war actually looks like. Also, if TPP fails (which it probably will under a Trump Administration) it will very likely mean that <b><i>our</i></b> trade policies will end up being dictated to us by China. And the Tea Party and Bernie-bros can blow that off all they want (and what a peculiar meeting or the minds <i>that</i> represents), but <i>that's</i> the reality. The Soviets found out the hard way that when you allow ideology to blind you to reality, reality will inevitably bite you in the ass -- and hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that in a lot of ways, Clintonomics ended up hurting the country more than it helped. To be absolutely clear, his economic policies didn't hurt as much as Reagan's Trickle Down economics did, but many of Clinton's core economic ideas - free trade, deregulation, an uninhibited free market balanced by only the lightest of touches on regulation of business practices and taxes on the wealthy, have caused no end of problems for America.<br /> <br /> I don't expect Trump to be an improvement on that. He's probably going to make things worse in some ways, though a few of his ideas about closing various tax loopholes would be nice <i>if</i> he follows through. Regardless though the Democrats need to realize that following Bill Clinton's economic playbook is absolutely not a a method to success, either at the voting booth or in the real world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T15:40:50-08:00","id":1002382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002354#post1002354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">9% of democracts voted for Trump.</div> </div> </div> </div>9% of the people who voted for Trump were Democrats. Just like 7% of the people who voted for Clinton were Republicans. Please get your facts straight before posting. The video you showed earlier, for instance, <a href=\"http://www.snopes.com/black-mob-beats-white-man-for-voting-trump/\" target=\"_blank\">was the result of a traffic dispute</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002377#post1002377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I<span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> don't expect Trump to be an improvement on that. He's probably going to make things worse in some ways, though a few of his ideas about closing various tax loopholes would be nice </span><i>if</i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> he follows through. Regardless though the Democrats need to realize that following Bill Clinton's economic playbook is absolutely not a a method to success, either at the voting booth or in the real world.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Yes, it's nice to believe we'd live in a land of milk and honey if the election went another way but there's no guarantee. Still, Clinton's economics were a progressive step towards globalization, getting everyone working together. It looks like Trump is going to change a lot of our environmental and clean energy priorities, which won't really sit well after years of trying to get the rest of the world to move towards cleaner energy. Though it would likely free up some jobs around here.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-12-2016, 06:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T15:54:27-08:00","id":1002387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002382#post1002382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The video you showed earlier, for instance, <a href=\"http://www.snopes.com/black-mob-beats-white-man-for-voting-trump/\" target=\"_blank\">was the result of a traffic dispute</a>.[/FONT]</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably true. But it doesn't help that while the mob is beating him, they're yelling &quot;**** Donald Trump!&quot; and &quot;beat that Trump bitch's ass!&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: After doing more research, and seeing exactly what transpired from the parties involved, it looks like what started as a traffic issue, QUICKLY turned into a hate crime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 11-13-2016, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T16:15:39-08:00","id":1002392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002382#post1002382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it's nice to believe we'd live in a land of milk and honey if the election went another way but there's no guarantee. Still, Clinton's economics were a progressive step towards globalization, getting everyone working together. It looks like Trump is going to change a lot of our environmental and clean energy priorities, which won't really sit well after years of trying to get the rest of the world to move towards cleaner energy. Though it would likely free up some jobs around here.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the end of the day, the American people vote to elect a president who will do the best he (or she) can possible do to improve the lives of Americans, first, foremost and period. The well-being of the citizens of other countries comes as a distinct second to that. Presidents and candidates who put (or who are perceived as putting) the well-being of the people of other nations ahead of the well-being of Americans are not going to be popular presidents or candidates. Policies that get everyone working together are nice, but not if they come at the expense of Americans being able to find work themselves.<br /> <br /> And I would definitely say that Clinton was the one who moved the Democratic party firmly into the &quot;pro-globalization&quot; category. It's also what made any attempts on Hillary's part to take an anti-globalist stance ring completely hollow. She and her husband had spent years focusing on pro-globalist policies designed to benefit corporations in exchange for donations, at the expense of the common American. <br /> <br /> These days, globalization is viewed as something of a dirty word throughout much of America due to things like NAFTA and other Clinton-style economic initiatives that ended up costing American jobs. I think this election kind of reminded the Democrats about the fact that they need to worry more (or at least appear to worry more) about American workers and American problems and less about the greater global issues that most Americans don't feel are terribly pressing. A candidate whose dream is a common market with open trade and open borders is not something many Americans will appreciate.<br /> <br /> I mean, issues like Global Warming don't seem very important when the business you were working for moved oversees and you're having trouble finding a new job so you can put food on the table. Nobody cares if it's easier for people in Mexico or Canada or any other country to find jobs if they themselves can't find one at home. Hopefully the utterly shellacking the Democrats got hit with this year causes the Democrats to realize that many Americans believe the Democratic Party has lost way on a number of issues over the last two-dozen years and Democrats will take the next several years to rediscover themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 11-12-2016, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T16:21:46-08:00","id":1002395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002382#post1002382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though it would likely free up some jobs around here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Getting the state-level Republicans to stop screwing solar over would free up vastly more jobs than loosening up fossil fuel restrictions could possible do. And we actually sell solar panels to other countries which would help more with trade deficits than increasing use of locally sourced fossil fuels because we'd be exporting as well as reducing our imports of energy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002392#post1002392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, issues like Global Warming don't seem very important when the business you were working for moved oversees and you're having trouble finding a new job so you can put food on the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, the problem is that we're already at the point where Global Warming is harming US citizens, not just in theory, or not just people in other countries. Not valuing climate change abatement efforts isn't valuing America over other countries, it's screwing other Americans over for your own interests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T16:22:18-08:00","id":1002396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002352#post1002352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Madison and Hamilton's reasoning for the EC is a bit more nuanced than that; though it certainly is true that it was an extremely elitist minded decision. One of their reasons which is a bit more compelling is that the US is a compromise of direct democracy and representative democracy in the form of multiple bodies. Just like the House is supposed to be the people's chamber of Congress and the Senate is supposed be the states' chamber of Congress, the EC was intended to also embody that same mindset. A mixture of power between the general electorate and the power of individual states that's more fair between them despite differences in size.<br /> <br /> Not that it worked, and at least Madison and Hamilton recognized that and tried to fix it, but once they failed to stop their fellow Founding Fathers political savvy, only the elitist aspect of the EC remained as functional.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know, and I know not all of the Founding Fathers were like that... but I'm not in a very charitable mood. But yeah, you're right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002358#post1002358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doink, my mistake there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Far as I'm concerned, I'd rather you were right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002377#post1002377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say that in a lot of ways, Clintonomics ended up hurting the country more than it helped. To be absolutely clear, his economic policies didn't hurt as much as Reagan's Trickle Down economics did, but many of Clinton's core economic ideas - free trade, deregulation, an uninhibited free market balanced by only the lightest of touches on regulation of business practices and taxes on the wealthy, have caused no end of problems for America.<br /> <br /> I don't expect Trump to be an improvement on that. He's probably going to make things worse in some ways, though a few of his ideas about closing various tax loopholes would be nice <i>if</i> he follows through. Regardless though the Democrats need to realize that following Bill Clinton's economic playbook is absolutely not a a method to success, either at the voting booth or in the real world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not sure that I agree that Clinton didn't do as much damage as Trickle Down, BUT... yeah, basically I agree with you. I think in some ways, Clinton did way more damage with the legacy of neoliberalism (which you could say has pushed both party mainstreams to the right). This year has definitely been one staring hard at neoliberalism and saying people are tired of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T16:42:13-08:00","id":1002400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002395#post1002395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, the problem is that we're already at the point where Global Warming is harming US citizens, not just in theory, or not just people in other countries. Not valuing climate change abatement efforts isn't valuing America over other countries, it's screwing other Americans over for your own interests.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to a <a href=\"http://www.cnsnews.com/news/article/lauretta-brown/pew-most-americans-dont-believe-scientific-consensus-climate-change\" target=\"_blank\">Pew survey</a>, over 3/4ths of Americans don't trust that there is a scientific consensus on global warming. Only around 1/4th of Americans believe Global Warming is caused by humans. Further less than 1/3rd of Americans believe climate scientists actually understand whether global climate change is even happening. And finally less than 20% (fewer than 1 in 5) Americans believe that climate scientists actually know how to fix the problem (if there even is one). <br /> <br /> So Global Warming is not viewed as a particularly major or important issue by most Americans. In fact, for many Americans, Global Warming is just an excuse for the government to channel money into the pockets of various special interest groups, both domestic and foreign. <br /> <br /> Of course, we can argue over the realities of Global Warming, but the fact is that the <i>perception among many voters</i> is that Global Warming is a dog whistle used by Democrats to justify globalist policies at the expense of American workers. And in the end, that's all that matters - not whether something is or is not true, but what the voters believe is true or untrue. And candidates and political parties have to accept and work with that perception if they want to get votes. <br /> <br /> In this election, the Democrats completely failed to do so and as a result had one of the most historic losses that their party has ever experienced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T17:45:36-08:00","id":1002408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002400#post1002400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to a <a href=\"http://www.cnsnews.com/news/article/lauretta-brown/pew-most-americans-dont-believe-scientific-consensus-climate-change\" target=\"_blank\">Pew survey</a>, over 3/4ths of Americans don't trust that there is a scientific consensus on global warming. Only around 1/4th of Americans believe Global Warming is caused by humans. Further less than 1/3rd of Americans believe climate scientists actually understand whether global climate change is even happening. And finally less than 20% (fewer than 1 in 5) Americans believe that climate scientists actually know how to fix the problem (if there even is one).</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not an accurate representation of that survey.<br /> <br /> 27% of respondents trust that there is a scientific consensus on global warming being man-made, not that it isn't happening at all. Which also less than 3/4s of Americans not trusting in this, not more.<br /> <br /> Some counter cherry-picking:<br /> <br /> 48% of US adults believe that man made global warming is occurring (not sure where you're getting that 1/4 figure, possibly people that think only man-made change is occurring and no natural change?).<br /> <br /> 61% believe that over the next 50 years, climate change will have major impacts of their lifestyle.<br /> <br /> 67% believe scientists should have a major role in making policy on the subject (compared to the general public at 56% and elected officials at 44%, oh and foreign leaders at 45%... so apparently we trust other countries' elected officials a tad more than our own...)<br /> <br /> So... no. I don't think what you're trying to infer from that survey is accurate. Especially telling is the 61% of Americans believing that climate change will have a major impact on how we live in the next 50 years. So most Americans actually do believe that climate change is going to be a problem, even if they don't agree on why it's happening. As well, Americans actually trust scientists to fix things, both in policy and technology, more than anyone else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In fact, for many Americans, Global Warming is just an excuse for the government to channel money into the pockets of various special interest groups, both domestic and foreign. </div> </div> </div>I agree. But we can also solidly put this on Republican politicians and their donors waging a decades long crusade to create this perception; to the point where now that Republicans are finally being forced to confront the reality of climate change, they screw themselves because if they do anything about it they get primary challenges.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And candidates and political parties have to accept and work with that perception if they want to get votes. </div> </div> </div>True, but there's more ways to get votes than just caving to public misconceptions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In this election, the Democrats completely failed to do so and as a result had one of the most historic losses that their party has ever experienced. </div> </div> </div>Again, this argument is inane. Sure, the lose was historic because of the insane nature of this election cycle. But this is not the first time the Democrats have lost both chambers and the Presidency. They've lost by much, much larger margins before.<br /> <br /> Trump didn't flip a single non-battle ground state. Trump didn't get the popular vote. Trump just eked in through the electoral college.<br /> <br /> Stop treating this like Trump won by 5 points in California.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T18:20:03-08:00","id":1002411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002408#post1002408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, this argument is inane. Sure, the lose was historic because of the insane nature of this election cycle. But this is not the first time the Democrats have lost both chambers and the Presidency. They've lost by much, much larger margins before.<br /> <br /> Trump didn't flip a single non-battle ground state. Trump didn't get the popular vote. Trump just eked in through the electoral college.<br /> <br /> Stop treating this like Trump won by 5 points in California.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Republicans took control of both chambers of Congress and the presidency. That's pretty big in and of itself. Then you need to consider the state level gains Republicans made - 33 states now have Republican governors the largest number of Republican governors in almost a century (the last time they had that many was back in 1922). Republicans also have a &quot;trifecta&quot; (controlling the governor-ship, house and senate) in almost half of American states, vs the Democrat's six. Overall, the Democrats took one of the worst shellackings they've ever suffered, Republicans are in one of the best places they've ever been in, and Democrats should be counting their blessings it wasn't even worse.<br /> <br /> It's also probably not going to get much better in two years - most of the Congressional districts up for reelection are currently have Democrats sitting in them, and many of those districts are fairly red-leaning. The best that Democrats can really hope for is that the Republicans will fuck up and the Democrats will be able to hold onto their current seats. If people think the Republicans are doing a halfway decent job, the Republicans could find their control over the House and Senate growing even wider. <br /> <br /> To just say that pointing out that the Democrat's losses in this election at the government and state level were historic are, &quot;insane&quot; is just silly. The Democrats managed to lose huge on what should have been an easy win win (I mean how the @#%&amp; do you lose to Donald freaking Trump?) and that loss was due to the way they lost the trust of so many voters, specifically blue-collar union voters in the Rustbelt who felt ignored and left behind by Democrat policies. The Democrats need to figure out how to regain the trust of those voters.<br /> <br /> And one of the first steps to doing that is for Democrats to admit that, yeah, they got their butts kicked because the American public did not like the Democratic ideas, values and nominees that were put forth during this campaign. Then they need to find some ways of either embracing newer ideas, values and candidates that will appeal to voters in the next election cycle, or they need to figure out how to make their current message more appealing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T18:32:57-08:00","id":1002413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002411#post1002411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To just say that pointing out that the Democrat's losses in this election at the government and state level were historic are, &quot;insane&quot; is just silly. The Democrats managed to lose huge on what should have been an easy win win (I mean how the @#%&amp; do you lose to Donald freaking Trump?) and that loss was due to the way they lost the trust of so many voters, specifically blue-collar union voters in the Rustbelt who felt ignored and left behind by Democrat policies. The Democrats need to figure out how to regain the trust of those voters.<br /> <br /> And one of the first steps to doing that is for Democrats to admit that, yeah, they got their butts kicked because the American public did not like the Democratic ideas, values and nominees that were put forth during this campaign. Then they need to find some ways of either embracing newer ideas, values and candidates that will appeal to voters in the next election cycle, or they need to figure out how to make their current message more appealing.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there was never a question of leaked e-mails or Benghazi, do you think Clinton would have more voters? Because he's pointing out it was a close race, and the Democrats almost won with a lot stacked against them.<br /> <br /> Yes, for many people not electing Trump seems obvious. But for many other people, not electing Clinton was just as obvious.<br /> <br /> Also, he said 'inane.' He said the election cycle was what was insane. Like two weeks before the election an FBI director said there might be incriminating e-mails that could lead to unspecified criminal charges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-12-2016, 09:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T19:10:17-08:00","id":1002421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002413#post1002413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there was never a question of leaked e-mails or Benghazi, do you think Clinton would have more voters? Because he's pointing out it was a close race, and the Democrats almost won with a lot stacked against them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, of course, if Clinton hadn't fucked up and started her private email servers and hadn't dropped the ball on Benghazi (and hadn't said and done, well, a lot of the stupid things she's said and done over the years) it goes without saying she would have had more voters. As I said earlier, I think the presidential election was more a referendum on Hillary than anything else.<br /> <br /> But focusing solely on how &quot;close&quot; the Hillary/Trump election obfuscates the the real losses that Democrats had. They had historic losses throughout many of the state and local governments across the country and the Republican control at the state level is the strongest it's been in at least a century of not longer. Hillary lost the election by such a margin that there was no point in trying to fight it like Gore did (Bush vs Gore was a close race). The Democrats lost Congress - even compared to 2000 the Democrats didn't lose quite that badly (they walked away with a 50/50 split in the Senate and then Republicans gained a seat in the 2002 election).<br /> <br /> The American people turned against the Democrats, not just on the presidential election, but on the Congressional elections, in state governor elections, in state congress elections and even in many smaller local elections across the country. Let's be honest here - this was probably the worst showing the Democrats have had in most any living person's lifetime at the local, the state and the national levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T19:18:01-08:00","id":1002422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not suggesting a full on trade war.<br /> <br /> But the truth is along side automation, manufacturing has already been devestated by free trade, national soveriegnty has been devestated, tax revenues have hurt as corporations and the rich play nation against nation.<br /> <br /> The rich and corporations were at the table for these treaties, but regular people effected by them were not.<br /> <br /> It sends the message that the 1% can't just do whatever they want with these treaties, and fuck everybody else.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002377#post1002377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say that in a lot of ways, Clintonomics ended up hurting the country more than it helped. To be absolutely clear, his economic policies didn't hurt as much as Reagan's Trickle Down economics did, but many of Clinton's core economic ideas - free trade, deregulation, an uninhibited free market balanced by only the lightest of touches on regulation of business practices and taxes on the wealthy, have caused no end of problems for America.<br /> <br /> I don't expect Trump to be an improvement on that. He's probably going to make things worse in some ways, though a few of his ideas about closing various tax loopholes would be nice <i>if</i> he follows through. Regardless though the Democrats need to realize that following Bill Clinton's economic playbook is absolutely not a a method to success, either at the voting booth or in the real world.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is though that if you don't like Clinton's (Bill's that is) economic policies and stuff like NAFTA, you really need to keep it in the context of &quot;compared to what?&quot;, because they don't exist in a vacuum. I just got this week's edition of The Economist in, and their econo-wonks have been running projections. Their position is that if Trump <i>actually</i> follows through on all of his campaign pledges (including killing TPP and ripping up NAFTA), one of those plausible projections has a net loss of 4.8 <i>million</i> American jobs by the end of his first term. Essentially <i>no</i> reputable macro-economic experts think that Trump's policies will create jobs. The only dispute between them is <i>how much </i>the economy will contract and how <i>many</i> jobs will be <i>lost</i>. If Americans don't lose this goofy idea that free trade somehow <i>hurts</i> America's economy, we're going to be in for some <i>seriously</i> rough weather ahead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T19:55:41-08:00","id":1002437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002422#post1002422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Americans don't lose this goofy idea that free trade somehow <i>hurts</i> America's economy, we're going to be in for some <i>seriously</i> rough weather ahead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then the Democrats need to be able to articulate how free trade helps Americans. So far they have colossally fucked that up - in fact, Hillary lost states like Pennsylvania, Michigan, etc, primarily because of blue collar union workers who felt that her and her husband's free trade initiatives had hurt them and their towns and neighbors.<br /> <br /> Yes, some members of the voting populace have really benefited from free trade. But many others have been hurt by free trade legislation. It shouldn't be a surprise that those voters who feel that their lives were harmed by free trade initiatives would not want to vote for the candidate that champions free trade.<br /> <br /> And as long as Democrats can't explain to blue collar workers how factories shutting down in the US and firing hundreds of workers so they can set up shop in other countries actually benefits those out-of-work workers who have to take jobs making less money, and how their lives and their children's lives are better off because of that, you're not going to see those voters being very sympathetic to free trade candidates like Hillary Clinton.<br /> <br /> In the end, due to Bill Clinton's initiatives, the Democrats have become the party of free trade. So it's on them to demonstrate to the American voting populace that every American benefits from free trade and that supporting free trade candidates is in their best personal interest. I think we can generally agree that at the least in this last election, they failed rather badly at doing that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T20:07:14-08:00","id":1002444,"title":"","content":"Only Americans have benefitted from free trade in almost every conceivable way -- not &quot;some&quot;, most. Many have been hurt by it, but far fewer than is generally believed by the public. Most of those job losses -- like, the vast majority -- have nothing whatsoever to do with off-shoring or foreign competition. The main takeaway from this election was best articulated by Newt Gingrich when he stated that if people believed something, that somehow made it analogous to being fact (and the fact that he was willing to say that on CNN's live air without falling out of his chair from embarrassment is even more telling). Most Americans get their information from the internet without much if any review by people with any real knowledge. The idea that somehow it's the job of the Democrats to make sure the American public isn't ignorant and gullible is absurd. This is democracy in action. Americans will get the government we deserve -- and if we're too lazy (or paranoid) to listen to reason or educate ourselves to know any better, then Donald Trump is the government that we deserve.<br /> <br /> And that's why I'm so ashamed to be an American right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T20:08:18-08:00","id":1002445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002421#post1002421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Democrats lost Congress...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe Democrats picked up 6 seats in the House and at least 2 seats in the Senate. Not great but not the loss you claim either. The GOP has held both House and Senate majority since 2014, they didn't gain that control this year, and the Republicans don't have a filibuster proof majority in the Senate so that's at least a bit of a silver lining to those who dislike GOP policies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T20:13:13-08:00","id":1002447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002445#post1002445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and the Republicans don't have a filibuster proof majority in the Senate...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not entirely. As part of the package deal that averted Sequester 2.0 this last time, the Senate changed some procedural rules that allow <i>some</i> filibusters to be stopped by simple majority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T20:17:40-08:00","id":1002448,"title":"","content":"Now the question I really want answered is what kind of fucked up project required a Trump presidency as Infrastructure? The GM must have something spectacularly shitty waiting in the wings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T22:09:12-08:00","id":1002465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002411#post1002411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Republicans took control of both chambers of Congress and the presidency. That's pretty big in and of itself. Then you need to consider the state level gains Republicans made - 33 states now have Republican governors the largest number of Republican governors in almost a century (the last time they had that many was back in 1922). Republicans also have a &quot;trifecta&quot; (controlling the governor-ship, house and senate) in almost half of American states, vs the Democrat's six. Overall, the Democrats took one of the worst shellackings they've ever suffered, Republicans are in one of the best places they've ever been in, and Democrats should be counting their blessings it wasn't even worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>As noted, this is completely ignoring the state of the country before the election. As noted the Republicans already controlled both chambers of Congress and actually lost seats this election.<br /> <br /> Also, the US puts a lot of odds against the party of a two-term leaving president. As Obama put it, the public gets a desire for that &quot;new car smell.&quot; Loses are expected in traditional poli-sci theory for the party of a two term president (even Bush Sr. saw loses compared to Reagan's second term despite keeping the presidency).<br /> <br /> 31 states had Republican governors before the election... so the Republicans had a gain of two. It's important, but it's not some tidal wave of Republican control. The Republicans have had a huge advantage in the states since the 2010 census redistricting; most of the damage in the states is far more traceable to that than anything this election. It's also a basic demographic issue. The Republicans have solid control over the mid-West and Big Sky, which means a lot of small population (and those high value voters due to their over-representation in the Senate and House, and thus the EC as well) states give them power way above the popular vote. As you yourself noted, the country is set up so California and New York don't let the party that dominates urban centers doesn't just control the country with those centers alone.<br /> <br /> Again, the trifectas? The Republicans had a net gain of three.<br /> <br /> So, like I said, stop treating this as the massive &quot;shellacking&quot; you're talking about. The Democrats were in a shitty position before all this, so being a shitty position after all this isn't really a big change.<br /> <br /> Losing ground of course is bad for the Democrats, but there was not seismic shift here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To just say that pointing out that the Democrat's losses in this election at the government and state level were historic are, &quot;insane&quot; is just silly. </div> </div> </div>I didn't?<br /> <br /> I'm calling the insistence on treating this election as a massive red wave across the country is insane. The Republicans made net gains, but nothing earth shaking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Democrats managed to lose huge on what should have been an easy win win (I mean how the @#%&amp; do you lose to Donald freaking Trump?) </div> </div> </div>Over a dozen Republicans managed to lose to Trump to. And so did all the NeverTrump primary activists in the Republican party.<br /> <br /> If Hillary won, there's plenty of people on the right saying the same thing, given Hillary's own image problems and the massive success for the decades of the Clinton smear-machine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...and that loss was due to the way they lost the trust of so many voters, specifically blue-collar union voters in the Rustbelt who felt ignored and left behind by Democrat policies. The Democrats need to figure out how to regain the trust of those voters. </div> </div> </div>The problem with this is that these voters didn't express specific dissatisfaction with Democratic policies, but with the political establishment as a whole, which the successor to the current president embodies the most in public perception. It's not that they specifically lost faith with Democrats, but they lost faith with whoever was in-charge and that was Obama and thus the Democrats.<br /> <br /> That's how Trump also beat the Republican establishment despite having so little institutional support in the primaries. The Republican blue-collar workers rejected Bush and Kaisch just the same.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T22:37:30-08:00","id":1002467,"title":"","content":"Okay. Well, we haven't seen an election map like this after a presidential election in over 100 years. I think that makes it fairly historic, even if it was just a a bit of a shift from where it was before the election.<br /> <br /> Hopefully however the Democrats take things pretty seriously, learn from their mistakes and ramp up their outreach and attempts to connect with voters who felt marginalized by Democratic positions and policies to the point that many of them decided to vote for Trump (specifically noting the otherwise solid blue union voters of states like Michigan and Pennsylvania). Because if the Democrats can't start winning those voting blocks back in the future, the Democratic party is going to find itself in a difficult position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 11-13-2016, 01:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T03:12:02-08:00","id":1002490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002465#post1002465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As noted, this is completely ignoring the state of the country before the election. As noted the Republicans already controlled both chambers of Congress and actually lost seats this election.<br /> <br /> Also, the US puts a lot of odds against the party of a two-term leaving president. As Obama put it, the public gets a desire for that &amp;quot;new car smell.&amp;quot; Loses are expected in traditional poli-sci theory for the party of a two term president (even Bush Sr. saw loses compared to Reagan's second term despite keeping the presidency).<br /> <br /> 31 states had Republican governors before the election... so the Republicans had a gain of two. It's important, but it's not some tidal wave of Republican control. The Republicans have had a huge advantage in the states since the 2010 census redistricting; most of the damage in the states is far more traceable to that than anything this election. It's also a basic demographic issue. The Republicans have solid control over the mid-West and Big Sky, which means a lot of small population (and those high value voters due to their over-representation in the Senate and House, and thus the EC as well) states give them power way above the popular vote. As you yourself noted, the country is set up so California and New York don't let the party that dominates urban centers doesn't just control the country with those centers alone.<br /> <br /> Again, the trifectas? The Republicans had a net gain of three.<br /> <br /> So, like I said, stop treating this as the massive &amp;quot;shellacking&amp;quot; you're talking about. The Democrats were in a shitty position before all this, so being a shitty position after all this isn't really a big change.<br /> <br /> Losing ground of course is bad for the Democrats, but there was not seismic shift here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I didn't?<br /> <br /> I'm calling the insistence on treating this election as a massive red wave across the country is insane. The Republicans made net gains, but nothing earth shaking.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Over a dozen Republicans managed to lose to Trump to. And so did all the NeverTrump primary activists in the Republican party.<br /> <br /> If Hillary won, there's plenty of people on the right saying the same thing, given Hillary's own image problems and the massive success for the decades of the Clinton smear-machine.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The problem with this is that these voters didn't express specific dissatisfaction with Democratic policies, but with the political establishment as a whole, which the successor to the current president embodies the most in public perception. It's not that they specifically lost faith with Democrats, but they lost faith with whoever was in-charge and that was Obama and thus the Democrats.<br /> <br /> That's how Trump also beat the Republican establishment despite having so little institutional support in the primaries. The Republican blue-collar workers rejected Bush and Kaisch just the same.</div> </div> </div> </div> Agreed. The Republicans have nothing to crow about, Trump hijacked their party, its now the Trump party effectively, not the party of Reagan anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T03:48:24-08:00","id":1002494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1002467#post1002467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. Well, we haven't seen an election map like this after a presidential election in over 100 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um... huh? Just looking at major Republican wins here going back to the 60s:<br /> <br /> 1988: Bush Sr. trashed Dukakis. Dukakis got 10 states + DC, for a total of 111 EC votes, and Dukakis lost the popular vote by ~7 million. The Democrats had the Senate and the House and managed to hold steady with very small gains (just like this election).<br /> <br /> 1984: Reagan's epic thrashing of Mondale. Mondale got one state + DC for a grand total of 13 EC votes, and lost by ~17 million votes. Republicans held the Senate despite minor Democrat gains, and Democrats held the House despite losing 16 seats.<br /> <br /> 1980: Reagan trounces Carter. Carter got 6 states + DC for a total of 49 EC votes, and lost by ~8.5 million votes. Republicans took over the Senate with a massive gain of 12 seats, and the Democrats held the House despite a huge 34 seat lose (the Democratic hold on the House in the 80s was insanely strong when you consider how many seats they could afford to lose without losing control of the Chamber).<br /> <br /> 1972: Nixon curbstomps McGovern. McGovern got one state + DC for 17 EC votes, and lost by ~17 million votes. Democrats held the Senate and had a small gain, and held the House despite significant losses (OK so that whole Democratic hold on the house was more than the 80s).<br /> <br /> 1968: The Wallace run makes it hard to compared directly even if the results were similar to the above examples.<br /> <br /> The only difference here is that the Democrats in all those elections were much, much stronger in the Congress before the presidential elections, so despite similar (or worse) swings the government remained divided. The only thing we haven't seen from the Republicans in 100 years was getting control across the federal board (though we have seen it multiple times in the past 100 years for the Democrats).<br /> <br /> Those were historic blow out elections.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hopefully however the Democrats take things pretty seriously, learn from their mistakes and ramp up their outreach and attempts to connect with voters who felt marginalized by Democratic positions and policies to the point that many of them decided to vote for Trump (specifically noting the otherwise solid blue union voters of states like Michigan and Pennsylvania). Because if the Democrats can't start winning those voting blocks back in the future, the Democratic party is going to find itself in a difficult position. </div> </div> </div>Again, you keep asserting that the marginalized motivation for Trump supporters was specifically anti-Democratic. What's your evidence on this? Everything I've seen suggests that it was not motivated by specific party positions and policies over general dissatisfaction with the establishment. The Parties of the nominees was incidental to the motivation of why they voted.<br /> <br /> Also, the Democrats can't rely on unions, because the Republicans have union busted so hard that unions aren't strong enough to carry that voter bloc any more. What remains of the industrial unions in the Rust Belt is a shadow of their former power and influence. All of the strong unions that can really pull in votes are ones like teacher and service unions which overlap more with urban population centers anyway. <br /> <br /> Can we stop asserting that the Democrats lost these votes purely by apathy or laziness? There's decades of active political attacks on the institutions the Democrats relied on to organize those votes by the Republicans (because hey, that's part of politics, divide and conquer the other side's voting blocs) that have been trying to pry at those very voters' loyalty to the Democrats.<br /> <br /> It's one of the reasons I'm continually frustrated by this whole, &quot;Trump is liberals fault!&quot; thing. It ignores decades of attempts by the Republican party and conservative activists to make this happen to try to open the space for another Regan. The problem is Trump squatted on that space instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"