ng> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1004170#post1004170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Republicans control too many states for that to work. Still if Trump had won more votes then Hillary, but Hillary won the electoral college would you still support this movement?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. And actually no thats not how it works. I also might add its a bi partisan movement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Need some Tunes for your Exalted Game? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1071249-exalted-tunes\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-exalted-tunes</a><br /> Want some help managing your PCs? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882498-new-anathema-character-management-anathema-reincarnated\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...a-reincarnated</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2442-arian-dynas","name":"Arian Dynas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T20:30:24-08:00","id":1004221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arian Dynas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1003822#post1003822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Call me a thread sniper, but uh, just gotta say; everyone who's against Trump, look into the Pan-State Popular Vote initiative. We're trying to convert over to the popular vote, since the constitution states the states can dispose of their electors in their own way, meaning that if it happens before December, the presidency will reflect the will of the American people.<br /> <br /> Anyway, AWAAAYYYYY!</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the National Popular Vote?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.nationalpopularvote.com/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.nationalpopularvote.com/sites/default/files/npv_logo_225x225.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.nationalpopularvote.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> National Popular Vote </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.nationalpopularvote.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.nationalpopularvote.com/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> State status: AK AL AR AZ CA CO CT DC DE FL GA HI IA ID IL IN KS KY LA MA MD ME MI MN MO MS MT NC ND NE NH NJ NM NV NY OH OK OR PA RI SC SD TN TX UT VA VT WA WI WV WY The National Popular Vote Interstate Compact will guarantee the Presidency to the candidate who receives the most popular votes in all 50 states and the District of Columbia. The Compact has been enacted by 18 states and DC (CA, CO, CT, DE, DC, HI, IL, MA, MD, ME, MN, NJ, NM, NY, OR, RI, VA, VT, WA). These places together possess 222 of the 270 electoral votes needed to activate the Compact. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T07:49:08-08:00","id":1004418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/qOOVDJJ77F0\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/qOOVDJJ77F0\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/qOOVDJJ77F0\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/qOOVDJJ77F0 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Secular Talk on why Hillary lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T07:50:04-08:00","id":1004419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arian Dynas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1004215#post1004215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yup. And actually no thats not how it works. I also might add its a bi partisan movement.</div> </div> </div> </div> As long as its bipartisan that's fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T17:36:52-08:00","id":1004718,"title":"","content":"Hmm, it's a minor thing, and it was said a few days ago, but it will just be stuck in my head if I don't get it out:<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Simpsons did not <i>predict</i> Donald Trump becoming president; the show made a joke out of the idea as a bit of background for a vision of a bad future for America, and used him specifically because Trump has been saying that he wants to be president for <i>decades</i>.<br /> <br /> Hell, Barrack Obama made a joke out of the idea of Donald Trump becoming president several years ago, which was probably not a serious prediction that the man would actually seek the Republican nomination this time.<br /> <br /> Considering his age, it wouldn't really be outlandish to think that &quot;become president&quot; was a literal item on Trump's bucket list, that he finally saw an urgency in ticking off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T04:57:51-08:00","id":1004880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/11a3KASGUlc\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/11a3KASGUlc\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/11a3KASGUlc\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/11a3KASGUlc </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> John Stewart on the Trump win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T05:11:23-08:00","id":1004884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/DrGDY7jyXU4\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/DrGDY7jyXU4\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/DrGDY7jyXU4\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/DrGDY7jyXU4 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Secular Talk on Team Hillary who are still trying to blame &quot;Bern Bros&quot; for her defeat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T05:49:33-08:00","id":1004894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/y3-uNxmNj5o\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/y3-uNxmNj5o\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/y3-uNxmNj5o\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/y3-uNxmNj5o </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Bill Mahar makes an excellent point, that is completely lost on the woman on the panel, who just chalks it up to people being threatened by equality (ignoring the fact that many of these people voted for Barrack Obama).<br /> <br /> This is lazy thinking, just blame it on sexist, racism, ect... Anything so that Hillary supporters don't have to take responsiblity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T10:00:49-08:00","id":1004999,"title":"","content":"Eh? His point isn't exactly that great. &quot;PC bullshit,&quot; is an invention of the right (explicitly, right wing people came up with the phrase specifically for this purpose) to make it easier to dismiss left wing arguments without engaging with them. The whole point of labeling something PC, is to say that it doesn't matter who's right or wrong, or who has the best solution, but what matters is what tribe you're in when you say something before you can be listened to. This is why &quot;post-truth&quot; just got named word of the year by Oxford. Anna Marie Cox (she has a name, she's not just the token woman), was right (even Trae Crowder agreed with her), the issue jut comes down to something that's already been discussed:<br /> <br /> Should Democrats follow down the &quot;post-true&quot; rabbit hole and abandon core ideology for political wins, or should they stick to their guns and hope the country goes back to remembering that the Republicans might talk a good game but they don't actually do anything to help.<br /> <br /> Also, the whole, &quot;be nice to Muslims&quot; thing is crap. Besides the fact that leaders of every political stripe (ex: Bush Jr.) have been solidly behind both going after terrorists with Muslim ideologies, while simultaneously calling on the country to respect that the majority of Muslims are good people and should not be targeted for the actions of a few radicals, if we cared about stopping terrorism in the US... we'd be looking just as hard at white men as people insist on looking at Muslims. While Jihadist terrorism in the US has the larger body count (though 9/11 skews that massively), white male natural born citizens of the US carry out far more terrorist attacks (and there are plenty of nasty attacks from that cohort in our history, ex: Oklahoma City, which is the second deadliest terrorist attack in US, third including the '98 embassy attacks, and both of the ones above it were coordinated multiple simultaneous strikes instead of one attack).<br /> <br /> Bill Maher's &quot;excellent point,&quot; amounts to, &quot;lets continue to enable the echo chamber of rural white America,&quot; which might have some merit as a crass political strategy, but has nothing to offer beyond that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T12:42:29-08:00","id":1005065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1004894#post1004894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://youtu.be/y3-uNxmNj5o\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/y3-uNxmNj5o</a><br /> <br /> Bill Mahar makes an excellent point, that is completely lost on the woman on the panel, who just chalks it up to people being threatened by equality (ignoring the fact that many of these people voted for Barrack Obama).<br /> <br /> This is lazy thinking, just blame it on sexist, racism, ect... Anything so that Hillary supporters don't have to take responsiblity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Saw this earlier and I agree with what he said. Despite not being a fan of Bill, I'd say he definitely echoes a lot of the same beliefs I've heard from a number of people, including my friends. There are so many aspects to political correctness it's hard to keep track. I definitely think it's used by some in a way to end a conversation without engaging in any sort of positive talk. Kind of like how &quot;hater&quot; was used for the last five or so years. It almost completely negates the chance for successful discourse.<br /> <br /> However, there are aspects of &quot;PC&quot; that definitely drive me up a wall. Bill seems to get it perfectly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T13:21:25-08:00","id":1005078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1004999#post1004999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh? His point isn't exactly that great. &quot;PC bullshit,&quot; is an invention of the right (explicitly, right wing people came up with the phrase specifically for this purpose) to make it easier to dismiss left wing arguments without engaging with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThis happens to be how those same right wing people are made to feel when we keep talking to them about white male privilege when they are worried about providing a living for themselves and their families. They feel their concerns are being dismissed out of hand. It's language that makes them feel like their concerns are being dismissed and diminished. I've made the point repeatedly to my right wing friends that when we (people on the left) are speaking of privilege we aren't saying that they don't have their own problems and don't have their own obstacles to overcome but rather are saying that other groups of people have obstacles in their way that straight white men don't have to deal with. I tell them that if we want to address the concerns they have we need to have everyone on the same page and facing those same issues so we can effectively address the shared problem instead of fighting over who has it worse. That requires we recognize issues that aren't a problem for us but are a problem for other people. I'm not diminishing their problems, I do my best to illustrate that there are things we don't have to deal with without demonizing my friends for wanting their concerns heard.<br /> <br /> They feel excluded and reinforcing this idea of exclusion via language policing isn't productive for anyone. Addressing their feelings isn't &quot;catering to them&quot; That's what Maher is addressing when he calls something &quot;PC Bullshit&quot;. He's directly attacking exclusionary language that happens to target the least disadvantaged group because you are alienating and othering people who rationally should be working with you instead of against. It reinforces tribalism rather than reduces it.<br /> Should I tell someone who isn't a straight white man they shouldn't comment with an opinion about straight white men because they aren't a straight white man? Should I tell them since they don't have the same experiences as a straight white man they should keep their mouths shut? I really don't think so, and that works both ways. You don't need to agree with or apply the same weight to an outside opinion as someone living the experience, but don't demand recognition that you won't offer the opposing side. Don't apply the most negative interpretation of what someone is saying without engaging and clarifying what exactly that person is trying to convey. I've seen too much of that coming from my side and that shit needs to fucking stop, unless you enjoy seeing irrational reactionary divisive politics, then by all means continue what you are doing and keep eating your own. The RNC thanks you for it because based on the election results they've learned how to leverage it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 11-18-2016, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T13:53:38-08:00","id":1005089,"title":"","content":"Does anyone actually tell straight white men they're not allowed to have opinions or to contribute to discussions of sociopolitical issues? Cause I've seen a lot of people object to being told &quot;You must be this oppressed to participate&quot;, but I've never actually seen anyone tell someone that. Maybe it's just the circles I hang out in, but in my anecdotal experience that particular grievance is a strawman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T14:01:06-08:00","id":1005090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005089#post1005089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone actually tell straight white men they're not allowed to have opinions or to contribute to discussions of sociopolitical issues?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. I've seen it on NUMEROUS occasions. On social media, college campuses, and in person. I usually live in New York City for 2-3 months out of the year, and in Florida the rest. <br /> <br /> Granted, my experiences with hearing, seeing, or reading about it only go back the last three or four years. But it's definitely happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 11-18-2016, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T14:03:40-08:00","id":1005093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005089#post1005089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone actually tell straight white men they're not allowed to have opinions or to contribute to discussions of sociopolitical issues? Cause I've seen a lot of people object to being told &quot;You must be this oppressed to participate&quot;, but I've never actually seen anyone tell someone that. Maybe it's just the circles I hang out in, but in my anecdotal experience that particular grievance is a strawman.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was in a chat room and one of the participants said that he was on a college campus and was told by some girl that his opinions didn't matter because of his white maleness (I'm paraphrasing). I didn't dig for the details because it turned into an argument about whether or not privilege even exists.<br /> <br /> EDIT: It occurs to me that I typically don't hear that in person because when social issues come up when I'm around my non-male white cisgender friends I shut my mouth because I don't believe I have anything to say as a male white cisgender. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":1923,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","user":"BigDamnHero","date":". 11-18-2016, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T14:13:06-08:00","id":1005097,"title":"","content":"Absolutely agreed Darksider. One of the issues with &quot;white male privilege&quot; is that, rather than using it as a method to bring white males <i>aboard</i> and get them to help to help tear down discrimination against all people and develop a level playing field, instead white privilege is often used as a method of <i>attacking</i> white males - the classic, &quot;Check your privilege&quot; and such, and using it as a way demonize white males as a whole and shut them out of the conversation entirely because of their sex and race.<br /> <br /> So rather than getting white males to go, &quot;Oh yeah, I see how other people lack some of the benefits that I do because of my skin color - we need to change that,&quot; instead they feel as though they are under attack because of their skin color or sex and (like any group feeling itself under attack) they tend to huddle more together and avoid interacting or engaging with the people who are attacking them and then start fighting back. Which is, you know, kind of the <i>opposite</i> effect that the people looking to end white privilege were hoping for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T14:30:15-08:00","id":1005105,"title":"","content":"My anecdotal evidence/experience differs from yours (Charlaquin's). I've seen it in personal conversations, mostly in conversations I have with Black/African American friends of mine on Facebook. Because my great grandmother was a freed (non-American) slave and I grew up seeing my grandfather face discrimination in the 70's I get a pass in some of those conversations, but there is a lot of (justifiable) anger in those conversations. My role tends to be &quot;those guys don't understand what you are facing and the only way to get them to is to do some handholding while you walk them through the minefield.&quot; I give the outsider perspective without being hostile about it, and because I have some shared experience with what those friends have experienced sometimes they listen to what I have to say when they would have ignored or shouted down someone else. I've certainly been on the receiving end of the &quot;but you're one of the good ones&quot; jokes from those friends.<br /> \u200b<br /> As far as sexism goes, I get told quite often enough by Hillary supporters that if I point out weaknesses her campaign had I'm just being a sexist white male Berniebro (as if that isn't sexist itself) and couldn't possibly understand what it was like for her. They're right, I don't know what it's like to be a filthy rich white woman who gets exorbitant speaking fees from Wall Street firms with the full weight of the DNC machine behind me, but I do understand which policies and actions she's supported in the past that I don't agree with or support. David Hill has been much more eloquent than I in expressing those same concerns for the past few months on his Facebook feed and some opinion pieces he's written, so I can recommend checking that out for further clarification. The point being though is that my opinion has been dismissed rather than being engaged with and reflected on. Since I used to have a headshot as my avatar (until I changed it to the Rangers logo because fuck yeah the team is great this year) it was quite easy to see I was a White male (even if my background isn't quite as &quot;White&quot; as my appearance).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 11-18-2016, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T14:39:24-08:00","id":1005111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005097#post1005097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So rather than getting white males to go, &quot;Oh yeah, I see how other people lack some of the benefits that I do because of my skin color - we need to change that,&quot; instead they feel as though they are under attack because of their skin color or sex and (like any group feeling itself under attack) they tend to huddle more together and avoid interacting or engaging with the people who are attacking them and then start fighting back. Which is, you know, kind of the <i>opposite</i> effect that the people looking to end white privilege were hoping for.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bExactly this, when I'm talking to a friend who feels like they're being bludgeoned over the head it makes it harder for me to get them on board with the idea of &quot;hey, we have an advantage we can use to make things better rather than worse.&quot; When they feel attacked (doesn't matter if justified or not, feelings aren't necessarily rational) they close minds and ranks. Then it boils down to tribalism, It's like me trying to argue with my Islander fan friends that their team is objectively worse than mine. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 11-18-2016, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T15:10:33-08:00","id":1005125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005078#post1005078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThis happens to be how those same right wing people are made to feel when we keep talking to them about white male privilege when they are worried about providing a living for themselves and their families.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apples and oranges.<br /> <br /> &quot;PC&quot; is a phrase of propaganda. It's first wide-spread use was actually far left checking against being dogmatic (the first minor use being dogmatic political following of Communist principles), which was then appropriated by the right in the late 80s/early 90s for the express purpose of enabling the dismissal of the entire liberal academic movement. A freaking President used it openly and publicly to decry liberalism as a whole.<br /> <br /> White male privilege can be used bluntly in a fashion that puts people off, but it isn't a term that's used solely for that purpose. The discussion of privilege as a sociological force is important academically.<br /> <br /> You're comparing the purposeful attempt to create a language of distrust and dismissal, to the evolution of different ways of talking in different echo-chambers leading to negative social interactions.<br /> <br /> They're simply not the same thing. The conflation of them is a &quot;success&quot; for elements of the right because it lets them distract people from left policies that would actually help them make a living and provide for their families more easily, and instead vote for right-wing policies that will a best make no positive change, by slapping the &quot;PC&quot; label on all leftist anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They feel their concerns are being dismissed out of hand. </div> </div> </div>Yes. That doesn't mean those feelings have any real solid grounding in reality. Those feelings need to be dealt with in politics, but the only solution can't be to cater to the bubble.<br /> <br /> As well... things like white male privilege isn't exactly common place in political speeches. You don't see candidates running against it. You see people on the Internet and people in academia discussing it. Meanwhile you absolutely see PC as something that is campaigned against actively by politicians.<br /> <br /> Even if the heavily condemned &quot;basket of deplorables&quot; speech by Clinton... if you actually read the whole thing, she spends a ton of time talking about addressing the concerns of blue collar working class folks. The idea that the left doesn't already try to talk about these things, and address them, just isn't factually true. The problem is that facts don't matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's what Maher is addressing when he calls something &quot;PC Bullshit&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Not really. I've watched enough of the man. That's not generally what he means. He doesn't want liberals to get cooperative. He wants them to get nasty. He <b>loves</b> mocking people that disagree with him, belittling them, and offending them for their &quot;ignorance.&quot; When he calls on people to not be &quot;PC&quot; it's not to be nicer and reach common ground, it's to stoop to a lower level.<br /> <br /> He's exactly the kind of liberal that is a horrible messenger because he doesn't actually care about having meaningful conversations to try to dissolve the bubbles and break through the echo-chambers. He wants liberals to stop holding back and just steamroll conservatives as politically nastily as possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't apply the most negative interpretation of what someone is saying without engaging and clarifying what exactly that person is trying to convey. </div> </div> </div>And... I wish that was what Maher actually argues. But it isn't. I've seen him clarify, and this isn't his message.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T15:18:36-08:00","id":1005127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005089#post1005089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone actually tell straight white men they're not allowed to have opinions or to contribute to discussions of sociopolitical issues? Cause I've seen a lot of people object to being told &quot;You must be this oppressed to participate&quot;, but I've never actually seen anyone tell someone that. Maybe it's just the circles I hang out in, but in my anecdotal experience that particular grievance is a strawman.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has been told to be a few times even to my face, but is even saying &quot;You must be this oppressed to participate&quot; any better?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T15:32:38-08:00","id":1005133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JBRocky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005127#post1005127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It has been told to be a few times even to my face, but is even saying &amp;quot;You must be this oppressed to participate&amp;quot; any better?</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh? No, I'm saying &quot;you must be this to participate&quot; isn't something people <i>say</i> in my experience, to people's faces or otherwise. I'm not exactly surprised to hear people have actually been told that, but I asked because I haven't seen it happen, so from my perspective seeing so many people object to being told that and no one actually saying it, it seems odd. Of course, I am well aware that my experience is not universal and is probably not even typical, so I asked for some outside perspectives. It still seems odd to me that it's apparently so common for folks to hear, but I guess that's the way it is. At any rate, I stand by my opinion that privilege does not and should not disqualify people from discussions, and that most arguments that are typically dismissed as &quot;PC bullshit&quot; are in fact valuable to the discussion, just as white dudes' opinions are valuable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T15:54:16-08:00","id":1005140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JBRocky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005127#post1005127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has been told to be a few times even to my face</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to ask the context of these situations. I could see it in certain places in college or high school or among college and high school-aged people but is this happening to you at the office or at family reunions?<br /> <br /> It's just curiousity, when I get confrontations they're usually not liberally oriented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T16:18:40-08:00","id":1005148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005133#post1005133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh? No, I'm saying &quot;you must be this to participate&quot; isn't something people <i>say</i> in my experience, to people's faces or otherwise. I'm not exactly surprised to hear people have actually been told that, but I asked because I haven't seen it happen, so from my perspective seeing so many people object to being told that and no one actually saying it, it seems odd. Of course, I am well aware that my experience is not universal and is probably not even typical, so I asked for some outside perspectives. It still seems odd to me that it's apparently so common for folks to hear, but I guess that's the way it is. At any rate, I stand by my opinion that privilege does not and should not disqualify people from discussions, and that most arguments that are typically dismissed as &quot;PC bullshit&quot; are in fact valuable to the discussion, just as white dudes' opinions are valuable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry if you took what I said the wrong way, I do not believe at any time you have said that. In fact you have done quite the opposite and been very polite when discussing different topics. I do agree with everyone has an opinion and has the right to speak it, it's part of free speech. But when you do you need to respect that others can and do disagree with you and that needs to be respected. That's the problem with the PC culture many times it's used to silence dissent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9486,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","user":"JBRocky","date":". 11-18-2016, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T16:28:57-08:00","id":1005151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005140#post1005140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to ask the context of these situations. I could see it in certain places in college or high school or among college and high school-aged people but is this happening to you at the office or at family reunions?<br /> <br /> It's just curiousity, when I get confrontations they're usually not liberally oriented.</div> </d