after a Vamp LARP (yes I like LARP's) had a guy tell me opinion didn't matter when it came to something to do with voting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disappointing to hear, thanks for clarifying. Glad that the rest of the group stood up for you, at least in the first case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T17:06:56-08:00","id":1005158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/TMvmLF2Mbg4\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/TMvmLF2Mbg4\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/TMvmLF2Mbg4\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/TMvmLF2Mbg4 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Democract estabishment still in denial, blaming Comer, that FBI guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T17:25:48-08:00","id":1005164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005158#post1005158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://youtu.be/TMvmLF2Mbg4\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/TMvmLF2Mbg4</a><br /> <br /> Democract estabishment still in denial, blaming Comer, that FBI guy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether FBI Director Comey actually affected the election or not, I still think he should be investigated for potential Hatch Act violations for trying to influence the election. He recklessly broke long standard policy to make a public announcement for an ongoing investigation, during a time frame that the impartiality of the government agencies is crucial. But now he's made the FBI political.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T17:39:32-08:00","id":1005168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005078#post1005078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThis happens to be how those same right wing people are made to feel when we keep talking to them about white male privilege when they are worried about providing a living for themselves and their families. They feel their concerns are being dismissed out of hand. It's language that makes them feel like their concerns are being dismissed and diminished. I've made the point repeatedly to my right wing friends that when we (people on the left) are speaking of privilege we aren't saying that they don't have their own problems and don't have their own obstacles to overcome but rather are saying that other groups of people have obstacles in their way that straight white men don't have to deal with. I tell them that if we want to address the concerns they have we need to have everyone on the same page and facing those same issues so we can effectively address the shared problem instead of fighting over who has it worse. That requires we recognize issues that aren't a problem for us but are a problem for other people. I'm not diminishing their problems, I do my best to illustrate that there are things we don't have to deal with without demonizing my friends for wanting their concerns heard.<br /> <br /> They feel excluded and reinforcing this idea of exclusion via language policing isn't productive for anyone. Addressing their feelings isn't &amp;quot;catering to them&amp;quot; That's what Maher is addressing when he calls something &amp;quot;PC Bullshit&amp;quot;. He's directly attacking exclusionary language that happens to target the least disadvantaged group because you are alienating and othering people who rationally should be working with you instead of against. It reinforces tribalism rather than reduces it.<br /> Should I tell someone who isn't a straight white man they shouldn't comment with an opinion about straight white men because they aren't a straight white man? Should I tell them since they don't have the same experiences as a straight white man they should keep their mouths shut? I really don't think so, and that works both ways. You don't need to agree with or apply the same weight to an outside opinion as someone living the experience, but don't demand recognition that you won't offer the opposing side. Don't apply the most negative interpretation of what someone is saying without engaging and clarifying what exactly that person is trying to convey. I've seen too much of that coming from my side and that shit needs to fucking stop, unless you enjoy seeing irrational reactionary divisive politics, then by all means continue what you are doing and keep eating your own. The RNC thanks you for it because based on the election results they've learned how to leverage it.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I've made the point repeatedly to my right wing friends that when we (people on the left) are speaking of privilege we aren't saying that they don't have their own problems and don't have their own obstacles to overcome but rather are saying that other groups of people have obstacles in their way that straight white men don't have to deal with&quot;<br /> <br /> I've seen lefties do exactly that on multiple occasions, I've seen then act like white people don't have issues, look around the web and you see lefties roll their eyes and talk about how silly it is that cis white males have issues and concerns, don't they know they're privledged.<br /> <br /> When your losing your job, your home, your health, ect..., it doesn't feel good to be told how priveldged you are. Too many on the left have a charicture of what life is like for white people. We're not threatened by equality, I have supported equality my whole life, I've supported gay marriage, I supported free surgury for the trans community, I was happy with Obama's win in 2008, I have voted repeatedly for women in my own country, prochoice, I support diversity in my community, I have defended muslim individuals against what I thought were unfair complaints, I have defended Sihks and their turbans, I didn't vote for our lesbian Premier, but that had nothing to do with her being a Lesbian, I don't vote for the Liberal Party, but I've complimented her when I feel she does something right such as offering HPV vaccines to boys, her BCI pilot project, cutting some bad deals for green energy (I'm pro green energy, its just all the bad deals did was turn people off green energy and raise prices).<br /> <br /> I've voted my whole life for what I felt was the best approach to equality. I still support that goal.<br /> <br /> But this fantasy that Cis White Males lives are all roses, and that everyday is International Men's Day, and there are people who really do believe it, that attidude has to stop, its just drives people away.<br /> <br /> My hope is that some good can come from this and most people on the left realized that they or other lefties have become hypocritical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T17:59:44-08:00","id":1005174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005168#post1005168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;I've made the point repeatedly to my right wing friends that when we (people on the left) are speaking of privilege we aren't saying that they don't have their own problems and don't have their own obstacles to overcome but rather are saying that other groups of people have obstacles in their way that straight white men don't have to deal with&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so you quoted this. How do you feel about this, as opposed to what you've heard most lefties do on multiple occasions? <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T18:25:06-08:00","id":1005182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005158#post1005158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Democract estabishment still in denial, blaming Comer, that FBI guy.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not denial.<br /> <br /> Again, with the hair margins Trump won by, these sorts of things matter.<br /> <br /> As I've heard a few pundits phrase it, when you lose a game by 10 to 9, you have ten times you failed on defense, and a bunch of times you failed on offense. Changing one of them could have reversed the game. <br /> <br /> Comey is one of those points; and to further the analogy a point that was lost because of a horrible call by the ref. Obviously there's no way to tell for sure, but the numbers all indicate that Comey's violation of DoJ standards, the ethics of his position, and the Hatch Act, cost Clinton a significant number of votes compared to the margins of victory in a few key states.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T19:19:05-08:00","id":1005195,"title":"","content":"Abolish the electoral college TJ<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/ys-qICrZzHw\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/ys-qICrZzHw\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/ys-qICrZzHw\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/ys-qICrZzHw </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T19:27:12-08:00","id":1005197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005182#post1005182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not denial.<br /> <br /> Again, with the hair margins Trump won by, these sorts of things matter.<br /> <br /> As I've heard a few pundits phrase it, when you lose a game by 10 to 9, you have ten times you failed on defense, and a bunch of times you failed on offense. Changing one of them could have reversed the game. <br /> <br /> Comey is one of those points; and to further the analogy a point that was lost because of a horrible call by the ref. Obviously there's no way to tell for sure, but the numbers all indicate that Comey's violation of DoJ standards, the ethics of his position, and the Hatch Act, cost Clinton a significant number of votes compared to the margins of victory in a few key states.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hillary should never have been vulnerible in the first place to it, any effect it had only did so, because she was such a weak nominee in the first place. <br /> <br /> And truth is is blaming it on that is a way to avoid being held to account by powerful democracts who are hoping the Democractic party establishment can continue as usual, you don't get a say in what Comey does or doesn't do, and pointing the finger at Comey doesn't fix the democracts issues, it doesn't prepare you for 2020, its misdirection so that the powers that be don't get held to account, same for those who blame sexism, who blame Bern Bros, who blame everybody, but themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T19:40:50-08:00","id":1005201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005174#post1005174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, so you quoted this. How do you feel about this, as opposed to what you've heard most lefties do on multiple occasions? <br /></div> </div> </div> </div> I agree with most of what you said, I'm just pointing out that your rightwing friends aren't wrong, the left, and again include myself in this, can be arrogent, and condsending as well towards rightwingers, whites, cis and men.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T19:57:10-08:00","id":1005207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005197#post1005197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hillary should never have been vulnerible in the first place to it, any effect it had only did so, because she was such a weak nominee in the first place.<br /> <br /> And truth is is blaming it on that is a way to avoid being held to account by powerful democracts who are hoping the Democractic party establishment can continue as usual, you don't get a say in what Comey does or doesn't do, and pointing the finger at Comey doesn't fix the democracts issues, it doesn't prepare you for 2020, its misdirection so that the powers that be don't get held to account, same for those who blame sexism, who blame Bern Bros, who blame everybody, but themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pointing out that these things can happen isn't placing blame or trying not to be held accountable. It's pointing out that these things happen so you need to have candidates who these things won't happen to.<br /> <br /> I also find this a strange stance for you to hold since most of your posts have blamed the left as if they were a unified force that had no opposition.<br /> <br /> There's any number of things that could have changed the state of the election, and it's safe to say that Comey's public announcement that 'for some reason the husband of Hillary Clinton's long-time aid had e-mails that related to Hillary Clinton', with the implied 'and this may lead to imprisonment,' was one of those things. Just like people thinking Trump would never be president and deciding not to vote. And just like Bill Clinton's affairs and marriage to Hillary Clinton.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T20:23:05-08:00","id":1005211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005197#post1005197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hillary should never have been vulnerible in the first place to it, any effect it had only did so, because she was such a weak nominee in the first place. <br /> <br /> And truth is is blaming it on that is a way to avoid being held to account by powerful democracts who are hoping the Democractic party establishment can continue as usual, you don't get a say in what Comey does or doesn't do, and pointing the finger at Comey doesn't fix the democracts issues, it doesn't prepare you for 2020, its misdirection so that the powers that be don't get held to account, same for those who blame sexism, who blame Bern Bros, who blame everybody, but themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess Comey shouldn't have made himself vulnerable by going against long standing policies at the FBI and the DoJ, and publicly announce a new investigation right before an election involving one of the candidates. And then have nothing to show for it. If he'd FOUND something he'd be a little vindicated... But no, false alarm. <br /> <br /> Ultimately, I don't care about Clinton's emails. I don't care she lost. I really do care about the FBI Director breaking his own bureaus policies in order to play partisan politics and make his entire agency suspect. <br /> <br /> His own Bureau is lividly furious with him. And on top of this, Director Comey tried to throw his own agents under the bus saying, &quot;The case was investigated by career FBI agents, so if I blew it, they blew it too.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T20:37:58-08:00","id":1005215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005168#post1005168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But this fantasy that Cis White Males lives are all roses, and that everyday is International Men's Day, and there are people who really do believe it, that attidude has to stop, its just drives people away.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not at all what the concept of privilege is about. And, granted, I'm sure there are <i>some</i> folks out there who actually hold this view, but they are definitely in the minority. Being white, cis, male, tall, thin, able-bodied, neurotypical, etc. etc. etc. by no means guarantees you will have a cushy life, and acknowledging the privilege inherent in those qualities is not meant to discount or downplay the struggles of anyone who have those privileges. It is merely meant to express that a person in otherwise identical circumstances without those privileges would face other and/or greater challenges, because of the systematic biases that still exist in favor of people who do have them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T21:27:14-08:00","id":1005230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005197#post1005197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hillary should never have been vulnerible in the first place to it, any effect it had only did so, because she was such a weak nominee in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no way to be not vulnerable to what happened. The FBI Director can tank any campaign they want by doing exactly what Comey did. That's why there's standing policy to not announce investigations 60 days before an election unless there is extremely compelling <b>evidence</b> (not just suspicion). No politician can actually stop the FBI from announcing an investigation in a politically damaging fashion. As this instance proved, the FBI doesn't have to have a solid case to make a stir.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that Trump and his campaign <b>were also being investigated</b> by the FBI because of the Russian hacks, and the only reason we know that is FBI members leaking it in disgust of Comey's hypocrisy. It makes Comey's actions doubly worse. He didn't just break protocol and announce things about Clinton, he didn't announce similar things about Trump.<br /> <br /> If you can't see how one of the top law enforcement agents in the country can sway an election by leaking information in a partisan manner, I'm not sure what we can say. <br /> <br /> Imagine two candidates. One is mired in minor political scandals. Nothing major by DC standards, but enough that it's turning people away. The other is apparently a saint. Nobody's gotten anything to stick. There's no skeletons in the closet. A miracle of politics. Then, a week before the election, the FBI announces that the seemingly saintly candidate is under investigation for 10 counts of child abuse. The day of the election the FBI quietly announces the child abuse investigation was crap and it was dropped. The saintly candidate loses by a tiny margin.<br /> <br /> Would seriously think that the FBI in this scenario didn't impact the election?<br /> <br /> If you accept that this can actually have an impact, why do you think it didn't have in impact this year?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...its misdirection so that the powers that be don't get held to account,... </div> </div> </div>You mean like Comey? If his actions get ignored - considering his immense power - he doesn't get held to account for his actions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...who blame everybody, but themselves. </div> </div> </div>First, I'll reiterate the inane nature of, &quot;we need to blame the liberals for losing to Trump instead of blaming the conservatives for allowing him to happen.&quot;<br /> <br /> And second, there's been plenty of self flagellation by the left. That you seem to pay no attention to it doesn't mean anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T21:32:36-08:00","id":1005234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005215#post1005215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not at all what the concept of privilege is about. And, granted, I'm sure there are <i>some</i> folks out there who actually hold this view, but they are definitely in the minority. Being white, cis, male, tall, thin, able-bodied, neurotypical, etc. etc. etc. by no means guarantees you will have a cushy life, and acknowledging the privilege inherent in those qualities is not meant to discount or downplay the struggles of anyone who have those privileges. It is merely meant to express that a person in otherwise identical circumstances without those privileges would face other and/or greater challenges, because of the systematic biases that still exist in favor of people who do have them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, while being a white man is nice, there are other factors that have a much bigger role in how people are treated - like money. The black child of a wealthy man who gets to attend the best private schools, has the money to attend an Ivy League School and such, is probably going to have more advantages and a better life than the son of a dirt poor white guy, who is born and raised in poverty.<br /> <br /> This was Bernie Sander's message, that the biggest issues facing Americans that make the playing field &quot;unfair&quot; tend to be economic issues rather than racial issues. Poor people get the shaft, regardless of their race. Yes, poor African-Americans and Latinos and women and gays get it worse than poor straight white men, but poor straight white men get it pretty bad too and ignoring their plight or talking down to them and dismissing it because of their race and sex is inherently unjust.<br /> <br /> Dealing with income inequality among African-Americans, trans people, closing the Female Wage Gap, etc would do a <i>lot</i> in providing them better lives, and would be a far easier and more realistic issue to try and tackle than attempting to end prejudice, discrimination and &quot;white privilege&quot; - especially since government attempts to &quot;force&quot; racial equality often end up with systems that themselves promote and hardcode racial discrimination.<br /> <br /> Sadly however the wealthy Democratic elites didn't want to listen to someone chiding them about how money was the biggest problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T22:09:16-08:00","id":1005241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005234#post1005234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is, while being a white man is nice, there are other factors that have a much bigger role in how people are treated - like money. The black child of a wealthy man who gets to attend the best private schools, has the money to attend an Ivy League School and such, is probably going to have more advantages and a better life than the son of a dirt poor white guy, who is born and raised in poverty.<br /> <br /> This was Bernie Sander's message, that the biggest issues facing Americans that make the playing field &amp;quot;unfair&amp;quot; tend to be economic issues rather than racial issues. Poor people get the shaft, regardless of their race. Yes, poor African-Americans and Latinos and women and gays get it worse than poor straight white men, but poor straight white men get it pretty bad too and ignoring their plight or talking down to them and dismissing it because of their race and sex is inherently unjust.<br /> <br /> Dealing with income inequality among African-Americans, trans people, closing the Female Wage Gap, etc would do a <i>lot</i> in providing them better lives, and would be a far easier and more realistic issue to try and tackle than attempting to end prejudice, discrimination and &amp;quot;white privilege&amp;quot; - especially since government attempts to &amp;quot;force&amp;quot; racial equality often end up with systems that themselves promote and hardcode racial discrimination.<br /> <br /> Sadly however the wealthy Democratic elites didn't want to listen to someone chiding them about how money was the biggest problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's like you didn't even read my post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T22:52:43-08:00","id":1005249,"title":"","content":"To give a more earnest, less qippy reply, you're basically agreeing with me. Note the part where I said &quot;in otherwise identical circumstances.&quot; That part is important. Of course a wealthy person of color is going to have advantages and an overall easier life compared to a white person living in poverty. That kinda goes without saying. However, a wealthy person of color is going to face challenges a wealthy white person will not, and a poor person of color is going to face challenges a poor white person will not. Having a particular type of privilege doesn't mean you're better off than everyone who doesn't have that privilege, it means all other things being equal, you're better off than you would be if you didn't have that privilege.<br /> <br /> Re: Bernie Sanders, yes, I agree that he had the right idea. I would much rather have him in the Whitehouse than Trump <i>or</i> Clinton, or anyone else who was on the ticket for that matter. But he wasn't on it. And yes, dealing with income inequality among the underprivileged is an important step towards overall equality. It really seems like we're on the same side, here.<br /> <br /> I really think a lot of folks on both sides of the fence want the same things, and the real issue is folks (on both sides) refusing to listen to each other. That's why it's frustrating to see anything that acknowledges the concept of privilege being dismissed as &quot;PC bullshit&quot;, because more often than not (based on my personal experience, of course), it isn't meant to shut anyone down, but it will if people assume it is and shut themselves down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T03:47:44-08:00","id":1005294,"title":"","content":"A wealthy person of colour is also going to face challenges that almost no white person will face, such as incidents in which they're implicitly assumed to be a criminal, and the higher likelihood of being killed if they should have any kind of altercation with police.<br /> <br /> \u200bThis is what we call &quot;intersectionality&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T06:35:20-08:00","id":1005328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005249#post1005249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To give a more earnest, less qippy reply, you're basically agreeing with me. Note the part where I said &quot;in otherwise identical circumstances.&quot; That part is important. Of course a wealthy person of color is going to have advantages and an overall easier life compared to a white person living in poverty. That kinda goes without saying. However, a wealthy person of color is going to face challenges a wealthy white person will not, and a poor person of color is going to face challenges a poor white person will not. Having a particular type of privilege doesn't mean you're better off than everyone who doesn't have that privilege, it means all other things being equal, you're better off than you would be if you didn't have that privilege.<br /> <br /> Re: Bernie Sanders, yes, I agree that he had the right idea. I would much rather have him in the Whitehouse than Trump <i>or</i> Clinton, or anyone else who was on the ticket for that matter. But he wasn't on it. And yes, dealing with income inequality among the underprivileged is an important step towards overall equality. It really seems like we're on the same side, here.<br /> <br /> I really think a lot of folks on both sides of the fence want the same things, and the real issue is folks (on both sides) refusing to listen to each other. That's why it's frustrating to see anything that acknowledges the concept of privilege being dismissed as &quot;PC bullshit&quot;, because more often than not (based on my personal experience, of course), it isn't meant to shut anyone down, but it will if people assume it is and shut themselves down.</div> </div> </div> </div> Bottom line is if you barely scrapping by and someone calls you privledged, that going to piss you off, you rationalize it all you want, but you'll lose their vote all the same.<br /> <br /> Instead of focusing on priveldge and turning whose more oppressed, which has only benifitted the right at this point as shown by President Trump, go back focusing on the common interest, accessible free education for everyone, good jobs, universal single payer healthcare, universal healthcare, universal dental care, BMI, peace internationally, support for Due Process and freedom of speech, rising all boats.<br /> <br /> All privledge talk did is make people feel exluded, and I've talked to tons of people who have made this clear to me, it adds nothing to the conversation by turning oppression in a contest, instead of focusing on prosperity and freedom for all.<br /> <br /> Look I know people who started along this line had good intentions, they wanted to help minorities who were falling behind and had suffered historically mistreatment by government and individuals, but it became corrupted and became bigotry.<br /> <br /> The left needs to go back to it roots of universality and focusing on our commonalities, instead of pointing out our differences. We have to go back to the Martin Luther King Jr, Tommy Douglas, and others.<br /> <br /> Now Tommy Douglas was real leadership.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/kdwySCMovHk\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/kdwySCMovHk\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/kdwySCMovHk\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/kdwySCMovHk </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> What the left has turned into is the mice pointing to each other and declaring each other to be privledged based on the colour of their fur and their gender, while the Cats in charge laugh and keep eating the mice. Some of Cats have black fur, some has white fur, some are male, some are female, some are trans, but at the end of the day, they're still Cats!<br /> <br /> And the mice have different colours of fur, genders ect..., too, but their still all mice!<br /> <br /> All the infighting amoung mice does is make it easier for cats to catch them and eat them!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 11-19-2016, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T06:42:57-08:00","id":1005333,"title":"","content":"Anyone noticed that the Trumpites stole the term working class while the left wasn't looking.<br /> <br /> For a while working class was the word no one would say, you said middle class, but now Trumpites have actually started using the term again and people like it.<br /> <br /> They took the ground the leftwing had conceded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T07:52:02-08:00","id":1005347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005328#post1005328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bottom line is if you barely scrapping by and someone calls you privledged, that going to piss you off, you rationalize it all you want, but you'll lose their vote all the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>People aren't voting for me, and Hillary Clinton didn't go around telling people they were privileged.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005328#post1005328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of focusing on priveldge and turning whose more oppressed, which has only benifitted the right at this point as shown by President Trump, go back focusing on the common interest, accessible free education for everyone, good jobs, universal single payer healthcare, universal healthcare, universal dental care, BMI, peace internationally, support for Due Process and freedom of speech, rising all boats.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, acknowledging privilege isn't about who's more oppressed, it's about shining a light on the fact that, despite the progress civil rights has made, inequality is still alive and well, and shifting the focus from individuals to systems. Second of all, we didn't stop focusing on accessible education, jobs, health and dental care, BMI, international relations, due process, or freedom of speech. Just because we're also talking about the elephant in the room, institutionalized bias, doesn't mean we still don't want to raise the quality of life for everyone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005328#post1005328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All privledge talk did is make people feel exluded, and I've talked to tons of people who have made this clear to me, it adds nothing to the conversation by turning oppression in a contest, instead of focusing on prosperity and freedom for all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, it's not an oppression contest, it's the logical next step of civil rights. Great, so we've gotten to the point where people aren't segregated based on race, and overt expressions of biggotry are socially frowned upon (sometimes. Other times it gets you elected president, I guess). That doesn't mean we're done and everyone is equal, it just means the conversation needs to move on from individuals to systems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005328#post1005328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look I know people who started along this line had good intentions, they wanted to help minorities who were falling behind and had suffered historically mistreatment by government and individuals, but it became corrupted and became bigotry.<br /> <br /> The left needs to go back to it roots of universality and focusing on our commonalities, instead of pointing out our differences.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing &quot;pointing out our differences&quot; is bigotry to your mind. The thing is, we need to acknowledge that being different still puts you at a disadvantage in our society, and to do that we need to acknowledge that there are differences. The systems in place don't treat everyone equally, so trying to pretend we're all the same just hides those inequalities. If we want people to be equal, we need to address the standing inequalities, and in order to do that, we need to acknowledge that we do have differences and that those differences are still causes of inequality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T10:40:53-08:00","id":1005405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005241#post1005241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To give a more earnest, less qippy reply, you're basically agreeing with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Err, well yes, I <i>was</i> agreeing with you. I was making a comment based on what you said earlier not trying to actually argue with you.<br /> <br /> I think income inequality is the bigger source of problems among minority communities (and among white communities) than race, and tackling income inequality would have a much larger, much more profound and much more immediate effect on minority communities than any sort of campaign to &quot;end racism.&quot;<br /> <br /> Unfortunately in the Democratic Party has always been more interested in race baiting to various degrees, and you can't blame them for that. It's a subject that gets passions up and gets people to the polls to vote. Income inequality is a more cerebral issue that doesn't get people as emotionally invested in it as problems revolving around race or sex (and the Republican Party has always race baited in its own ways as well).<br /> <br /> Plus at the time of the Primary races, race was dominating the headlines - as an example, look at the Black Lives Matter movement. Many members very publicly hijacked the stage from Democratic candidates (and Republicans to a degree) demanding they say &quot;Black Lives Matter,&quot; and hurling insults at anyone who suggested that, &quot;All Lives Matter.&quot;<br /> <br /> Unfortunately the BLM movement largely flamed out because being so based around race meant that it was incapable of making inroads to members of other communities (as well as being a leaderless movement and so not having anyone with the power or authority to disavow people who do dumb stuff like riot and loot). But not being able to make inroads with other communities was a big, big problem that BLM has never been able to overcome.<br /> <br /> As an example, I live in a predominantly Hispanic part of the country with very few African-Americans. Black Lives Matter had almost zero effect here - the one rally that BLM tried to hold was largely overwhelmed by Hispanic counter-protesters.<br /> <br /> Many Hispanics (in this area at least) felt &quot;Black Lives Matter&quot; meant that Hispanic lives <i>didn't</i> matter - that BLM wasn't interested in what happened to Hispanics. Which is funny because Hispanics often face the same sort of racial problems from police officers. Hispanics should have been flocking to the movement. And yet, because BLM was a black racial movement rather than a movement around police corruption, Black Lives Matter was never able to form the multi-ethnic coalition that it really needed in order to be a success.<br /> <br /> Whites and Latinos and Asians and others who said, &quot;Yeah, Black lives matter, but <i>our</i> lives matter too,&quot; were largely met with jeers and accusations of racism from Black Lives Matter. And unfortunately due to that, the BLM movement came across to many whites as less of an anti-police corruption movement and more of an &quot;anti-white&quot; movement.<br /> <br /> This was just another example, like various PC issues, white privilege, etc, that helped set the stage for the 2016 election a stage on which many white people in America feel like they were under attack because of their race.<br /> <br /> And that also helped set the stage for why many people on the left weren't terribly interested in Bernie's message - that income inequality was a bigger, easier to solve issue that would help people a lot more than yelling about race.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T11:36:25-08:00","id":1005416,"title":"","content":"I'm afraid at the moment I cannot parse everything you've said in that post, but I feel as though it's worth noting that Black Lives Matter doesn't strike me as some kind of zero-sum challenge so much as it is an affirmation in the face of how many cases there have been in which African-Americans were murdered by police.<br /> <br /> Not a case of &quot;our lives matter and yours don't&quot; so much as &quot;our lives matter, so the fact that you keep on ending them is disgusting&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T12:13:30-08:00","id":1005427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005416#post1005416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm afraid at the moment I cannot parse everything you've said in that post, but I feel as though it's worth noting that Black Lives Matter doesn't strike me as some kind of zero-sum challenge so much as it is an affirmation in the face of how many cases there have been in which African-Americans were murdered by police.<br /> <br /> Not a case of &quot;our lives matter and yours don't&quot; so much as &quot;our lives matter, so the fact that you keep on ending them is disgusting&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the intent, though to be fair, it does come across as zero sum to a lot of its detractors. It is extremely frustrating to see people who feel such a strong need to be reassured that Black Lives Matter isn't implying that their lives matter less, that they're willing to oppose the name solely on the basis of its name not including them. Like, yes, of course all lives matter. BLM isn't meant to imply that they don't. The fact that all lives matter should be a given, but yet the police force doesn't seem to have much regard for the lives of black people, which is why the movement used a name that emphasized that inequality.<br /> <br /> Sometimes I wonder if it would have more support if it was called &quot;Black Lives Matter <i>Too</i>.&quot; And then I get pissed off because the name of the movement is such a stupid, petty reason for people to oppose it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-19-2016, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T12:22:05-08:00","id":1005432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005416#post1005416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm afraid at the moment I cannot parse everything you've said in that post, but I feel as though it's worth noting that Black Lives Matter doesn't strike me as some kind of zero-sum challenge so much as it is an affirmation in the face of how many cases there have been in which African-Americans were murdered by police.<br /> <br /> Not a case of &quot;our lives matter and yours don't&quot; so much as &quot;our lives matter, so the fact that you keep on ending them is disgusting&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is kind of the point - who is the &quot;you&quot; in your statement that is ending lives? Police? Or white people? I mean, <i>I</i> know what you're saying and that you intended to focus on the police of course.<br /> <br /> But for many Americans, that's what it felt like - that BLM was not an &quot;Americans united against police brutality&quot; movement but rather a black vs white movement. A lot of whites felt unfairly attacked, feeling like they were being blamed for the murders of African-Americans by police, murders which they had nothing to do with beyond the fact that they happened to (sometimes) share the same skin color as the police officer.<br /> <br /> And then other minority groups, also viewing it as a black vs white conversation, often felt completely excluded altogether. Which is unfortunate because other minority groups like Latinos and Native Americans often face very similar problems with the police that African-Americans do. But many members of those minorities didn't feel welcomed in the BLM movement because they weren't black.<br /> <br /> Black Lives Matter made a good rallying cry, but it was largely an <i>exclusive</i> cry rather than an inclusive one and it felt like a cry specifically directed at white people and one that ignored everyone who wasn't black or white.<br /> <br /> A lot of that ultimately (to go back to an earlier post I made) has to do with the way that things like white privilege or the BLM movement, which have important ideas, are instead used to sometimes <i>attack</i> white people, or used as reasons to exclude white people from the conversation, rather than as ways to get them on board and get them to help fix the problem.<br /> <br /> That makes white people feel like they're unfairly under attack because of their skin color and that helped form the environment in which Donald Trump ran - an environment in which many white people felt that they were being unfairly demonized and blamed for problems solely because they were white.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 11-19-2016, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T12:26:01-08:00","id":1005434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005432#post1005432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of that ultimately (to go back to an earlier post I made) has to do with the way that things like white privilege or the BLM movement, which have important ideas, are instead used to sometimes <i>attack</i> white people, or used as reasons to exclude white people from the conversation, rather than as ways to get them on board and get them to help fix the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we rejected every idea that sometimes gets used to attack or exclude people, we would never accept any ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T12:33:05-08:00","id":1005439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005434#post1005434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we rejected every idea that sometimes gets used to attack or exclude people, we would never accept any ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but demanding that people simply deal with it and accept being attacked because of their skin color is also clearly a non-starter.<br /> <br /> The reality is, if you want to have social movements and changes, you need to get the majority of the population in on your side. And if people feel like you're attacking and demonizing them because of traits they have no control over, they're probably not going to be very interested in helping out.<br /> <br /> Too many white people have been attacked because of these ideas (we have several people in this thread talking about how &quot;white privilege&quot; was used to shut them down). It shouldn't be a surprise when they say, &quot;Hey, I don't really appreciate that, and I'm not going to help you attack me.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T12:41:22-08:00","id":1005444,"title":"","content":"<b>race baiting</b> \u200e(uncountable) The act of using racially derisive language, actions, or other forms of communication in order to anger or intimidate or coerce.<br /> <br /> With regards to the use of the term Race-baiting. I'm going to call bullshit on the claim that Democrats use it more than Republicans, that is a self serving conservative myth. I won't say Democrats don't use it as a tactic because that would be equally false, but the Democrats didn't run a campaign attacking racial groups as criminals that we needed to build a wall against. The Democrats did not run a campaign against lawlessness being perpetrated by members of a particular racial group. When Trump is running a campaign against illegal aliens people surely aren't thinking of the Europeans who overstay their visas and find off the books work in the US. They aren't thinking of models that come on a tourist visa and then stay to do fashion shoots they don't have work visas for. They certainly aren't thinking of the 50k Irish who have moved to the US without following our immigration laws. They are looking squarely at Latinos and Hispanics because that's who their candidate said is causing the problems they face. That's race-baiting. Pointing out a particular racial group has advantages over another? Stating that one racial group, as a matter of historical record, mistreated practically every other racial group it has come in contact with? Still not race baiting. Trying to influence people to act out of anger towards people of the previously mentioned group? OK, that is race baiting. I'd like to see people actually understand terms before they start throwing them around so casually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 11-19-2016, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T12:52:04-08:00","id":1005446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005432#post1005432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is kind of the point - who is the &quot;you&quot; in your statement that is ending lives? Police? Or white people? I mean, <i>I</i> know what you're saying and that you intended to focus on the police of course.<br /> <br /> But for many Americans, that's what it felt like - that BLM was not an &quot;Americans united against police brutality&quot; movement but rather a black vs white movement. A lot of whites felt unfairly attacked, feeling like they were being blamed for the murders of African-Americans by police, murders which they had nothing to do with beyond the fact that they happened to (sometimes) share the same skin color as the police officer.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAnd who started that narrative that it was Black vs White rather than Blacks vs an abuse of police power that disproportionately affected them? The same people who were pushing the idea that Obama was a divisive, race baiting, Kenyan born Muslim socialist. The same news sources that claim every year Starbucks is leading the war against Christmas because of their coffee cup designs. The same people who claim if we just had a more homogenous society that followed the same religion (conveniently, the one they follow) everything would be A-O-fucking K. The same people who have created a false victimhood narrative, a narrative that they are somehow the ones being oppressed when there isn't a shred of actual aggregate evidence to support their claims. The people who believe that civil rights are a zero sum game where they somehow lose rights when someone else's rights are affirmed. Yeah, fuck those guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T13:21:41-08:00","id":1005453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005439#post1005439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but demanding that people simply deal with it and accept being attacked because of their skin color is also clearly a non-starter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did I ever say people should accept being attacked because of their skin color? No. What I said was, Black Lives Matter, both as a movement and as a statement, is not an attack against anyone. Some people who support the movement have attacked people because of their skin color, just like literally every movement ever. That doesn't mean the movement as a whole should be rejected, any more than it means people should have to put up with being attacked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005439#post1005439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reality is, if you want to have social movements and changes, you need to get the majority of the population in on your side. And if people feel like you're attacking and demonizing them because of traits they have no control over, they're probably not going to be very interested in helping out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure would be nice if &quot;the majority of the population&quot; didn't feel like they were being attacked and demonized by the statement that the lives of people in the minority matter. Like, does &quot;the majority of the population&quot; need to be coddled and constantly reassured that they matter too, despite already being in the majority? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005439#post1005439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Too many white people have been attacked because of these ideas (we have several people in this thread talking about how &quot;white privilege&quot; was used to shut them down). It shouldn't be a surprise when they say, &quot;Hey, I don't really appreciate that, and I'm not going to help you attack me.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, when so many people seem to take statements that support a group that they don't belong to as attacks against the group(s) they do belong to, I can't help but wonder how much of people who have had &quot;White priveledge&quot; used to shut them down might be reading more into it than what was actually said. I'm willing to give folks the benefit of the doubt that they have indeed been attacked and shut down on the basis of privilege, but that isn't what the concept is <i>about</i>, and we shouldn't blame the concept for people misusing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-19-2016, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T13:44:56-08:00","id":1005465,"title":"","content":"Your right that republicans race bait more, at least rescently, but as the writer said, if you play the identity politics, be prepared to lose. Then is not a field the left has the advantage on, its won some battles and many got stupid about it.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying you don't fight for equality, absolutely everyone should, I'm just saying do it in a way that is more inclusive, a way that is smarter and listen to people outside of the leftwing bubble.<br /> <br /> And your right that she didn't say priveldge, it was in what she didn't say were it was implied, were she mentioned every group GLBT, African Anericans, ect..., but she often left out Men, Whites, Cis.<br /> <br /> In previous years that wouldn't mattered, but many on the left have reminded people that they are white, male, cis at every opportunity. You really should read the New York Times article I posted.<br /> <br /> I mean until rescently Cis wasn't even a thing to people, you'd call someone who is Cis and they'd look at you in confusion. Now its an identity manufactured by the left. I don't know why none trans people needed a name honestly, while I am Cis, it was just background noise to me, but after all the fingers pointed at me calling me Cis, you start to emerge as an identity, even if you don't want it too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T14:32:50-08:00","id":1005481,"title":"","content":"Cis literally means not trans. It's Latin. The same prefixes are used are used in organic chemistry too, to describe geometric isonomism. The reason a term is needed for describing people who are not trans is so the language doesn't alienate trans people. The alternative is calling non-trans people &quot;normal&quot;, which implies that trans people are abnormal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T14:41:08-08:00","id":1005483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005465#post1005465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean until rescently Cis wasn't even a thing to people, you'd call someone who is Cis and they'd look at you in confusion. Now its an identity manufactured by the left. I don't know why none trans people needed a name honestly, while I am Cis, it was just background noise to me, but after all the fingers pointed at me calling me Cis, you start to emerge as an identity, even if you don't want it too.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only places I've ever seen it being used are here and the rpgnet forums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T15:01:59-08:00","id":1005488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005481#post1005481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cis literally means not trans. It's Latin. The same prefixes are used are used in organic chemistry too, to describe geometric isonomism. The reason a term is needed for describing people who are not trans is so the language doesn't alienate trans people. The alternative is calling non-trans people &amp;quot;normal&amp;quot;, which implies that trans people are abnormal.</div> </div> </div> </div> I get that, my point is not that Cis isn't a state of being, its that Cis wasn't an identity before, it did not emerge as an identity naturally like trans, few if anyone felt the need to identitfy as Cis, but the left picked the name, and started hurling it like an insult, and in general making it a thing, until people started identitfying as Cis, and when they started to see themselves like that, and seeing people vilifying said group for being Cis, well that won't go well for the left and I'd argue its not going well for the Trans community either.<br /> <br /> In practice whatever the theory might say, intersectionalism has been a disaster for the left.<br /> <br /> Trust me, as an MRA we've benifited from all the people alienated by current leftwing politics (although at the cost for those of us on the MRA left who have been isolated from the rest of the left and demonized and falsely accused of hating women and all sorts of hienous conduct that wasn't true, like being associated with the KKK who disgust me and who I think are morons).<br /> <br /> In fact if you asked me if I would become an MRA 2 years ago, I'd have been insulted and said no fucking way, not a chance in hell.<br /> <br /> I was pushed away towards the MRA by the conduct of the left, time and again. And I've heard this from lefties and centre lefties again and again and again, who end up MRA or other dissentent groups over it.<br /> <br /> This helped create fertile ground for Trump.<br /> <br /> And yes by itself it wouldn't be enough, but on top of it you have Hillary who should never have been chosen, a bad campaign, and Trump who promised to stop the TPP, which the left failed to do, amoung other elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T17:45:38-08:00","id":1005522,"title":"","content":"I feel as though &quot;this wasn't a thing that was apparent to me as a distinction before&quot; is often what the word privilege refers to.<br /> <br /> \u200bI don't think it's about making people feel bad about something (by which I mean, that is my personal stance on my priorities in communication; <u>I</u> do not intrinsically seek to make anybody feel about something), I think it's about emphasizing awareness of differences between people, and how certain of those differences have a lot of terrible things directed at them.<br /> <br /> \u200bI recognize myself as cisgendered to condition myself to normalize awareness of transgendered people, as well as to understand and articulate the fact that being transgendered carries with it a whole host of struggles that I will never personally experience or feel. I utilize the term to rebuild myself as seeing people in terms of an eclectic collection and a spectrum, rather than a default and all of the ways something deviates from it.<br /> <br /> \u200bI, personally, won't attack people from certain sections of society that have more benefits, but I will at least have a measure of disdain for people who get pissy and defensive about these things being pointed out to them and being emphatic over how the discourse needs to be carefully constructed to not step on any of their toes.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut perhaps I'm biased; my own experience is that when people have been rather stark about things that have hurt them, I have had cause to look upon my own personality and past and find things resembling those complaints, that I judge to be shortcomings. Not even as things people have said directly to me or pointed out about me (although those are things that have happened more recently); it was just enough to hear that this was a thing, and to recognise that thing in myself, and for knowing what it did to people being the motivation to try and make it less of a thing in myself.<br /> <br /> \u200bI value having my toes stepped on, because I know from experience that I wouldn't know somebody was standing there otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T17:53:49-08:00","id":1005523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.buzzfeed.com/lesterfeder/this-is-how-steve-bannon-sees-the-entire-world?utm_term=.rbDeGZLzE#.hsyOBb3vZ\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://img.buzzfeed.com/buzzfeed-static/static/2016-11/15/15/asset/buzzfeed-prod-fastlane01/sub-buzz-25776-1479240882-1.jpg?crop=1600:1062;0,0&amp;resize=1250:830\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.buzzfeed.com/lesterfeder/this-is-how-steve-bannon-sees-the-entire-world?utm_term=.rbDeGZLzE#.hsyOBb3vZ\" target=\"_blank\"> This Is How Steve Bannon Sees The Entire World </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.buzzfeed.com/lesterfeder/this-is-how-steve-bannon-sees-the-entire-world?utm_term=.rbDeGZLzE#.hsyOBb3vZ\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.buzzfeed.com/lesterfeder/this-is-how-steve-bannon-sees-the-entire-world?utm_term=.rbDeGZLzE#.hsyOBb3vZ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The soon-to-be White House chief strategist laid out a global vision in a rare 2014 talk where he said racism in the far right gets &ldquo;washed out&rdquo; and called Vladimir Putin a kleptocrat. BuzzFeed News publishes the complete transcript for the first time. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I have deep concerns about Bannon, but I'd love to see the Trump administration go after the Banksters who were responsible for the fincial crisis and will likely cause the next one if their not stopped, put those fuckers in jail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T19:16:53-08:00","id":1005541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005488#post1005488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get that, my point is not that Cis isn't a state of being, its that Cis wasn't an identity before,...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not having a name doesn't mean it wasn't an identity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (although at the cost for those of us on the MRA left who have been isolated from the rest of the left and demonized and falsely accused of hating women and all sorts of hienous conduct that wasn't true, like being associated with the KKK who disgust me and who I think are morons). </div> </div> </div>I hope you can recognize the astounding mental loops it takes to simultaneous by saying at movements like BLM are to blame for the negative feelings they inspire in others based on something as superficial as a slogan, but then also blaming other people for not respecting a movement you belong to due its PR nightmare of members that frequently engage in online harassment campaigns, doxxing, ruining people's careers, rape threats, and death threats.<br /> <br /> It really just says, &quot;the fault is always with whoever disagrees with me,&quot; rather than any willingness to get into the whys and hows of all this stuff; let alone what to do about any of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ....the TPP, which the left failed to do,... </div> </div> </div>Um, the left did promise to not to the TPP, so I don't see how they &quot;failed&quot; to do that. Even if Clinton's attempt to thread the needle didn't sit well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 11-19-2016, 10:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T19:39:37-08:00","id":1005547,"title":"","content":"I am just going to note something that has nothing to do with the ongoing conversation - Trump is a media genius. He knows how to lead the press by the nose to the point that it's ridiculous. Two tweets about Pence at the Hamilton play and the much more important story about Trump University setting the fraud lawsuit for 25 million just falls off the front page. You'd think by now the press would have wised up to how he does things, causing a little stink to bury a much larger pile of shit, but they just keep falling for it time and time again.<br /> <br /> This is what we have to look forward to for the next 4 years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T20:46:02-08:00","id":1005570,"title":"","content":"I've seen a few people comment about that. The question for the media is what the story is going to be Monday, and if the story either goes back to Trump U, or even starts to be &quot;Tweets tried to distract us from Trump U lawsuit,&quot; after the weekend is over and regular news restarts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T22:24:37-08:00","id":1005602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005230#post1005230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's no way to be not vulnerable to what happened. The FBI Director can tank any campaign they want by doing exactly what Comey did. That's why there's standing policy to not announce investigations 60 days before an election unless there is extremely compelling <b>evidence</b> (not just suspicion). No politician can actually stop the FBI from announcing an investigation in a politically damaging fashion. As this instance proved, the FBI doesn't have to have a solid case to make a stir.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that Trump and his campaign <b>were also being investigated</b> by the FBI because of the Russian hacks, and the only reason we know that is FBI members leaking it in disgust of Comey's hypocrisy. It makes Comey's actions doubly worse. He didn't just break protocol and announce things about Clinton, he didn't announce similar things about Trump.<br /> <br /> If you can't see how one of the top law enforcement agents in the country can sway an election by leaking information in a partisan manner, I'm not sure what we can say.<br /> <br /> <br /> You mean like Comey? If his actions get ignored - considering his immense power - he doesn't get held to account for his actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>To add some potential information to this. <br /> <br /> Now this is all federal scuttlebutt, and its unlikely to ever be confirmed on the record, so people are free to believe or not believe it as they will. <br /> <br /> The Bureau's New York office has a great deal of autonomy, and they like to stick it to DC pretty much whenever possible. It's leadership is also deeply conservative, even moreso than the rest of the already pretty red-skewing Bureau. They're also a pretty much a sieve of information where Rudy Giuliani is concerned. Most of the leaks about the investigation exploited by the Trump campaign flowed through that channel. Comey's announcement was an attempt to get out ahead of the information before the NY office inevitably handed it to Giuliani, Trump, and the media. It didn't make the whole situation any better, but it wasn't deliberate malfeasance on Comey's part. The reason why the investigation of the Trump-Russia connection wasn't broadcast more is because people mostly observed proper protocol surrounding it and didn't break the rules just because other people did. <br /> <br /> Had Trump not won there was a good chance that NY was going to get a house cleaning. Since he did though they suddenly have friends in high places and they're likely going to stay right where they are. The Trump-Russia investigation is (again: scuttlebutt) still ongoing and being taken very, <i>very</i> seriously. Problem is with the AG being who he's going to be who the hell knows if they'd move forward with legal action even if the Bureau turns up a smoking gun. <br /> <br /> I'd personally put good odds that Comey will be forced to resign, not for putting his finger on the election, but for <i>not</i> leading a witch hunt the way the Trump clique wanted him to.<br /> <br /> Comey's gone from hero to villain to hero to villain so many times over the last year depending on your political persuasion that I'm amazed the man doesn't have whiplash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T22:47:22-08:00","id":1005609,"title":"","content":"I still think there is deliberate malfeasance on Comey's part. Even if the NY branch leaked that those emails were found and Comey stayed quiet, it would be the NY branch that broke policy and should be investigated under the Hatch Act. Comey would have some congresscritters accusing him of not bringing it up, but Comey could point to the policy not to publicly talk about investigations 60 days before an election as support of why he did what he did.<br /> <br /> Honestly, Comey was going to have politicians angry at him no matter what he did. But when the time came to choose how he's going to do his job, he chose very poorly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T23:54:44-08:00","id":1005626,"title":"","content":"Comey's actions are additionally of odd suspicion considering his testimony regarding the initial email investigation. He gave a lot of loaded answers (and mostly speculation) in response to leading questions that were instantly turned into anti-Clinton ads. They lost a lot of influence because of how far ahead of the election they were, but were already questionable.<br /> <br /> He also had a lot of time after the initial email investigation to start up some serious in-house cleaning before late October, instead the FBI's notoriously opaque unity in the face of anyone wanting any information out of them has fallen to factions within the Bureau that have turned it into a warring political machine leaking and counter leaking. This is a horrible thing for country. It doesn't matter who won the election or not.<br /> <br /> What's worse, is that Comey's revolving door of villain/hero stems from what was until this point an almost unshakeable record on ethics. He had repeatedly made enemies by putting ethics over politics. He got where he did by doing the exact opposite of getting dragged into this sort of mess by sticking to the ethics despite any political hot water he might get in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T10:00:17-08:00","id":1005743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005541#post1005541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not having a name doesn't mean it wasn't an identity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I hope you can recognize the astounding mental loops it takes to simultaneous by saying at movements like BLM are to blame for the negative feelings they inspire in others based on something as superficial as a slogan, but then also blaming other people for not respecting a movement you belong to due its PR nightmare of members that frequently engage in online harassment campaigns, doxxing, ruining people's careers, rape threats, and death threats.<br /> <br /> It really just says, &amp;quot;the fault is always with whoever disagrees with me,&amp;quot; rather than any willingness to get into the whys and hows of all this stuff; let alone what to do about any of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Um, the left did promise to not to the TPP, so I don't see how they &amp;quot;failed&amp;quot; to do that. Even if Clinton's attempt to thread the needle didn't sit well.</div> </div> </div> </div> I have no problem with BLM slogan, I actually supported BLM at first, unarmed people shouldn't be shot, but I didn't care for their methods, going after Bernie Sanders and the Toronto Gay Pride Parade was just stupid and there has been alot of obnxuous behavior.<br /> <br /> If you want create positive change they should have asked themselves what policies, police training, tools, ect... would lead to a more positive outcome, which is less people shot by police.<br /> <br /> Example instead of fucking with Gay Pride, they could go and start pushing police to have body cameras, which has been shown to encourage better behavior and more conscious behavior, which would help lead to fewer killings, better police conduct, and would protect police from false accusations misconduct. Everybody wins, public safety increased.<br /> <br /> I don't want innocent black people shot (or white or asian, ect... for that matter), I'm not a monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T10:07:22-08:00","id":1005745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/4VYo8mxGGUQ\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/4VYo8mxGGUQ\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/4VYo8mxGGUQ\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/4VYo8mxGGUQ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think the cast of Hamilton expressed themselves civilly, and Trumps whining over such a mild rebuke of his VP is pathetic.<br /> <br /> If anyone should apologize it should be Pence, to the people of Indiana. He was a horrible governor, homophobic, wasted tax payers dollars on quakery, ect...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T10:33:46-08:00","id":1005753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005743#post1005743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Example instead of fucking with Gay Pride, they could go and start pushing police to have body cameras, which has been shown to encourage better behavior and more conscious behavior, which would help lead to fewer killings, better police conduct, and would protect police from false accusations misconduct. Everybody wins, public safety increased.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say that like BLM <i>didnt</i> make a push for police body cameras.<br /> <br /> People do know it's possible to advocate for more than one thing at a time, right? I keep seeing comments like &quot;SJWs should be supporting closing the income gap instead of focusing on intersectionality&quot; and &quot;BLM should be pushing for police body cams instead of protesting at large public events&quot; and I'm just like...<br /> <img src=\"https://i.kinja-img.com/gawker-media/image/upload/s--sXmOrBZL--/c_fit,fl_progressive,q_80,w_636/1238895886504840879.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T12:07:25-08:00","id":1005791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005743#post1005743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want innocent black people shot (or white or asian, ect... for that matter), I'm not a monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if you feel the need to say this, then you weren't actually listening to what I was saying. I made no statements regarding the positions of either BLM or MRAs. I was speaking solely about your criticisms of BLM being hypocritical compared to your upset at how you've been treated as someone that openly identifies as a MRA.<br /> <br /> And as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> has already covered, you're rather incorrect about BLM not advocating for policy positions. The issue is that BLM is not, ultimately, about policy rather than community organization and awareness building (both internally getting different demographics of black Americans to be more aware and accepting each other, and externally of getting recognition of how the forced conditions plaguing the black communities are both horrible for their own lives but fixing them also elevates everyone).<br /> <br /> BLM isn't just about not getting shot by police, which is why they're not focused on specific police oriented policy positions (and most would point out that a few shooting after body-cams started becoming more common just resulted in the body-cams managing to be off for the key moments they should have captured, so their focus on larger social issues is more important than these sorts of measures in the long term).<br /> <br /> One example of this - that does have a policy component but it extends too far to sum up with nice little changes like body-cams - is the BLM focus on changing the American model of focusing on individual families in policy while failing to recognize the centrality of &quot;the village&quot; of interlocking local community support that minorities and poor families rely on. They argue that policy failures to include minority/poor villages and hinge everything on the 50s era concept of the nuclear family as part of how to address problems in those communities is a large contributor to the continuation of the status quo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T16:24:13-08:00","id":1005898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005743#post1005743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have no problem with BLM slogan, I actually supported BLM at first, unarmed people shouldn't be shot, but I didn't care for their methods, going after Bernie Sanders and the Toronto Gay Pride Parade was just stupid and there has been alot of obnxuous behavior.<br /> <br /> If you want create positive change they should have asked themselves what policies, police training, tools, ect... would lead to a more positive outcome, which is less people shot by police.<br /> <br /> Example instead of fucking with Gay Pride, they could go and start pushing police to have body cameras, which has been shown to encourage better behavior and more conscious behavior, which would help lead to fewer killings, better police conduct, and would protect police from false accusations misconduct. Everybody wins, public safety increased.<br /> <br /> I don't want innocent black people shot (or white or asian, ect... for that matter), I'm not a monster.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have no problem with what most of BLM stands for, including the way they usually go about fighting for those things. I do believe there are a small number of idiots that pretend to be BLM activists, when in reality they are nothing of the sort and simply sully the BLM name. This was especially true at the beginning of the year when there were a number of violence attributed to BLM; which in no way should be the case.<br /> <br /> Bad seeds in every garden. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T16:58:16-08:00","id":1005905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005898#post1005898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have no problem with what most of BLM stands for, including the way they usually go about fighting for those things. I do believe there are a small number of idiots that pretend to be BLM activists, when in reality they are nothing of the sort and simply sully the BLM name. This was especially true at the beginning of the year when there were a number of violence attributed to BLM; which in no way should be the case.<br /> <br /> Bad seeds in every garden.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I really feel for a lot of people involved in the Black Lives Matter movement. There is a very real and legitimate problem that exists and desperately needs to be corrected and a large part of that problem is the relationship Police Departments have with the communities they serve.<br /> <br /> But what is said and what is done can be very different. And you cannot separate out the activists you like as being BLM activists and activists you don't like as not being BLM activists.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.buzzfeed.com/laurenstrapagiel/black-lives-matters-pride-toronto?utm_term=.jl2Z58G7N9#.grAGZ12ENM\" target=\"_blank\">Here's an interesting article.</a> It's about how and why the Black Lives Matter Toronto Chapter was named Pride Toronto's honored group of 2016 and invited to participate in the parade. And during the Pride Parade, the BLM blocked the Pride Parade from continuing until Pride's leadership accepted their demands, one of those demands being &quot;Removal of all police floats/booths in all pride marches/parades/community spaces.&quot; There were other demands, with legitimate concerns.<br /> <br /> I have a really big problem with banning the police from participating in Pride parades. The inclusion of the police is meant to better knit the LGBTQ community with the police community, so that officers better know these people. To provide better understanding, to improve the community relationship and to just better get along. And I think this tactic really works.<br /> <br /> And the BLM Toronto Chapter was honored and invited to the Pride Parade, and then they protested the Pride Parade to exclude the police from it.<br /> <br /> I don't think these actions will have the results they want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T17:58:07-08:00","id":1005922,"title":"","content":"BLM is a mass, leaderless movement. Anybody can say they're part of BLM and claim that any actions or statements they make speak for BLM. The organization only has a few vague talking points and goals - and even those are not accepted by everyone. BLM specifically went with a leaderless movement to prevent the &quot;usual&quot; African-American authority figures (like Rev. Jessie Jackson) from trying to usurp control of the movement, as well to reduce the possibility of the leaders of such a movement being discredited (which is historically something that has often happened to the leadership of black protest movements in the United States).<br /> <br /> So it's not like that decision was, in and of itself a bad one. In fact, it's entirely understandable.<br /> <br /> On the other hand however, the big problem is that without actual leaders, there isn't anyone who has the authority to disavow assholes from the Black Lives Matter movement. You can end up having BLM protesters hijack gay Pride Parades or politician's stump speeches or causing riots, which doesn't get anybody on your side - it just makes the public think <i>everyone</i> in your movement is a jerk. And there isn't anyone with the power to correct that perception and make an official statement to say, &quot;Those people don't represent the values of Black Lives Matter and we categorically reject them and their actions.&quot;<br /> <br /> In a way, it's not too different from the early Tea Party movement, where anybody could make a sign or get up and say whatever and claim they represented the Tea Party movement. So you had a lot of white nationalist racists latching onto the movement, and nobody was able to kick those guys out or disavow what they said. But the Tea Party eventually began nominating leaders who drew up plans and ideas and started getting specific people (often those leaders) elected to carry the Tea Party's message to Washington, and those leaders tended to (at least publicly) criticize some of the more vocal and disgusting racial supremacists who claimed to be part of the Tea Party.<br /> <br /> Black Lives Matter hasn't really done anything like that yet. They have succeeded at getting the American public <i>aware</i> of the issue, and they have managed to make some small headway in certain segments of America where African-American communities have a lot of power. But outside of those few enclaves there hasn't really been very many broad social changes and indeed, in many parts of the country you hear, &quot;Blue Lives Matter&quot; more often than &quot;Black Lives Matter,&quot; and for many people the when they think of the BLM movement they think of the Baltimore riots.<br /> <br /> Hopefully Black Lives Matter gets its shit together because I think systematic racial abuses against all minorities by the police are a serious issue that absolutely needs to get addressed <u><b>now</b></u>, not later, and for the time being BLM is the only major movement that has any real shot of being able to do so. But if there aren't some fundamental changes in how BLM operates, I imagine most people in the movement will eventually grow bored and disillusioned by the lack of results and BLM will implode, just like the Occupy movement did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 11-20-2016, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T01:18:00-08:00","id":1006053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005547#post1005547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am just going to note something that has nothing to do with the ongoing conversation - Trump is a media genius...</div> </div> </div> </div>Um... or just has good timing. Sorry but I saw the debates. He looked like a complete idiot. Clinton played him like a fiddle in all three.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T02:47:01-08:00","id":1006081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1005898#post1005898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I have no problem with what most of BLM stands for, including the way they usually go about fighting for those things.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYou know, it's funny how we saw BLM supporters protesting the shootings of some White people over the course of the last year but not a single All Lives Matter supporter show up. I wonder why that is? I even saw BLM people show up in support of cops who were shot on the job, imagine that. I'm only quoting Larry because I agree with his statement and wanted to add to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T05:13:39-08:00","id":1006132,"title":"","content":"Y'all might want to check this out:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.change.org/p/electoral-college-electors-electoral-college-make-hillary-clinton-president-on-december-19?\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://assets.change.org/photos/3/wj/sh/UlWjsHsjAGkGqdP-1600x900-noPad.jpg?1540669021\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.change.org/p/electoral-college-electors-electoral-college-make-hillary-clinton-president-on-december-19?\" target=\"_blank\"> Sign the Petition </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.change.org/p/electoral-college-electors-electoral-college-make-hillary-clinton-president-on-december-19?\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.change.org/p/electoral-college-electors-electoral-college-make-hillary-clinton-president-on-december-19? </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Electoral College: Make Hillary Clinton President. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Normally, I'd say that online petitions don't do anything, and there's a snowball's chance in hell that the electoral college will change its mind unless Trump does something catastrophic between now and the 19th. But it's been a crazy election season, and I'm not willing to rule out anything at this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T11:50:33-08:00","id":1006314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1006053#post1006053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um... or just has good timing. Sorry but I saw the debates. He looked like a complete idiot. Clinton played him like a fiddle in all three.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, looking like a complete idiot worked to get him more media exposure. He may not have any political experience, but he has a lot of reality TV experience, and he treated the election like America's Next Top President or Who Wants To Be Commander-In-Chief. And it worked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T12:36:27-08:00","id":1006333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1006132#post1006132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Y'all might want to check this out:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.change.org/p/electoral-college-electors-electoral-college-make-hillary-clinton-president-on-december-19?\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.change.org/p/electoral-c...n-december-19?</a><br /> <br /> Normally, I'd say that online petitions don't do anything, and there's a snowball's chance in hell that the electoral college will change its mind unless Trump does something catastrophic between now and the 19th. But it's been a crazy election season, and I'm not willing to rule out anything at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Not to be a billy buzzkill but I don't think this is the correct way to go. </span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">For one thing most delegates get the position from their state parties because they are supporters of the nominee, and as such most genuinely want to see the person they support get elected. It's possible that one could find anti-Trump Republicans among his delegates, but most of them are not going to vote for Clinton, and it would take a large number of <span style=\"color:#454545\">faithless</span> electors to flip the result. </span></span><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">For another, it would be unprecedented in American history for the electoral college to make such an about face and change the result of a presidential election. As much as one can argue that the electoral college is undemocratic, allowing them (let alone telling them) to ignore the results of their state elections (national popular vote or no) would be even more undemocratic. </span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Finally, even if they did do that I don't think it would be a good thing. Not in the big picture. Having established that kind of precedent the electoral college only gets more powerful. Even if you abolish the electoral college immediately afterward or change the rules so it has to follow the popular vote I guarantee that this would come back to bite us in the ass a generation down the road. This kind of thing is how military coups get started. While I genuinely believe Trump is an autocrat and a threat to our democracy barring him from the office he was legally elected to only proves his dictatorial rhetoric right. </span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Moreover, we have to acknowledge that a startlingly, sickeningly large number of Americans voted Trump into office. Even putting aside the question of invalidating their votes, however wrongheaded, they're not going to just go away. Clinging to power through technicalities is not only pure desperation it also reinforces to them that the democratic process is illegitimate, which Trump has been trying to do since the beginning.<br /> <br /> Let's not win the battle by throwing away the war. </span></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T13:06:49-08:00","id":1006357,"title":"","content":"Several ideas went into the Electoral College when it was being designed (as I mentioned in a previous post). One of those ideas was that the Electoral College electors would be able to overturn the will of the people if they felt that the people were electing someone who would be a danger to the country. The Constitutional framers were well aware of the damage that various demagogues did to Athens and how they were, in effect, responsible for that city-states collapse. They didn't want to see something like that happen in America. <br /> <br /> That's one of the reasons why the Electoral College was created in the first place - to keep the decision of the president outside of the direct hands of the populace. It wasn't because the Constitutional framers &quot;hated&quot; or &quot;despised&quot; the common man, but because they were deathly afraid of the power of a populism and were familiar with what could happen when it wasn't kept in check. I dare say in the time since, whether looking at countries like France, or Italy or Germany, we've seen many occasions in which populist candidates, politicians and leaders ended up doing irreparable harm to the people of that country.<br /> <br /> So if the electors did decide to not vote for Trump because they felt that he posed a danger to America if nominated president, that would be Electoral College functioning exactly as it was originally envisioned as doing. Of course, I suppose in the end, they were also alright with slavery and denying women the ability to vote and all kinds of other things, so just because the Constitutional framers thought something was a good idea doesn't necessarily mean it was.<br /> <br /> Still, I'm generally in favor of the Electoral College and feel it performs a vital role in maintaining the power of the individual states and ensuring that candidates don't just have to &quot;win the two coasts and then ignore everything in between.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T13:32:24-08:00","id":1006371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1006357#post1006357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Several ideas went into the Electoral College when it was being designed (as I mentioned in a previous post). One of those ideas was that the Electoral College electors would be able to overturn the will of the people if they felt that the people were electing someone who would be a danger to the country. The Constitutional framers were well aware of the damage that various demagogues did to Athens and how they were, in effect, responsible for that city-states collapse. They didn't want to see something like that happen in America.<br /> <br /> That's one of the reasons why the Electoral College was created in the first place - to keep the decision of the president outside of the direct hands of the populace. It wasn't because the Constitutional framers &quot;hated&quot; or &quot;despised&quot; the common man, but because they were deathly afraid of the power of a populism and were familiar with what could happen when it wasn't kept in check. I dare say in the time since, whether looking at countries like France, or Italy or Germany, we've seen many occasions in which populist candidates, politicians and leaders ended up doing irreparable harm to the people of that country.<br /> <br /> So if the electors did decide to not vote for Trump because they felt that he posed a danger to America if nominated president, that would be Electoral College functioning exactly as it was originally envisioned as doing. Of course, I suppose in the end, they were also alright with slavery and denying women the ability to vote and all kinds of other things, so just because the Constitutional framers thought something was a good idea doesn't necessarily mean it was.<br /> <br /> Still, I'm generally in favor of the Electoral College and feel it performs a vital role in maintaining the power of the individual states and ensuring that candidates don't just have to &quot;win the two coasts and then ignore everything in between.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My preferred fix is to do away with the Winner take all Electoral College and have each of the electors votes be divided based on the state's popular vote. That way you still get candidates campaigning in the entire country and you don't get situations where you feel your vote doesn't count in certain states. <br /> <br /> I doubt the Electoral College is going to make Hillary Clinton president. If they do overturn Trump's vote, they will choose one of the other Republican nominees. Or Mike Pence, god forbid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T14:19:35-08:00","id":1006392,"title":"","content":"Instead you can do something like have more than one possible candidate available per party. Count all votes per party, and the person with the most votes of the party with the most votes becomes POTUS.<br /> <br /> Of course, this can net you a situation where the POTUS got less votes than the person with the most votes in the other party, but no system's perfect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T15:28:12-08:00","id":1006429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1006314#post1006314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is, looking like a complete idiot worked to get him more media exposure. He may not have any political experience, but he has a lot of reality TV experience, and he treated the election like America's Next Top President or Who Wants To Be Commander-In-Chief. And it worked.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYou know, I'm not sure I completely buy that argument. By the time that the debates came around, he'd already gotten the nomination and it was almost impossible for him to have any higher profile than he already had. Moreover, by that point, he was spewing out a pretty much non-stop torrent of totally absurd (and easily fact-checked) nonsense and outright fabrications. Any extra media attention that he got from that point forward was basically just every reputable media outlet running stories about how almost nothing he said actually stood up (or how racist, sexist, homophobic, or just outright paranoid his statements were).<br /> <br /> \u200bI don't think the media coverage had anything to do with it. The thing what was really at play (as evidenced by the Access Hollywood tape scandal) was that he was the Teflon-Candidate. People were so deep into the F***-The-World mindset that he could have sexually assaulted Hillary Clinton right there at the debate on live national television and I'm frankly not sure that it would have hurt him at the polls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T16:06:39-08:00","id":1006451,"title":"","content":"I think there is something to be said for the fact that the harder the media tried to &quot;fact check&quot; Trump, the more it fired up his base because they saw it as an attack by a biased media against their candidate. Really, the only thing that had a serious impact on his campaign was the video footage of his &quot;locker room banter&quot; because there was no way he could really spin that as an unjust attack against him. And, up till that point, everything else that he said never stuck to him.<br /> <br /> Trump realized what was going on and proved more than capable of playing the media like a violin, saying one outrageous thing after another while taking comfort in the fact that the media going after him and discussing it would only help his ratings - err, poll numbers.<br /> <br /> And the media? They kept falling for it hook, line and sinker, giving lots of airtime to whatever the current controversy was, because every time they just knew that surely, <i>this</i> was the controversy that was going to bring down Trump's campaign once and for all. So they'd spend a bunch of time and energy on Trump's latest controversy and then shake their heads in shock as his numbers either stayed the same or would actually go up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T18:58:04-08:00","id":1006502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1006451#post1006451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there is something to be said for the fact that the harder the media tried to &quot;fact check&quot; Trump, the more it fired up his base because they saw it as an attack by a biased media against their candidate. Really, the only thing that had a serious impact on his campaign was the video footage of his &quot;locker room banter&quot; because there was no way he could really spin that as an unjust attack against him. And, up till that point, everything else that he said never stuck to him.<br /> <br /> Trump realized what was going on and proved more than capable of playing the media like a violin, saying one outrageous thing after another while taking comfort in the fact that the media going after him and discussing it would only help his ratings - err, poll numbers.<br /> <br /> And the media? They kept falling for it hook, line and sinker, giving lots of airtime to whatever the current controversy was, because every time they just knew that surely, <i>this</i> was the controversy that was going to bring down Trump's campaign once and for all. So they'd spend a bunch of time and energy on Trump's latest controversy and then shake their heads in shock as his numbers either stayed the same or would actually go up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except they really didn't talk about him all that much. Not compared to the Emails and Clinton Scandal Part What-The-Hell.<br /> <br /> His poll numbers <i>did </i>go down when they actually focused on something, as shown by Curiel, the Khans, and yes, Pussygate. But they didn't <i>remain </i>focused, and that's when his numbers stabilized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T20:14:29-08:00","id":1006531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1006502#post1006502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except they really didn't talk about him all that much. Not compared to the Emails and Clinton Scandal Part What-The-Hell.<br /> <br /> His poll numbers <i>did </i>go down when they actually focused on something, as shown by Curiel, the Khans, and yes, Pussygate. But they didn't <i>remain </i>focused, and that's when his numbers stabilized.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, it felt like I couldn't open the newspaper or look at an online news site without seeing a picture of Donald Trump's big fat head and the latest dumb thing to pop out of his mouth.<br /> <br /> The Atlantic (and several other similar studies) <a href=\"http://www.theatlantic.com/politics/archive/2015/08/graphic-whos-the-most-popular-candidate-mentioned-on-television/402451/\" target=\"_blank\">found that Trump got about twice as much media coverage as Hillary</a> did in the campaign - over 1,200,000 mentions to Hillary's 630,000 on the major news networks. Additionally, by September, <a href=\"http://www.theatlantic.com/technology/archive/2016/09/trumps-media-saturation-quantified/498389/\" target=\"_blank\">Trump had already racked up over</a> $2 billion dollars in free media time compared to Hillary's $750 million (so she got around a little more than 1/3rd of the free coverage as Trump did).<br /> <br /> Further, <a href=\"http://www.motherjones.com/kevin-drum/2016/09/who-gets-better-press-coverage-hillary-clinton-or-donald-trump\" target=\"_blank\">Mother Jones</a> says that their study showed that Trump's coverage was generally far more negative than Hillary's was.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mother Jones</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nonetheless, the fact remains that Trump apparently got significantly more negative coverage than Clinton. What's frustrating for a lot of Democrats, I think, is that Trump's voluminous negative coverage doesn't seem to do him any harm. And that's largely because of a disconnect about what counts as &quot;negative.&quot; In the normal world inhabited by journalists, lying, cheating, bullying, insulting, and general ignorance are considered bad things. In Trumpworld they're good things. His followers seem to agree that he's a bastard, but by God, he's going to be <b>their</b> bastard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course the last week of the election tilted things more heavily against Hillary since much of that was discussing her emails, but that last week didn't really make up for the months of earlier, much more anti-Trump news coming out of the media - not that it really did any good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T20:35:47-08:00","id":1006545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1006451#post1006451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the media? They kept falling for it hook, line and sinker, giving lots of airtime to whatever the current controversy was...</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Falling for it&quot;?<br /> \u200bThey're<i> journalists</i>. What<i> should </i>they do? <b><i>Not</i></b> report that a presidential candidate is seriously considering first-strike use of <i>nuclear weapons</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T21:10:45-08:00","id":1006559,"title":"","content":"I believe AnubisXy was suggesting that he wasn't seriously considering it and, instead, was just saying things to get attention.<br /> <br /> That said, based on how he's responded during debates and other matters, while I'm inclined to believe he's said a lot of things he didn't mean, such as wanting to imprison Hillary Clinton, solely for the cheers in his audiences, it does look like he's not fully aware of matters like the Geneva Convention and why we don't just nuke all our enemies, beyond it being a PR nightmare.<br /> <br /> Whether or not he was 'honestly' running, he doesn't seem to have prepared for what being president entails. While I fully expect him to be a reactionary hothead, I think the severity of nuclear annihilation would be the sort of thing that would make him balk. It's one thing to kick people out of a building, or bilk them out of money. It's another to wipe them and their families off the face of the planet.<br /> <br /> Of course, that's just going by what's happening now. We're not dealing with effective attacks on the United States and who knows what may come.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-22-2016, 12:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T23:11:31-08:00","id":1006602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1006545#post1006545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Falling for it&quot;?<br /> \u200bThey're<i> journalists</i>. What<i> should </i>they do? <b><i>Not</i></b> report that a presidential candidate is seriously considering first-strike use of <i>nuclear weapons</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that just plays into the argument that the Trump campaign (I'm not sure Trump himself deserves all the credit here) completely nailed the PR side of the media war of the election. The mainstream media was completely unprepared for what happened. They reported news, stuck with the need to be journalists and report it, while knowing it was playing into Trump's campaign's desires. They had no defense mechanisms ready for someone that was so willing to throw away the norms of politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T23:20:44-08:00","id":1006606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1006545#post1006545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Falling for it&quot;?<br /> \u200bThey're<i> journalists</i>. What<i> should </i>they do? <b><i>Not</i></b> report that a presidential candidate is seriously considering first-strike use of <i>nuclear weapons</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Trump was just spouting off and making the most extreme statements because he knew it would get him free media attention. In fact, he was constantly bragging about how he spent less money in advertising than anyone else because the press was salivating at the mouth for the next crazy statement of his. He'd say some dumb thing, the media would go into a tizzy reporting on it and endlessly discussing it and bemoaning how terrible it was, and in the process they'd plaster Trump's name and face all over the place.<br /> <br /> Trump would laugh, wait a few days and do it again and the media would be biting at the bit for the next crazy attention grabbing statement to pop out of Trumps mouth - they couldn't wait to see his words drive up more hits on their websites and viewers or readers.<br /> <br /> I mean, I guess you're right though. &quot;Falling for it&quot; was a poor choice of words since the media didn't really &quot;fall&quot; for anything. After all, it's not like it's the media's job to hold a politician's feet in the fire or anything like that. There's a great quote from one of the Superman movies (IV I think?), &quot;The business of a newspaper is business, not news.&quot; So if those stories about Trump were making the media big profits. I can't really blame them for choosing to run with and publish those stories, even if they were basically playing right into Trump's hand.<br /> <br /> Like I said - Trump is a media genius, he knew exactly what the media thrived on, what they wanted and he was more than happy to give it to them in exchange for publicity. Like they say, in a way even the worst publicity can be good publicity, and I think Trump managed to demonstrate that better than nearly anyone else ever has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T01:01:01-08:00","id":1006626,"title":"","content":"&quot;There is no such thing as bad publicity&quot; was absolutely proven by Trump's campaign. The worse the stories were the harder his supporters denied or disregarded them. Too bad they couldn't show the same level of skepticism of all the debunked fake news articles about Clinton. Hillary was going to definitely be charged and FBI Agents were going to stage mass resignations if she wasn't? Totally true, indisputable truth. Heads of multiple federal intelligence and law enforcement agencies say on the record that Russia was tampering with the elections? That was &quot;obviously&quot; bullshit made up to discredit their candidate. Forget about him being on tape admitting to sexually harassing and assaulting women, and then victims of said treatment coming forward. That was clearly all a big conspiracy and all those women must have been lying for some kind of big payday. I wish I could say I was surprised at the level of willful ignorance and stupidity on display, but I have a Facebook account and saw the shit some of my friends shared enthusiastically and with no trace of irony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T03:59:34-08:00","id":1006647,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\">The &quot;I was just kidding about the nukes thing.&quot; doesn't strike me as the best version of roulette to play or for world leader to have to think about either. Meanwhile a &quot;White nationalist&quot; rally and straight up neo Nazi event apparently happened.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Gosh you know, I really really hope that Trump's staff of lobbyists, climate change deniers and gay conversion therapy advocates really takes those people's &quot;economic anxiety&quot; seriously and makes sure to address their concerns in a substance filled first one hundred days of office. I mean as a bisexual/pansexual (I hope Omega is not triggered by that) white man I really can relate to their concerns in Middle America and set aside my own economic anxiety for them.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Hopefully I picked the right shade for sarcasm.</span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T18:10:18-08:00","id":1007510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1006647#post1006647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The &amp;quot;I was just kidding about the nukes thing.&amp;quot; doesn't strike me as the best version of roulette to play or for world leader to have to think about either. Meanwhile a &amp;quot;White nationalist&amp;quot; rally and straight up neo Nazi event apparently happened.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Gosh you know, I really really hope that Trump's staff of lobbyists, climate change deniers and gay conversion therapy advocates really takes those people's &amp;quot;economic anxiety&amp;quot; seriously and makes sure to address their concerns in a substance filled first one hundred days of office. I mean as a bisexual/pansexual (I hope Omega is not triggered by that) white man I really can relate to their concerns in Middle America and set aside my own economic anxiety for them.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Hopefully I picked the right shade for sarcasm.</span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div> It'd take alot more then what you got to trigger me ;p<br /> <br /> Look I know shit is about to get rough, I feel bad for you Americans, even if this was largely collectively self inflicted.<br /> <br /> But you will endure and survive and hopeful learn and not make the same mistakes, and grow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T02:48:18-08:00","id":1007625,"title":"","content":"I would really not use the term &quot;self inflicted&quot; in this situation. People in USA will literally die because of the outcome of this election. Most of those either tried to prevent this outcome or couldn't vote for various reasons. The people who voted for Trump and republican senators are people who most likely will only suffer the consequences of an economic decline. The true victims are forced to go through at least four years of this because others either willfully or ignorantly elected people who encourages (either explicitly or through refusal to help) racism, sexism, homophobia, transphobia, islamophobia and other -isms and -phobias I can't recall right now.<br /> <br /> But I'm not really surprised that it was a Republican victory. Here in Europe we've had a wave of populist right-wing extremist parties getting seats in parliaments for at least half a decade. Compared to many European nations USA basically has a right-wing party and a far right-wing party. When a nation leans that much to the right during a wave of populism and racism in the Western hemisphere, I'm really not surprised they elected the most populist head of state Europe and NA has seen since the fourties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T16:06:10-08:00","id":1007864,"title":"","content":"You know why the right is on the rise here in Europe? Because people feel like they're not being taken seriously. They see billions being pulled out of their countries' already middling economies and poured into projects they never profit from. They see asylum seekers pour in by the thousands every day, with news of violence and sexual assault being commonplace. They see murderers and rapists walk free or be given token punishments. They see their politicians give up national sovereignity bit by bit, just so that they have some temporary wealth and power.<br /> <br /> And then someone comes along and says that's not how things should be. That the country is not doing well and that it should be fixed. Yet the media will tell you that this person you agree with is a horrible person for saying these things and that they should be ignored at best, killed at worst. And that you are a horrible person for agreeing with their views. Every time this person speaks up you have this crammed down your throat, just how bad of a person you are for agreeing with someone who says &quot;no&quot; to the current conditions.<br /> <br /> You'll become annoyed. Irritated. Angry. Eventually you'll be voting for this person, perhaps not even because you agree with them, but just because you can stick it to the stuck-up ponces. THAT is the self-inflicted situation. That is the face of Brexit. Of Trump. Of the coming victories of the right in Europe. People are angry not because they are hateful. But because they've been made angry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T17:30:07-08:00","id":1007884,"title":"","content":"Man, could you pick a worse reason to vote for someone with no experience and I inconsistent policy than &quot;I'm angry&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T17:46:38-08:00","id":1007887,"title":"","content":"Yeah, anger would have gone for Bernie Sanders too. Trump brings a lot more to the table, hatred and fearmongery. One doesn't just get angry and join the KKK unless you've got a very specific anger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T17:55:16-08:00","id":1007891,"title":"","content":"In order to use anger as a tactic one needs to provide a target for that anger. Trump provided one that had no effective way of defending itself, Sanders' targeted millionaires and billionaires. If you had to bet money which fight would you have bet on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 11-25-2016, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T21:38:32-08:00","id":1007941,"title":"","content":"The whole argument of Trump as white working class protest is one that I simultaneously understand but have no sympathy for. <br /> <br /> It's easy for people to say &quot;Wake up, manufacturing jobs are never coming back!&quot; when they aren't the people who depended on those jobs and who have no prospects without them. It's easy for people to say &quot;Get an education and get out of your shitty dead end town!&quot; when they already live in a white collar metropole, or got there by a combination of technical disposition, good luck, and start up capital. If you're a rural or rust belt American you are capital F fucked, and sad brutal truth is that nobody actually cares. <br /> <br /> I <i>get it </i>. I'm from there. I've seen the hopelessness and I've seen the almost universal indifference to it. I feel that shit in the pit of my soul and it makes me sick. I understand. <br /> <br /> But I don't have sympathy. <br /> <br /> Because while that is awful, equally awful is the toxic retrograde oppressive bullshit culture that permeates these places. The culture that isn't just hateful it's self-loathing and self-destructive. Maybe it's because I've been getting into fist fights with rednecks all my life, but I've long run out of any desire to compromise with or even politely tolerate it. Sure, some of it is education. It certainly helped me. Some motherfuckers don't want to learn though, and when you worship ignorance you cease being someone who deserves to matter in my philosophy. <br /> <br /> Is that fair? Or just? Or American? Probably not. I also don't care. <br /> <br /> I want to help the people trapped in our country's very own Third World. The people who have inherited nothing and have nothing to look forward to. The people who receive nothing but scorn for the fact that their lives are for shit. The &quot;working class&quot; that became synonymous with &quot;poor&quot; while we weren't looking. There's a price for that though. You can take a hand up into the twenty first century or you can rot. It's that simple. <br /> <br /> Does that make me part of the problem? One of the out of touch liberal elites? Maybe, but frankly I'm past giving a fuck. <br /> <br /> Rant over. Enjoy your holidays.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T22:38:15-08:00","id":1007954,"title":"","content":"I've seen similar statements before, only they were concerning inner city (primarily African-American) enclaves and bemoaning the 'pro-gang/drug/crime attitude' there and how it helped to foster a a regressive, self-destructive culture - and that's why people living in that area didn't deserve sympathy concerning things like a lack of job opportunities, good education, etc. These were problems they &quot;brought on themselves,&quot; etc, etc.<br /> <br /> And I've heard similar words about immigrant enclaves in France, Britain and other parts of Europe. <br /> <br /> Maybe some of those ideas are right to a degree or not.<br /> <br /> Regardless, I think writing off people like that though is a fairly dangerous attitude to have - that sense of &quot;I don't give a shit,&quot; about segments of your country's population is <i>never</i> a good one. They're still your fellow citizens, and in a democracy their thoughts and opinions are just as important and valid as yours are (as we've seen in this election). You can choose to write them off and not have sympathy for them, but at the same time, they will probably write you off and not have sympathy for you - and that's not a good attitude to have for other people in the same country.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T01:16:25-08:00","id":1007985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1007941#post1007941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's easy for people to say &quot;Wake up, manufacturing jobs are never coming back!&quot; when they aren't the people who depended on those jobs and who have no prospects without them. It's easy for people to say &quot;Get an education and get out of your shitty dead end town!&quot; when they already live in a white collar metropole, or got there by a combination of technical disposition, good luck, and start up capital. If you're a rural or rust belt American you are capital F fucked, and sad brutal truth is that nobody actually cares.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't found it that hard to say living in the rural/rust belt. It just doesn't do any good because the majority of people that would listen are the people that already agree, or are young and their parents get very angry with you (though I'm used to that being a biologist out in a part of the world were people are proud to declare evolution an anti-religion conspiracy).<br /> <br /> Though we're not as fucked as everyone seems to think. My town is doing alright all things considered because we had people smart enough to move to modern manufacturing over the old rust bust manufacturing so that we've got to factories still alive and well. Since two companies read the writing on the wall well over 20 years ago now, we've got some jobs instead of no jobs, and people got over the idea of being a Nth generation worker in the same industry really quickly when that was the choice available to them.<br /> <br /> The problem is that we're a pretty big exception in that regard. Well that and people don't like much actual change to their concept of their community identity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1007954#post1007954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen similar statements before, only they were concerning inner city (primarily African-American) enclaves and bemoaning the 'pro-gang/drug/crime attitude' there and how it helped to foster a a regressive, self-destructive culture - and that's why people living in that area didn't deserve sympathy concerning things like a lack of job opportunities, good education, etc. These were problems they &quot;brought on themselves,&quot; etc, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that most of the time the response to this is to push back against how wrong it is. In far too much of the rural small town white America, the response is to take pride in it instead.<br /> <br /> This isn't even a new thing either. I have a friend that used to work as a campaign aid for a Republican in her (traditionally blue) state. As someone that was an intellectual conservative that cares a lot about policy and being able to actually defend political positions, she worked with her boss to make binders of prep material for local volunteers to use to have more than talking points for town halls and what not.<br /> <br /> And they stopped using them because it actually cost them votes. Coming in with facts to shut Democrats up with didn't turn them into leaders, it alienated their own voters who resented the facts for their own side's positions as being elitist. She quit politics after a few years of being reduced to a distributor of base-comforting talking points and meaningless empty red-meat promises.<br /> <br /> Whether you like a given phrasing of things, or think it compares to something else well, this embrace of disdain for intellectualism is a problem that's not just resentment. It's something that's been cultivated and accepted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Regardless, I think writing off people like that though is a fairly dangerous attitude to have - that sense of &quot;I don't give a shit,&quot; about segments of your country's population is <i>never</i> a good one. </div> </div> </div>Is it? I mean, am I supposed to give a shit about what the members of the KKK and the alt-right, beyond, &quot;that's fucking disgusting and you're lucky you asshats live in a country that tolerates your existence.&quot; but I don't see any value in caring about them. Being informed and educated yes. But I'm happier if people like that are solidly voiceless in political representation.<br /> <br /> So... if I don't accept this absolute idea that nobody should get written off, I think there needs to be a bit better of a reason to not stop giving a shit about the cult of ignorance people have successfully propagated in parts of the US.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They're still your fellow citizens, and in a democracy their thoughts and opinions are just as important and valid as yours are (as we've seen in this election). </div> </div> </div>Their thoughts and opinions are important if they vote on them. That doesn't make them valid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T05:25:29-08:00","id":1008034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1007941#post1007941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole argument of Trump as white working class protest is one that I simultaneously understand but have no sympathy for. <br /> <br /> It's easy for people to say &amp;quot;Wake up, manufacturing jobs are never coming back!&amp;quot; when they aren't the people who depended on those jobs and who have no prospects without them. It's easy for people to say &amp;quot;Get an education and get out of your shitty dead end town!&amp;quot; when they already live in a white collar metropole, or got there by a combination of technical disposition, good luck, and start up capital. If you're a rural or rust belt American you are capital F fucked, and sad brutal truth is that nobody actually cares. <br /> <br /> I <i>get it </i>. I'm from there. I've seen the hopelessness and I've seen the almost universal indifference to it. I feel that shit in the pit of my soul and it makes me sick. I understand. <br /> <br /> But I don't have sympathy. <br /> <br /> Because while that is awful, equally awful is the toxic retrograde oppressive bullshit culture that permeates these places. The culture that isn't just hateful it's self-loathing and self-destructive. Maybe it's because I've been getting into fist fights with rednecks all my life, but I've long run out of any desire to compromise with or even politely tolerate it. Sure, some of it is education. It certainly helped me. Some motherfuckers don't want to learn though, and when you worship ignorance you cease being someone who deserves to matter in my philosophy. <br /> <br /> Is that fair? Or just? Or American? Probably not. I also don't care. <br /> <br /> I want to help the people trapped in our country's very own Third World. The people who have inherited nothing and have nothing to look forward to. The people who receive nothing but scorn for the fact that their lives are for shit. The &amp;quot;working class&amp;quot; that became synonymous with &amp;quot;poor&amp;quot; while we weren't looking. There's a price for that though. You can take a hand up into the twenty first century or you can rot. It's that simple. <br /> <br /> Does that make me part of the problem? One of the out of touch liberal elites? Maybe, but frankly I'm past giving a fuck. <br /> <br /> Rant over. Enjoy your holidays.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not giving a fuck got you Donald Trump.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T05:26:24-08:00","id":1008035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1007954#post1007954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen similar statements before, only they were concerning inner city (primarily African-American) enclaves and bemoaning the 'pro-gang/drug/crime attitude' there and how it helped to foster a a regressive, self-destructive culture - and that's why people living in that area didn't deserve sympathy concerning things like a lack of job opportunities, good education, etc. These were problems they &amp;quot;brought on themselves,&amp;quot; etc, etc.<br /> <br /> And I've heard similar words about immigrant enclaves in France, Britain and other parts of Europe. <br /> <br /> Maybe some of those ideas are right to a degree or not.<br /> <br /> Regardless, I think writing off people like that though is a fairly dangerous attitude to have - that sense of &amp;quot;I don't give a shit,&amp;quot; about segments of your country's population is <i>never</i> a good one. They're still your fellow citizens, and in a democracy their thoughts and opinions are just as important and valid as yours are (as we've seen in this election). You can choose to write them off and not have sympathy for them, but at the same time, they will probably write you off and not have sympathy for you - and that's not a good attitude to have for other people in the same country.</div> </div> </div> </div> Very wise words.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T12:41:27-08:00","id":1008239,"title":"","content":"Trump win, backlash against the media?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T15:46:53-08:00","id":1008298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1007954#post1007954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen similar statements before, only they were concerning inner city (primarily African-American) enclaves and bemoaning the 'pro-gang/drug/crime attitude' there and how it helped to foster a a regressive, self-destructive culture - and that's why people living in that area didn't deserve sympathy concerning things like a lack of job opportunities, good education, etc. These were problems they &quot;brought on themselves,&quot; etc, etc.<br /> <br /> And I've heard similar words about immigrant enclaves in France, Britain and other parts of Europe.<br /> <br /> Maybe some of those ideas are right to a degree or not.<br /> <br /> Regardless, I think writing off people like that though is a fairly dangerous attitude to have - that sense of &quot;I don't give a shit,&quot; about segments of your country's population is <i>never</i> a good one. They're still your fellow citizens, and in a democracy their thoughts and opinions are just as important and valid as yours are (as we've seen in this election). You can choose to write them off and not have sympathy for them, but at the same time, they will probably write you off and not have sympathy for you - and that's not a good attitude to have for other people in the same country.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bMorally, and more importantly logically, that kind of behavior is destructive to the health of any nation. Even if you are a selfish sociopath that doesn't give a crap about entire segments of the population (like me) it behooves you to not just let them wither and die. Doing so will just cause these enclaves to commit more and more acts of criminal and subversive behavior, which than results in the need for an expanded police and surveillance forces, which than results in me paying more taxes. As a selfish asshole me having to pay more taxes for something that shouldn't have even been a significant problem in the first place annoys me to no end. Poverty and crime is something that people are going to have to pay for no matter what. Having my taxes actually go to something, like say a reformed welfare system, that actual helps the situation instead of just making it worse seems far more productive in my opinion.<br /> <br /> \u200bPlus, the last thing I want is to get robbed again by some half-starved urbanite, so there's that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T16:05:43-08:00","id":1008308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1007985#post1007985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Is it? I mean, am I supposed to give a shit about what the members of the KKK and the alt-right, beyond, &quot;that's fucking disgusting and you're lucky you asshats live in a country that tolerates your existence.&quot; but I don't see any value in caring about them. Being informed and educated yes. But I'm happier if people like that are solidly voiceless in political representation.<br /> <br /> So... if I don't accept this absolute idea that nobody should get written off, I think there needs to be a bit better of a reason to not stop giving a shit about the cult of ignorance people have successfully propagated in parts of the US.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYou don't have to care about them, or anyone for that matter. The real problem is what to do about them. Facts don't stop them. Protests don't stop them. Ridicule doesn't stop them. Indifference doesn't stop them. Time hasn't stopped them. And now Hillary couldn't stop them. So what is to be done about these deplorable? Maybe if we could have all registered and perhaps concentrated somewhere. Yeah, have them all sent to concentrated zones and reeducated, or better yet, just done away with entirely. We could call them these zones...<br /> <br /> \u200bWait. Nah. Thought I had something going there but I just found out some German guy did it all already. Must have half-remembered all that from some 4chan post I read awhile ago. Oh well. Sounded like a terrible and heinous idea anyway. So, guess hoping that they go away over time and that compassion, reason, forward-thinking well prevail is our best option. I can live with that.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T17:55:05-08:00","id":1008345,"title":"","content":"Is there any reason you felt the need to imply that I was advocating for concentration camps instead of just focusing on a reasonable conclusion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T18:04:57-08:00","id":1008351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1008345#post1008345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any reason you felt the need to imply that I was advocating for concentration camps instead of just focusing on a reasonable conclusion?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was bored...<br /> <br /> \u200bIn all seriousness though I in no way believe that you're advocating for something so miserable and admit that the above was in bad taste. I've just been seeing one to many so-called liberals suggest such tactics and wanted to vent. Sorry you got to be the butt of the joke.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnyways, I am honestly asking what you think is the best way to handle this far-right phenomenon and actually get these zealots to see reason. Writing them off or waiting for them to die off as the demographics change doesn't to be a great solution to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T19:40:12-08:00","id":1008384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1008351#post1008351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAnyways, I am honestly asking what you think is the best way to handle this far-right phenomenon and actually get these zealots to see reason. Writing them off or waiting for them to die off as the demographics change doesn't to be a great solution to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>More integration, I think. <br /> <br /> Only the nuttiest nutters harbor an irrational hatred for people they see every day and get to learn to live with. The problem with too many alt-right people is that they rarely or never encounter LGBT people, immigrants, minorities, etc. They are raised in or create isolated enclaves that shelter them from outside influences. Even internet access, if they have that, cannot push cosmopolitanism to them because it's easy to limit your internet use to only things that reinforce your worldview. But if they had enough first-hand experience with other kinds of people, enough for them to become normalized, they'd probably chill out. <br /> <br /> Now, the follow-up question - how do you get people who are initially inclined to fear each other to live in peace? - is something we've been struggling with at least since Brown. vs. Board.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T23:45:03-08:00","id":1008440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1008351#post1008351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry you got to be the butt of the joke.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for that... it was a... fairly sensitive point for me and I do appreciate this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bAnyways, I am honestly asking what you think is the best way to handle this far-right phenomenon and actually get these zealots to see reason. Writing them off or waiting for them to die off as the demographics change doesn't to be a great solution to me. </div> </div> </div>Getting them to see reason? The problem is that, effectively, that's not possible. If someone does not want to vote on reason and facts, there is no way to convince them to do so. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar908_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"908\" data-vbnamecard=\"908\">semicasual</a> has the best idea in theory of how to make an emotional play to blunt the cult of ignorance, but enforcing it has been tried and repeatedly failed. For example forced busing had kids from different neighborhoods getting mixed together in the same schools to promote this sort of thing. Regardless of how people feel about how well it did things like improve funding in poorer schools now having wealthier students, or increasing academic performance for students that didn't have access to things richer school distracts have before, the cultural diversity exposure aspect was probably successful... right up until white flight set in and ruined that.<br /> <br /> As well, getting minorities out into those communities can be very difficult because it can be literally dangerous. A lot of members of these groups end up moving to urban enclaves for their safety. <br /> <br /> Even for those of us that feel safe despite minority status find being representatives of the values of diversity taxing. I'm open about my religion in my community - though we're not too far away from towns with larger Jewish communities - but you can only deal with questions like, &quot;You're a Jew, do you pick up money off the ground?&quot; &quot;Hey do you know a good lawyer/accountant/etc.?&quot; &quot;Why aren't you rich? Jews control the banks and Hollywood.&quot; &quot;How can you be Jewish when Jews killed Jesus?&quot; and, &quot;What do you use in those weird crackers since you can't use Christian blood any more?&quot; so many times before you can't keep you're cool about it.<br /> <br /> I have been asked all of those questions by people that are from all appearances good, decent, kind, and not-bigoted people. It was always out of ignorance (and frequently a sincere desire to hear my stance on these things), but I still have to live knowing that most of my neighbors have insanely anti-Semitic beliefs that they've internalized no matter how long they've known me. Knowing a Jew doesn't undo that programming. It doesn't undo the systems that taught them those things in the first place.<br /> <br /> So... to an extent we are playing a waiting game because there's very little to practically do besides wait. I have hope about the next generation because they seem to be much less susceptible to this stuff than their parents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T04:41:29-08:00","id":1008488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1008440#post1008440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you for that... it was a... fairly sensitive point for me and I do appreciate this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Getting them to see reason? The problem is that, effectively, that's not possible. If someone does not want to vote on reason and facts, there is no way to convince them to do so. <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> has the best idea in theory of how to make an emotional play to blunt the cult of ignorance, but enforcing it has been tried and repeatedly failed. For example forced busing had kids from different neighborhoods getting mixed together in the same schools to promote this sort of thing. Regardless of how people feel about how well it did things like improve funding in poorer schools now having wealthier students, or increasing academic performance for students that didn't have access to things richer school distracts have before, the cultural diversity exposure aspect was probably successful... right up until white flight set in and ruined that.<br /> <br /> As well, getting minorities out into those communities can be very difficult because it can be literally dangerous. A lot of members of these groups end up moving to urban enclaves for their safety. <br /> <br /> Even for those of us that feel safe despite minority status find being representatives of the values of diversity taxing. I'm open about my religion in my community - though we're not too far away from towns with larger Jewish communities - but you can only deal with questions like, &amp;quot;You're a Jew, do you pick up money off the ground?&amp;quot; &amp;quot;Hey do you know a good lawyer/accountant/etc.?&amp;quot; &amp;quot;Why aren't you rich? Jews control the banks and Hollywood.&amp;quot; &amp;quot;How can you be Jewish when Jews killed Jesus?&amp;quot; and, &amp;quot;What do you use in those weird crackers since you can't use Christian blood any more?&amp;quot; so many times before you can't keep you're cool about it.<br /> <br /> I have been asked all of those questions by people that are from all appearances good, decent, kind, and not-bigoted people. It was always out of ignorance (and frequently a sincere desire to hear my stance on these things), but I still have to live knowing that most of my neighbors have insanely anti-Semitic beliefs that they've internalized no matter how long they've known me. Knowing a Jew doesn't undo that programming. It doesn't undo the systems that taught them those things in the first place.<br /> <br /> So... to an extent we are playing a waiting game because there's very little to practically do besides wait. I have hope about the next generation because they seem to be much less susceptible to this stuff than their parents.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not Jewish, but if I find money on the groubd of course I pick it up, that seems like a stupid question to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T04:42:15-08:00","id":1008489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.kirklandreporter.com/news/female-admits-claim-of-sexual-assault-in-kirkland-was-fabricated/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.kirklandreporter.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/14/2016/11/web1_KIR-LOGO-PoliceCropped.jpg?w=270\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.kirklandreporter.com/news/female-admits-claim-of-sexual-assault-in-kirkland-was-fabricated/\" target=\"_blank\"> Female admits claim of sexual assault in Kirkland was fabricated - Kirkland Reporter </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.kirklandreporter.com/news/female-admits-claim-of-sexual-assault-in-kirkland-was-fabricated/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.kirklandreporter.com/news/female-admits-claim-of-sexual-assault-in-kirkland-was-fabricated/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The following is a release from the Kirkland Police Department: </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> People need to stop nonesense like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T05:41:37-08:00","id":1008503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/rjmz9K59a7E\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/rjmz9K59a7E\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/rjmz9K59a7E\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/rjmz9K59a7E </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Both Trump supporters and Hillary supporters are doing hoax hate crimes. <br /> <br /> The sad thing is some people really do end up victims of hate crimes and this BS puts them at risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T09:52:53-08:00","id":1008585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1008488#post1008488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not Jewish, but if I find money on the groubd of course I pick it up, that seems like a stupid question to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It must be nice to be sheltered from anti-Semitic indoctrination methods. If you don't get it, you could ask instead of trying to downplay something you don't have the context to understand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1008489#post1008489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People need to stop nonesense like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Cops shouldn't interview potential sexual assault victims in places that are statistically demonstrated to result in recantations; even from people who were probably actual victims.<br /> <br /> Oh wait. You mean false reporting. It happens. You can't stop it. However focusing on sexual assault reporting is silly since all attempts to study it show that false reports are far lower than other crimes, and an insanely large number of actual victims cite a number of reasons they recant even when confronted by the police because there is a very reasonable perception that going through with a sexual crime report is far more traumatic than any potential pay off for seeing justice done.<br /> <br /> We should really fix those problems first (and I don't want to hear any MRA based retort, because men are more likely to recant because of those factors when they're the victims of sexual assault than women).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_conta