tisemites, I apologize if that wasn't clear.<br /> <br /> And actually studies have shown that false reporting of sexual assaults is in fact higher then many other crimes.<br /> <br /> To be fair the research in that area of study is not as extensive and unbiased as it should, but one works with what one has to work with.<br /> <br /> I'll gather my data for a rebuttal.<br /> <br /> Sexual Assualt/Rape is a hugely serious crime as is a false accusation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 11-26-2016, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T11:39:40-08:00","id":1008631,"title":"","content":"A Kanin's study showed 41% rate of false accusations.<br /> <br /> As for being pressured to recant, plenty of innocent people are pressured to admit guilt, should we ignore those who confessed to rape because they were pressured to confess?<br /> <br /> The truth is everyone is under pressure, because the police usually want to shake the truth free.<br /> <br /> I can only treat someone recanting as a false allegation unless there is evidence of police being genuinely abusive, not just challenging their story, but actually abusive, or evidence they were blackmailed into recanting, because that's the evidence I have.<br /> <br /> Just as I have to take a confession of rape seriously as a reasonable fact unless evidence comes up of abuse, blackmail, or delusion occurs, because its the best information I have.<br /> <br /> Interesting to note the Kanin was the darling of the feminists in the 50s and 60s, who happily used his earilier studies, until his studies in the 90s came out showing a high rate of false rape accusations, which did not serve their narrative.<br /> <br /> Look I used to think it was about 8% false accusations (the 2% was never credible, as there was no study that showed this to be true, but its ironically given out by so called myth busters), but its not.<br /> <br /> Anyway I didn't intend for this to become about this, I originally only intended to show both protrump and antitrump forces were acting irresponsibly and that hate crimes are serious and should be treated seriously, you the one responsible for the thread drift.<br /> <br /> As the erosion of due process, there is plenty of evidence for that.<br /> <br /> Universities has denied accused access to lawyers, cross examination, ect..., and are now increasingly being sued for it.<br /> <br /> Anyways perhaps we can get back to President Trump and his election?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T15:57:39-08:00","id":1008703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1008595#post1008595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it a contest now?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but false equivalencies shouldn't be tolerated. If fake news stories are a much bigger issue on one side of a political division than the other, it is a disservice to the actual debate to treat is as the same on both sides.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I didn't down play antisematism, I take it very seriously, I was pointing out the stupidity of those antisemites, I apologize if that wasn't clear. </div> </div> </div>However seriously you take it, you still clearly don't get this one.<br /> <br /> This is a reference to an old anti-Semitic myth that you can find a Jew hiding in the ground by dropping coins and waiting for the first people that can't help but pick them up; because Jews are just that greedy.<br /> <br /> This isn't stupidity, it's just plain old persistent bigoted stereotypes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And actually studies have shown that false reporting of sexual assaults is in fact higher then many other crimes. </div> </div> </div>Not really. But I'll get to that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To be fair the research in that area of study is not as extensive and unbiased as it should, but one works with what one has to work with. </div> </div> </div>Clearly you're not, because you're going right to Kanin.<br /> <br /> [QUOTE=Omegaphallic;n1008631]A Kanin's study showed 41% rate of false accusations.[/quote<br /> <br /> Kanin's study is complete crap. There are two core issues with it:<br /> <br /> 1) The sample size is insanely small (109 cases in one city over nine years). On it's face it's a mathematically insignificant study due to lack of proper sample size.<br /> <br /> 2) Kanin doesn't differentiate between false accusations and unfounded (or whatever term you want to use) accusations. That is, it treats people actually lying about their assault as the same as people that cannot be shown to be lying about their assault but there isn't enough evidence for the police to act on.<br /> <br /> FBI crime statistics put the probable range at 2% to 8% since even they don't have a really solid grasp on this, and unlike Kanin aren't going to put out a definitive number without actual statistics to back them up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for being pressured to recant, plenty of innocent people are pressured to admit guilt, should we ignore those who confessed to rape because they were pressured to confess? </div> </div> </div>Well that's a bullshit response. And I think you know it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The truth is everyone is under pressure, because the police usually want to shake the truth free. </div> </div> </div>The problem is that the police are consistently shown to make sexual assault accusers feel like they're liars instead of neutrally pursuing the truth. Even though modern police agencies have tried to do a lot of work to end this, the perception that accusing someone of sexual assault or rape will ruin your life is far stronger than the attempts to change how police agencies approach sexual crime investigations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Look I used to think it was about 8% false accusations (the 2% was never credible, as there was no study that showed this to be true, but its ironically given out by so called myth busters), but its not. </div> </div> </div>I'll take the FBI over Kanin on this one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway I didn't intend for this to become about this, I originally only intended to show both protrump and antitrump forces were acting irresponsibly and that hate crimes are serious and should be treated seriously, you the one responsible for the thread drift. </div> </div> </div>I don't have a problem with this drift, because I absolutely care about calling out the nonsense of the desire to establish a narrative of a false equivalence here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T20:05:44-08:00","id":1008778,"title":"","content":"I personally wouldn't expect much nuance on the subject of discrimination from an MRA, Arms, just saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T23:25:47-08:00","id":1008833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1007954#post1007954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen similar statements before, only they were concerning inner city (primarily African-American) enclaves and bemoaning the 'pro-gang/drug/crime attitude' there and how it helped to foster a a regressive, self-destructive culture - and that's why people living in that area didn't deserve sympathy concerning things like a lack of job opportunities, good education, etc. These were problems they &quot;brought on themselves,&quot; etc, etc.<br /> <br /> And I've heard similar words about immigrant enclaves in France, Britain and other parts of Europe.<br /> <br /> Maybe some of those ideas are right to a degree or not.<br /> <br /> Regardless, I think writing off people like that though is a fairly dangerous attitude to have - that sense of &quot;I don't give a shit,&quot; about segments of your country's population is <i>never</i> a good one. They're still your fellow citizens, and in a democracy their thoughts and opinions are just as important and valid as yours are (as we've seen in this election). You can choose to write them off and not have sympathy for them, but at the same time, they will probably write you off and not have sympathy for you - and that's not a good attitude to have for other people in the same country.</div> </div> </div> </div>This argument simply does not apply to the average citizen as it pertains towards the American election. At best it pertains only towards those people of power and influence in the Democratic party over the last fifty plus years who have been guilty of falling into the same trap of neo-liberalism that the Republicans mostly gleefully support. The latter how also is particular unrealistic as very very rarely is it that even the average American is going to be a single issue person when it comes to writing off other segments of the population. Also the ugly reality is that there are going to be people, again specifically talking about just America here but it's applicable to other countries who are going to hate other people and dismiss their humanity regardless. American liberals and liberal media outlets need to make sure they do not fall into the dangerous illusion that they are ultimately responsible for this because they are not and no amount of uncertainty justifies self destructive behavior on a societal level like this.<br /> <br /> What I DO blame what passes for the American left and in reality as far as power structure goes, the American center right is this. They cede far too much ground by default.<br /> <br /> Personally I am grim. There are a million historical scenarios that play out all kinds of different ways as it involves the rise of nationalistic right wing forces in Europe, America and elsewhere, the clashes arising from the reactions to global climate change and rising industrializing nations, and the part that corporatism is playing in the economic angles of these and other politic tides. But I personally do not see this ending peacefully, whether it is manifests as nation vs nation or otherwise, I see it ending in a lot of bloodshed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 11-27-2016, 02:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T05:27:34-08:00","id":1008888,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Heavy Arms;n1008703]<br /> <br /> No, but false equivalencies shouldn't be tolerated. If fake news stories are a much bigger issue on one side of a political division than the other, it is a disservice to the actual debate to treat is as the same on both sides.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> However seriously you take it, you still clearly don't get this one.<br /> <br /> This is a reference to an old anti-Semitic myth that you can find a Jew hiding in the ground by dropping coins and waiting for the first people that can't help but pick them up; because Jews are just that greedy.<br /> <br /> This isn't stupidity, it's just plain old persistent bigoted stereotypes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Not really. But I'll get to that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Clearly you're not, because you're going right to Kanin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1008631#post1008631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Kanin's study showed 41% rate of false accusations.[/quote<br /> <br /> Kanin's study is complete crap. There are two core issues with it:<br /> <br /> 1) The sample size is insanely small (109 cases in one city over nine years). On it's face it's a mathematically insignificant study due to lack of proper sample size.<br /> <br /> 2) Kanin doesn't differentiate between false accusations and unfounded (or whatever term you want to use) accusations. That is, it treats people actually lying about their assault as the same as people that cannot be shown to be lying about their assault but there isn't enough evidence for the police to act on.<br /> <br /> FBI crime statistics put the probable range at 2% to 8% since even they don't have a really solid grasp on this, and unlike Kanin aren't going to put out a definitive number without actual statistics to back them up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well that's a bullshit response. And I think you know it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The problem is that the police are consistently shown to make sexual assault accusers feel like they're liars instead of neutrally pursuing the truth. Even though modern police agencies have tried to do a lot of work to end this, the perception that accusing someone of sexual assault or rape will ruin your life is far stronger than the attempts to change how police agencies approach sexual crime investigations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'll take the FBI over Kanin on this one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't have a problem with this drift, because I absolutely care about calling out the nonsense of the desire to establish a narrative of a false equivalence here.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.datagoneodd.com/blog/2015/01/25/how-to-lie-and-mislead-with-rape-statistics-part-1/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://www.datagoneodd.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2015/01/False-Reporting-Rates-Resized.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.datagoneodd.com/blog/2015/01/25/how-to-lie-and-mislead-with-rape-statistics-part-1/\" target=\"_blank\"> How To Lie And Mislead With Rape Statistics: Part 1 &ndash; Data Gone Odd </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.datagoneodd.com/blog/2015/01/25/how-to-lie-and-mislead-with-rape-statistics-part-1/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.datagoneodd.com/blog/2015/01/25/how-to-lie-and-mislead-with-rape-statistics-part-1/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.datagoneodd.com/blog/2015/01/27/how-to-lie-and-mislead-with-rape-statistics-part-2/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://www.datagoneodd.com/blog/wp-content/uploads/2015/01/Ad-small.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.datagoneodd.com/blog/2015/01/27/how-to-lie-and-mislead-with-rape-statistics-part-2/\" target=\"_blank\"> How To Lie And Mislead With Rape Statistics: Part 2 &ndash; Data Gone Odd </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.datagoneodd.com/blog/2015/01/27/how-to-lie-and-mislead-with-rape-statistics-part-2/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.datagoneodd.com/blog/2015/01/27/how-to-lie-and-mislead-with-rape-statistics-part-2/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.datagoneodd.com/blog/2015/06/28/what-do-we-know-about-false-rape-allegations/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/6ac7563337f57a80127e49682d7ba9cf9f6bcd457e527b3e4d712c21e2538633?s=50&amp;d=identicon&amp;r=g\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.datagoneodd.com/blog/2015/06/28/what-do-we-know-about-false-rape-allegations/\" target=\"_blank\"> What do we know about false rape allegations? &ndash; Data Gone Odd </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.datagoneodd.com/blog/2015/06/28/what-do-we-know-about-false-rape-allegations/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.datagoneodd.com/blog/2015/06/28/what-do-we-know-about-false-rape-allegations/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T13:14:22-08:00","id":1009022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1008888#post1008888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.datagoneodd.com/blog/2015/01/25/how-to-lie-and-mislead-with-rape-statistics-part-1/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.datagoneodd.com/blog/2015...istics-part-1/</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.datagoneodd.com/blog/2015/01/27/how-to-lie-and-mislead-with-rape-statistics-part-2/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.datagoneodd.com/blog/2015...istics-part-2/</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.datagoneodd.com/blog/2015/06/28/what-do-we-know-about-false-rape-allegations/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.datagoneodd.com/blog/2015...e-allegations/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Few things to note:<br /> <br /> 1) I didn't know of this blog. It's pretty awesome! This guy really does break down problems with papers based on how the research is done. Really fascinating.<br /> <br /> 2) I really wish you gave more commentary with these links, especially since you seem to do a lot of posting that just provides links, so that you can better have a conversation going on about them. A lot of the time I just see you post a link and then I don't know what else to say on it, since you don't really seem interested in discussing it.<br /> <br /> 3) You really should include <a href=\"http://www.datagoneodd.com/blog/2015/05/19/narrative-in-search-of-a-statistic/\" target=\"_blank\">this link</a> too, because here the writer goes into the problems of the Kanin study in particular. A particular quote from that article: &quot;<span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> In fact, I see it all the time from people trying to claim the </span></span></span><a href=\"https://archive.org/details/FalseRapeAllegations\" target=\"_blank\">Kanin study</a><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> is the benchmark study on the topic. Don\u2019t get me wrong, </span></span></span><a href=\"http://www.davidlisak.com/wp-content/uploads/pdf/SARFalseAllegationsofRape.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Lisak\u2019s critique</a><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> of the Kanin study is </span></span></span><a href=\"http://www.datagoneodd.com/blog/2015/01/25/how-to-lie-and-mislead-with-rape-statistics-part-1/\" target=\"_blank\">pretty awful</a><span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">, but that doesn\u2019t mean the Kanin study should be taken as at all representative of the country of the whole.</span></span></span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Still, thank you for sharing this regarding whats a pretty sensitive topic. It's pretty relevant and the only bias I can really find here is a desire for solid research methods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":". 11-27-2016, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T13:29:56-08:00","id":1009029,"title":"","content":"Given the rebuttal here is a blog that tears Kanin's study to shreds, I think we can solidly agree then that the Kanin study is crap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T13:58:39-08:00","id":1009042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1009029#post1009029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the rebuttal here is a blog that tears Kanin's study to shreds, I think we can solidly agree then that the Kanin study is crap.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's... not the conclusion that the blog reaches. He points out that there's a potential issue of bias on Kanin's part, similarly to the Lisak's critique of it, and that the data which Kanin uses comes from 1978-1987 which is outdated, before concluding with: &quot;<span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Overall, while the Kanin study can provide an interesting counterpoint to the \u201conly 2-8%\u201d narrative, grounding your view that false complaints are extremely prevalent in a single, extremely dated study is just as foolish as the logic employed by those who swear by the other studies I have covered.</span></span></span>&quot;<br /> <br /> From what the writer of the blog says regarding the 2-8% narrative, from their review of the study that it comes from, is pretty much: &quot;<span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">At the end of the day, my point is this \u2013 If someone tries to advocate a particular policy based on the fact that \u201conly 2-8% of rape reports are false\u201d an appropriate response might be \u201cSure, but only 1-8% are true.\u201d</span></span></span>&quot; As the 2-8% reports being false is a bottom floor, not a ceiling. I really recommend reading <a href=\"http://www.datagoneodd.com/blog/2015/01/27/how-to-lie-and-mislead-with-rape-statistics-part-2/\" target=\"_blank\">their analysis</a> of that study. It's really interesting to see how the study was set up.<br /> <br /> Edit: Regarding the 8% statistic being cited by the FBI of reports being &quot;unfounded&quot; (or false), that's still above the 2% statistic of other crimes being unfounded. How this can impact things is shown in <a href=\"http://www.datagoneodd.com/blog/2015/07/14/professor-twitter-and-the-problem-of-the-low-false-rape-narrative/\" target=\"_blank\">this blog post</a> as to how even a low percentage of false reports still shows a relevant problem existing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":". 11-27-2016, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T21:54:56-08:00","id":1009176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1009042#post1009042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's... not the conclusion that the blog reaches.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's critical of all of the studies and statistics people cite.<br /> <br /> However he's pretty clearly - as you note - not even in the slightest advocating the Kanin study should be considered accurate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How this can impact things is shown in <a href=\"http://www.datagoneodd.com/blog/2015/07/14/professor-twitter-and-the-problem-of-the-low-false-rape-narrative/\" target=\"_blank\">this blog post</a> as to how even a low percentage of false reports still shows a relevant problem existing. </div> </div> </div>Yes it is still a problem. But that was never really the point of any of this. Nobody is suggesting that purposeful false accusations are an acceptable thing (the closest thing I said was that you can't actually stop them from happening).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T06:55:15-08:00","id":1009310,"title":"","content":"The Kanin study has flaws and weaknesses, crap is too harsh, it has some value, but its has flaws, I admit that Kanin himself admitted that, it should be treated merely as a single piece of a much larger puzzle, that too many vested interests don't really want explored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T07:06:11-08:00","id":1009315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1009310#post1009310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Kanin study has flaws and weaknesses, crap is too harsh, it has some value, but its has flaws, I admit that Kanin himself admitted that, it should be treated merely as a single piece of a much larger puzzle, that too many vested interests don't really want explored.</div> </div> </div> </div>At best its a look into policing results of limited locations during a time that's probably not very relevant anymore, as the blogger notes.<br /> <br /> The other study, though, really comes across to me as being purposefully deceptive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T12:08:30-08:00","id":1009423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1009310#post1009310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Kanin study has flaws and weaknesses, crap is too harsh, it has some value, but its has flaws, I admit that Kanin himself admitted that, it should be treated merely as a single piece of a much larger puzzle, that too many vested interests don't really want explored.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any study that's unverifiable is crap as a scientific study. One of the principles of scientific inquiry is the ability to reproduce the results. Nobody can replicate Kanin's study to see if they get the same results from the same sources of data, because Kanin's never released which city the study was about. We have to completely trust him, which isn't how this is supposed to work.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/cor