ass=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1012050#post1012050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://2.bp.blogspot.com/-gX8cD61aeeM/WEQSfddqLVI/AAAAAAABIQw/olk7tBs2MWgSZYAQ5WbI_wK5fvBqgSb3wCLcB/s1600/coulter%2Btrump.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://2.bp.blogspot.com/-gX8cD61ae...er%2Btrump.jpg</a><br /> <br /> Yeah it seems Prez Trump has already sold out to Sachs and the other Banksters. The was quick.<br /> <br /> Anyone surprised? *crickets*</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't she talking about his immigration agenda?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T14:37:04-08:00","id":1012185,"title":"","content":"She was. Of course, it's fairly ridiculous for her to spout of on how the voters did what they could and anything Trump does not isn't our fault... considering she actively supported Trump. She thinks she's smart because she predicted Trump would win far in advance, but apparently wasn't smart enough to realize how bad of an idea that would be for her own personal ideological goals due to his lack of any commitment to any ideological goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T18:34:40-08:00","id":1013513,"title":"","content":"Honestly looking at Donald Trumps team, this is going to be bad, very, very, very bad, maybe worse then I expected.<br /> <br /> Fuck, what did you do to yourselves America.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T21:42:32-08:00","id":1013584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1013513#post1013513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly looking at Donald Trumps team, this is going to be bad, very, very, very bad, maybe worse then I expected.<br /> <br /> Fuck, what did you do to yourselves America.</div> </div> </div> </div>The body had an arm wrestling match with itself, and now that one hand has won over the other, it is unceremoniously shoving our collective head up our collective ass.<br /> <br /> We fucked ourselves against our better judgment, is what I'm saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T19:23:33-08:00","id":1014101,"title":"","content":"Trump's presidency might honestly be genuinely amusing just for the staggering amount of mistrust it generates between the American Right and the Republican Party. I'm kind of waiting for the screaming to begin over the &quot;traitor tax&quot; being rebuffed.<br /> <br /> Seriously, though, unless you guys get yourselves some electoral reform, this is going to keep happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T15:36:37-08:00","id":1014487,"title":"","content":"While significant voting reform would be nice, there are other factors at play. The Obama presidency didn't have as much clusterfucks in it because of things that could be solved with voting reforms. Fixing voting in this country isn't going to suddenly repair the norms that would have prevented things like the use of Continuing Resolution bills to try to ram through partisan legislation without discussion by attaching it to must pass laws, or stop an insane number of votes to repeal Obamacare that were never going to work while not passing a single bill to fix any of the broken parts of the law.<br /> <br /> If a significant number of voters are going to reward politicians that are focused on breaking the system instead of making it work, we're going to keep having a broken system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T17:44:05-08:00","id":1014537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1013513#post1013513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly looking at Donald Trumps team, this is going to be bad, very, very, very bad, maybe worse then I expected.<br /> <br /> Fuck, what did you do to yourselves America.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNah, I don't think so. I mean, things are bad and will likely get more messed up, sure, but America has survived much worse within the past century alone. Certain groups of people are going to get fucked over, harassed and bullied, but even under Hillary (or Bernie for that matter) that was still going to be a terrible thing that was always going to continue for a very, very long time. Trump and his team getting elected has just emboldened the jackassess to a degree.<br /> <br /> The fact is I think America is too big to fail and even the most jaded Calexiter or insane Neo-Confederate knows that. Plus, as a great man once said, &quot;Americans can always be counted on to do the right thing\u2026after they have exhausted all other possibilities&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bIn a couple of decades this whole Alt-Right nonsense will be seen as an embarrassing hangover that America went through in the past.<br /> <br /> \u200bThen again, people probably said the same thing about the KKK, Nazis, and Russian autocracy...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T18:18:30-08:00","id":1014559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1014537#post1014537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bNah, I don't think so. I mean, things are bad and will likely get more messed up, sure, but America has survived much worse within the past century alone. Certain groups of people are going to get fucked over, harassed and bullied, but even under Hillary (or Bernie for that matter) that was still going to be a terrible thing that was always going to continue for a very, very long time. Trump and his team getting elected has just emboldened the jackassess to a degree.<br /> <br /> The fact is I think America is too big to fail and even the most jaded Calexiter or insane Neo-Confederate knows that. Plus, as a great man once said, &quot;Americans can always be counted on to do the right thing\u2026after they have exhausted all other possibilities&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bIn a couple of decades this whole Alt-Right nonsense will be seen as an embarrassing hangover that America went through in the past.<br /> <br /> \u200bThen again, people probably said the same thing about the KKK, Nazis, and Russian autocracy...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the country is irrevocably doomed, but I'm not planning to spend the next presidential term waiting for the deplorable and delusional to tire themselves out, either. Now is the time for protest, petition, and organization.<br /> <br /> I'm getting ready for a long fight. I'm mostly concerned about my blood pressure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T18:34:26-08:00","id":1014564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1014559#post1014559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the country is irrevocably doomed, but I'm not planning to spend the next presidential term waiting for the deplorable and delusional to tire themselves out, either. Now is the time for protest, petition, and organization.<br /> <br /> I'm getting ready for a long fight. I'm mostly concerned about my blood pressure.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI look forward to watching that fight play out from my ivory tower, with popcorn in hand. It's sure to be a joyously divisive and horrific spectacle to behold. Hope you and your side come out on top. <br /> <br /> \u200bOh, and good luck with the blood pressure. You'll need it given America's health care system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T20:56:56-08:00","id":1014604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1014487#post1014487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While significant voting reform would be nice, there are other factors at play. The Obama presidency didn't have as much clusterfucks in it because of things that could be solved with voting reforms. Fixing voting in this country isn't going to suddenly repair the norms that would have prevented things like the use of Continuing Resolution bills to try to ram through partisan legislation without discussion by attaching it to must pass laws, or stop an insane number of votes to repeal Obamacare that were never going to work while not passing a single bill to fix any of the broken parts of the law.<br /> <br /> If a significant number of voters are going to reward politicians that are focused on breaking the system instead of making it work, we're going to keep having a broken system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fixing voting is a necessity. It makes solving future problems <i>possible</i> by shattering the bipartisan divide; by making the votes of a given state represent the state. It'd break the stranglehold the Democrats and Republicans have on the electoral system and end the problem of single issue voters.<br /> <br /> When you only have a binary option, extremes become the norm. If you want to end extremes and have productive conversations, you <i>need</i> to have moderation. That means attacking the root of the problem and the root of the problem is an unrepresentative government that minimizes party diversity in favour of maximizing the hegemony of the parties.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1014537#post1014537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact is I think America is too big to fai</div> </div> </div> </div>It's hard for me to respond to this because, generally, I'm the one telling other people to keep things in perspective. The truth is, the majority of politicians in office at the moment have one goal: Stay the course. Maintain the status quo. The truth is, while everyone says they want things to move forward, the majority <i>accept</i> how things are now. They might not <i>like</i> it, but they <i>accept</i> it. If they didn't, there'd be riots in the streets (well, more so). Bloodshed. The first strings of revolution.<br /> <br /> The fact is, for the majority of Americans, the next four years will see Trump have an indirect effect rather than a direct one.<br /> <br /> The thing is, though, the status quo is an illusion. It is one very carefully and very well maintained by the systems of governance and economics that are in place but it is well and truly illusory. The idea that there is something - <i>anything</i> - too big to fail has been proven again and again by history. The idea that just because too many people rely on it, too many lives depend upon it, too much harm would be caused by its downfall does nothing to prevent reality calling its payment due. Monarchies and democracies, empires and city-states, all have fallen into anarchy, terror, and chaos; all often carrying the certainty that they were immortal.<br /> <br /> <i>Nothing</i> is too big to fail. Inertia alone is not enough to guarantee survival. If your hope is that &quot;Eh, it can't happen&quot; because it hasn't yet, you are in for very grim surprises. Testament to this fact is that Britain is about four months away from possibly walking itself out back behind the shed and giving itself a shotgun tonsillectomy out of some naive belief that reducing its leverage at trade negotiations will somehow make it stronger.<br /> <br /> Truth be told, I'm not expecting the worst either, but not because anything is too big to fail; merely because the Republicans have spent the past eight years building an increasingly radical and rabid base that is demanding blood and they just... Aren't going to get it. The blood they promised will not manifest because at the end of the day, the Republican Party's first god is Mammon and always has been. There will be plenty of victims but the things people want - good-paying jobs - just won't manifest. Not in the numbers needed. The factories will remain in Mexico and China and Bangladesh and Haiti.<br /> <br /> Mammon likes things as they are. That won't change any time soon. So here we are.<br /> <br /> Phew...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T23:44:56-08:00","id":1014636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1014604#post1014604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fixing voting is a necessity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, though one has to agree on what the problems are before you can even start to pick the best approach to fixing them.<br /> <br /> Very few of the issues with the US voting system are binary things. Esp. since the US operates in a strange balance of each state being &quot;equals&quot; in power and the general public.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It makes solving future problems <i>possible</i> by shattering the bipartisan divide; by making the votes of a given state represent the state. It'd break the stranglehold the Democrats and Republicans have on the electoral system and end the problem of single issue voters. </div> </div> </div>Which fix exactly accomplishes all that? How is that fix at all practical? It sounds a lot less like a &quot;fix&quot; and a lot more like trying to amend the Constitution to completely alter the way elections are handled.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When you only have a binary option, extremes become the norm. </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's as true of the course of history as it needs to be to assert this. The US political system has gone through a number of waves of polarized extremes and pushes towards pragmatic centrism despite the Two Party approach. And while the politicians are hardly blameless, it comes down to the mood of the public. When the public is unified, moderation and bipartisanship rule the government. When the public is divided, ideological extremes are the norm.<br /> <br /> Everyone fears that this time the polarization will be so bad there's no turning back... but the ebb and flow of history - just as it suggests that all countries rise and fall over time - tells us this isn't the case. It's just how much damage a period of polarization does before it ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T06:35:30-08:00","id":1014728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1014559#post1014559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the country is irrevocably doomed, but I'm not planning to spend the next presidential term waiting for the deplorable and delusional to tire themselves out, either. Now is the time for protest, petition, and organization.<br /> <br /> I'm getting ready for a long fight. I'm mostly concerned about my blood pressure.</div> </div> </div> </div> Do you honestly think Donald Trump and his team care about protests, petititions, focus instead on organizing and reforming the democractics party, push out all the rot you can and make sure you have a uncorrupt candiate, with a progressive agenda, who focuses on working class issues like social programs, the economy, jobs, climate change, the working class, poverty, fighting neoliberalism, ect..., and keep the identity politics to a minium, some who is a uniter not a divider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T07:11:49-08:00","id":1014745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1014728#post1014728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you honestly think Donald Trump and his team care about protests, petititions, focus instead on organizing and reforming the democractics party, push out all the rot you can and make sure you have a uncorrupt candiate, with a progressive agenda, who focuses on working class issues like social programs, the economy, jobs, climate change, the working class, poverty, fighting neoliberalism, ect..., and keep the identity politics to a minium, some who is a uniter not a divider.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSo, basically focus on a white middle class base and leave African Americans, Hispanics, the LBGT, and Muslims hanging in the wind? I'm not sure that's really going to win any elections given that most of those marginalized groups only vote Democrat because they're terrified of the Republicans and their &quot;Fuck them all to Death&quot; attitude. Hell, I think most younger Democrats only vote Democrat because of the obvious (and much easier to understand than economics) identity politics that are going on. Without that the Democrats are just largely just Republicans in a donkey suit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T07:12:28-08:00","id":1014746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1014728#post1014728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you honestly think Donald Trump and his team care about protests, petititions, focus instead on organizing and reforming the democractics party, push out all the rot you can and make sure you have a uncorrupt candiate, with a progressive agenda, who focuses on working class issues like social programs, the economy, jobs, climate change, the working class, poverty, fighting neoliberalism, ect..., and keep the identity politics to a minium, some who is a uniter not a divider.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two things:<br /> 1. That's approximately what I meant. I don't expect to be able to influence Trump or his cabinet directly, but I can do what I can to manipulate the political system around them. <br /> 2. You could have asked me what I meant. Instead, it appears you decided to make assumptions and then mock what you presumed to be my methodology. Kindly do not do that again to me or anyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T07:16:53-08:00","id":1014750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1013584#post1013584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The body had an arm wrestling match with itself, and now that one hand has won over the other, it is unceremoniously shoving our collective head up our collective ass.<br /> <br /> We fucked ourselves against our better judgment, is what I'm saying.</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">What's with all this <i><b>we</b></i> stuff? All I know is that a bunch of people who happen to live in the same country as a couple of my buddies decided to do something incredibly (but predictably) stupid. I would never assortment them in any collective category as my buds.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">\u200b#NotAllAmericans</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T08:35:51-08:00","id":1014784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1014750#post1014750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">What's with all this <i><b>we</b></i> stuff? All I know is that a bunch of people who happen to live in the same country as a couple of my buddies decided to do something incredibly (but predictably) stupid. I would never assortment them in any collective category as my buds.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">\u200b#NotAllAmericans</span></div> </div> </div> </div>We don't exist in a vacuum. Just because I, personally, didn't contribute to Donald winning the election (and indeed voted against it, and my state was blue this time), doesn't mean I don't share in the responsibility for the results. I may have a lesser share of the responsibility than those who actively supported the man, but I also have a greater share of the responsibility than those who contributed money to his opposition's campaign, for example. As much as I disagree with the &quot;Donald is the American Left's fault&quot; narrative, it's still irresponsible not to accept that the election results were caused by a large number of factors and to try to address the factors that we could have affected. If we don't learn from this, we won't be able to stop it from happening again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T09:39:38-08:00","id":1014803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1014784#post1014784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We don't exist in a vacuum. Just because I, personally, didn't contribute to Donald winning the election (and indeed voted against it, and my state was blue this time), doesn't mean I don't share in the responsibility for the results. I may have a lesser share of the responsibility than those who actively supported the man, but I also have a greater share of the responsibility than those who contributed money to his opposition's campaign, for example. As much as I disagree with the &quot;Donald is the American Left's fault&quot; narrative, it's still irresponsible not to accept that the election results were caused by a large number of factors and to try to address the factors that we could have affected. If we don't learn from this, we won't be able to stop it from happening again.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat makes sense. More things could have been done an individual level to stop the rise of The Drumpf, even through I imagine that contributing financial resources to Hillary's campaign just wasn't in the cards for a lot of Left voters, and learning from one's mistakes is always a healthy project. It's just that the idea of looking at this whole incident as somehow being a collective mistake just bothers me fundamentally. As a black man I've blamed for somehow being responsible or a part of the &quot;lazy&quot;, &quot;criminal&quot;, and &quot;coonish&quot; activities that apparently exist in my demographic and as consequence I've always been wary of broad, generalized finger pointing of any kind, especially when it results in self-flagellation and misdirected guilt. Now of course internalized racism based on crap stereotypes and whether Americans on the Left should feel bad about their hand in this election isn't equivalent by any means but they both seem to have this blindspot in realizing the arseholes responsible for much of everything going wrong is from without not within.<br /> <br /> \u200bI dunno, I probably sound like an argumentative #NotAllMen fanatic right now, but I think that the Left's main priority right now should be figuring out how to defeat the opposition rather than feeling sorry about itself. That, and maybe reconsidering its push to the Centre-Left.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1675,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","user":"Weirdboyz","date":". 12-09-2016, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T09:41:04-08:00","id":1014804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1014784#post1014784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we don't learn from this, we won't be able to stop it from happening again.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> What I have seen, and what I continue to see (albeit a bit less) from the left is a complete lack of empathy for the right. Bluntly, the trend I see is for leftists to assume that the right (especially the alt-right) are knuckle-dragging throwbacks who are too stupid to understand that the world they want shouldn't exist and too stubborn to try to change. That, or that they're all amoral bastards who claim a loose moral high ground in order to justify preying on the weak and underprivileged - mostly for money. Consequently, we treat them as an enemy to be stomped down, shut out of society by social pressure, and left to starve.<br /> <br /> I know personally that it's hard to reach out, to try to understand people whose ideologies are truly antithetical to yours, and grasp what their priorities actually are. It's even harder to accept that, in some way, their priorities are actually correct and their actions are logical according to whatever assumptions their priorities are based on.<br /> <br /> Hardest of all is trying to change someone's core assumptions. But that's that only way I know to really change people's minds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T09:53:22-08:00","id":1014811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1014803#post1014803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThat makes sense. More things could have been done an individual level to stop the rise of The Drumpf, even through I imagine that contributing financial resources to Hillary's campaign just wasn't in the cards for a lot of Left voters, and learning from one's mistakes is always a healthy project. It's just that the idea of looking at this whole incident as somehow being a collective mistake just bothers me fundamentally. As a black man I've blamed for somehow being responsible or a part of the &amp;quot;lazy&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;criminal&amp;quot;, and &amp;quot;coonish&amp;quot; activities that apparently exist in my demographic and as consequence I've always been wary of broad, generalized finger pointing of any kind, especially when it results in self-flagellation and misdirected guilt. Now of course internalized racism based on crap stereotypes and whether Americans on the Left should feel bad about their hand in this election isn't equivalent by any means but they both seem to have this blindspot in realizing the arseholes responsible for much of everything going wrong is from without not within.<br /> <br /> \u200bI donna, I probably sound like an argumentative #NotAllMen fanatic right now, but I think that Left's main priority right now should be figuring out how to defeat the opposition rather than feeling sorry about itself. That, and maybe reconsidering its push to the Centre-Left.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I see where you're coming from, and I agree. Blaming the left isn't any more productive than telling ourselves there was nothing more we could have done. And learning from what happened means challenging the issues with the right as well as self-reflection on what we could have done better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T10:10:22-08:00","id":1014819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1014804#post1014804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This.<br /> <br /> What I have seen, and what I continue to see (albeit a bit less) from the left is a complete lack of empathy for the right. Bluntly, the trend I see is for leftists to assume that the right (especially the alt-right) are knuckle-dragging throwbacks who are too stupid to understand that the world they want shouldn't exist and too stubborn to try to change. That, or that they're all amoral bastards who claim a loose moral high ground in order to justify preying on the weak and underprivileged - mostly for money. Consequently, we treat them as an enemy to be stomped down, shut out of society by social pressure, and left to starve.<br /> <br /> I know personally that it's hard to reach out, to try to understand people whose ideologies are truly antithetical to yours, and grasp what their priorities actually are. It's even harder to accept that, in some way, their priorities are actually correct and their actions are logical according to whatever assumptions their priorities are based on.<br /> <br /> Hardest of all is trying to change someone's core assumptions. But that's that only way I know to really change people's minds.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOh, I have to agree with you there. Even within this very forum a strong sediment of &quot;fuck those people&quot; is going around. That being said, its not as if the Democrats haven't done their level best to try and educate and reach out to voters on the Right. As the Republicans have gone further and further Right, the Democrats have been increasingly Centrist (and quite honestly Centre-Right by European standards) for decades. To the point where real socialistic policies were almost entirely purged or shelved until Bernie showed up. Add that to the fact that almost every liberal news agencies, online paper, political critic, and Daily Show-wannabe has tried throughout this election, desperately and passionately, to show those on their Right, through facts and reason, that their politics are have been screwing the most improvised of them for years, and yet still get a Trump victory regardless...<br /> <br /> \u200bWell, look, their were definitely faults made by the Democrats during the election and statistics have shown that a full-term of any one party's reign gets long in the tooth for a lot of people, but I think attempting to try and change's one assumptions can be rather hopeless when someone would much rather listen to blatant lies and finds notions of universal equality a dangerous idea that will likely result in them losing their privileged status. How do you cater to that without losing your responsibility to marginalized groups?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T10:51:03-08:00","id":1014840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1014819#post1014819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bWell, look, their were definitely faults made by the Democrats during the election and statistics have shown that a full-term of any one party's reign gets long in the tooth for a lot of people, but I think attempting to try and change's one assumptions can be rather hopeless when someone would much rather listen to blatant lies and finds notions of universal equality a dangerous idea that will likely result in them losing their privileged status. How do you cater to that without losing your responsibility to marginalized groups?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you have to. I think part of the narrative that can get lost in the hyperbole generated on all parts of the political spectrum is that <i>most</i> Americans are more-or-less Centrist. They <i>aren't</i> unreasonable, self-deluding, or insistent on the idea that their rights must come at the expense of everyone else's. They are people who can be persuaded, as long as they feel like they're not being ignored or treated poorly.<br /> <br /> Going by the popular vote,<i> most</i> Americans voted for Hillary Clinton. <i>M</i><i>ost</i> Americans probably think the incoming administration will be somewhere in between &quot;incompetent&quot; and &quot;disasterous.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>Most</i> republicans did not vote for Trump in the republican primary. He won by a plurality, not a majority. He won a majority of the electoral college in the general election (apparently), but that doesn't mean most of the county or even his own party shares his values.<br /> <br /> Media of all kinds covering politics tends to behave - most of the time - as though both parties are equal in our two-party system, and each party is more or less unified in its values. Neither of those premises holds up if you look closely. It's a useful heuristic, but its important to remember that there is a wealth of diversity in these parties, and every sub-demographic has its own priorities.<br /> <br /> You don't need to court the hate groups - although, if you think you have any means of reforming them, I encourage you to try. Instead, you can to reach out to the excluded middle, the vast, heterogenous collection of &quot;normal&quot; people who voted Republican this year because they thought that would mean greater prosperity or security, and downplayed the potential hazards of a Trump administration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T11:23:00-08:00","id":1014849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1014750#post1014750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">What's with all this <i><b>we</b></i> stuff? All I know is that a bunch of people who happen to live in the same country as a couple of my buddies decided to do something incredibly (but predictably) stupid. I would never assortment them in any collective category as my buds.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">\u200b#NotAllAmericans</span></div> </div> </div> </div>We. It means I'm part of a community. It means my actions affect other people and their actions affect me. It means it's not all about me. It means I have no room to be fucking selfish, to sit pretty in my self-justification. It means I don't sit there while people's lives are burning down around them, that I don't get to sit in fucking smugness and say &quot;Well I didn't vote for Trump.&quot; It means I have to sit up and take accountability for my community, the sins that will be perpetrated against people I don't think deserve it. It means I have to <i>act</i>, that I have to be involved in the nations politics, that I have to be willing to lay my flesh down for people other than me, my family, and my friends. It means caring and getting angry on behalf of others.<br /> <br /> We, because #NotAllAmericans is a shit attitude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 12-09-2016, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T11:31:41-08:00","id":1014856,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I am reminded of the last speech of Ben Franklin at the Constitutional Convention (he was too sick and old and had a friend say it for him). Part of what he said was:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">&quot;... I agree to this Constitution, with all its faults - if they are such; because I think a general Government necessary for us, and there is no form of government but what may be a blessing to the people, if well administered; and I believe, farther, that this is likely to be well administered for a course of years, and can only end in despotism, as other forms have done before it, when the people shall become so corrupted as to need despotic government, being incapable of any other.&quot;<br /> <br /> I find myself agreeing with old Ben. The problems we are facing here in in the US (and in Italy and in Britain and so on) are not problems with forms of government. The problems are with a populace that is changing in fundamental ways, and is becoming (using Franklin's terminology) &quot;corrupted&quot;. In a democratic form of government, people have to be willing to compromise their own ideals for the sake of the general good, but that often isn't what's happening. Powerful groups on all sides of the political spectrum in many nations have learned that while they may not have the power to force through legislation they want, they can block legislation they don't want, even shutting everything down. They learned it in the US and also in Italy and elsewhere.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">In a despotic form of government, this doesn't happen. The despot has the power to ram through whatever he wants no matter what the other powers in society may think about it. That's what despots do. But this does not happen in a democracy. Groups must be willing to lose once in awhile, or let their opponents win a little bit once in awhile, but they refuse to do that today. So they decide to stop everything and everybody ends up with blocked government, which makes those who are currently doing well very happy indeed - because no changes mean they will continue to do well.</span></span><br /> <br /> People have to start being willing to lose and let the other guy win - the Republicans have certainly been the worst offenders in this regard, but even the Democrats are guilty of this. This sense of political gridlock is the biggest problem that many Americans have with their government (and Italians have with their government and many other people with their own governments).<br /> <br /> I think it's safe to say we haven't reached the point in time that Ben Franklin was thinking of when the people became so corrupted that they needed a despotic government, but I think we <i>are</i> beginning to get there. Many Americans voted for Trump, not so much because they agreed with his views, but because they thought of him as a strong person who would get things done - someone who could tear through the bureaucratic mess that is Washington and bring badly needed change.<br /> <br /> Basically, a lot of people voted for Trump because he has the dictatorial qualities that they have started to believe are necessary for an American leader because of the endemic problems with our form of government as they misunderstand what is happening. And while Trump isn't a dictator (I'd label him a Technocrat), the fact that this is the direction that a lot of Americans are beginning to turn is rather worrisome. And as long as there is a sense of political gridlock in Washington, those feelings on the part of the voters - that the government is inherently broken, are only going to continue to get worse and worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 12-09-2016, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T12:05:33-08:00","id":1014873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1014849#post1014849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We. It means I'm part of a community. It means my actions affect other people and their actions affect me. It means it's not all about me. It means I have no room to be fucking selfish, to sit pretty in my self-justification. It means I don't sit there while people's lives are burning down around them, that I don't get to sit in fucking smugness and say &quot;Well I didn't vote for Trump.&quot; It means I have to sit up and take accountability for my community, the sins that will be perpetrated against people I don't think deserve it. It means I have to <i>act</i>, that I have to be involved in the nations politics, that I have to be willing to lay my flesh down for people other than me, my family, and my friends. It means caring and getting angry on behalf of others.<br /> <br /> We, because #NotAllAmericans is a shit attitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bCool. Can I point out that I didn't actually say or want to imply that nothing should be done or that personal actions don't affect others or that being selfish was a viable option. It's just that we, or seemingly your use of the word, implies an absolute homogeneity within the American people that kind of forgets the very real differences between Americans their goals, desires, and ideology that can't be ignored or easily reconciled, which I'm sure you know. You can't really steer the ship anywhere when about half of your wants to go in an entirely different direction for a hundred different reasons that may be incompatible with your own.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, the #NotAllAmericans thing was a joke. It was supposed to be a parody of the #NotAllMen movement/clusterfuck. But, hey, if you still think I'm a smug asshole, indifferent jerk, I implore you to explore that anger and point it at me. Wouldn't want to explode on someone in the real world in a fit of pique. Rarely does something like that end well. Believe me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T13:28:39-08:00","id":1014923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1014840#post1014840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They <i>aren't</i> unreasonable, self-deluding, or insistent on the idea that their rights must come at the expense of everyone else's.</div> </div> </div> </div>They also don't vote, giving for more power to the people that cause the stereotyping about this. Recent polling showed that most Americans - regardless of party - know the major facts about the results of the election and various economic indicators (like the unemployment rate) correctly. The only group where more people believe the factually incorrect things polled on... were Trump voters.<br /> <br /> Even if those people only really represent ~10% of the total voting eligible population, it means a lot of people that could have been persuaded simply didn't vote (and this was frankly more important in the primaries where voter turnout among the majority of voters that don't fit the above stereotype is drastically lower); and Trump is only winning with ~26% of the popular vote.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1014856#post1014856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People have to start being willing to lose and let the other guy win - the Republicans have certainly been the worst offenders in this regard, but even the Democrats are guilty of this. This sense of political gridlock is the biggest problem that many Americans have with their government (and Italians have with their government and many other people with their own governments).</div> </div> </div> </div>Going beyond this, I think people also need to be willing to realize that they won. The idea that that the Republicans &quot;lost&quot; because of Obamacare is kind of silly when you look at the history of the legislation. The framework of Obamacare is a <i>conservative</i> pro-business alternative to universal healthcare. The Democrats dropping universal healthcare in favor of a conservative &quot;voucher&quot; style program to cover the people in the gap between public assistance and employee benefits was essentially a victory for the Republicans... that they then treated as a loss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T15:53:36-08:00","id":1014981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1014856#post1014856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[COLOR=#222222][FONT=arial]People have to start being willing to lose and let the other guy win - the Republicans have certainly been the worst offenders in this regard, but even the Democrats are guilty of this. This sense of political gridlock is the biggest problem that many Americans have with their government (and Italians have with their government and many other people with their own governments).</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of what I have read agrees that these are problems with the US today, but I don't know about generally. Matteo Renzi just lost his referendum that was intended to centralize power and reduce gridlock. From the perspective of Britain, no one really talks about political gridlock in the sense of, you know, governments can't pass legislation and everyone's blocking everything and so leaders are operating outside the normal channels of legislation (Obama's executive actions, etc.) and an activist / muscular judiciary are increasingly taking control of the actual process of generating law and managing government. It does seem like that actually is because of the particular political structures of the USA - note <a href=\"http://www.the-american-interest.com/2013/12/08/the-decay-of-american-political-institutions/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.the-american-interest.com...-institutions/</a>.<br /> <br /> With the cooperation / competition, &quot;willing to lose&quot; angle, one theory about why this happens is that with the big postwar boom of increasing mass education (and to a lesser extent the decline of discrimination), you ended up having a lot more people potentially ending up competing to hold power and influence. More &quot;elite aspirants&quot;. So competition between them becomes more ruthless and high stakes and selects for more ruthless competitors. I don't know if I totally believe it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T15:27:15-08:00","id":1015869,"title":"","content":"Has this thread brought up the news about investigations into Russia interfering in the election in Trump's favour yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T19:20:52-08:00","id":1015941,"title":"","content":"It's been touched on, but at this point it's mostly not really going to go anywhere until we have something meatier to discuss besides the confidence of the US intelligence agencies that Russia was responsible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T20:11:14-08:00","id":1015954,"title":"","content":"At this point I'm guessing if brought up, even if incontrovertible evidence is found, Trump and the GOP backers will just insist it doesn't matter for the next four years. As long as they're in charge, why should they care who put them there? I'm unaware of any specific laws involving foreign governments leaking some information but not all information so I don't think legally it would be an issue. Though I'm not a lawyer.<br /> <br /> Ideally a stronger candidate will come forward in other parties, and I'm sure with Trump as president they'll have ample opportunity to make a name for themselves.<br /> <br /> The conservatives seem happy, though. I can't really understand the viewpoint but wanting predatory capitalists, oil executives and the wives of politicians in charge of the government is apparently more appealing than Hillary Clinton. The white nationalists seem to be taking advantage of the new flow of support for similar ideals, they're revamping their image and trying to downplay the whole racism thing. They're just about 'nationalism' now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T22:37:57-08:00","id":1015989,"title":"","content":"Donald Trump made it his express opinion since practically day one that he wanted better, closer relations with Russia. Even if he did believe Russia was responsible for the hack, and even if he wasn't privately quite grateful for the hack, his stance would still probably be one that it's &quot;water under the bridge&quot; and the US should continue to have closer relations with Russia. <br /> <br /> So for Trump this is a non-issue. He doesn't want to pursue it and try to hold Russia accountable because doing so would obviously cause problems with his earlier &quot;pro-Russia&quot; stance. <br /> <br /> Further, it's unlikely that Congress is going to take any action without a smoking gun tying Russia to the hacks - the kind of evidence that one could use in a court of law (which unfortunately I doubt our Intelligence Agencies can produce). And absent that kind of definitive, hard evidence, I doubt Congress as a whole will be willing to act or stake a stance on it.<br /> <br /> Most likely the whole issue is basically already a dead one - it's just not the kind of thing to get a lot of traction with most Americans. Liberals might discuss it, but I just haven't found much evidence that conservatives are interested in pursuing it. In my experience the response from most conservatives when the hack is brought up, is that liberals are being &quot;sore losers&quot; for trying to blame Russia for their election losses rather than blaming themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T23:39:13-08:00","id":1015998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1015954#post1015954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm unaware of any specific laws involving foreign governments leaking some information but not all information so I don't think legally it would be an issue. Though I'm not a lawyer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there are laws against it, but not ones that would impact Trump.<br /> <br /> The bigger deal for Trump is the Logan Act, which bars citizens without federal authority from engaging in specific activities with foreign governments/agents. If Trump, or someone in Trump's campaign staff, asked the Russians to hack the Democrats, there's a set law against that. So if there's an investigation of the hacks, and finds any solid evidence that someone in the Trump campaign communicated with Russia about having the hacks happen, coupled with Trump's &quot;joke,&quot; about it, there would be a solid case for a Logan Act charge; which would be hard to ignore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can't really understand the viewpoint but wanting predatory capitalists, oil executives and the wives of politicians in charge of the government is apparently more appealing than Hillary Clinton. </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure mainstream conservatives are generally happy because the appointments so far are not the, &quot;lets blow up the system,&quot; picks that would indicate Trump actually plans on being a president that disrupts the current state of US politics. This is a sign that we're likely to see status-quo in D.C. with conservative policies being passed by the all Republican government.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T08:18:43-08:00","id":1016560,"title":"","content":"And I the only one open to the possiblity that the Russians weren't the ones to hack it? <br /> <br /> Hillary Clinton has earned many enemies over the years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T09:18:42-08:00","id":1016591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1016560#post1016560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I the only one open to the possiblity that the Russians weren't the ones to hack it? <br /> <br /> Hillary Clinton has earned many enemies over the years.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the intelligence agencies to take a stance that Russia is responsible... That takes them having access to convincing evidence of that. So, it's possible someone else is responsible, but if so, then it would probably be a case of them deliberately trying to frame Russia. <br /> <br /> And that starts to get a bit convoluted...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T10:08:09-08:00","id":1016619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1016591#post1016591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the intelligence agencies to take a stance that Russia is responsible... That takes them having access to convincing evidence of that. So, it's possible someone else is responsible, but if so, then it would probably be a case of them deliberately trying to frame Russia.<br /> <br /> And that starts to get a bit convoluted...</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://arstechnica.com/security/2016/12/the-public-evidence-behind-claims-russia-hacked-for-trump/\" target=\"_blank\">Publicly available information</a> ties the DNC hack to &quot;Fancy Bear&quot;, a known Russian hacking group. There's little doubt that it was Russian hackers. <br /> <br /> <i>However</i>, that doesn't necessarily mean the Kremlin ordered this - it could have been private hacktivists trying to influence the election. That said, the Kremlin does have a history of supporting citizen groups, such as <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nashi_(youth_movement)\" target=\"_blank\">Nashi</a>, who engage in these kinds of acts with the government's funding and tacit blessing. But then, if the Russian government supports a private organization that commits an act of cyberwar, who do you hold responsible?<br /> <br /> I don't know what the CIA knows. If they've gotten hold of intelligence that explicitly links Fancy Bear to any Russian official, I'd call that solid enough proof. But even if that were the case, I doubt that anyone in Russia will face legal consequences (from their own government) for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T10:12:32-08:00","id":1016622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1016560#post1016560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I the only one open to the possiblity that the Russians weren't the ones to hack it?<br /> <br /> Hillary Clinton has earned many enemies over the years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking it's all about Hillary is a bit narrow. Russia doesn't want the recent American stance on Russia to continue, because it's crushing their economy while they're trying to build up the EAEU.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T12:06:16-08:00","id":1016673,"title":"","content":"Yeah. The Russians were much more pro-Trump because of his very friendly to Russia stance, than anything to do with anti-Clinton animus.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that the Russians hacked everybody (from what we know now the RNC at least was hacked as well), and have been doing this for years (Obama, Mccain, and Romney were all hacked by the Russians as well).<br /> <br /> The difference this year is that in the past there hasn't been a pro-Russia candidate for Russia to get behind. This isn't the first time Russia has hacked the DNC/RNC or a presidential campaign. This is the first time there's evidence that they hacked and did anything with it to influence an election in their favor.<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> <br /> To be fair, I am open to the idea it wasn't the Russians in the sense of there's always the possibility that human knowledge is wrong. But the levels of certainty are high enough that skepticism falls on the side of Russians being responsible and against someone else doing it.<br /> <br /> This is one of the things I dislike about how skepticism gets used in modern discussions. People seem to want to use skepticism to follow down the Cartesian rabbit hole, and then stop and refuse to follow Descartes back up out following his reasoning on why you need to be willing to make assumptions about the world around you confidently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T17:35:42-08:00","id":1016833,"title":"","content":"Well, I read all 31 pages of this thread and I have say that while I disagree with a few running attitudes presented I respect the fact that the vast majority of disagreements and such in this thread have been largely devoid of personal attacks and shouting down that dominates social media outlets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12752-mist-walker","name":"Mist-Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12752_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T18:33:05-08:00","id":1016856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1016673#post1016673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. The Russians were much more pro-Trump because of his very friendly to Russia stance, than anything to do with anti-Clinton animus.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that the Russians hacked everybody (from what we know now the RNC at least was hacked as well), and have been doing this for years (Obama, Mccain, and Romney were all hacked by the Russians as well).<br /> <br /> The difference this year is that in the past there hasn't been a pro-Russia candidate for Russia to get behind. This isn't the first time Russia has hacked the DNC/RNC or a presidential campaign. This is the first time there's evidence that they hacked and did anything with it to influence an election in their favor.<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> <br /> To be fair, I am open to the idea it wasn't the Russians in the sense of there's always the possibility that human knowledge is wrong. But the levels of certainty are high enough that skepticism falls on the side of Russians being responsible and against someone else doing it.<br /> <br /> This is one of the things I dislike about how skepticism gets used in modern discussions. People seem to want to use skepticism to follow down the Cartesian rabbit hole, and then stop and refuse to follow Descartes back up out following his reasoning on why you need to be willing to make assumptions about the world around you confidently.</div> </div> </div> </div> Interesting perpective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T18:34:20-08:00","id":1016857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mist-Walker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1016833#post1016833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I read all 31 pages of this thread and I have say that while I disagree with a few running attitudes presented I respect the fact that the vast majority of disagreements and such in this thread have been largely devoid of personal attacks and shouting down that dominates social media outlets.</div> </div> </div> </div> Me too. Its been interesting and far more contructive then most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T17:11:34-08:00","id":1017863,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I've never understood the panic over Trump. He's basically a Reagan Democrat, who ran on a variant of the Democratic platform from the Nineties. <br /> <br /> For example, the whole &quot;deportation&quot; issue. I followed the Republican primaries this year, and dug into the various candidate's position papers. Trump didn't run on deporting anyone - he's actually advocating &quot;touchback amnesty&quot;, which was a <i>Democratic</i> proposal endorsed by the New York Times, back in the Nineties. Under his proposal, anyone kicked out by the Trump Administration will immediately move to the front of the line for the next batch of immigration slots. Inconvenient, perhaps, but hardly a &quot;the brownshirts are coming to get you&quot; moment.<br /> <br /> Or gay rights. Even back during the primaries, Trump was very pro-LGBT, making a point of posing with the rainbow flag, having gay speakers introduce him, criticizing the bathroom bills . . . And since the election, he's come out in support of gay marriage. I'm not really sure what else people want him to do, but my Facebook feed has been full of people freaking out about Trump and LGBT rights for weeks now. <br /> <br /> So I really don't understand the collective freak out* so many Democrats have been having. Democratic pundits have been saying for years that the Republicans will have to moderate (i.e. become more like Democrats), and, well, they have. Pro-Social Security &amp; universal healthcare, anti-Wall Street . . . Trump's probably the most moderate candidate the Republicans have fielded since, oh, the Rockefeller days. There's a reason he and Bill Clinton used to hang out, after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *now, if Sen. Ted Cruz had just been elected, <i>then</i> I could understand the panic, given just how conservative/right wing he is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T18:13:15-08:00","id":1017885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1017863#post1017863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, I've never understood the panic over Trump. He's basically a Reagan Democrat, who ran on a variant of the Democratic platform from the Nineties.<br /> <br /> For example, the whole &quot;deportation&quot; issue. I followed the Republican primaries this year, and dug into the various candidate's position papers. Trump didn't run on deporting anyone - he's actually advocating &quot;touchback amnesty&quot;, which was a <i>Democratic</i> proposal endorsed by the New York Times, back in the Nineties. Under his proposal, anyone kicked out by the Trump Administration will immediately move to the front of the line for the next batch of immigration slots. Inconvenient, perhaps, but hardly a &quot;the brownshirts are coming to get you&quot; moment.<br /> <br /> Or gay rights. Even back during the primaries, Trump was very pro-LGBT, making a point of posing with the rainbow flag, having gay speakers introduce him, criticizing the bathroom bills . . . And since the election, he's come out in support of gay marriage. I'm not really sure what else people want him to do, but my Facebook feed has been full of people freaking out about Trump and LGBT rights for weeks now.<br /> <br /> So I really don't understand the collective freak out* so many Democrats have been having. Democratic pundits have been saying for years that the Republicans will have to moderate (i.e. become more like Democrats), and, well, they have. Pro-Social Security &amp; universal healthcare, anti-Wall Street . . . Trump's probably the most moderate candidate the Republicans have fielded since, oh, the Rockefeller days. There's a reason he and Bill Clinton used to hang out, after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *now, if Sen. Ted Cruz had just been elected, <i>then</i> I could understand the panic, given just how conservative/right wing he is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Reagan democrat implies a kind of social backsliding since the 80s were 30 years ago and we've broken down a fair number of social barriers since then. He's also gathered much, much consistently worse people around him, such as Bannon, which puts terrible things that he's said into much more serious territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T18:32:01-08:00","id":1017897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1017863#post1017863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I really don't understand the collective freak out* so many Democrats have been having. Democratic pundits have been saying for years that the Republicans will have to moderate (i.e. become more like Democrats), and, well, they have. Pro-Social Security &amp; universal healthcare, anti-Wall Street . . . Trump's probably the most moderate candidate the Republicans have fielded since, oh, the Rockefeller days. There's a reason he and Bill Clinton used to hang out, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because he keeps tweeting stuff like \u201cNobody should be allowed to burn the American flag \u2014 if they do, there must be consequences \u2014 perhaps loss of citizenship or year in jail!\u201d, ran his campaign on implicit threats to racial minorities, and promises to elect conservative justices to the supreme court (who likely WOULD be anti-LGBT rights, even if Trump himself is not). Plus, he's got Steve Bannon (the Alt-Right provocateur) as his chief strategist, Ricky Perry (who wanted to abolish his dept.) as Sec. of Energy, Scott Pruitt (climate-change denier) for EPA, and Steven Mnuchin (forclosure profiteer) for Treasury among his starting cabinet picks.<br /> <br /> If discovering that he's really a hypocrite who will only pay lip service to his campaign promises is the <i>best</i> outcome, I don't want to see the worst. Possibly we're all crying that the sky is falling and in four years we'll look back at this and laugh. But right now, it really does look like a lot of the progress we've made in social, technological, economic, and environmental policy is at risk of going out the window. I think concern is more than justified.<br /> <br /> Oh, and Mike Pence is VP, in case you forgot. He's fought against gay rights and for &quot;religious freedoms&quot; for years.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter to me if the policies are what Democrats espoused in the nineties - <i>we're not in the nineties. </i>People have changed, moved on, learned new things and shifted their priorities. Gay marriage was taboo in the nineties. Broken Windows was cool in the nineties. Women in the military were just barely denting the combat barrier in the nineties. I was born in the nineties, and I can't say I thought it was that great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 12-15-2016, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T19:12:05-08:00","id":1017907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1017863#post1017863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or gay rights. Even back during the primaries, Trump was very pro-LGBT, making a point of posing with the rainbow flag, having gay speakers introduce him, criticizing the bathroom bills . . . And since the election, he's come out in support of gay marriage. I'm not really sure what else people want him to do, but my Facebook feed has been full of people freaking out about Trump and LGBT rights for weeks now.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about not hiring a man who has literally advocated for defunding AIDS research in favor of funding &quot;conversion therapy&quot; programs as his VP, for starters? I don't care what Donald claims to support, because he has made it abundantly clear that his word is completely worthless. What I care about is his actions, and no amount of posing with flags makes up for handing that much power to a man who would rather pay people to torture LGBT children into conformity or suicide than pay people to research treatment for a life-threatening disease that affects people of all genders and sexual orientations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T19:30:22-08:00","id":1017914,"title":"","content":"Another thing is that Trump has basically spewed out every position possible on many key issues. Not just things he said 10 years ago vs. now, but even during the campaign.<br /> <br /> That's a huge part of the &quot;freak out.&quot; We don't know which Trump we're actually going to get. Do we get the pragmatic business man who avoids the culture wars because discrimination is bad for business, or do we get the fiery radical that's said a Muslim registry would be a good idea? I don't know. Nobody knows. And not knowing is scary as hell.<br /> <br /> The only indicator we have are his actions during the interim from the election to inauguration... we have not been reassuring. As noted, whatever Trump says and thinks, he's surrounded by people that we have every reason to be worried about. It's scary that the least problematic appointments we're seeing are minor appointments for his major campaign contributors (yes, he has those, and some of them seem to be getting to pay to play), or nepotism (Cho isn't really an offensive choice, but she's also Mitch McConnell's wife which gets weird politically). Things that in most years would be disqualifying are ignored because so many of the other picks are just that bad.<br /> <br /> So, why are people worried? Because Trump's said a lot of things. But if you're concerned about the fights over oil pipelines and Native lands (not just Standing Rock, there's other fights on the horizon), are you going to trust in Trump wanting to be the president of all Americans, or look at what Rick Perry's public history on energy concerns and get freaked out? You're going to look at Perry and freak out.<br /> <br /> Also, there's the huge amount of rather ignored foreign influences on Trump. If the UAE is doing something against the USA's interests, how far is Trump going to do to defend us, when the UAE can privately threaten to stop shielding him from the massive human rights violations his company (and many others) are guilty of there? He never got his tax returns to try to start tracking down how bad these things might be, but what people have managed to turn up about Trumps obligations to foreign powers are not pretty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T18:39:59-08:00","id":1018288,"title":"","content":"In consideration that even if we take it at face value the &quot;best&quot; scenario situation that Trump is nothing but a narcissistic blowhard who is all talk, which is hardly a comfort. That does nothing to address the fact that there are literally millions of people who DO take what he says seriously as fuel to their already insane conspiracies that they are quite zealous to vote on, does nothing to address the ever increasingly zealousness of a Republican party that isn't simple engaging in ever increasingly bizarre and dangerous forms of purity politics, but also is using legalism to gerrymander district, enact voter suppression, and in the case of areas like N.C. are even using a loss to attempt to enact legislation to increase their own power by taking it from their opposition. It does nothing to address the already significant damage that the party has done to America for decades that they are looking to expand upon.<br /> <br /> Nothing in his cabinet choices suggests that the people put in it are anything more than out of touch rich people that for the most part are diametrically opposed to the purpose of the stations they've been appointed to. Trump himself doesn't have to be an ideologue of their ilk to cause massive harm both in an immediate sense or for generations to come. He simply has to create a playground for the people that are to work freely within. And not a damn thing so far suggests to the otherwise. This isn't a Democrat vs Republic thing. This is increasingly a rational people vs dangerously irrational people thing. If BLM, Bernie Sanders or any of the actual progressive figures in America received even half so much of the benefit of the doubt that some of the white nationalists and others associated with Trump have been given America would look rather different and no amount of tone policing attempts here or otherwise are going to change that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T08:39:07-08:00","id":1019259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BB38DvTV5kc\" data-code=\"BB38DvTV5kc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/BB38DvTV5kc/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> WOW. <br /> <br /> I...almost don't even know what to say to this. Except that the truly awful thing here, is that as Mr. Trump <i>blatantly admits to lying</i> and saying whatever would get him elected to his own supporters, that instead of slowly lowering their placards in shock and booing him, like most sensible folks would, they are going to go home and somehow rationalize this entire thing, probably based on the idea that &quot;well, at least our side didn't lose&quot;! <br /> <br /> The guy isn't even in office yet, and he's already weasled out of most of his promises! What's it going to take before we start seeing some real outrage from the supporters who finally wake up and realize that they're just his victims, too??<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The human propensity for self-deception is matched only by its skill at self-destruction...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T09:18:26-08:00","id":1019286,"title":"","content":"I remember reading an article in my local newspaper (yeah, I still get one) a few weeks ago.<br /> <br /> It mentioned how many presidential candidates run into problems when they fail to fulfill campaign promises. But compared to those guys, many of Trump's supporters polled said they wouldn't be very upset if Trump were to back out on his promises, with many stating they never believed he would fulfill them in the first place. On top of that, many liberals would be thrilled if Trump backed out on many of his campaign promises, putting Trump in the extremely unusual situation where not fulfilling the things he promised would very likely end up improving his popularity with the populous overall.<br /> <br /> So the thing is, most Trump supporters took the things he said seriously, but not literally. They knew he wasn't going to follow through on many, or even a lot, of the more hyperbolic things he said on the campaign trail, but many people were simply excited at finally having someone the political stage say the sorts of things they've been thinking for a long time. Plus, you know, a lot of people supported him because he wasn't Hillary Clinton, Jeb Bush or another career politician.<br /> <br /> All that said, I do find it rather amusing that as Trump has backed down on many of his more controversial positions, such as appointing a special prosecutor to investigate Hillary, or building a physical wall along the Mexican border, it seems as though liberals are much more mad about him backing down on those positions than conservatives are. You'd think they'd be happier about that...<br /> <br /> *EDIT* And I mean, to be fair with Hillary Clinton's statements about how she has a &quot;public&quot; and &quot;private&quot; position on different issues, she also admitted to blatantly lying to people in order to get herself elected. I think that's just one of those things that people are fairly realistic about - you can't get elected to political office if you tell the truth. But a lot of Trump's supporters were glad that, unlike other politicians, he was &quot;telling it like it is&quot; even if he wasn't going to actually carry through on everything he said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 12-19-2016, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T11:41:10-08:00","id":1019352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1019259#post1019259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BB38DvTV5kc\" data-code=\"BB38DvTV5kc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/BB38DvTV5kc/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> WOW.<br /> <br /> I...almost don't even know what to say to this. Except that the truly awful thing here, is that as Mr. Trump <i>blatantly admits to lying</i> and saying whatever would get him elected to his own supporters, that instead of slowly lowering their placards in shock and booing him, like most sensible folks would, they are going to go home and somehow rationalize this entire thing, probably based on the idea that &quot;well, at least our side didn't lose&quot;!<br /> <br /> The guy isn't even in office yet, and he's already weasled out of most of his promises! What's it going to take before we start seeing some real outrage from the supporters who finally wake up and realize that they're just his victims, too??<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The human propensity for self-deception is matched only by its skill at self-destruction...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps the starkest reminder for me of where this is all going was in North Carolina recently. The Republican legislation there, angry that people don't vote how they &quot;should&quot; have and got rid of Mcrory and now basically couping the incumbent gov. by crafting legislation to take power from the governor's office and give it to themselves or other Republican controlled groups, a move I have no problem calling seditious. People angry, particularly at other actions they're taking to gut the public education system there, held up a number of signs. One said that the eyes of the nation were watching. That's it though, no one is watching. Not where it counts anyway.<br /> <br /> On another note, no liberals are not mad that he's backing down on his more insane positions. It's far more that he doesn't seem to have anything even remotely coherent enough to truly have much of a position at all, and is appointing a disturbing cabinet,etc that DO have positions that are dangerous and destructive. Trump doesn't have to be an intelligent ideologue to be dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T14:59:08-08:00","id":1019436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1019286#post1019286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*EDIT* And I mean, to be fair with Hillary Clinton's statements about how she has a &quot;public&quot; and &quot;private&quot; position on different issues, she also admitted to blatantly lying to people in order to get herself elected. I think that's just one of those things that people are fairly realistic about - you can't get elected to political office if you tell the truth. But a lot of Trump's supporters were glad that, unlike other politicians, he was &quot;telling it like it is&quot; even if he wasn't going to actually carry through on everything he said.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course... this isn't true. Which has been a constant problem this year.<br /> <br /> Clinton never admitted to lying to get herself election. And the &quot;public and private&quot; position in the context of the speech she was giving, was discussing the process of successfully turning campaign promises into reality as being inherently unsavory to the public. She compared it to making sausages. The difference she was clearly talking about was the public image of selling legislation, and the private behind-closed-doors political process of negotiations and compromises that actually makes up politics.<br /> <br /> And if people actually cared about telling the truth, Trump would have lost in a crushing Clinton landslide. He made it abundantly clear that people aren't being realistic about this, and vote for the people that &quot;tells it like they want to hear,&quot; not the one that tells it like it is. Because he couldn't get through a single public appearance without getting caught in a lie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T15:13:13-08:00","id":1019443,"title":"","content":"Again, I think for the most part Trump's supporters cared more about the sentiments behind Trump's words than the actual words themselves (taking what he said seriously but not literally) which is why they generally didn't care that the words he was saying might not have made sense or might have come across as lies. I think that's something that many liberals and many people in the media never managed to understand, and why so many people couldn't comprehend how Trump's support would rise even after he'd say the dumbest stuff.<br /> <br /> But, it's all kind of irrelevant at this point - Trump's been confirmed as the next president, most of his supporters are pretty happy with what he's been doing and saying so far even though he's backtracked on a fair number of his more incendiary campaign statements and promises.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T15:28:00-08:00","id":1019450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1019436#post1019436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And if people actually cared about telling the truth, Trump would have lost in a crushing Clinton landslide. He made it abundantly clear that people aren't being realistic about this, and vote for the people that &quot;tells it like they want to hear,&quot; not the one that tells it like it is. Because he couldn't get through a single public appearance without getting caught in a lie.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mr. Pot, allow me to introduce you to Mr. Kettle...<br /> <br /> To compare Trump's lies and walkbacks to Clinton's long and storied career of lying, fraud, criminal acts and corruption is quite laughable. He is an amateur compared to her. Yes, Trump is a rather large douchebag. But if he delivers on even just one of his promises, he will deliver on more than any president in over 25 years.<br /> <br /> Just about anyone was preferable to Clinton. I'd wager that like me, many if not most of the Trump &quot;supporters&quot; that get hyped on the MSN and facebook don't actually support Trump all that much per se. Rather, they (or should it be we?) simply opposed Clinton. Trump was just the form that our Gozer took.<br /> <br /> But as of 5:35 P.M. EST, with 304 Electoral votes, none of the second guessing, armchair quarterbacking, name calling, histrionics, or other endeavors to deny the outcome makes any difference.<br /> <br /> HILLARY CLINTON WILL NEVER BE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES.<br /> <br /> Being able to say that, just in itself, makes having to put up with Trump for the next four years worth it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10978-azenogoth","name":"Azenogoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10978_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T16:13:06-08:00","id":1019474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1019450#post1019450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if he delivers on even just one of his promises, he will deliver on more than any president in over 25 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>President Obama came through on about half of his.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Being able to say that, just in itself, makes having to put up with Trump for the next four years worth it. </div> </div> </div>Enjoy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T17:49:49-08:00","id":1019523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1019443#post1019443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, I think for the most part Trump's supporters cared more about the sentiments behind Trump's words than the actual words themselves (taking what he said seriously but not literally) which is why they generally didn't care that the words he was saying might not have made sense or might have come across as lies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Were lies. Blatant, easily demonstrated, lies. There are countless clips (take them for what you will given they're just reporters talking to people at rallies and such) of Trump supporters being confronted with actual lies Trump has spewed for over a year. They didn't care. &quot;Politicians all lie,&quot; even as they're voting for someone on the grounds that he's not a politician.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But, it's all kind of irrelevant at this point - Trump's been confirmed as the next president, most of his supporters are pretty happy with what he's been doing and saying so far even though he's backtracked on a fair number of his more incendiary campaign statements and promises. </div> </div> </div>Sorta? He's backtracked, or hedged, or just flat out stated both sides, on plenty of them. And it seems to be working if people think he's backtracked on pretty much anything instead of trying to play the radical guy shaking things up and the pragmatist that's going to work for all Americans at the same time in different formats and he's paying no price for being completely two-faced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1019450#post1019450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mr. Pot, allow me to introduce you to Mr. Kettle...</div> </div> </div> </div>Mr Azenogoth, I'd like to introduce you to Mr. Truth, you don't seem to know him when you see him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To compare Trump's lies and walkbacks to Clinton's long and storied career of lying, fraud, criminal acts and corruption is quite laughable. </div> </div> </div>Yes, just in the complete opposite fashion of what you're claiming. Clinton's never been found guilty of anything in court... Trump has repeatedly (even if in civil courts instead of criminal ones). Just as an example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just about anyone was preferable to Clinton. </div> </div> </div>Hyperbolic nonsense. I hope you enjoy the future you voted for were the wealthiest Americans get paid millions in tax payer money to &quot;only&quot; ship half of the jobs out of the country instead of all of them, because that's already what Trump has done with Pence before he's even president.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd wager that like me, many if not most of the Trump &quot;supporters&quot; that get hyped on the MSN and facebook don't actually support Trump all that much per se. Rather, they (or should it be we?) simply opposed Clinton. Trump was just the form that our Gozer took. </div> </div> </div>Most of the polls around the election (rather than significantly before it) say about 50/50. Of course, voting against the other candidate has been between 33-55% of the prime reason in most modern elections. So there's nothing new here. ~47% of Romney voters were voting against Obama... so Trump did all of 3% &quot;better&quot; in that regard.<br /> <br /> Republican candidates also usually do worse in this regard, as in getting more voters that are anti-other than pro-Republican. Clinton voters only polled ~40% anti-Trump as a primary motivation in comparison.<br /> <br /> All this really shows is how good the Republicans are at getting their voters to vote based on mudraking over facts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Being able to say that, just in itself, makes having to put up with Trump for the next four years worth it. </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you feel comfortable with that. It means to me that I need to go back and get my firearms licenses re-upped so I feel more safe with all the neo-Nazi alt right doucebags running around talking about how in Trump's American I should be gassed to death.<br /> <br /> But those of us in that position are used to the inane selfishness of voters that don't care about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T18:27:27-08:00","id":1019539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1019523#post1019523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm glad you feel comfortable with that. It means to me that I need to go back and get my firearms licenses re-upped so I feel more safe with all the neo-Nazi alt right doucebags running around talking about how in Trump's American I should be gassed to death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, all of the tens of millions of neo-Nazi's running around... I mean, how many neo-Nazi's <i>are</i> running around? Oh, at their <a href=\"http://www.pennlive.com/news/2016/11/neo-nazis_outnumbered_by_count.html\" target=\"_blank\">big rally last month</a> one of the largest neo-Nazi groups in America managed to get a whole 50 people to show up for their protest. Scary. Honestly the fear of neo-Nazi's is somewhat overblown, probably about on par with worries of Islamic terrorism.<br /> <br /> That said, it's always a good idea to get your any kind of firearms licenses re-upped regardless of who currently happens to have political power. You never know when you might find yourself in a position where you need to protect yourself or your family, whether from a neo-Nazi, a radical Islamist, a mugger, or a mass shooter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T18:31:46-08:00","id":1019542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1019539#post1019539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, all of the tens of millions of neo-Nazi's running around... I mean, how many neo-Nazi's <i>are</i> running around? Oh, at their <a href=\"http://www.pennlive.com/news/2016/11/neo-nazis_outnumbered_by_count.html\" target=\"_blank\">big rally last month</a> one of the largest neo-Nazi groups in America managed to get a whole 50 people to show up for their protest. Scary. Honestly the fear of neo-Nazi's is somewhat overblown, probably about on par with worries of Islamic terrorism.</div> </div> </div> </div>This may come as a shock to you, but people who attend neo-nazi rallies are not the only dangerous bigots who have been emboldened by the results of the election.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T19:23:09-08:00","id":1019564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1019542#post1019542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may come as a shock to you, but people who attend neo-nazi rallies are not the only dangerous bigots who have been emboldened by the results of the election.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was responding to Heavy Arms who mentioned neo-Nazi's.<br /> <br /> But I do agree that there have been quite a few people on the left and the right have called for violence in the wake of the election.<br /> <br /> Still, I think most of it's talk, and figure your chances of actually being assaulted by a neo-Nazi's or alt-right douchebags attempting to gas you to death are probably comparable to getting caught up in an Islamic terrorist attack or a mass shooting. If you do get assaulted or attacked it's more likely to be a simple criminal or mugger. Just like the fears of being in a radical Islamic terrorist attack are rather overblown, I think the fear of being attacked by neo-Nazi's or similar people is rather overblown.<br /> <br /> Still, like I said, it certainly never hurts to take steps to protect yourself from such a thing occurring, just in case - with the added benefit that taking steps to keep yourself safe from neo-Nazi's and alt-right douchebags will probably also keep you safe from all the other people who are realistically much more likely to pose a threat to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T22:43:42-08:00","id":1019623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1019564#post1019564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was responding to Heavy Arms who mentioned neo-Nazi's.<br /> <br /> But I do agree that there have been quite a few people on the left and the right have called for violence in the wake of the election.<br /> <br /> Still, I think most of it's talk, and figure your chances of actually being assaulted by a neo-Nazi's or alt-right douchebags attempting to gas you to death are probably comparable to getting caught up in an Islamic terrorist attack or a mass shooting. If you do get assaulted or attacked it's more likely to be a simple criminal or mugger. Just like the fears of being in a radical Islamic terrorist attack are rather overblown, I think the fear of being attacked by neo-Nazi's or similar people is rather overblown.<br /> <br /> Still, like I said, it certainly never hurts to take steps to protect yourself from such a thing occurring, just in case - with the added benefit that taking steps to keep yourself safe from neo-Nazi's and alt-right douchebags will probably also keep you safe from all the other people who are realistically much more likely to pose a threat to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two words of political jargon, useful.idiots. I mean knocking over fascist strawmen is fun and whatnot but that's not how the sausage of oligarchy is made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T04:01:50-08:00","id":1019695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1019523#post1019523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...so I feel more safe with all the neo-Nazi alt right doucebags running around talking about how in Trump's American I should be gassed to death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Much like the mythical unicorn or successful socialist country, I keep hearing about this, but never actually see it. Except for the cases that are shown to be hoaxes performed by leftists seeking attention or sympathy. If this actually does happen to you, it is wrong. But swimming in the sewer of 4chan or some similar places is sure to get you death threats no matter who or what you are. There are a lot of crazy and messed up people in the world. Some of them happen to wrap themselves in certain uniforms.<br /> <br /> But unlike the reported neo-nazi and fascist (which are both left wind socialist ideologies, not sure why people keep using those terms to describe anyone who oppose leftism) attacks that never seem to happen, leftists and members of the Free Shit Army (FSA) HAVE been out rioting, looting, attacking, and hurting people. Both before the election and after. Electors HAVE been getting death threats and doxxed. The only documented acts of violence seem to be coming from the left. And to paint anyone who voted for Trump as a neo-nazi fascist who wants to kill you and your way of life seems to be a lot of projection. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1019523#post1019523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But those of us in that position are used to the inane selfishness of voters that don't care about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>As opposed to the selfishness of the voters who want to take the money earned by others in order to give it to themselves without working for it? It may be anecdotal, and come as a shock to you, but everyone I know and read on the right doesn't scheme over ways to screw you over and ruin your life. All we want is to be left alone by you and the overreaching government.<br /> <br /> If the divide between those of us who want to be left alone and those who want to rule every facet of our lives is so great that any difference of opinion is met with death threats and demonization, then perhaps it's time for a national divorce. The coastal city states could try to engineer their utopian societies, and us inbred redneck unwashed hillbillies in flyover land can have our freedom to do as we wish.<br /> <br /> Everybody wins!<br /> <br /> Or is that not amicable enough?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10978-azenogoth","name":"Azenogoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10978_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T04:07:46-08:00","id":1019700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1019539#post1019539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, all of the tens of millions of neo-Nazi's running around.</div> </div> </div> </div>It only takes one shitheel with a gun to kill a lot of people. <br /> <br /> Also, I know where I live. And we have a lot of skinheads, alt-right, and neo-Nazis. Plain and simple fact is my state is lousy with them. One of the founders of Keystone United (who was convicted of terrorizing a black man) is currently an elected official about 1.5 hrs from where I live. Hell, I live in KU's home territory.<br /> <br /> So, you know, just because you get to be safe and happy and secure away from that, doesn't mean everyone else is.<br /> <br /> I'm a hell of a lot safer from Islamists, because they don't give two shits about a small rural town in the middle of nowhere PA. There are bars I don't go near here, because simply being harassed would represent the best possible outcome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You never know when you might find yourself in a position where you need to protect yourself or your family, whether from a neo-Nazi, a radical Islamist, a mugger, or a mass shooter. </div> </div> </div>Well, yes, but only one of those groups is a group I've ever had to actually defend myself against physically... guess which? Hint, it didn't happen when I was being openly Jewish and walking around in the West Bank.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1019564#post1019564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, I think most of it's talk, and figure your chances of actually being assaulted by a neo-Nazi's or alt-right douchebags attempting to gas you to death are probably comparable to getting caught up in an Islamic terrorist attack or a mass shooting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on who you are and where you live. That's the thing about hate crimes. You can't just flat compare them to general crime rates because they are targeting specific people. The odds of being subjected to hate crimes for the general public are extremely small, but that's because the majority of the country aren't people that are targeted for hate crimes... which makes comparing them pointless. It's like including all the people in the country that don't have testes as &quot;surviving&quot; when calculating the mortality rates of testicular cancer; it just doesn't work that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you do get assaulted or attacked it's more likely to be a simple criminal or mugger. </div> </div> </div>Statistically sure. That doesn't make it a non-zero risk though.<br /> <br /> [quote...]I think the fear of being attacked by neo-Nazi's or similar people is rather overblown.[/quote]<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm biased, but I disagree rather adamantly.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T04:49:21-08:00","id":1019714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1019695#post1019695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Much like the mythical unicorn or successful socialist country, I keep hearing about this, but never actually see it.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I never see it, so it can't be true.&quot; Ignorance is bliss I guess...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And to paint anyone who voted for Trump as a neo-nazi fascist who wants to kill you and your way of life seems to be a lot of projection. </div> </div> </div>Good thing I didn't do that. I'm perfectly happy to hold rather negative views of people that decided to hold their noses and vote for Trump despite it though.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm pretty sure it's not a good way to defend your position... you know the thing where you just lie about what I said and respond to ridiculous strawmen instead. It betrays.. a lack of confidence in your convictions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As opposed to the selfishness of the voters who want to take the money earned by others in order to give it to themselves without working for it? </div> </div> </div>Yes, selfishly voting for a candidate that's actually promised to screw over people besides you is something that should be opposed instead of the non-existent lie of the &quot;socialist leech,&quot; voter.<br /> <br /> Of course, if you don't like people that make their money by taking money and other items of value from other people for themselves without working for it... you should really, really, hate Trump... because that's basically his whole business model. He even brags about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It may be anecdotal, and come as a shock to you, but everyone I know and read on the right doesn't scheme over ways to screw you over and ruin your life </div> </div> </div>That's not the problem. Their ignorance of the lives they're screwing over is the problem; esp. after some of us have spent years trying to say, &quot;hey that's screwing me over, stop that please.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All we want is to be left alone by you and the overreaching government. </div> </div> </div>No, they don't. They want their overreaching government to screw over people that threaten their ability to be left alone.<br /> <br /> As evidenced by conservative state-level politics across the country, government overreach is fine if to those voters as long as they don't feel targeted by it. And they do not vote with the idea of it targeting others as a consequence of their choices; hence selfish. If they cared about stopping overreach for all, Trump would have never gotten past the primaries, because Libertarians (and actual ones, not Republicans looking for a different party/ideological label) would be getting all those votes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the divide between those of us who want to be left alone and those who want to rule every facet of our lives is so great that any difference of opinion is met with death threats and demonization, then perhaps it's time for a national divorce. </div> </div> </div>Well, if you want to come at this by demonizing the other side from the get go... why are you expecting them to respond well exactly?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The coastal city states could try to engineer their utopian societies, and us inbred redneck unwashed hillbillies in flyover land can have our freedom to do as we wish. </div> </div> </div>Besides the clearly inane concept of the division of where voters actually are in this country, you do realize this would screw rural America completely, right? Without the massive taxes generated by the coasts for the federal government, that are then spent in rural states, those states would tank economically. Just look at the financial mess in Kansas after Brownback tried to end the state's reliance on the federal government (well besides all those juicy defense contracts and tax breaks for fossil fuel companies...).<br /> <br /> This attitude doesn't guarantee freedom, it guarantees economic collapse. So unless you think being forced into subsistence farming to survive is freedom... I have no idea what you're on about.<br /> <br /> Nobody wins.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T09:38:40-08:00","id":1019823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1019450#post1019450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being able to say that, just in itself, makes having to put up with Trump for the next <b>four </b>years worth it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have far more confidence in the Democratic Party than I do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T13:13:16-08:00","id":1019942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1019695#post1019695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Much like the mythical unicorn or successful socialist country, I keep hearing about this, but never actually see it. Except for the cases that are shown to be hoaxes performed by leftists seeking attention or sympathy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there's <a href=\"http://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/20/us/whitefish-montana-jews-daily-stormer.html?_r=0\" target=\"_blank\">this happening in Montana</a>. I suppose it's possible <a href=\"http://www.motherjones.com/politics/2016/10/richard-spencer-trump-alt-right-white-nationalist\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> is faking his political views to seek sympathy but it seems unlikely. There's also Dylann Roof.<br /> <br /> If you've lived without meeting these people, that's great, but they don't solely exist online.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-20-2016, 04:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T15:35:13-08:00","id":1020009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1019942#post1019942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well there's <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/20/us/whitefish-montana-jews-daily-stormer.html?_r=0&amp;quot;]this</a> happening in Montana[/URL]. I suppose it's possible <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.motherjones.com/politics/2016/10/richard-spencer-trump-alt-right-white-nationalist&amp;quot;]Richard</a> Spencer[/URL] is faking his political views to seek sympathy but it seems unlikely. There's also Dylann Roof.<br /> <br /> If you've lived without meeting these people, that's great, but they don't solely exist online.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad the police are looking into that. It's concerning. And I also find it concerning on how our political discourse seems to be affecting our schools. <br /> <br /> Apparently around the time of the election, an 11 year old was attacked by fellow students for saying they supported Trump while at the school. Police were involved and the kid got taken to the emergency room. <a href=\"http://www.fox26houston.com/news/216600137-story\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.fox26houston.com/news/216600137-story</a><br /> <br /> In Maryland, a high school student got beaten by other students when some students were doing a protest of Trump at the school. <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/local/education/student-wearing-trump-hat-arguing-with-protesters-is-punched-kicked-to-ground/2016/11/16/cb9d909e-ac14-11e6-8b45-f8e493f06fcd_story.html?utm_term=.f0dc2a8a9f1e\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.washingtonpost.com/local...=.f0dc2a8a9f1e</a><br /> <br /> There are multiple incidents I can find of this political discourse being turned into violence at schools and targeting students. That bothers me a lot. I don't remember politics at school drawing violence like this during my days attending, which makes me wonder if I was just blind to it or if times have changed. <br /> <br /> If so, I'm very conflicted on it. I like students being aware and caring about politics. It IS their future. But I don't like hearing of these outbreaks of violence due to differing politics. It's polarizing the discussion and normalizing these behaviors. And I can't see that as being good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T16:02:36-08:00","id":1020028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1020009#post1020009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If so, I'm very conflicted on it. I like students being aware and caring about politics. It IS their future. But I don't like hearing of these outbreaks of violence due to differing politics. It's polarizing the discussion and normalizing these behaviors. And I can't see that as being good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been thinking this for a long time. It seems to me that our national political discourse has been growing more divisive over time, but it really came to a head this year. And if we don't make a concerted effort to change directions, it will get worse.<br /> <br /> See, violence is the natural outcome of demonizing anyone who disagrees with you. If you've already settled in your mind that 1) this person's ideas have no value and 2) there is no point in you trying to impart your values to them or negotiate a common set of values, what else is there to do except act unilaterally?<br /> <br /> If people are trying to be civilized, this means trying to do an end-run around whatever your opposition is to achieve your desired goal. In politics you see this principle enacted by whoever is in power using their legal authority to force their will on the unwilling, and the powerless trying to undermine that authority. No negotiation, just social battles for control.<br /> <br /> If people <i>aren't</i> trying to be civilized, this means you straight up kill anyone you don't like. Without a greater power threatening punishment, or a moral doctrine against violence, there's little incentive <i>not</i> to use force.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T22:58:41-08:00","id":1020195,"title":"","content":"&quot;But it is not enough for me to stand before you tonight and condemn riots. It would be morally irresponsible for me to do that without, at the same time, condemning the contingent, intolerable conditions that exist in our society. These conditions are the things that cause individuals to feel that they have no other alternative than to engage in violent rebellions to get attention. And I must say tonight that a riot is the language of the unheard. And what is it America has failed to hear?...It has failed to hear that the promises of freedom and justice have not been met. And it has failed to hear that large segments of white society are more concerned about tranquility and the status quo than about justice and humanity.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T10:15:45-08:00","id":1020468,"title":"","content":"Kids in your schools didn't fight? My friends and I in middle and high school got into fist fights over <i>everything</i>. Politics wasn't anything special, just one more excuse to vent out pent up aggression.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I mean, nobody ended up in the hospital because of it, but we would usually get broken up before that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-21-2016, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T10:46:56-08:00","id":1020492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1020468#post1020468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, nobody ended up in the hospital because of it, but we would usually get broken up before that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always thought that was sort of the problem with the school-to-real life transition. Cops will break up fights but more often aren't there the way teachers were. In the end after graduation few are prepared to ease down anger-verging-on-violence situations, so it's often just going to boil over until someone gets seriously hurt.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T11:02:26-08:00","id":1020502,"title":"","content":"We never really got into fist fights over politics specifically at my schools, but the things that politics tends to be about (class, race, culture, identity)? Punches got thrown all the time over that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T13:38:29-08:00","id":1020610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1020502#post1020502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We never really got into fist fights over politics specifically at my schools, but the things that politics tends to be about (class, race, culture, identity)? Punches got thrown all the time over that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's kind of how it went for us too. Probably helped by the fact that <i>nobody</i> liked G.W. Bush, so there wasn't much to fight about there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T14:12:16-08:00","id":1020641,"title":"","content":"I'm a member of my local Pant Suit Nation and I am slightly distressed by what has happened with the national group. The Local Group is moving forward with Political Activism, trying to break away from Facebook Activism and do something. However, the National Group went Non-profit and decided to devote itself to &quot;sharing stories.&quot; They trademarked the name &quot;Pant Suit Nation&quot; and forced local political active groups to change their name. I was disappointed in this change. Pant Suit Nation squandered their political capital and didn't really do anything. Thankfully the Local Group is still moving forward with activism.<br /> <br /> Today, <a href=\"http://www.thedailybeast.com/articles/2016/12/21/pantsuit-nation-is-the-worst-why-a-book-of-uplifting-facebook-posts-won-t-heal-america.html\" target=\"_blank\">this article</a> was posted on the Local Group. All the decisions made by the national group make sense in hindsight. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 12-21-2016, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T15:51:32-08:00","id":1020685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1020195#post1020195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;But it is not enough for me to stand before you tonight and condemn riots. It would be morally irresponsible for me to do that without, at the same time, condemning the contingent, intolerable conditions that exist in our society. These conditions are the things that cause individuals to feel that they have no other alternative than to engage in violent rebellions to get attention. And I must say tonight that a riot is the language of the unheard. And what is it America has failed to hear?...It has failed to hear that the promises of freedom and justice have not been met. And it has failed to hear that large segments of white society are more concerned about tranquility and the status quo than about justice and humanity.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>While I regretfully agree with the overall sentiment, I do not believe that an elementary school or even a high school is the place for that. <br /> <br /> They are minors, and so I believe they have no obligation, responsibility or right to take a stand on one political position or another. I can understand a desire to be an activist for whatever causes they believe in, but they are given no franchise or legal power, and I do not believe there exists an expectation of obligation or responsibility for a person who does not have legal agency to be recognized for such efforts.<br /> <br /> Its a very relevant quote for the broader political landscape of the United States. But I'm curious on how you mean to apply it to minors that are under the care and responsibility of a third party institution?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T16:57:46-08:00","id":1020709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1020468#post1020468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kids in your schools didn't fight? My friends and I in middle and high school got into fist fights over <i>everything</i>. Politics wasn't anything special, just one more excuse to vent out pent up aggression.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I mean, nobody ended up in the hospital because of it, but we would usually get broken up before that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a really interesting post, considering your choice of words here. You use the word &quot;fight&quot;, seemingly in response to what I posted about. But I didn't use that word at all. I used &quot;beaten&quot; and &quot;attacked&quot;. <br /> <br /> Your use of &quot;fight&quot; and the context of &quot;my friends and I.. Got into fist fights&quot; as if they're the same thing as being &quot;beaten&quot; or &quot;attacked&quot;. By using the term &quot;fight&quot;, you're equating the two kids as being mutually responsible for what happened. I strongly disagree with that. It's a view of &quot;boys will be boys&quot; (though I also found a few instances of girls attacking girls regarding the election, too) which is a permissive culture of violence that condones bullying and erases victimization. I'm sorry to say this, but it is blaming the victim of the violence they had inflicted on them. <br /> <br /> So were there &quot;fights&quot; at my school, probably? I never saw any myself. But I was the victim of violence at my school by other kids who thought they had a right to hurt me. If that was a &quot;fight&quot;, then it was very one sided. They even told teachers that we were &quot;friends&quot; so they could isolate me. <br /> <br /> I think the video of the eleven year old who got beaten was perhaps played up a little for the news. But when he said he was worried about going back? Oh, I understand that feeling. I know it intimately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T17:33:28-08:00","id":1020724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1020685#post1020685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I regretfully agree with the overall sentiment, I do not believe that an elementary school or even a high school is the place for that.<br /> <br /> They are minors, and so I believe they have no obligation, responsibility or right to take a stand on one political position or another. I can understand a desire to be an activist for whatever causes they believe in, but they are given no franchise or legal power, and I do not believe there exists an expectation of obligation or responsibility for a person who does not have legal agency to be recognized for such efforts.<br /> <br /> Its a very relevant quote for the broader political landscape of the United States. But I'm curious on how you mean to apply it to minors that are under the care and responsibility of a third party institution?</div> </div> </div> </div>Did I quote you in that, or reference minors, or schools? If all three questions have an answer of no, then don't you ever ask me a leading question again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 12-21-2016, 08:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T18:05:56-08:00","id":1020735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1020724#post1020724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did I quote you in that, or reference minors, or schools? If all three questions have an answer of no, then don't you ever ask me a leading question again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was that a leading question? I'm sorry if I gave offense with the question. I would've found an answer of, &quot;I'm not citing that quote to apply it to that scenario, it's just a quote that has been on my mind lately&quot; or something like that to be a solid response.<br /> <br /> I really wish you had added some context as to why you were citing that quote. With just the quote, the only context I could think of is the posts of others around a similar time frame as to when you posted. And well... It seems that was misleading. So I'm sorry for misunderstanding. ^^;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T19:41:52-08:00","id":1020761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1020709#post1020709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a really interesting post, considering your choice of words here. You use the word &quot;fight&quot;, seemingly in response to what I posted about. But I didn't use that word at all. I used &quot;beaten&quot; and &quot;attacked&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. I didn't say the incidents of violence you were referring to were equivalent to those I experienced as a kid?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1020709#post1020709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your use of &quot;fight&quot; and the context of &quot;my friends and I.. Got into fist fights&quot; as if they're the same thing as being &quot;beaten&quot; or &quot;attacked&quot;. By using the term &quot;fight&quot;, you're equating the two kids as being mutually responsible for what happened. I strongly disagree with that. It's a view of &quot;boys will be boys&quot; (though I also found a few instances of girls attacking girls regarding the election, too) which is a permissive culture of violence that condones bullying and erases victimization. I'm sorry to say this, but it is blaming the victim of the violence they had inflicted on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not in any way blaming the children who were attacked, nor am I trying to downplay the attackers' responsibility for the attacks. You said,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't remember politics at school drawing violence like this during my days attending, which makes me wonder if I was just blind to it or if times have changed. </div> </div> </div>I was responding to <i>that statement</i> by saying that I <i>do</i> remember politics drawing violence at my school. Among many other things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1020709#post1020709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So were there &quot;fights&quot; at my school, probably? I never saw any myself. But I was the victim of violence at my school by other kids who thought they had a right to hurt me. If that was a &quot;fight&quot;, then it was very one sided. They even told teachers that we were &quot;friends&quot; so they could isolate me.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a different sort of violence than what I experienced at school, and I am sorry you had to go through that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1020709#post1020709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the video of the eleven year old who got beaten was perhaps played up a little for the news. But when he said he was worried about going back? Oh, I understand that feeling. I know it intimately.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's awful. Not saying it isn't. Just saying I don't think it's a sign of changing times as you wondered out loud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T20:09:27-08:00","id":1020767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1020761#post1020761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. I didn't say the incidents of violence you were referring to were equivalent to those I experienced as a kid?<br /> <br /> I am not in any way blaming the children who were attacked, nor am I trying to downplay the attackers' responsibility for the attacks. You said,<br /> <br /> I was responding to <i>that statement</i> by saying that I <i>do</i> remember politics drawing violence at my school. Among many other things.<br /> <br /> This is a different sort of violence than what I experienced at school, and I am sorry you had to go through that.<br /> <br /> Yeah, it's awful. Not saying it isn't. Just saying I don't think it's a sign of changing times as you wondered out loud.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. Thank you for clarifying and you very well might be right.<br /> <br /> Something that definitely supports you is the sheer prevalence of smartphones with cameras that can record incidents like those in the article and share them so quickly using social media. It can certainly be a factor of greater available evidence being due to those two factors, rather than an increase in how often such incidents occur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T19:51:53-08:00","id":1021459,"title":"","content":"Seriously? Is there actual violence occurring between students over political views. Wow. Just wow. Call me sheltered but that never happened in my elemental or high school experience. If there were fights they usually happened because we wanted to fight for fighting's sake. It was fun. Stupid but fun. Sometimes there would be a disagreement over a broken promise or something minor like that, but politics was never an issue, even in high school.<br /> <br /> That being said, I was raised in Toronto, Canada, the most multicultural city on the planet, so pretty much everyone, including my teachers, were homogeneously on the Left. Actually, now that I think about it a lot of potential issues of difference that could have caused fights were non-existent. No one at my high school cared about the almost weekly &quot;foreign&quot; holiday acknowledgements and celebrations. No one cared that we had a Gay-Straight Alliance club. No one cared that intelligent design wasn't taught. And no one cared that Muslim students were allowed to leave the class to pray.<br /> <br /> It was all just normal and nothing worth fighting over.<br /> <br /> Jeez, if this election has taught me anything is that Americans are weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T17:22:46-08:00","id":1022540,"title":"","content":"As many of you would love to believe otherwise, this is the real reason why Trump won:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GLG9g7BcjKs\" data-code=\"GLG9g7BcjKs\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/GLG9g7BcjKs/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T18:55:52-08:00","id":1022577,"title":"","content":"No, that's just a long unproductive rant that offers almost nothing of real substance on what happened. It betrays a severe lack of knowledge of a number of things (such as why Sanders couldn't take the primary), as well as engages in inane hypocrisy where painting all Trump voters like &quot;X&quot; is bad, but then complains that the problem with the left is that all the left are a homogeneous stereotyped hive mind that all should be painted with the same thing.<br /> <br /> There's also just a significant lack of appreciation for trying to win in a political climate where the current President and his policies are actually extremely popular (at least when you don't tell people Obama did them; like seriously if you look at the polls on the ACA or individual ACA mandates most Americans like it, but you call it Obamacare and it drops significantly), and at the same time people are clamoring for change.<br /> <br /> Trying to win when you're on the side of the current administration when the public (and more importantly your core voters) is saying, &quot;We don't want you to change anything, but we want change,&quot; makes it really hard to make a simple sales pitch. And Clinton put out a ton of in-depth stuff that the public promptly ignored. The Democratic debates were actual debates on policy compared to the Republican ones. Etc. etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T15:40:08-08:00","id":1023002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1022577#post1022577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to win when you're on the side of the current administration when the public (and more importantly your core voters) is saying, &quot;We don't want you to change anything, but we want change,&quot; makes it really hard to make a simple sales pitch. And Clinton put out a ton of in-depth stuff that the public promptly ignored. The Democratic debates were actual debates on policy compared to the Republican ones. Etc. etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the best example I've ever seen of that mentality (we want change but don't change anything) was when Schwarzenegger got elected. He campaigned (primarily) on a handful of reforms, tax changes, and financial re-directions for the state. He got in. Then getting everything in order all the major changes he campaigned on were put up as ballot measures, so the people themselves could say yes or no on each of them, because hey that's how america does things. Every one of the major changes got rejected.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T17:04:10-08:00","id":1023031,"title":"","content":"The two things the American voter base hates the most are change and the way things are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T17:12:11-08:00","id":1023035,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately the US doesn't have federal ballot measures considering the number of measures that should pass based on public opinion but get slammed shut by one side or the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T20:33:26-08:00","id":1023089,"title":"","content":"Eh, the american system (and many others) worked well enough for the times and technology it was developed and refined in. Unfortunately the last century has seen significant technological changes (communication, transportation) that have given rise to national and multi-national corporations, which operate on a far broader field than anything really conceived of previously. Many political systems are based on money, anything that relies on public awareness is going to be driven by it, and now it's coming to a bit of a head. Companies have far broader interests and have via money can influence far more layers of government than what was planned for originally... which was a far more localized corporate interest scheme... someone who might own a dozen factories and own a bunch of farm land that is leased out to hundreds of farmers was a power-house, but also a regionalized one... You might rule half of Detroit via your factories so that's where you were concerned about influence. Now... it's significantly different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T21:41:26-08:00","id":1023106,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure that really has anything to do with the amount of separation the American system puts between the people and the federal government. In most democracies - even equally indirect ones - a policy with ~85 support by the public would (for better or worse) be considered something politicians practically have to do to keep their power even if it goes against corporate interests.<br /> <br /> Also, the Founding Fathers pretty much saw the corporation thing well ahead of now. The original laws governing corporations were very clearly a response to the incredible political power wielded by the British trading companies founded in the 1600s to exploit colonial holdings. I do not doubt for a second they would simply be disappointed with the current state of things getting so far off from what they wanted rather than surprised by the level of power corporations have; they knew all about things like the East India Company and the power it had to influence the Crown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T13:44:30-08:00","id":1023410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1022577#post1022577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that's just a long unproductive rant that offers almost nothing of real substance on what happened. It betrays a severe lack of knowledge of a number of things (such as why Sanders couldn't take the primary), as well as engages in inane hypocrisy where painting all Trump voters like &quot;X&quot; is bad, but then complains that the problem with the left is that all the left are a homogeneous stereotyped hive mind that all should be painted with the same thing.<br /> <br /> There's also just a significant lack of appreciation for trying to win in a political climate where the current President and his policies are actually extremely popular (at least when you don't tell people Obama did them; like seriously if you look at the polls on the ACA or individual ACA mandates most Americans like it, but you call it Obamacare and it drops significantly), and at the same time people are clamoring for change.<br /> <br /> Trying to win when you're on the side of the current administration when the public (and more importantly your core voters) is saying, &quot;We don't want you to change anything, but we want change,&quot; makes it really hard to make a simple sales pitch. And Clinton put out a ton of in-depth stuff that the public promptly ignored. The Democratic debates were actual debates on policy compared to the Republican ones. Etc. etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose that pretty much is the real problem in politics. Hidebound voters refusing to accept policies that come from the other side of the aisle, even when they agree with them or desperately need them.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm kind of starting to get annoyed by every political pundit in the world trying to create these singular silver bullet reasons as to why Trump won. It was gerrymanding, it was sexism, it was the rise of the Alt-Right, it was political correctness and SJW's, it was Russia, it was BernieBros, it was the Rust Belt, it was Hillary being a weak Centre-Left candidate, it was a whitelash. Nobody seems willing to say it was complex cluster of reasons that involved the above and more that got him in the White House and that worries me more than anything because I can just imagine Democrats just focusing on one of these issues and forgetting the rest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T17:38:44-08:00","id":1024016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1023410#post1023410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose that pretty much is the real problem in politics. Hidebound voters refusing to accept policies that come from the other side of the aisle, even when they agree with them or desperately need them.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm kind of starting to get annoyed by every political pundit in the world trying to create these singular silver bullet reasons as to why Trump won. It was gerrymanding, it was sexism, it was the rise of the Alt-Right, it was political correctness and SJW's, it was Russia, it was BernieBros, it was the Rust Belt, it was Hillary being a weak Centre-Left candidate, it was a whitelash. Nobody seems willing to say it was complex cluster of reasons that involved the above and more that got him in the White House and that worries me more than anything because I can just imagine Democrats just focusing on one of these issues and forgetting the rest.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's not one thing, but many of those had a major impact and should be taken into consideration. <br /> <br /> One think I keep hearing is that it was because she was a woman, bullshit, you put the right woman in as nominee she'll win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T17:43:43-08:00","id":1024020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1024016#post1024016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not one thing, but many of those had a major impact and should be taken into consideration.<br /> <br /> One think I keep hearing is that it was because she was a woman, bullshit, you put the right woman in as nominee she'll win.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue isn't that a woman can't possibly win a presidential election in America. The issue is that the bar for &quot;the right woman&quot; is much higher than the bar for &quot;the right man&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T03:09:50-08:00","id":1024179,"title":"","content":"On top of the higher bar set, there's also the numerous double standards at play. To use a non-Clinton example back from the primaries: Trumps unscrupulous business dealings that resulted in him getting paid while everyday workers got screwed by him is a sign of his &quot;genius,&quot; while Carly Fiorina's use of the same business tactics is a sign that she's incompetent and can't be the outsider businessperson that will use that experience to &quot;fix&quot; the county.<br /> <br /> Or the fact that Trump's counter to criticisms of his sexism and inappropriate behaviors was to attack Clinton... for her husband's sleaze. Which sadly worked far better than it should have (aka at all).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T13:29:35-08:00","id":1024481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1024016#post1024016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not one thing, but many of those had a major impact and should be taken into consideration.<br /> <br /> One think I keep hearing is that it was because she was a woman, bullshit, you put the right woman in as nominee she'll win.</div> </div> </div> </div>As bad as Clinton is, <i>she went against Trump</i>.<br /> <br /> There's no reason that should have been a contest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T15:32:42-08:00","id":1024522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1024481#post1024481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As bad as Clinton is, <i>she went against Trump</i>.<br /> <br /> There's no reason that should have been a contest.</div> </div> </div> </div>One could say that about all of Trump's Republican opponents during the primary - as bad as they were, they were against Trump. There's no reason that should have been a contest.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately this was a season in which people wanted political change and were angry at the political establishment. And there is nobody in American politics who represents the political establishment more than Hillary Clinton. She was, in effect, stuck swimming against the political anti-establishment zeitgeist, whereas Trump rode that anti-establishment wave to victory in the Republican primaries and then again general election.<br /> <br /> I think if the Democrats had run someone who less represented the Washington status quo they might have done better, or at least Trump would have done a lot worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T16:51:10-08:00","id":1024559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1024481#post1024481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As bad as Clinton is, <i>she went against Trump</i>.<br /> <br /> There's no reason that should have been a contest.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's only true if everyone in America had the same, or even similar, criteria for what makes a credible president.<br /> <br /> The reasons why Trump is a monstrous prick in your eyes is the same reasons why people liked him and voted for him in droves.<br /> <br /> There was always going to be a contest even if a lot of people found it morally unacceptable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1675,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","user":"Weirdboyz","date":". 12-30-2016, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T16:53:36-08:00","id":1024561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1024522#post1024522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there is nobody in American politics who represents the political establishment more than Hillary Clinton.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems fairly silly. I mean, most people would argue that Joe Biden probably would have managed to beat Trump because he probably could have held the Rust Belt with a much better emotional appeal to the white working class voters that tipped towards Trump and gave Trump the electoral college.<br /> <br /> But you stack up Biden against Clinton as who is more representative of the political establishment... and I don't see how Biden wouldn't &quot;win&quot; that position. Or I could list any number of Democrats that are undeniably more representative of the political establishment than Clinton in any far comparison but didn't run for President recently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think if the Democrats had run someone who less represented the Washington status quo they might have done better, or at least Trump would have done a lot worse. </div> </div> </div>Except, of course, as the Democratic primary proved, the core Democratic voters are not as swayed by the &quot;anti-establishment&quot; mood. Sander did OK, but solidly lost (even without any help by the DNC). There's no guarantee any &quot;outsider&quot; Democrat wouldn't do more damage by reducing core voter enthusiasm greater than votes pulled in from the progressive left up swelling that gave Sanders even the hint of a chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T17:17:18-08:00","id":1024574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1024561#post1024561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That seems fairly silly. I mean, most people would argue that Joe Biden probably would have managed to beat Trump because he probably could have held the Rust Belt with a much better emotional appeal to the white working class voters that tipped towards Trump and gave Trump the electoral college.<br /> <br /> But you stack up Biden against Clinton as who is more representative of the political establishment... and I don't see how Biden wouldn't &quot;win&quot; that position. Or I could list any number of Democrats that are undeniably more representative of the political establishment than Clinton in any far comparison but didn't run for President recently.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's very logical Heavy Arms and makes a whole lot of sense. Unfortunately, logic based on fact and perception based on what you hear aren't always the same. Everyone <b>said </b>that Clinton was the firm establishment candidate who wouldn't deviate from the political norm and that suddenly became fact regardless of Clinton's actual record or promises.<br /> <br /> Clinton being a Centre-Left Neoliberal and Bernie being a Left Socialist is easy to understand and thus easier to tell everyone on major news networks and social media. Anything more complex wouldn't feed into the political tribalism that a lot political pundits make their money from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T23:19:13-08:00","id":1024642,"title":"","content":"I was responding to someone that stated Clinton's &quot;status&quot; as the most establishment person in American politics as a fact; not as a matter of perceptions.<br /> <br /> Clinton was an establishment candidate. She never tried to run from that, because it would have been inane. And the left focused punditry did go beyond &quot;Center-Left Neoliberal vs. Left Socialist,&quot; because ultimately most of their positions were the same or extremely close. One of the big differences between Clinton and Sanders that was very hotly debated in the left pundit-sphere was the incrementalists arguing for protecting the gains made and focusing on small changes unless a political opportunity presented itself, vs. the radicals arguing the party needed to push a far stronger progressive agenda to shift the window of mainstream political discussions back towards the middle instead of as far right as it's become in the US in the past 40 years.<br /> <br /> It really shouldn't be surprising that the incrementalists won out. The Obama years represented a lot of major gains for the progressive movement that were already facing State level backlash by the center-right, &quot;you're moving too fast to let society adjust!&quot; crowd. There was a lot more pressure among the more active voters to be protectionist in their choices.<br /> <br /> And of course, none of that mattered in the actual presidential election because for numerous reasons that wouldn't have changed for any Democratic candidate (as they didn't change for any of the other Republican primary candidates) that let Trump win despite news cycles that are traditionally campaign killers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T11:25:54-08:00","id":1024851,"title":"","content":"As soon as Clinton was proven to have accepted debate questions provided in advance... if she wasn't 'the established interests' then, she became so in the minds of many voters very rapidly. It's impossible to view that sort of thing charitably. It was damning regardless of how it was glossed over in mainstream media (which was also obvious and somewhat insulting). I say this as a very frustrated Clinton voter who feels she would have done fine without CNN's help.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T22:20:53-08:00","id":1025006,"title":"","content":"The democrats lost to <i>Donald Trump</i> because of <i>their</i> hubris. Sad!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Meow! Meow meow meow. Purrrrrr.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11326-misterscruffles","name":"Misterscruffles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T22:58:24-08:00","id":1025312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Misterscruffles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1025006#post1025006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The democrats lost to <i>Donald Trump</i> because of <i>their</i> hubris. Sad!</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire 2016 election practically was a Greek tragedy.<br /> <br /> Or it was a spectacular comedy depending on your point of view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T03:35:16-08:00","id":1025359,"title":"","content":"It was neither really. By Greek theater traditions, it would be a farce. Which of course makes sense, because in a farce nobody really wins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T10:07:20-08:00","id":1027106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1025359#post1025359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was neither really. By Greek theater traditions, it would be a farce. Which of course makes sense, because in a farce nobody really wins.</div> </div> </div> </div>The theatre person in me wants to second this and be really sad that this is what our modern world has come to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T22:38:25-08:00","id":1050329,"title":"","content":"Well. <i>That</i> happened.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T07:05:26-08:00","id":1050472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1050329#post1050329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well. <i>That</i> happene