b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happened?</div> </div> </div> </div>Trump yesterday (replace 'cloud' with any topic he brought up in his press conference)<br /> <img src=\"http://i1.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/newsfeed/001/044/247/297.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T08:04:38-08:00","id":1050505,"title":"","content":"Ah yes. One hour and seventeen minutes of semi-coherent stream-of-consciousness and some outright lies. A good capstone to a week full of the administration shooting itself in the foot.<br /> <br /> Now seems like a good time to pass around <a href=\"http://petitions.signforgood.com/TrumpNukes?code=RA\" target=\"_blank\">this petition</a> supporting a bill to remove the President's power to arbitrarily declare nuclear war. Online petitions aren't worth much, but if you can talk to your representatives about this legislation, good on you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 02-17-2017, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T14:22:29-08:00","id":1051142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1050478#post1050478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Presumably the rant yesterday where he blamed everything on everyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div> Isn't that like most of his rants?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T20:30:12-08:00","id":1051342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1024642#post1024642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And of course, none of that mattered in the actual presidential election because for numerous reasons that wouldn't have changed for any Democratic candidate (as they didn't change for any of the other Republican primary candidates) that let Trump win despite news cycles that are traditionally campaign killers.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would normally be the case if news media as a whole wasn't completely distrusted. And while I'm no republican I certainly don't trust them myself. The media was borderline propaganda on clintions side and it didn't even bother to address the problems in a partisian manner or at the very fucking least address the issues of trump being president. Like his actual platforms, because they kept calling him a clown and attacking him the wrong way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T20:55:42-08:00","id":1051345,"title":"","content":"Well, that's a heck of a jump backwards.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the news media is not &quot;as a whole&quot; completely distrusted. A Gallup poll before the election found that ~51% of Democratic aligned voters had positive attitudes towards the media (the poll didn't get into mixed/negative), and ~14% of Republican align voters had positive attitudes towards the media.<br /> <br /> That's why it didn't really matter who the Democratic candidate was. The trust in the media is completely lopsided. The media could have covered Trump perfectly and it wouldn't have had a drastic impact because the core voters for the guy that one don't trust them anyway.<br /> <br /> And of course, covering Trump's &quot;platform&quot; was a ridiculous idea. He's been president for almost a month and he still doesn't know what his platform actually is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T21:13:22-08:00","id":1051351,"title":"","content":"Thats my point. We don't know anything and the media didn't bother. It wasn't about republicans so much as people on the fence. Swing states that voiced blue last two elections switched because they felt they weren't being heard and when all you know about a man is that he has a billion dollars but the media are just resorting to names instead of facts then it leaves a bad taste in your mouth.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm more annoyed how bias the news has become its not new but its so blantant its disgusting. The last gallup poll I saw said hilary was at a 90% chance of winning. Like as much as I hate trump the media has been just as bad. They should honestly have a higher standard and critiqued from a better position but I guess when you need clickbait to keep yourself running who gives a fuck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T22:13:24-08:00","id":1051370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1051345#post1051345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that's a heck of a jump backwards.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the news media is not &amp;quot;as a whole&amp;quot; completely distrusted. A Gallup poll before the election found that ~51% of Democratic aligned voters had positive attitudes towards the media (the poll didn't get into mixed/negative), and ~14% of Republican align voters had positive attitudes towards the media.<br /> <br /> That's why it didn't really matter who the Democratic candidate was. The trust in the media is completely lopsided. The media could have covered Trump perfectly and it wouldn't have had a drastic impact because the core voters for the guy that one don't trust them anyway.<br /> <br /> And of course, covering Trump's &amp;quot;platform&amp;quot; was a ridiculous idea. He's been president for almost a month and he still doesn't know what his platform actually is.</div> </div> </div> </div> 51% percent among Democrats is not exactly a ringing endorsement for the media, a bare majority, and the difference between majority and minority of Democrats here would likely be within the margin of error.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T22:55:15-08:00","id":1051383,"title":"","content":"It's not a ringing endorsement, but keep in mind that the national average hasn't gone over 54% for this poll in over 20 years.<br /> <br /> The salient point towards electoral politics in the USA is that one party is significantly impacted by the mainstream media, and one isn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T00:10:17-08:00","id":1051398,"title":"","content":"What happened in Sweden? Our media have absolutely no idea what Trump is talking about, and our security service (S\u00c4PO) has specifically announced that they don't have a clue what Trump might be referring to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T00:38:54-08:00","id":1051404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1051398#post1051398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happened in Sweden? Our media have absolutely no idea what Trump is talking about, and our security service (S\u00c4PO) has specifically announced that they don't have a clue what Trump might be referring to.</div> </div> </div> </div>You didn't hear? It was as bad as the Bowling Green Massacre.<br /> <br /> More seriously, nothing happened. People suspect it's because he was listening to <a href=\"http://www.slate.com/blogs/the_slatest/2017/02/18/did_fox_news_segment_lead_trump_to_believe_there_was_a_terror_attack_in.html\" target=\"_blank\">Fox News</a>. Which is a weird kind of irony considering he just ranted about how the news is all fake, even though the leaks they reported were real and how the media is the enemy of America but also the president's source of news.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-19-2017, 03:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T12:19:31-08:00","id":1051610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1051404#post1051404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You didn't hear? It was as bad as the Bowling Green Massacre.<br /> <br /> More seriously, nothing happened. People suspect it's because he was listening to <a href=\"http://www.slate.com/blogs/the_slatest/2017/02/18/did_fox_news_segment_lead_trump_to_believe_there_was_a_terror_attack_in.html\" target=\"_blank\">Fox News</a>. Which is a weird kind of irony considering he just ranted about how the news is all fake, even though the leaks they reported were real and how the media is the enemy of America but also the president's source of news.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aweHmowmtVo\" target=\"_blank\">CONTRADICTION IS TRUTH!</a><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> (Incidentally, later in the series, the same character making the speech admits that it was the way of the real big bad and that she (Satsuki) was wrong for trying to fight fire with fire.)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":".  Editing is hard, apparently. 02-19-2017, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T12:35:12-08:00","id":1052697,"title":"","content":"I'm still thrilled, tbh. I think that a strong, somewhat dictatorial leader is exactly what the country needs. Nobody is HAPPY when the dictator is in power, but in the end, they are either vilified or praised by history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12852-silver_smoulder","name":"Silver_Smoulder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12852_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T12:57:19-08:00","id":1052712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Silver_Smoulder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1052697#post1052697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still thrilled, tbh. I think that a strong, somewhat dictatorial leader is exactly what the country needs. Nobody is HAPPY when the dictator is in power, but in the end, they are either vilified or praised by history.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like you to explain the first part.<br /> <br /> As to the second, there <i>are </i>people who are pleased when a dictator is in power - those who benefit from the dictator's actions. In our case, that means large corporate entities who benefit from deregulation and social conservatives. There are others who <i>think</i> they will benefit - working class people who have bought the hype that Ol' Donny Boy will bring them jobs - but I'm skeptical that they will ever be served. Much as I'd like to see him universally reviled, I suspect Ol' Donny Boy will have a more complex legacy than &quot;he sucked and everyone hated his guts&quot; OR &quot;He Made America Great Again!(TM)&quot;. Especially if he continues to fight the media, take credit for things he had no responsibility for, and somehow keep up his supporters who take him at face value.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T13:41:10-08:00","id":1052737,"title":"","content":"He's not a strong leader. In a month he's proven to be an incredibly weak and ineffectual leader.<br /> <br /> And the &quot;country needs this,&quot; argument is a very poor one in the face of all the people that will suffer for it. The country might need the end results of the backlash against Trump, but the results could be achieved without all of the bad shit that will happen in the mean time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T13:43:38-08:00","id":1052740,"title":"","content":"The one good thing I will say about Trump is that he's managed to get a lot more people interested in politics who were previously completely apathetic about the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T14:20:12-08:00","id":1052769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1052740#post1052740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one good thing I will say about Trump is that he's managed to get a lot more people interested in politics who were previously completely apathetic about the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, when a loved one comes down with a terminal illness, the whole family suddenly becomes <i>very</i> interested in the medical field.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T14:35:15-08:00","id":1052785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1052737#post1052737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the &quot;country needs this,&quot; argument is a very poor one in the face of all the people that will suffer for it. The country might need the end results of the backlash against Trump, but the results could be achieved without all of the bad shit that will happen in the mean time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know. I mean, I don't like it, but if Trump got this far, then I think the population needs a serious wake-up call and the harshness of his actions might be what it takes.<br /> <br /> I heard about a lot of people not voting because they didn't like the choices. That stubbornness or apathy led to this result (along with several other total screw-ups).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 02-21-2017, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:13:24-08:00","id":1052814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1052785#post1052785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know. I mean, I don't like it, but if Trump got this far, then I think the population needs a serious wake-up call and the harshness of his actions might be what it takes.<br /> <br /> I heard about a lot of people not voting because they didn't like the choices. That stubbornness or apathy led to this result (along with several other total screw-ups).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I have a feeling if everyone who showed up at the Women's March and anti-Trump rallies had actually voted for Hillary when they had the chance, Trump wouldn't be president. He won, to a large degree, elected because of apathy and a desire to not &quot;pick the lesser of the two evils&quot; among many Americans, which ended up with the greater of the two evils in office. I think quite a few people of people have gotten the message that their vote matters. And if they haven't gotten it yet, hopefully they will by the time November rolls around in 2020.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T15:47:56-08:00","id":1052855,"title":"","content":"Everyone I know who did show up to the Woman's March did vote for Hillary Clinton. Trump did lose the population vote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T17:11:09-08:00","id":1052917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1052785#post1052785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know. I mean, I don't like it, but if Trump got this far, then I think the population needs a serious wake-up call and the harshness of his actions might be what it takes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the disparity in the popular vote, I don't think the population really needs a serious wake up call. The issue is not the politically active populace, but the structural elements of the system.<br /> <br /> And, again, estimates from HIV/AIDs prevention groups working in Africa are preparing for 9 million deaths from reduced services due to just one of Trump's orders. I cannot abide by a moral calculus that says the US voters need a &quot;lesson&quot; that is worth the cost of 9 million lives that had no say in our election. And that's just one thing Trump has done.<br /> <br /> Again, I'm not saying that the lesson in question isn't important. I'm saying an argument that it's a good thing that this is how we're getting it isn't something I can support.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I heard about a lot of people not voting because they didn't like the choices. That stubbornness or apathy led to this result (along with several other total screw-ups). </div> </div> </div>The voter turn out was not significantly low (it was actually slightly above average for the last 10 elections). It seems low because we had an uptick in turn out during the second W election and the first Obama election, but those are rather clearly the outlier data points if you look at the numbers.<br /> <br /> &quot;A lot of people not voting,&quot; didn't really play out into, &quot;significantly less people voted.&quot; So pretty much everyone turned off must have been countered by someone that felt activated.<br /> <br /> Now, if we focus in on the Rust Belt states that went Trump by exceedingly narrow margins, this specific issue might be the case, but again, that wasn't actually &quot;a lot of people&quot; it was a very small number of people in states that normally go Democrat by small margins (hence are generally considered swing states).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T18:00:14-08:00","id":1052945,"title":"","content":"Someone asked me to justify my position for being &quot;thrilled.&quot; Perhaps &quot;thrilled&quot; is the wrong word, but I'm definitely pleased. Reasons:<br /> 1 - I am a Russian American<br /> 2 - I am a Jewish Russian American Zionist<br /> 3 - I lived in the ghetto (projects past West 21st near Coney Island) for about 6 years.<br /> 4 - I lost people in both 9/11 and in the airport terrorist bombing.<br /> <br /> Am I 100% satisfied with Trump. Fuck no. I am unhappy with him hiring people from Wall Street, I am unhappy with his anti-science and anti-climate change rhetoric. But the reasons I outlined above should be sufficient to see why I would prefer Trump over Hillary.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12852-silver_smoulder","name":"Silver_Smoulder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12852_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T19:13:52-08:00","id":1052975,"title":"","content":"Not.. to me.<br /> <br /> I have a lot of friends in the Russian Diaspora. The majority of them hate Putin and didn't like Trump's talk on Putin during the election.<br /> Most of those friends are also Russian American Jews, and they really don't like Putin's support for Syria and facilitating the pipeline of weapons into Lebanon to fuel Hezbollah.<br /> I'm a Jewish American, and a Zionist, and Trump's mindless caving to AIPAC's bullshit doesn't make me or any of my Zionist friends happy as AIPAC continues to pull their &quot;support the ruling party in Israel or you're an anti-Semite&quot; nonsense no matter how horrible BeBe is being.<br /> Losing people in 9/11 and whichever airport bombing you're talking about doesn't really say, &quot;vote for the guy the anti-terrorism agencies of the US all pretty much decried as being horrible on actual anti-terrorism policies.&quot;<br /> <br /> So yeah, that doesn't outline a sufficient case to me in the slightest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T19:21:27-08:00","id":1052979,"title":"","content":"Okay, see, I know you're lying. Because, I don't know what part of the US you're from, but the Russian diaspora in NYC voted for Trump AND they support Putin, because he is a strong leader.. The Middle-Eastern Jews predominantly voted for Trump.<br /> <br /> Also - unless you ever lost someone in a terror attack, you never get to judge. Like, literally never. I'm not going to go into details of why I think so, but &quot;horrible anti-terrorism&quot; policies are better than the ones before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12852-silver_smoulder","name":"Silver_Smoulder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12852_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T20:30:42-08:00","id":1053015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Silver_Smoulder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1052979#post1052979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, see, I know you're lying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, you just know what you can see with your head up your ass.<br /> <br /> You do realize that south Brooklyn does not actually represent all American Russian Jews right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because, I don't know what part of the US you're from, but the Russian diaspora in NYC voted for Trump AND they support Putin, because he is a strong leader. </div> </div> </div>And the Philly Russian Diaspora voted Clinton and hate Putin. So yeah, wow, people aren't monolithic groups, and just saying, &quot;I'm an American Russian Jew from Brooklyn that's a Zionist&quot; doesn't actually mean, &quot;it's clear that Trump was my guy!&quot; Especially since the age spread in your demographic there wasn't exactly even.<br /> <br /> 70% of Jews voted Clinton, 25% voted Trump... and that 25% is not a solid block of Russian American Jews.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Middle-Eastern Jews predominantly voted for Trump. </div> </div> </div>I can't find any reports that back up this claim. Given that the Mizrahi American Jewish community is so small, reliable polling is going to be extremely difficult. Can you point me to a source here?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also - unless you ever lost someone in a terror attack, you never get to judge. </div> </div> </div>Goody. I get to judge. Though I didn't actually judge anything there. I made the point that &quot;lost friends to terror attacks&quot; doesn't mean, &quot;vote for the guy that experts all say will be crappy for preventing more terror attacks.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not going to go into details of why I think so, but &quot;horrible anti-terrorism&quot; policies are better than the ones before. </div> </div> </div>Considering &quot;horrible&quot; in this case means, &quot;are high risk to allow more attacks,&quot; I think this does merit more detail to lend credence to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T21:22:31-08:00","id":1053030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Silver_Smoulder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1052979#post1052979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, see, I know you're lying. Because, I don't know what part of the US you're from, but the Russian diaspora in NYC voted for Trump AND they support Putin, because he is a strong leader.. The Middle-Eastern Jews predominantly voted for Trump.<br /> <br /> Also - unless you ever lost someone in a terror attack, you never get to judge. Like, literally never. I'm not going to go into details of why I think so, but &quot;horrible anti-terrorism&quot; policies are better than the ones before.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not part of the Eastern European Jewish diaspora, nor do I have friends/family in Israel, nor did I lose any family members in the 9/11 attacks, nor do I work in counter terrorism.<br /> <br /> My best friend is all of those things though, and I have obtained his permission to tell you that he goddamn despises Trump.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T23:53:53-08:00","id":1053072,"title":"","content":"To be a bit fair, I'm half Ukrainian by ethnicity, which qualifies me as half Eastern European, but that half of the family being from the solidly &quot;Ukrainian, not Russian there's a difference,&quot; side of Ukraine provides me with a very different cultural attitude regarding Putin and how Trump's talk about Putin and Russia impacts my feelings towards him compared to the current climate in the more recent Russian Jewish immigration to south Brooklyn.<br /> <br /> There is also a lot of differences between the Jews that came from Russia to the US after the fall of the Tsars, after WII and the Stalin purges, and after the fall of the Soviet Union regarding a number of political issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T21:58:42-07:00","id":1074516,"title":"","content":"And now a Syrian airfield is taken out and the alt right claim to be abandoning the 'Trump Train' left and right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T04:57:43-07:00","id":1074591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1074516#post1074516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now a Syrian airfield is taken out and the alt right claim to be abandoning the 'Trump Train' left and right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I see some articles elaborating on this? I would have thought the alt-right would be supportive of a &quot;tough&quot; move like launching an airstrike. That it was done without waiting for congressional permission would be icing on the cake. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T08:24:21-07:00","id":1074665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1074591#post1074591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I see some articles elaborating on this? I would have thought the alt-right would be supportive of a &quot;tough&quot; move like launching an airstrike. That it was done without waiting for congressional permission would be icing on the cake.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could look at their tweets. Richard Spencer called it a '<a href=\"https://twitter.com/RichardBSpencer/status/850141611652763648\" target=\"_blank\">Total Betrayal</a>' and condemned the thing, David Duke is using it as an example to suggest the '<a href=\"https://twitter.com/DrDavidDuke/status/850349499973283840\" target=\"_blank\">Zio Deep State</a>' is a thing. If you want you could check out /pol/, though it's got as many neocons as it does alt-righters. Ah, <a href=\"http://www.salon.com/2017/04/07/trolls-jump-off-the-trump-train-as-the-alt-right-expresses-anger-over-syria-actions/\" target=\"_blank\">here's an article</a>. Looks like various alt-right websites are talking about it as a betrayal too.<br /> <br /> They didn't want any more war in the Middle East until America is 'sorted out' and support governments using harsh methods to fight rebellion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-07-2017, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T10:31:18-07:00","id":1074737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1074516#post1074516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now a Syrian airfield is taken out and the alt right claim to be abandoning the 'Trump Train' left and right.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the few things I actually find myself glad that Trump has done.<br /> <br /> While I'm not a fan of the US being the world's police officer, and I've been against involvement in Syria since day one, at the same time I think there are some actions that are so monstrous and inhuman they demand a response. And the US, as a country that can respond to those nightmarish actions, <i>must</i> respond. In fact, a failure to respond not only sees other people hurt, but hurts and diminishes the US as well. Dropping chemical weapons on a civilian population, on women and children, is one of those actions.<br /> <br /> I always felt that the way Obama drew a hard line about the Syrian conflict and yet, when al-Asaad crossed it back in 2013 and used chemical weapons, the US did nothing, was serious blow to the US' integrity and moral standing. I understand, of course, that Obama wanted to get permission from Congress and was denied, but all the same it turned into a heavy blow to US prestige, not to mention that it encouraged al-Assad and other tyrants to believe that they could use chemical weapons against their own people and the world would do nothing.<br /> <br /> I'm uncertain if Trump has exceed his authority as president, by launching an attack against a foreign government. If so, there needs to be some kind of punishment. But I even if it was the wrong political choice (and if it was then he needs to be punished up to and including impeachment) nevertheless I think it was the right <i>moral</i> choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T12:21:12-07:00","id":1074794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1074737#post1074737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think it was the right <i>moral</i> choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. That depends a lot on what his reasons were for doing it, and what he does next.<br /> <br /> An aquaintance of mine today asked the question (paraphrased) - &quot;He launches tomahawk missiles at somebody to punish a crime they committed against their own country. No Americans or their allies were threatened. What would it take for him to launch a nuke at North Korea?&quot; Armed conflict isn't something that anyone should enter into casually or impulsively. The consequences of doing so may be so destructive that questions like &quot;who started it&quot; or &quot;who deserved it&quot; will lose all meaning.<br /> <br /> I agree that Assad is dangerous and that Syria may never know peace while he holds power. But it concerns me that some nasty news footage and public outcry is all it took for Ol' Donny Boy to basically commit an act of war, without congressional approval. Now Russia is sending a <a href=\"https://news.usni.org/2017/04/07/russia-sends-frigate-mediterranean-following-u-s-retaliation-strike-u-s-destroyers-remain-station\" target=\"_blank\">missile frigate</a> to the Mediterranean. This could escalate very quickly if cooler heads do not prevail.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T12:29:50-07:00","id":1074802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1074794#post1074794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An aquaintance of mine today asked the question (paraphrased) - &quot;He launches tomahawk missiles at somebody to punish a crime they committed against their own country. No Americans or their allies were threatened. What would it take for him to launch a nuke at North Korea?&quot; Armed conflict isn't something that anyone should enter into casually or impulsively. The consequences of doing so may be so destructive that questions like &quot;who started it&quot; or &quot;who deserved it&quot; will lose all meaning.<br /> <br /> I agree that Assad is dangerous and that Syria may never know peace while he holds power. But it concerns me that some nasty news footage and public outcry is all it took for Ol' Donny Boy to basically commit an act of war, without congressional approval.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair that's not quite accurate. It's meant to be because the world has, for the most part but including Syria, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chemical_Weapons_Convention\" target=\"_blank\">banned the use of chemical weapons</a> and all evidence points to Assad having been them against the rebels in his country despite this.<br /> <br /> It's a globalist move, supporting a UN convention, which is part of why the alt-right dislikes it so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-07-2017, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T12:44:41-07:00","id":1074813,"title":"","content":"This is all assuming that the theory about Trump warning russia about the strike so that Putin could warn Asad is wrong and that this whole thing isn't a huge distraction from something worse<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://wonkette.com/615283/trump-couldnt-possibly-have-weird-russian-ties-after-syria-attack-could-he-naaaaaah\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!J5tN!,w_1200,h_675,c_fill,f_jpg,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep,g_auto/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2f72552b-3bbc-4148-8cb0-3daf3c7f7f70_600x399.jpeg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://wonkette.com/615283/trump-couldnt-possibly-have-weird-russian-ties-after-syria-attack-could-he-naaaaaah\" target=\"_blank\"> Trump Couldn't POSSIBLY Have Weird Russian Ties After Syria Attack, Could He? Naaaaaah. </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://wonkette.com/615283/trump-couldnt-possibly-have-weird-russian-ties-after-syria-attack-could-he-naaaaaah\" target=\"_blank\"> https://wonkette.com/615283/trump-couldnt-possibly-have-weird-russian-ties-after-syria-attack-could-he-naaaaaah </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> FAKE NEWS </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T12:49:57-07:00","id":1074822,"title":"","content":"Yes, it would be an easy obfuscation, and necessary considering the evidence keeps piling up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T13:16:39-07:00","id":1074841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1074813#post1074813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is all assuming that the theory about Trump warning russia about the strike so that Putin could warn Asad is wrong and that this whole thing isn't a huge distraction from something worse<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://wonkette.com/615283/trump-couldnt-possibly-have-weird-russian-ties-after-syria-attack-could-he-naaaaaah\" target=\"_blank\">https://wonkette.com/615283/trump-co...ld-he-naaaaaah</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's obvious that the US government informed Russia and Syria that this was going to happen. We don't want to get into a war with Syria. Nor get into a war with Russia (whether directly or by proxy). Really, nobody wants the US to get into a war with Syria or Russia other than the neocons and, I guess some liberals who hate Trump? Who seem to be mad that he didn't kill a bunch of Syrian soldiers, in effect unilaterally declaring war on Syria? Strange people seem to be upset he <i>didn't</i> do that.<br /> <br /> Ultimately this attack was intended to primarily be a symbolic one, letting al-Assad know that there will be consequences if he continues to use chemical weapons against civilians. It was the equivalent of a police officer shooting his gun into the air as a warning, or intentionally missing the suspect to let him know that there he needs to stop doing whatever he's currently doing.<br /> <br /> It's something I think Obama should have done back in 2013 when al-Assad first used chemical weapons. So, a long time in coming but better late than never.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T13:21:30-07:00","id":1074843,"title":"","content":"Nothing about this has an upside to me. The moron in chief doing this or Americans firing more missiles at people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T13:28:12-07:00","id":1074847,"title":"","content":"It's also a nice gift to Putin. The world can focus on Trump swinging his aggression (which was most certainly illegal for no good reasons, Trump would not have had trouble getting an emergency vote for an authorization of force according to both parties' leadership) around, and ignore that Putin - as Syria's closest world power ally - completely let Assad continue the chemical attacks after Putin was supposed to be the one keeping Assad to &quot;just&quot; massacring people with conventional weapons.<br /> <br /> Putin now has more ammunition in Russia to justify more crack downs on dissidents, more military build up in western Russia, more propaganda to use against NATO and the EU to pressure former Soviet bloc countries back into the Russian fold, etc.<br /> <br /> I mean, I'm not against the use of force to crack down on atrocities, but the US application of this philosophy has been ethically unstable for decades. Our ability to claim the high ground is impossible because we repeatedly show we don't care about it as a general principle, so which ones we actually chose to do something about is always viewed under the lens of all the ones we ignore (or worse).<br /> <br /> I also think there's significant doubt this action will actually mean anything for the innocent civilians in Syria. They're still going to be gases with mustard and chlorine, even if Assad doesn't sarin anyone for a bit (though we also didn't wait for conclusive evidence of sarin gas attacks before launching this strike). There's also no clear reason why Assad would have done this if no to provoke Trump. He's currently winning against the moderate rebels while the US keeps ISIS off his back. There's no military reason to use sarin when you're winning, and your enemy is already demoralized and being slaughtered with more &quot;acceptable&quot; weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T13:30:29-07:00","id":1074848,"title":"","content":"I doubt the Russian diaspora all think alike, they both seem to be relying on antcodotal evidence to create an impression that they know what the Russian Diasora thinks, but they are individuals, with their own opinions, so I don't think anyone is lying, just different personal experiences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T20:21:59-07:00","id":1074967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1074737#post1074737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...And the US, as a country that can respond to those nightmarish actions, <i>must</i> respond...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe pivotal question always is &quot;Okay, what now?&quot; That was the primary reason that Obama never did any more in Syria than he absolutely needed to. Once you use military force, if you have no overall strategy, you have accomplished nothing. That was $70,000,000 Trump just flushed down the toilet (and that doesn't go anywhere near the potential disaster if any of the Russian military personnel at the base had been killed).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1074737#post1074737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I always felt that the way Obama drew a hard line about the Syrian conflict and yet, when al-Asaad crossed it back in 2013 and used chemical weapons, the US did nothing, was serious blow to the US' integrity and moral standing...</div> </div> </div> </div> And I <i>love</i> how Marco Rubio argued for half an hour on national television about how it was morally repugnant that Obama had not acted sooner (clearly upset that he had pushed off the responsibility onto Congress, and made it <i>their</i> problem) -- and then voted <i>against</i> the measure (because his voter base in Florida was dead-set against it). None of this stuff happens in a vacuum. Obama had good reasons for what he did. Oh, and Rubio is back at it, railing against Obama for failing to act -- despite the fact that he hasn't been president for three months.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T21:19:27-07:00","id":1074978,"title":"","content":"The general reaction to this I just find rather perplexing. Both the right and the left are justly horrified by Assad's chemical attacks, but while the right lauds a retaliatory action against Assad it continues to be against admitting the refugees escaping the conflict, and while the left wants to provide sanctuary for refugees it decries retaliatory action at the cause of the problem. Bring on the tomatoes, my body is ready.<br /> <br /> Lobbing a small fortune in exploding taxpayer dollars at someone as a wagging finger is pretty much America's post-Cold War jam. Trump has flimsy-to-nonexistent justification for ordering the strike, but the justifications for Obama's airstrikes against Libya and Clinton's airstrikes against Iraq were similarly gauzy. We've been pushing the boundaries of the War Powers Act and EO 11905 for a long-ass time now and it's a little late to suddenly remember we cared about them. Its going to take a brand new policy regime to re-articulate the limits of executive power in warmaking, and like with so many other things I lack faith in our collective political will to actually accomplish that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T23:39:06-07:00","id":1075027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1074978#post1074978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lobbing a small fortune in exploding taxpayer dollars at someone as a wagging finger is pretty much America's post-Cold War jam. Trump has flimsy-to-nonexistent justification for ordering the strike, but the justifications for Obama's airstrikes against Libya and Clinton's airstrikes against Iraq were similarly gauzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I imagine if Obama had did what Trump did, we would have seen a lot of liberals talking about what a good thing it was a conservatives decrying it. We basically saw that in Libya. Sadly, today for many people, party affiliation comes before morality. As much as the alt-right are a bunch of scummy jizzsocks, at least they're vocally pissed off about what Trump did, whereas a lot of the conservatives who would have given Obama hell over doing the same thing are cheering for Trump, purely because Obama's political affiliation started with a D and Trump's starts with an R.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T01:58:37-07:00","id":1075046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1074967#post1074967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I <i>love</i> how Marco Rubio argued for half an hour on national television about how it was morally repugnant that Obama had not acted sooner (clearly upset that he had pushed off the responsibility onto Congress, and made it <i>their</i> problem) -- and then voted <i>against</i> the measure (because his voter base in Florida was dead-set against it).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is sort of the Republican MO right now. The Democrats are guilty of it to, but less frequently.<br /> <br /> It really feels like the Republicans in the Congress are extremely afraid of actually being on the record of voting <b>for</b> anything. Voting against things, or just being hypocritical, doesn't seem to be costing them in elections, but actually voting to do things seems anathema to them.<br /> <br /> Though I'm curious (assuming he runs for reelection) how John Mccain is going to handle his rank hypocrisy on a far less morally demanding issue this week.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1074978#post1074978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and while the left wants to provide sanctuary for refugees it decries retaliatory action at the cause of the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's fair as a generalization. The left, while plenty of internal division exists, decries reactionary use of force. The left wants the use of force to come from a consistent strategy with a clear purpose and exit strategy. The left, in general, also doesn't like how much power the Executive has gained to use military force without the Legislature (and there was a lot of upset on the left at things like Obama's drone program) gving input as the Constitution demands.<br /> <br /> The left wants the Executive to be able to articulate a solid rationale of not just why we should use force, but how the use of force being discussed will actually matter to the goal.<br /> <br /> Which is why the left generally dislikes this specific use of force. It did nothing but let Trump show off his willingness to use force as a symbolic gesture. Assad launched conventional airstrikes from the base we attacked the next day. So what's the message then? Gas innocent civilians and we'll put on an expensive fireworks show?<br /> <br /> When Assad doesn't get the message to not gas people, because we didn't actually send that message effectively, what happens next?<br /> <br /> We don't know. And that's the problem.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T08:16:23-07:00","id":1075134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1074978#post1074978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The general reaction to this I just find rather perplexing. Both the right and the left are justly horrified by Assad's chemical attacks, but while the right lauds a retaliatory action against Assad it continues to be against admitting the refugees escaping the conflict, and while the left wants to provide sanctuary for refugees it decries retaliatory action at the cause of the problem. Bring on the tomatoes, my body is ready.<br /> <br /> Lobbing a small fortune in exploding taxpayer dollars at someone as a wagging finger is pretty much America's post-Cold War jam. Trump has flimsy-to-nonexistent justification for ordering the strike, but the justifications for Obama's airstrikes against Libya and Clinton's airstrikes against Iraq were similarly gauzy. We've been pushing the boundaries of the War Powers Act and EO 11905 for a long-ass time now and it's a little late to suddenly remember we cared about them. Its going to take a brand new policy regime to re-articulate the limitsi power in warmaking, and like with so many other things I lack faith in our collective political will to actually accomplish that.</div> </div> </div> </div> The tomato comment made me laugh. <br /> <br /> Has anyone considered the possibility that Syria is telling the truth and that the chemicals were unleashed when a bomb hit the rebels on stockpile of chemical weapons. <br /> <br /> I'm not saying I believe it or not, but it's worth investigating before action gets taken, which is why unilateral actions based on pure emotions are bad ones. <br /> <br /> If Syria did do it then I understand punishing them, but how can we really know if no investigation occurred? <br /> <br /> Investigators should have been sent to find out which side is telling the truth, if either of them is. <br /> <br /> People we're killed in America's attack, if they held the wrong people responsible than those people died for nothing. <br /> <br /> Again I'm not saying Syria is innocent, but just firing away without looking to allies and the international community and doing an actual on the ground investiagation sets a bad presciedience. <br /> <br /> Even if America got it right this time, what about next time? <br /> <br /> Does Trump just blow shit up every time he decides to shoot from the hip?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T15:12:51-07:00","id":1075267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1075046#post1075046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When Assad doesn't get the message to not gas people, because we didn't actually send that message effectively, what happens next?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I would say the warning we just sent Syria was a bit louder and clearer than the one we gave them back back in 2014. In fact, I imagine al-Assad had assumed we would react in a similar fashion - that after all of Trump's talk about wanting to stay out of the Middle East, and how he wanted to have closer ties to Russia, this meant that Syria would be able to get away with using chemical weapons and the US would again fail to take meaningful action and instead react the same way as it did 4 years earlier. That we would just wring our hands and say mean things about him to the UN like last time and that would be that.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately for him, he found out that's not the case, and no doubt Russia gave Syria a stern warning to lay off killing civilians with chemical weapons in the future. While Russia (and Syria) don't know for sure what the US will do if Syria uses chemical weapons again, they're probably not too eager to find it. At the least it's safe to say neither nation feels the continued use of chemical weapons against civilians is worth the possibility of an actual war with the US, or whatever escalated response the US may choose to dish out in the future.<br /> <br /> Whereas before al-Assad was (understandably) pretty confident in his ability to use chemical weapons without worrying about a response from the US or the rest of the world, now he's probably rather less certain that he can use a chemical weapon, free from facing some kind of retribution for doing so.<br /> <br /> Now, is making al-Assad and other dictators think twice before unleashing chemical weapons against civilian populations worth 80 million dollars? Personally I would say absolutely. Missiles are made to be used after all, and if we can use these missiles, in a way that doesn't actually kill anyone and helps ensure that chemical weapons aren't used to slaughter civilians, then I feel that's a fairly good way to use a missile all told. At the least it's a somewhat more moral use of a missile than using it to blow a bunch of dudes up.<br /> <br /> Some people, of course, disagree. I've seen people elsewhere essentially say that if you spend money on a missile and then fire it in a way that doesn't kill other people, or that doesn't dish out massive property damage, then you've &quot;wasted&quot; the money you invested in the weapon. But well, different people will have different judgments when it comes to cost/benefit analysis that involves human lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T22:12:56-07:00","id":1075374,"title":"","content":"Guys I just realized something, If trump is working with the Russians, then it would be a weird inversion of the team up between The US and Russia during the Civil War, the First republican president cuts a deal with Russia, and now a a repub who is a near complete opposite to him may be cutting a deal with Russia.<br /> <br /> Am I seeing something that isn't there, or does this mean something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T02:19:39-07:00","id":1075409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1074978#post1074978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The general reaction to this I just find rather perplexing. Both the right and the left are justly horrified by Assad's chemical attacks, but while the right lauds a retaliatory action against Assad it continues to be against admitting the refugees escaping the conflict, and while the left wants to provide sanctuary for refugees it decries retaliatory action at the cause of the problem. Bring on the tomatoes, my body is ready.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I don't think either set of positions is necessarily really inconsistent.<br /> <br /> Being for a strikes (and I'm not informed enough to say whether it was the right idea) doesn't mean you agree that the first safe country principle stops applying. The principle that people should seek asylum in the nearest countries with low cultural distance doesn't stop applying. It doesn't stop being a good argument that it makes more sense more long term sense for everyone for Syrian refugees to be accepted en masse by, for example, a more culturally and geographically proximate country like Israel rather than the US, France, Germany, etc.<br /> <br /> Also doesn't also seem inconsistent to accept refugees (rejecting the first safe country principle) while rejecting strikes as a good means of intervention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T02:56:42-07:00","id":1075419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1075267#post1075267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I would say the warning we just sent Syria was a bit louder and clearer than the one we gave them back back in 2014.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on what actual evidence of any change in Assad's positions?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...this meant that Syria would be able to get away with using chemical weapons... </div> </div> </div>Just because this bugs me:<br /> <br /> Syria's been using chemical weapons this whole time. The agreement was just to keep the super-bad WMD stuff like sarin and VX off the table. He's been dropping bombs on civilian targets this whole time.<br /> <br /> The agreement to get him to hold back at all was a good thing, but lets not kid ourselves that either Obama was or Trump is ready to use the amount of force necessary to actually end the atrocities in Syria. They'd both settle for the symbolic win because they've both said that trying to full on stop Assad isn't a politically realistic option.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ..and no doubt Russia gave Syria a stern warning to lay off killing civilians with chemical weapons in the future. </div> </div> </div>I very much doubt this. Russia's hasn't done anything publicly to indicate they care at all about stopping Assad from doing this again. All of Russia's recent bluster has been about how bad the US was by acting in a hasty unilateral fashion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While Russia (and Syria) don't know for sure what the US will do if Syria uses chemical weapons again, they're probably not too eager to find it. </div> </div> </div>I think Russia absolutely wants to find out. Either they get to diminish US credibility by showing Trump's missile strikes are just for show, or the US unilaterally declares war on a sovereign nation for emotional moral reasons and Putin gets to claim the same justification for military actions if he pulls another Crimea. There's very little downside for Russia if the US does this again, or escalates, because Assad crosses the line again. <br /> <br /> If Trump had taken the time to actually get the support of the International community first, Russia might have reasons to be more cautious.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, is making al-Assad and other dictators think twice before unleashing chemical weapons against civilian populations worth 80 million dollars? Personally I would say absolutely. </div> </div> </div>Again though, show me that this actually worked for that purpose. Because I've seen nothing in the news at all that indicates that the missiles did jack shit to scare any dictators. World leaders seem way more scared that Trump's going to set off a nuclear war with North Korea as the big take away from all this.<br /> <br /> It's not about whether or not weapons are made to be used. It's whether or not you used them in a way that actually accomplished anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T03:09:00-07:00","id":1075422,"title":"","content":"What bothers me is what is going to happen after Assad is oused. Democratic elections? Sure, we all saw how that turned out in northern Africa after its presidents were removed from power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T07:01:35-07:00","id":1075459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1075422#post1075422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What bothers me is what is going to happen after Assad is oused. Democratic elections? Sure, we all saw how that turned out in northern Africa after its presidents were removed from power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoah, you're puttin' the cart before the horse, mate!<br /> <br /> Who says Assad is being ousted? Seems to me that we're a ways off from that happening. In fact, I'm not sure how that CAN happen if Russia doesn't stop propping him up, regardless of what the US does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T09:33:02-07:00","id":1075502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1075419#post1075419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Russia absolutely wants to find out. Either they get to diminish US credibility by showing Trump's missile strikes are just for show, or the US unilaterally declares war on a sovereign nation for emotional moral reasons and Putin gets to claim the same justification for military actions if he pulls another Crimea. There's very little downside for Russia if the US does this again, or escalates, because Assad crosses the line again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Russia does not want the US to declare war on Syria and bring about regime change. Oh, they'd love to see us get mired in another war, but not one with Syria. Syria is far too valuable to Russia for many reasons. It's a major port that Russia can use for its navy. It's one of the few nations that is very friendly to Russia in the Middle East. It's on the other side of Turkey which gives it even more of a strategic advantage. There is a reason why Russia has been working so closely to prop up Assad's regime. It doesn't want to see Syria collapse and it really doesn't want to risk seeing the US go in and install an anti-Russian government.<br /> <br /> If Russia honestly believes that the US is going to go into Syria, they'll do what they can to stop it. And if Russia thinks that Assad's continued use of chemical weapons will lead to the US attempting a regime change in Syria, they'll tell Assad to not use chemical weapons. Regime change in Syria is absolutely not in Russia's best interest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T09:35:42-07:00","id":1075503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1075422#post1075422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What bothers me is what is going to happen after Assad is oused. Democratic elections? Sure, we all saw how that turned out in northern Africa after its presidents were removed from power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this wasn't about regime change, and so far nothing from Trump or his spokespeople suggests we're going to see a push for regime change. It was purely about sending Assad (and Russia) a message that Syria should be very careful if it decides to use Sarin gas again in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T14:24:54-07:00","id":1075585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1074841#post1074841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's obvious that the US government informed Russia and Syria that this was going to happen. We don't want to get into a war with Syria. Nor get into a war with Russia (whether directly or by proxy). Really, nobody wants the US to get into a war with Syria or Russia other than the neocons and, I guess some liberals who hate Trump? Who seem to be mad that he didn't kill a bunch of Syrian soldiers, in effect unilaterally declaring war on Syria? Strange people seem to be upset he <i>didn't</i> do that.<br /> <br /> Ultimately this attack was intended to primarily be a symbolic one, letting al-Assad know that there will be consequences if he continues to use chemical weapons against civilians. It was the equivalent of a police officer shooting his gun into the air as a warning, or intentionally missing the suspect to let him know that there he needs to stop doing whatever he's currently doing.<br /> <br /> It's something I think Obama should have done back in 2013 when al-Assad first used chemical weapons. So, a long time in coming but better late than never.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even though this is from a few days ago I am going to expand on it about what a friend told me happened about 20 years ago. He used to be in the Army and was one of the dismounts in a Bradley. One day after running a RPG game his unit got sent to Somalia and arrived just after the events in Black Hawk Down. So with that in mind he is what he told me. <br /> <br /> There was a hill top compound just outside Mogadishu that was causing some problems. So in order to send a message they dropped leaflets all over the place informing people not to be at the compound at a certain point in the next few days. So at the appointed time two AC-130 Gunships circled the compound and totally destroyed everything and left nothing standing. So bombing the airfield after warning Russia is an established practiced used by the US Military.<br /> <br /> The moral of this story is make sure you have your books on you at all times so when in the field you can still run a game, for all the bored people.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T20:25:04-07:00","id":1075696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1075502#post1075502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Russia does not want the US to declare war on Syria and bring about regime change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Russia doesn't want us to actually make regime change happen... but keep in mind that we're already basically doing that. The US has been supporting anti-Assad rebels the whole time.<br /> <br /> The US escalating things unilaterally doesn't necessarily harm Russia's interests, especially if it sabotages our attempts to support anti-Assad forces. leaving nobody for us to install instead of Assad besides ISIS (or whoever).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if Russia thinks that Assad's continued use of chemical weapons will lead to the US attempting a regime change in Syria, they'll tell Assad to not use chemical weapons. Regime change in Syria is absolutely not in Russia's best interest. </div> </div> </div>Well, we'll need to actually convince them that's the case. Saying we're going to lob missiles at them but not go in on the ground is saying we're not going to try to push harder for regime change than we are.<br /> <br /> As you say:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1075503#post1075503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, this wasn't about regime change, and so far nothing from Trump or his spokespeople suggests we're going to see a push for regime change.</div> </div> </div> </div>So why should Russia worry about regime change in Syria because of WMD use?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T23:14:30-07:00","id":1075740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1075696#post1075696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So why should Russia worry about regime change in Syria because of WMD use?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because if it becomes apparent that the <i>only</i> way to get Syria to stop using banned chemical weapons against civilians is through regime change because the other alternatives have not worked, then there isn't much left to do. Going to the UN, didn't work. We tried that back in 2014 the first time this happened. So this time the US escalated the response and fired some missiles. If that also doesn't work, and Assad keeps using banned chemical weapons, then the US' responses will continue to escalate. And continued escalation means that eventually regime change will be the only option on the table.<br /> <br /> Russia does not want the US' response to escalate to the point of regime change. They like having Assad in charge of Syria and don't want to see a government that would probably be rather more pro-US replace the one that exists now. Even if people in the new Syrian government didn't like the US much, they'd probably like it more than Russia who was helping the old Syrian regime carry out war-crimes against civilians. And Assad also doesn't want to see regime change happen. He's smart enough to realize that if regime change occurred he would probably end up like Saddam and Gaddafi. The best he could hope for would be a trial at the Hague for war-crimes and life in prison.<br /> <br /> And no, many in the US don't want a regime change either. It was no fun in Iraq, no fun in Afghanistan and no fun in Libya. What we wanted was for Assad to stop using banned chemical weapons in his civil war. But if it becomes apparent that regime change is the only way to do that then... well, who can say for sure what will happen? It's possible that the US could just back down and ultimately decide to do nothing. But if we get to that point we might also might say, &quot;Fuck it. We have no choice left but to get rid of Assad.&quot; And the many pictures of dead babies we would have seen by that point would have gotten a lot more of the American public behind that sentiment.<br /> <br /> I mean, would <i>you</i> want to take a bet on what Donald Trump's policy on regime change in Syria will be two years form now if the Syrian and Russian governments ignore him and Assad keeps using Sarin? Trump is extremely unpredictable and I don't think Putin or Assad would want to take a gamble like that.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* Though it looks Assad and Putin won't have to wait two years seeing as how the US is <a href=\"http://www.cnn.com/2017/04/09/middleeast/syria-missile-strike-chemical-attack-aftermath/index.html\" target=\"_blank\">now pushing for a regime change in Syria sooner rather than later.</a> It seems Trump has reached the opinion that regime change really <i>is</i> the only option on the table. So it'll be interesting to see what this means, Arming the anti-Assad rebels? Creating a no-fly zone for Syrian aircraft? Destroying military targets?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 04-10-2017, 02:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T00:13:55-07:00","id":1075761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1075740#post1075740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because if it becomes apparent that the <i>only</i> way to get Syria to stop using banned chemical weapons against civilians is through regime change because the other alternatives have not worked, then there isn't much left to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but it seems in the current political climate, the US would give up rather than actually go for full scale regime change. Esp. since it's going to be really hard for Trump to do anything more than long range ineffectual strikes without an AUMF to go to war with Syria (the current standing AUMFs have already be stretched to their theoretical limits as is), and there isn't the political support on a bipartisan level for that level of authorization.<br /> <br /> If there was a realistic risk of this level of escalation, Russia might have reasons to worry, but since there's no hint of it, there's no reason to.<br /> <br /> I think you also have to look at the history of how gas attacks have been used in the Syrian civil war. Assad's use of chemical weapons is part of strategy of modern siege warfare. He encircles rebel held areas, cuts off utilities, water, and food, and then makes life hell until they surrender or die. That's why out of over 400,000 dead only ~1,100 have been chalked up to gas attacks. The gas isn't being used like it was in WWI. It's being used as part of a larger escalation of demoralization and area denial. If Assad only uses banned weapons 2 or 3 more times... it basically means he's massacred his way to an undeniable victory anyway. He usually doesn't have to escalate that far to retake an area (though it's questionable if he ever did, and if the banned gas attacks are more him just teabagging the rebels, at which point again, if he has a few more uses before the US or international community will actually try to depose him, it isn't going to change his current tactics).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T10:13:06-07:00","id":1075941,"title":"","content":"You have much more faith in Donald Trump and the American public than I do Heavy Arms. I tend to view America as something of an unstable and irrational actor that often panics and makes poor choices and bad responses. That's also how Russia has traditionally viewed the US, especially during the Cold War where Putin (and many others) honestly believed the US would freak out and launch a nuclear first strike against Russia. In fact, in many ways I think Trump's election and subsequent actions perhaps show that there is some merit to that perception.<br /> <br /> This is why it's always been hard to say with any surety what America will be doing in several years, let alone now that Trump is in charge. He already did a 180 degree about face on Syria in a couple of days, and if he comes to the conclusion that regime change is necessary (and it seems he has) there are a lot of people in Congress on both sides of the aisle who would also like to see regime change - neocons, humanitarians, and others. And if we get more pictures and more stories about the horrors in Syria, you just might see many other Americans doing a 180 degree about face on Syria, just like Trump did.<br /> <br /> If Putin and Assad are too blind to realize that they're playing with fire and that continued use of banned chemical weapons only risks the likelihood that the US will choose to more deeply involve itself in Syria, then it will probably be unfortunate for many people. But I have a feeling that they're not. Assad will probably come to the conclusion that he can win his civil war without the use of banned chemical weapons. The only thing using them will do will be to cause the US to retaliate, and maybe the next time we retaliate and launch missiles we'll actually demolish some airbases, actually hurting his ability to wage war, which makes using something like Sarin far less attractive than it was before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T11:42:29-07:00","id":1075999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1075941#post1075941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have much more faith in Donald Trump and the American public than I do Heavy Arms.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a matter of &quot;faith.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's a matter of looking around and seeing where the public is, and what the politicians have actually done (instead of what they've said).<br /> <br /> I have little faith in Trump to do anything that isn't playing to the public image he wants to project. He accomplished that with a low risk low military reward action. He got heaps of praise for using the least effective military force possible, and got to flex his muscles as a strongman in front of China (again, the much more disturbing aspect of all this is the highly probable fact that Trump chose this specific option for no other reason than the chance to show China that he's ready to go hot in North Korea). The only &quot;faith&quot; I have here is that if Trump tries to significantly escalate in Syria, with the current climate of the rest of all of this, is that it will result in a lot of negative backlash and possibly another embarrassing failure in Legislature if they don't give him an AUMF to declare unilateral war on the sovereign nation of Syria (he esp. doesn't want to look like Obama did after that happened to him). <br /> <br /> I have more faith in the general public, if only because the public is exercising it's only real power right now: being loudly displeased. I don't have a lot of faith that we'll remember all this when it comes to the next few elections. But that aside, the public is also doing things that put a damper on this. Military (and Homeland Security) recruitment is suffering after the prolonged military actions in Afghanistan, Iraq, and what we're already doing in Syria. The fervor of the post 9/11 years is long since dead as we have a lot of vets back from overseas clearly soured on the value of their service. How ever much anger there is about Assad's actions, it's not translating into people lining up to go over there and get rid of him. The neo-cons and humanitarian interventionist lefties have all backed down in the past under these conditions. They don't want to go home and have to run a campaign defending adding Syria to the list of countries the US military is going to be mired down in for who knows how long<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I tend to view America as something of an unstable and irrational actor that often panics and makes poor choices and bad responses. </div> </div> </div>I don't entirely disagree... but that's exactly what I consider Trump's actions here, and the media/pundit/pol response to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if we get more pictures and more stories about the horrors in Syria, you just might see many other Americans doing a 180 degree about face on Syria, just like Trump did. </div> </div> </div>Six years hasn't moved most Americans as it is. Hell, it hasn't moved us to let a significant number of refugees fleeing that into our country (which is a far less troublesome action than going to war). I don't see any reason for the US public to do a 180 now unless Assad does something directly against us or our allies. If Assad does something insane like barrel bomb a bunch of US soldiers because they're with anti-Assad rebels? Then yeah, we'll 180 so fast our heads will spin off. But we've had six years of horrific images coming out of Syria. There's no reason to assume that the public is going to shift on it now.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T14:01:20-07:00","id":1076092,"title":"","content":"I think you are severely underestimating how fickle the American public can be, and how fickle Trump specifically can be. Just because they have an opinion about something last year doesn't mean they'll hold the same opinion next year. While previously you didn't have any major politicians besides John McCain talking about regime change, there is a growing sense in Trump's inner circle that regime change is the only way to bring peace to Syria and to end ISIS. You've even got Rex Tillerson and Nikki Haley giving dueling narratives in public, and it's clear Trump has no solid opinion one way or another. If Trump becomes convinced that regime change is necessary and begins pushing for it, you very well may see a change in public opinion on the subject. And he certainly won't find it hard to get allies, as there are quite a few Republicans and Democrats who would wholeheartedly support regime change in Syria.<br /> <br /> Regardless though, I still think Trump's response to this action on Assad's part was marginally superior to the response the world gave Assad the last time. Sure it could have been better (if I were president I would have maybe dropped a one of those missiles on Assad's house) but it was still better than not doing anything at all and giving Assad tacit approval to continue. When it's clear that the UN is incapable of taking action, even for egregious actions like this, I think it's a good thing that the US takes matters into its own hands. So while Trump's actions could have certainly been more thorough and, in my mind, fell short of the response he should have given, it was still somewhat better than the response Obama gave back in 2014.<br /> <br /> *Edit* Heck, now we have <a href=\"http://www.cnn.com/2017/04/10/politics/donald-trump-syria-barrel-bombs-gas/\" target=\"_blank\">Spicer saying that the US will respond to Assad in the same way if he uses barrel bombs or gas against civilians again.</a> I'm down with that. I think when countries commit war crimes, they need to held accountable. And if the UN won't do it then I have no problem with the US stepping up to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 04-10-2017, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T14:16:39-07:00","id":1076662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1075046#post1075046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I'm curious (assuming he runs for reelection) how John Mccain is going to handle his rank hypocrisy on a far less morally demanding issue this week.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess you haven't heard... McCain has already stated that this was his last election. It sounds like he's going the Boehner route and just throwing his hands up in disgust at the whole Tea Party / Freedom Caucus thing... and if they (and Trump) keep giving Paul Ryan sh**, I wouldn't be a bit surprised if he follows suit at some point. After the AHCA debacle, you could almost see the seething frustration in him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T14:58:11-07:00","id":1076671,"title":"","content":"So, just when you think Trump can't be anymore dangerous to the United States and the world at large, he tops himself and launches missiles into Syria.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, Al-Assad is a horrible dictator and I abhor the use of chemical weapons, especially against civilians. But this missile strike may be jumping the gun. Regime change shouldn't be done in a hurry, otherwise you end up with a disaster like Iraq after we toppled Saddam. Also, this brazen act, regardless of whether or not it is justified, could have massive repercussions, especially in regards to our relationship with Russia, which is already strained.<br /> <br /> I hate Al-Assad and in a perfect world, we'd oust him and establish a stable democratic republic, but we are not in a perfect world. And if we take out Al-Assad, could that give ISIS a second wind and gain more power in the region?<br /> <br /> This whole debacle has got me legitimately terrified and sometimes I wonder if this is the opening act of World War III. I'm not being hyperbolic here either, between the Russian and Iranian governments backing Syria and all the other countries in the region whose security is threatened by a regime change as well as ISIS, I think a conventional-scale World War III could happen. I doubt it would go nuclear like in the hypothetical Cold War scenarios, but it would ravage the global economy and a lot of innocent people would be killed.<br /> <br /> We dug our own graves the day we elected Trump.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T17:27:05-07:00","id":1076727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l-