uicide bombs. <br /> <br /> Sadly at the end of the day, Afghanistan is a shitshow and there's no easy solution. At the least, I think withdrawing and allowing the Taliban and ISIS to take control over the country would probably be the worst outcome, though unfortunately staying there for the next 10, or 20, or 30, or 100 years seems to be the only other real choice on the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T19:53:53-07:00","id":1078127,"title":"","content":"The reports that Russia may have begun providing support to the Taliban have a certain gruesome irony to them. Those tables never stop turning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T19:06:16-07:00","id":1093063,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://68.media.tumblr.com/f9f22c9c8adde6a7d6cd4fadfe1d7deb/tumblr_inline_oq0vkoHvJ61tti4cw_540.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> 45, everyone","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T03:12:02-07:00","id":1093169,"title":"","content":"<br /> <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/the-scariest-lesson-of-the-holocaust/2015/04/16/ffa8e23c-e468-11e4-905f-cc896d379a32_story.html?utm_term=.28818e14ee82\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.washingtonpost.com/opini...=.28818e14ee82</a><br /> [/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> <br /> This is the most unbelivable sh.t I ever read/heared of. It's just f...g unbelivable. This man is ignorant to the core. Propably he missed every history lesson about WWII. I just can't belive it. Just can't. I'm from Poland and when this news appeared everyone I know just said ,,wtf is he saying?&quot;. It's like I've been claiming that American nazis started world war 2 - ridiculous but dangerous. Cause if someone would repeat this lie many times it might become true 50 years later.<br /> <br /> Truly, I was happy seeing Trump elected. I have many objections against Clintons, both. But then Kissinger appeared again, a man who would erease my country from European map after WWII.<br /> <br /> The real problem USA has it China. And new silk road. China bought european countries with idea of silk road. Chinese bank is prospering for example in Warsaw. Chinese president was treated like chinese emperor during visit in Britain. Chinese companies are in South Africa and in the northern part of Russia.<br /> <br /> Second problem - migration from Africa to Europe and other places. It touches USA too. USA won't make good deals with unstable countries. Unstable european union. Thank God my country is safe place for it's citizens. For now. But what migration did to France? French companies are trying to move to Poland. Because of safety. And for that Poland is called enemy of democracy and worse. It's all about safety, sea/land trade = money and other very important thing I won't mention here.<br /> <br /> Oh. And last thing. We're in Poland are in big deep sh.t. Few young analysts after american academies returned to Poland and things they are saying aren't optimistic. My country goverment should recalibrate their thinking from local to global. From end of WW2 we weren't even pawns. We existed because we were allowed to. Before 2016 our ruling party was dancing in german tune. Now when we try to change that, try to have own political agenda, we're called fasists, nazis and other. The problem is Poland ows USA a lot (special forces for example, I've read a good book/interview with founder of polish Grom). But USA used us too. Now our prim minister is in China bowing before Xi Jin Ping and talking about silk road. Problem is - our politics are clumsy. They don't know how to balance things but they have to do it if they want to keep country safe and independent. Besides. We have our own migration problems and EU is blindly telling us about Africa imigrants. I'm telling about Ukrainian running from war. cause war in the Ukraine is still running and everybody forget about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1784,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","user":"werewolf43","date":". 05-16-2017, 07:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T11:39:55-07:00","id":1093355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1093063#post1093063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"https://68.media.tumblr.com/f9f22c9c8adde6a7d6cd4fadfe1d7deb/tumblr_inline_oq0vkoHvJ61tti4cw_540.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> 45, everyone</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's truly time for the American people, in tangible way, to come to grips that it's system of government is broken.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T11:53:23-07:00","id":1093364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1093355#post1093355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's truly time for the American people, in tangible way, to come to grips that it's system of government is broken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. So what?<br /> <br /> Don't leave with that. Don't just say &quot;shit's broke, yo&quot;, and then offer no solutions or alternatives. It's unhelpful at best and infuriating at worst.<br /> <br /> As for me, I refuse to accept that this &quot;broken&quot; system cannot be repaired. I'm working to flip congressional control in 2018, financially supporting protest groups (especially protest groups taking legal action against the Trump administration), and engaging in dialogue wherever I can to try to raise people's awareness of the chaos and dysfunction at the highest levels of our government. I believe things can be turned around, and quickly, if only enough people commit themselves to making that happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 05-16-2017, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T11:55:50-07:00","id":1093365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1093364#post1093364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. So what?<br /> <br /> Don't leave with that. Don't just say &quot;shit's broke, yo&quot;, and then offer no solutions or alternatives. It's unhelpful at best and infuriating at worst.<br /> <br /> As for me, I refuse to accept that this &quot;broken&quot; system cannot be repaired. I'm working to flip congressional control in 2018, financially supporting protest groups (especially protest groups taking legal action against the Trump administration), and engaging in dialogue wherever I can to try to raise people's awareness of the chaos and dysfunction at the highest levels of our government. I things can be turned around, and quickly, if only enough people commit themselves to making that happen.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This.<br /> <br /> I got too many people on my facebook who are cheering Trump on because he's going to dismantle the big bad government. I hate people who are like &quot;It's broken, let's burn it down!&quot; I mean, if you got a hole in the roof, you fix your roof, not burn the whole place down and become homeless. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T12:44:15-07:00","id":1093379,"title":"","content":"I think the system, as it is right now, is essentially broken. For a democratic republic to function, you well informed voters who come out to vote. And unfortunately, America does not really have this. People don't vote and a lot of people frankly don't care. &quot;Any politician is the same as any other - they're all crooks,&quot; is an old mantra and lots of people believe it. What that means is that special interests end up holding more sway with many politicians than the actual voters do. That's what's wrong with America's system - too much of the electorate simply isn't engaged and doesn't give a damn about the political system.<br /> <br /> I can't really blame people for that. I mean, what I keep coming back to is that before Trump got involved in the Republican primary, the prediction was that it would be Jeb Bush vs Hillary Clinton. And at the time <i>I</i> was considering just not voting at all and just giving up on the political process if it came to that. And, while I think Trump is a terrible scumbag, he <i>has</i> opened a lot of people's eyes. People are realizing that voting <i>does</i> matter, people are regretting they <i>didn't</i> vote, and a lot of people are waiting to be heard in 2018.<br /> <br /> So in a way, I would point towards someone like Trump as being an excellent method of fixing the system. By screwing up so badly, he's going to get people much more passionate about politics. They'll pay more attention to what's going on and be more willing to go vote. In theory, that's how you fix the system - by using your vote to remind politicians they work for you, not themselves and not special interest groups. Or at least that's what should happen.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately the political system in the US has been so heavily hijacked, rigged and gerrymandered that in many respects, having more people vote may not actually change much of anything. Even if more people show up to vote, in many places you already know who is going to win. And this means that the people who have to change the system are the very people who gained (and retain) power due to the system, which makes them the last people who will want to change it. And they have the power to limit what other people can do and how they can respond.<br /> <br /> So from where we're sitting right now, at the end of the day, the voters have to vote and hope that the people who have gained the most from the broken system are going to turn around and change things. Maybe burning down the system really is the only solution. At least sometimes it seems more reasonable that hoping the SOB's who broke the system in the first place, so that they'd get more power, will suddenly do an about-face and fix everything.<br /> <br /> I don't know. I'm feeling pretty cynical today. Maybe next week I'll be more bright, hopeful and cheerful about things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T12:45:00-07:00","id":1093381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1093364#post1093364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. So what?<br /> <br /> Don't leave with that. Don't just say &quot;shit's broke, yo&quot;, and then offer no solutions or alternatives. It's unhelpful at best and infuriating at worst.<br /> <br /> As for me, I refuse to accept that this &quot;broken&quot; system cannot be repaired. I'm working to flip congressional control in 2018, financially supporting protest groups (especially protest groups taking legal action against the Trump administration), and engaging in dialogue wherever I can to try to raise people's awareness of the chaos and dysfunction at the highest levels of our government. I believe things can be turned around, and quickly, if only enough people commit themselves to making that happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I felt like putting that in that post, I would have. Don't try to dictate to people what they do and do not post. As for me, since I still believe in the the system in the U.K. I am gladly going to return there, try to convince my daughter to look at prospects there or in Europe. Find your own solutions. Also, know what is unhelpful? thinking a table top rpg forum is the best place to post that sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 05-16-2017, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T12:49:20-07:00","id":1093384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1093365#post1093365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This.<br /> <br /> I got too many people on my facebook who are cheering Trump on because he's going to dismantle the big bad government. I hate people who are like &quot;It's broken, let's burn it down!&quot; I mean, if you got a hole in the roof, you fix your roof, not burn the whole place down and become homeless.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Then those people are idiots, because while he has put some people in positions that want to dismantle some current systems, their end goal isn't anarchy but to put more things in place that profit them and their elitist friends. If they think that is burning something down they're deluding themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T15:04:28-07:00","id":1093425,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2017/05/16/us/politics/james-comey-trump-flynn-russia-investigation.html\" target=\"_blank\">Comey Memo Says Trump Asked Him to End Flynn Investigation</a><br /> <br /> I'm glad he didn't use an email to do it. That would have been <i>terrible</i>.<br /> <br /> So how's that Swamp draining going, Trump voters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T15:59:32-07:00","id":1093437,"title":"","content":"Well, we may be talking about President Pence by the end of summer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T16:38:27-07:00","id":1093450,"title":"","content":"It's a possibility, if the house does it's job.At the very least, Pence would be a horrible person turned professional president, but I suspect that if Trump goes down he won't be going down alone if he can help it. It might be President Ryan when all is said and done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T17:37:43-07:00","id":1093465,"title":"","content":"Hasn't representatives of the house already stated they're not interested in getting a special prosecutor to investigate the Trump-Russia matters? And given the recent comments by important government departments that the whole &quot;Trump sharing secrets with Russia - Fake News&quot; thing is a distraction from the more serious crime of people leaking such information, makes me inclined to think the odds of anything happening to Trump anytime soon is negligible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T18:29:49-07:00","id":1093484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1093381#post1093381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I felt like putting that in that post, I would have. Don't try to dictate to people what they do and do not post. As for me, since I still believe in the the system in the U.K. I am gladly going to return there, try to convince my daughter to look at prospects there or in Europe. Find your own solutions. Also, know what is unhelpful? thinking a table top rpg forum is the best place to post that sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I challenge negativity wherever I find it. Here, IRL, doesn't matter. Nobody, anywhere, improves the world by dismissing it as unfixable. <br /> <br /> ...and you are also presenting a political position in a TTRPG forum, in a dedicated thread on the topic. I don't know why I should not do likewise. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1093379#post1093379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately the political system in the US has been so heavily hijacked, rigged and gerrymandered that in many respects, having more people vote may not actually change much of anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>The voter numbers are only a starting point. The gerrymandering you see now is partly the product of a deliberate Republican powermongering campaign that has been going on since 2008 - lookup REDMAP, or Redistricting Majority Project. But REDMAP can be reversed, if the right people are put in charge, and that <i>can</i> happen if enough of the middle class rallies against conservative politicians in the next 2-4 years. With someone as horrendously unpopular as Trump in charge, that might just happen. I can think of no better time to try and tip the scales. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1093465#post1093465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hasn't representatives of the house already stated they're not interested in getting a special prosecutor to investigate the Trump-Russia matters? And given the recent comments by important government departments that the whole &quot;Trump sharing secrets with Russia - Fake News&quot; thing is a distraction from the more serious crime of people leaking such information, makes me inclined to think the odds of anything happening to Trump anytime soon is negligible.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you call &quot;soon?&quot; If you mean &quot;this year&quot;, you're probably right - something really calamitously stupid would have to happen for the Republican majority to break away from him. Even Nixon <a href=\"https://fivethirtyeight.com/features/even-the-biggest-scandals-cant-kill-party-loyalty/\" target=\"_blank\">enjoyed majority support from his own party</a>. But once 2018 rolls around, we'll see...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T19:24:24-07:00","id":1093495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1093465#post1093465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hasn't representatives of the house already stated they're not interested in getting a special prosecutor to investigate the Trump-Russia matters? And given the recent comments by important government departments that the whole &quot;Trump sharing secrets with Russia - Fake News&quot; thing is a distraction from the more serious crime of people leaking such information, makes me inclined to think the odds of anything happening to Trump anytime soon is negligible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, there's no doubt that if Hillary had won the election and done the things Trump has done (obstructed justice, spilled top secret information to the Russians, etc) the Republicans would have already drawn up articles of impeachment against her.<br /> <br /> Eventually I think the Republicans will feel they have no choice but to get rid of Trump. They want to get legislation passed, and that won't happen when Trump's scandals are the only thing anyone is talking about. And this latest scandal, asking Comey to drop his investigation into Flynn, and then basically firing him when he refused to do so is pretty bad. Even many Republicans have to admit that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T19:56:23-07:00","id":1093507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1093495#post1093495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eventually I think the Republicans will feel they have no choice but to get rid of Trump. They want to get legislation passed, and that won't happen when Trump's scandals are the only thing anyone is talking about. And this latest scandal, asking Comey to drop his investigation into Flynn, and then basically firing him when he refused to do so is pretty bad. Even many Republicans have to admit that.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're getting the health care thing passed. They're still driving a LOT of changes through the process right now. If anything, I'd argue that the highly distracting actions of the president make for a fantastic thing for the houses, there's not enough attention paid to what they're doing, *because* it's all focused on the president and his antics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T20:10:51-07:00","id":1093513,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.cnbc.com/2017/05/16/trump-allegedly-asked-comey-to-consider-imprisoning-members-of-the-press.html\" target=\"_blank\">Trump reportedly asked Comey to consider imprisoning members of the press</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T20:28:19-07:00","id":1093516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1093495#post1093495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, there's no doubt that if Hillary had won the election and done the things Trump has done (obstructed justice, spilled top secret information to the Russians, etc) the Republicans would have already drawn up articles of impeachment against her.<br /> <br /> Eventually I think the Republicans will feel they have no choice but to get rid of Trump. They want to get legislation passed, and that won't happen when Trump's scandals are the only thing anyone is talking about. And this latest scandal, asking Comey to drop his investigation into Flynn, and then basically firing him when he refused to do so is pretty bad. Even many Republicans have to admit that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That mirrors my thoughts. Eventually they will have to get rid of him, but by then the damage done will be significant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T20:50:35-07:00","id":1093521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1093507#post1093507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're getting the health care thing passed. They're still driving a LOT of changes through the process right now. If anything, I'd argue that the highly distracting actions of the president make for a fantastic thing for the houses, there's not enough attention paid to what they're doing, *because* it's all focused on the president and his antics.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The House managed to barely pass a bill changing healthcare. The problem is though, the Senate may not be able to pass it via reconciliation depending on whether it adds to or subtracts from the deficit - if they can't, then the Democrats will be able to filibuster and it will be DOA. However even if the Senate can pass it without Democratic support, many of them have said they refuse to pass the bill as is. There are sections of it that they want to change. But those parts of the bill were primarily added to appease the far right members of the House. And if the Republicans in the Senate change those things, then the bill will lose those supporters in the House and won't pass<br /> <br /> What the Republicans need is the President to come out and hammer out an agreement between the Senate and the House. That's usually what the president does. But Trump is too busy dealing with his own BS to do something like that. Plus, with his approval ratings lower than practically any other president in history, he wouldn't be dealing from a position of strength anyway. More and more Republicans are beginning to view him a an anchor that's going to sink them in 2018.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T15:37:15-07:00","id":1093869,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/national-security/house-majority-leader-to-colleagues-in-2016-i-think-putin-pays-trump/2017/05/17/515f6f8a-3aff-11e7-8854-21f359183e8c_story.html?hpid=hp_hp-top-table-main_transcript-6pm%3Ahomepage%2Fstory\" target=\"_blank\">House majority leader to colleagues in 2016: \u2018I think Putin pays\u2019 Trump</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T04:17:56-07:00","id":1094832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1093365#post1093365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This.<br /> <br /> I got too many people on my facebook who are cheering Trump on because he's going to dismantle the big bad government. I hate people who are like &amp;quot;It's broken, let's burn it down!&amp;quot; I mean, if you got a hole in the roof, you fix your roof, not burn the whole place down and become homeless. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div> The only thing Trump is going to burn down is the Republican Party. <br /> <br /> Honestly watching the American system in action with it's Super majority rules and all that kind of stuff, it amazes me that anything actually gets done, no other country functions like this, even Italy with it's ever shifting coalition governments is more functional then this. <br /> <br /> And to the mix you add a goofy President making the system even less functional. <br /> <br /> To impreach President Trump the Republicans would actually have to pull it together long enough to actually get something done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T13:25:03-07:00","id":1094930,"title":"","content":"The American system was a complete and utter mess even before that guy with the musical came rolling around. Can't fix a system that is inherently broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T16:07:35-07:00","id":1094961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1094930#post1094930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The American system was a complete and utter mess even before that guy with the musical came rolling around. Can't fix a system that is inherently broken.</div> </div> </div> </div>By design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T04:28:08-07:00","id":1097483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1000616-2016-election-result-thread?p=1094832#post1094832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly watching the American system in action with it's Super majority rules and all that kind of stuff, it amazes me that anything actually gets done, no other country functions like this, even Italy with it's ever shifting coalition governments is more functional then this.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason that the super majority requirements exist(ed) was to attempt to force coalition building and compromise. Unfortunately over the last couple decades there have been diminishing political incentives to pursue coalition and compromise and greater incentive to engage in obstruction and sabotage. When faced with intractable deadlock the party in power at the time has increasingly turned to weakening the super majority requirements in order to push action through. Unfortunately this also means that when the shoe is on the other foot they have robbed themselves of a negotiating tool. <br /> <br /> Democracy has many strengths. Taking the long view is not one of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}